{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development","id":20836,"title":"[Dragon the Embers] Third Stage Development","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-30T15:57:00-08:00","id":20836,"title":"[Dragon the Embers] Third Stage Development","content":"You may or may not be aware of the fan template that Shock and I have been constructing for years now, but even if you were only passing through the old board's forums you probably saw the rather extensive discussion of revisions pop up once in a while.<br /> <br /> Dragon is a game about... well, what it's about is currently in flux, but essentially you play someone who through one means or another acquired and consumed a dragon's heart and as a result transformed into a new creature; an intermediate monstrosity.<br /> <br /> The game has two major types of powers: Ablutions--which are draconic traits your character can slowly assume and disband for a particular purpose, and Edicts--verbal declarations of your contempt for the laws of physics that bend reality to your whim.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B31Gud9WnwZXa1k2elNGV2oza0U/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon the Embers Second Stage PDF</a><br /> With bookmarks by Yue... which may or may not open automatically, I don't remember the last time I updated it.<br /> FYI, this is the old edition. There have been no changes made to this particular document since the previous discussion.<br /> <br /> EDIT [07-25-14] To celebrate the renewed interest in the project as well as the recent run of inspiration I've had, I present the first half of the Third Stage Development.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B31Gud9WnwZXTHU1OE8wSDVEQWM/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon the Embers Third Stage Christmas in July [07-25-14] First half of the book</a><br /> There are some formatting issues because I ran into a time cramp, and certain things are still a work in progress (such as three of the new Philosophies). Still, if you're just joining us in the project this file will help you get caught up on the changes to Breath, Ablutions, and Edicts, as well as some of the thematic adjustments.<br /> <br /> The game is currently undergoing extensive revisions to improve pretty much every component of its structure (Layout, balance, plot, premise, genre overlap, you name it and the new version works to fix it). It is also being updated to be compatible with both the original New World of Darkness AND the God Machine Chronicles (Highlighted material will appear at the end of paragraphs where God Machine rules differ significantly from the standard rules, explaining the difference).<br /> <br /> <br /> Some planned revisions include:<ul><li>A major overhaul of the Breath system. Breath will have various sources, which the dragon ponders on whenever she calls upon the heat of her Furnace. It is replenished by spending quality time with the source from which it was depleted (For example, if a particular source is a collection of valuable porcelain statuettes, it might have a rating of 3 dots and therefore a pool of 3 points of Breath. When the Dragon uses Inferno, she chooses to spend the Breath from this source. By spending a scene taking in the beauty of her collection, she may recover all points of breath affiliated with the collection [would be easier to explain with a visual example, sorry])</li> <li>A major overhaul to the Ethics system. Ethics is kaput, being replaced with a more GMC friendly mechanic called Honor. All 'sins' on the list trigger degeneration rolls regardless of where the Dragon's current Honor may fall (In GMC, these are dragon-specific breaking points that are NOT removed after they occur, ensuring they can occur repeatedly if the player does not correct his course</li> <li>A major overhaul to the layout of the book, moving all Ablutions and Edicts into their own chapter along with their systems to reduce confusion</li> <li>A major overhaul to the Dreamtide: IE, it's going to be removed.</li> <li>A minor overhaul to the organization of the Ablutions, removing the vestigial 'card suit' references</li> </ul>There are others, but you get the idea; the game is currently in a state of metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> If you need to read posts from the old discussion for some reason, they are collected in an astoundingly long PDF of 192 pages, which I will link to below:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B31Gud9WnwZXR2NOb1Y3dmxNYzA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon the Embers Old Thread Discussion PDF</a><br /> Unlike the Second Stage PDF, this discussion has NO bookmarks. I recommend only browsing it if you were a major contributor in the old thread and you absolutely need to find a post that you made. The posts are in chronological order and may have highlighted text for information I was paying special attention to. Other highlighted text is the name of the user making the post and quoted text.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, the Second Stage PDF isn't a total wash; feel free to harvest it for mechanics and whatever other purpose you may need. Also feel free to discuss the game here, even though most of the topics are already set for revisions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, we are not in any way affiliated with <b>Dragon the Hunted</b> by <i>Alastiel</i>, but that does not mean the games are incompatible. The two templates actually have very little overlap, and thematically they fit well alongside each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 07-26-2014, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T18:55:27-08:00","id":20918,"title":"","content":"I know this is pretty small but it seems all the concepts have lawyer in them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T18:59:31-08:00","id":20923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=20918#post20918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is pretty small but it seems all the concepts have lawyer in them</div> </div> </div> </div>The preponderance of marriage counselor Dragons is, in retrospect, a thing I forgot to point out in my initial runthrough of the Second Stage PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T19:16:23-08:00","id":20932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=20918#post20918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is pretty small but it seems all the concepts have lawyer in them</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the heads up. Philosophies too are getting an overhaul (either reconstructed into TYPES of rulers or being thoroughly modified by Shock. Part of that rewrite will be a better exploration of character concepts affiliated with the various Y-Splats.<br /> <br /> Oh, I thought I'd mention that I'm tossing the 'shade point' rule that is affiliated with Fossilization, in lieu of loss of Health DOTS. I figure that builds better on the RAW mechanic for Willpower Dot loss, and it also lets me do something fun like...<br /> <br /> Massive difference in size mechanics! I know Leviathan already has a set of rules, but I had a wonderful idea after revisiting something Vree wrote and I think it will work well:<br /> If a hostile creature is only half the size of the entity it is attacking, all incoming damage is downgraded in severity one level (possibly making bashing damage irrelevant). Likewise, for a creature that is double the size of its victim, the damage inflicted is upgraded in severity one level (possibly making agg damage remove DOTS OF HEALTH! Scary!).<br /> These steps increase for subsequent doublings, so a monster that is eight times your size inflicts damage that is three times as severe as the type usually affiliated with their weaponry. Lethal damage in such an instance would be instant death to the tiny victim, regardless of how much Health or Stamina they may possess.<br /> <br /> So how do you pick a fight with a goliath like that? Form a swarm! Swarming increases your &quot;group's&quot; effective size enough to inflict normal damage. But! You're treated as one entity, then, and each health box represents the entirety of one member in your swarm.<br /> <br /> I haven't worked out all the specifics yet, but it might be fun to run around as a gigantic DoD 8 dragon squashing hunters. Obviously if I put this in the book I'll come up with a better and more thorough explanation to make the mechanic clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T19:31:55-08:00","id":20938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=20932#post20932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the heads up. Philosophies too are getting an overhaul (either reconstructed into TYPES of rulers or being thoroughly modified by Shock. Part of that rewrite will be a better exploration of character concepts affiliated with the various Y-Splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm leaning towards the former. As much as it pains me to scrap the original philosophies, the types that Frog suggest make sense for a more cohesive game. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T19:45:13-08:00","id":20942,"title":"","content":"You know you could add stuff from other homebrew games such as princess the hopeful or Leviathan the tempest I kinda like your work a lot also can you add how others besides vampire and werewolves react to dragons such as sin eaters or changelings but i seriously like the concept of dragon hearts on weather or not you should cut it or keep it. Also you could add in the other two sins such as envy and gluttony they both seems compatible with whole evil fire school also have you ever thought of the Knights of St. George they always keep talking of hunting down dragons so why not make them the hunters for dragons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T19:14:41-08:00","id":21402,"title":"","content":"That does sound good... would agree that the dreamtide, and card suit references, are two princessy, and at this point, Princesss is pretty widely held to be Fanon.<br /> <br /> What ive seen in your PDF though, seems really promising... just an idea though? Keep the ethics system available for those who ARE NOT using GMC<br /> <br /> As some find its system a trifle overly cumbersome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T21:37:47-08:00","id":21447,"title":"","content":"@ReaperFrost<br /> <br /> Originally the Knights of the Bloody Chalice were meant to represent those that chose to take up the mantle of Saint George. Admittedly they are underdeveloped and they will be receiving some much needed attention in the revision (Specifically I think I will go into great detail about the construction of an Ascalon, or weapon specifically designed to slay a dragon).<br /> <br /> As for the references to other templates, I stuck with the main three as they are both the most familiar to me (and thus easiest to reference) as well as they easiest to quickly relate to by other players. This has been a tradition in most of the core books, explaining how the documented creature views and interacts with the three big games.<br /> I do not believe I could do such justice to other game lines in the intro, and I am hesitant to make any direct references to other fan templates. There is good reason for this; fan templates are significantly more fluid than the published works. Even this book will be changing significantly between this and the next edition, and I pity anyone who would directly reference <b>Embers</b> in their own fan material for that very reason. It's just too difficult to keep the references straight when they are changing constantly.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Prince of the Night<br /> <br /> <i>Technically</i> (I know, never start a sentence with that word as nothing good ever follows) we had both the card suit motif AND the Dreamtide in a released PDF before Princess began production. I DO agree that they need to go, though, and they will. Trust me, the things that will be replacing them will be much better and much easier to navigate.<br /> Ironically, before The Elder Scrolls Skyrim was released our dragons died by rapidly decaying into skeletons. They sort of stole the wind from our sails, though, so I changed the mechanic and repaid the favor by crafting the Edict system based on their Shouts.<br /> <br /> As for your concerns about Honor, you needn't worry. Dragon the Embers is, at Heart (heh), a pre-GMC game. The system I mentioned simply takes the usual list of &quot;morality&quot; sins and places them all at level 0. This not only makes degeneration easier to track, but it transitions well into the new system (so that very little effort need be made to make the game GMC compatible). It also builds on the thematic elements: dragons have a particular code of behavior and if they neglect it repeatedly they WILL suffer the consequences.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Ethics/Honor, I would also like to note at this point that the Hydra (Ethics 0 characters) referenced in the above version (the second edition) will NOT be present in the new edition. The mindless monstrosity antagonists will be Chimera, animals foolishly fed an Oroboros Heart by their master seeking a 'divine pet'. Multi-headed dragons will instead occur when an Oroboros consumes more than one Heart in her lifetime. But you'll have to wait to find out how that works.<br /> Dragons that bottom out on Honor (Honor 0 characters) will instead be rejected by their own Heart, which will refuse to relinquish Breath and will call out for other mortals to come claim it. Unless the offending Oroboros claims a new Heart (and thus accumulates a new shred of Honor), she is doomed to death by fossilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  clarification 12-02-2013, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T23:12:25-08:00","id":21460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=21447#post21447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ReaperFrost<br /> <br /> Originally the Knights of the Bloody Chalice were meant to represent those that chose to take up the mantle of Saint George. Admittedly they are underdeveloped and they will be receiving some much needed attention in the revision (Specifically I think I will go into great detail about the construction of an Ascalon, or weapon specifically designed to slay a dragon).</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've always pictured the Knights, as par Hunter the Vigil terminology, a Conspiracy among Conspiracies. They always tend to be at the lower end of the other hunter groups (Max status 3 in the org that they posing in) but if they catch whiff of a Dragon in an area, they will start organizing the cells that they individually belong to and start applying pressure on the dragon. <br /> <br /> Example, Knight A belongs to Cell A, Knight B belongs to Cell B, and Knight C shares membership between Cell C and D. Normally, the Knights may meet very infrequently or over an extreme long term (a year or so on) and thus are usually just sleeper agents.<br /> <br /> However, when one picks up a scent of a Dragon, they will start poking and prodding their Cell mates towards that area. The effect is subtly coordinated but usually results in more than one cell in a Dragon's turf at one time (and causing a massive headache for her as well).<br /> <br /> Now granted, it maybe wise to back away from that concept to allow the Knights to have their own flavor without bringing Vigil into the mix but it's something that I've always thought about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T06:19:15-08:00","id":21586,"title":"","content":"Heres a question on Meals? How much will resources factor into how readily he can acquire Meals.<br /> <br /> with Resources 5 You can probaly have an entire Staff on hand cooking for you.<br /> <br /> or simply order lots of takeout, and let them scratch their head that they dont see any of your guests.<br /> <br /> Just a curious point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:40:40-08:00","id":21710,"title":"","content":"Meals are getting the axe, actually, as there's been discussion of better means through which a Dragon acquires Breath. ArcaneArts made a very good point that the 'binge to gain Breath' mechanic doesn't help the setting; it only makes Dragons look silly.<br /> <br /> In the current edition yes, you are correct that higher resources would give the dragon more opportunities to gorge without being noticed, and will also decrease the need to resort to alternative fuel sources (like glasses of gasoline). But in the new edition the Furnace will be relocated from the stomach to the left lung, and dragons will need to consume food just like any other living creature (There's always the option to, you know, eat PEOPLE, but it will be a special case explained in Breath acquisition).<br /> The new Breath system will somewhat resemble how Pillars function in Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:17:23-08:00","id":21920,"title":"","content":"Hordes still an option I hope? As that IS Mythicaly resonant<br /> <br /> Might want to require a DICE Roll to recharge using ones Horde though, possibly an ever increeasing Penalty until the hordes been Left alone for a while. (Otherwise the dragon Can sit around his mansion and recharge with his sizable collection of imported VIolins basebal cards etc.<br /> <br /> If it says somewhere I apolagize, but can you tell me how I'll recharge Breath mostly in the new edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 12-02-2013, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T16:18:27-08:00","id":21962,"title":"","content":"Okay, picture a sample dragon (We'll use Cameron, since she's easy to model):<br /> <br /> Cameron has ten points of Breath available, tied to various sources that are important to her.<br /> <br /> Her Patients &lt;-- A Province<br /> O O O<br /> [ ][ ][ ]<br /> <br /> Her Musical Instruments &lt;-- A Hoard<br /> O O O O<br /> [ ][ ][ ][ ]<br /> <br /> Tommy the Coffee Boy &lt;-- A Maiden [Long story]<br /> O<br /> [ ]<br /> <br /> Jubilee Patisserie &lt;-- Another Province<br /> O O<br /> [ ][ ]<br /> <br /> Each has a rating from 1 to 10, depicting how invested the dragon is in that particular source. Players have ten dots to distribute among these sources any way they please at character creation, and they can increase and decrease at Storyteller discretion (they're not really trait dots, so they don't have experience costs).<br /> In this example, Cameron is reasonably attached to her patients, inseparable from her musical instrument collection, amicable to the coffee boy in her office, and fond of the bakery around the corner.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, suppose in this example Cameron pays her daily point of Breath to stave off disaster, and then during the course of her endeavors she depletes two more points. All three she chooses to take from her Hoard of musical instruments.<br /> <br /> Her Musical Instruments &lt;-- A Hoard<br /> O O O O<br /> [X][X][X][ ]<br /> <br /> That night she spends some quality time enjoying her instruments. Maybe she plays the violin. Or maybe she just takes an hour to stare at their beautiful handcrafted quality, piled up in a lump in her bedroom. For spending a scene with that particular source, she may empty out all the marks in that source.<br /> <br /> Her Musical Instruments &lt;-- A Hoard<br /> O O O O<br /> [ ][ ][ ][ ]<br /> <br /> There are less orthodox alternatives, though, to empty these boxes in a hurry. Suppose Tommy is out sick for weeks, thereby preventing Cameron from interacting with him. While it might seem that point of Breath is locked... she can take extreme measures to refresh it.<br /> Consuming livestock (preferably stolen) empties one source per animal ingested, regardless of whether or not the source can be accessed normally. Consuming HUMAN BEINGS, however, empties out all of the sources, completely refreshing the dragon's stores of Breath.<br /> <br /> <br /> This might seem like a really swift means of recovering Breath, but each is actually quite time consuming. Additionally, a dragon's stores of Breath only grow when she increases her attachments to these sources, meaning that raising the powerstat does not increase the available pool of energy. Finally, since Degree of Divinity accelerates the passive drain on Breath and since dragons have a relatively high-cost health recovery mechanic, it is reasonable that they should be able to replenish Breath in large bursts. The idea is to supply players with energy by emphasizing dragon goals and to avoid getting bogged down in 'recharge' sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T21:15:30-08:00","id":22884,"title":"","content":"Lost the stuff I had for the Dynasties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T21:35:20-08:00","id":22892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=22884#post22884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost the stuff I had for the Dynasties.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have it posted on the old mythweaver's forum, it should be accessible now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T04:27:57-08:00","id":23059,"title":"","content":"Will Hordes, Provinces and Maidens offer different abilities like Pillars?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, has any comments come of what I said in the last thread? That Honor should be safe if you do bad things in the name of getting stuff done, but not if you do it for selfish reasons or incompetently. For example, a public execution is no risk if it reduces dissent, but it is a problem if you just disliked the guy or if you're trying to reduce dissent but you're incompetent and end up fostering more unrest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T08:19:08-08:00","id":23158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=22892#post22892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you have it posted on the old mythweaver's forum, it should be accessible now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its back up, but lost the notebook that had the notes during the move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T17:50:10-08:00","id":23410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=23059#post23059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Hoards, Provinces and Maidens offer different abilities like Pillars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't considered it, though it'd be very easy to attach a 'resonance'-esque feature to Breath in regards to proclamation of Edicts. Did you have any ideas?<br /> <br /> EDIT: By resonance-esque, I mean perhaps Edicts that influence people would require Breath from a Province, while Edicts that manipulate objects would require Breath from a Hoard. I'd give specific examples but I don't have any good references on hand at the moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=23059#post23059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, has any comments come of what I said in the last thread? That Honor should be safe if you do bad things in the name of getting stuff done, but not if you do it for selfish reasons or incompetently. For example, a public execution is no risk if it reduces dissent, but it is a problem if you just disliked the guy or if you're trying to reduce dissent but you're incompetent and end up fostering more unrest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking the only sins against Honor will be:<ul><li>failure to protect a Hoard</li> <li>failure to protect a Province</li> <li>personally damaging the Province (including scandals)</li> <li>acting against an Ideology (forgot to list it as a type of source in the earlier post)</li> <li>poor etiquette (break a promise, do not respond to an invitation, refuse a challenge, flee from a fight, and other actions unfitting for a proper citizen of high culture)</li> <li>consuming another Oroboroi Heart (in addition to new Devourer rules)</li> <li>and dying (I'll explain later)</li> </ul><br /> Note there's nothing specific about murder. If a Dragon can commit murder--even a public execution--without violating good etiquette or her possessions then she gets away without a single scratch to her Honor.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for ideologies, well... Let's pretend Cameron has been at it for a while and has subjected herself to a new code of ethics.<br /> <br /> Vegetarian &lt;-- Ideology<br /> O<br /> []<br /> <br /> Ideologies fill the gap that has been left behind by the absence of Morality. A dragon can refresh her breath within an Ideology by deciding not to stray from her beliefs when confronted with a situation. For example, a dragon who possesses the Ideology &quot;Do Not Kill&quot; would refresh her breath in said ideology when she chooses to spare the man that was to be publicly executed.<br /> <br /> I'm sort of on the fence on this one. By including Ideologies we open up the option to use ANY NOUN to describe a source. But it doesn't seem as functional as the others. Are there any thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 12-04-2013, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T20:50:20-08:00","id":23491,"title":"","content":"I hope you keep True Heart and Green horn dragons to me they seem like hard mode in general","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T05:19:39-08:00","id":23692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=23410#post23410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: By resonance-esque, I mean perhaps Edicts that influence people would require Breath from a Province, while Edicts that manipulate objects would require Breath from a Hoard. I'd give specific examples but I don't have any good references on hand at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was what I was thinking for the most part.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=23410#post23410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]personally damaging the Province (including scandals)</div> </div> </div> </div> This is the one I was talking about. I would add &quot;without a good reason&quot;.<br /> <br /> For example, if your Province is 100 villages across a large geographic region and it was invaded by barbarians. I would say damaging the province by flying around burning the northernmost 10 villages and all their fields so the barbarians can't scavenge for food would not impinge your honor. However if you were incompetent enough to believe they intended to scavenge food when in fact they had plenty of supplies then your wasteful tactics would risk your Honor.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another suggestion btw. As your power stat rises your Breath Sources could become more demanding. A beginning Dragon might be ok with a coffee shop, but after time the minimum might rise to an entire shopping high street, then the entire town.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=23410#post23410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideologies fill the gap that has been left behind by the absence of Morality. A dragon can refresh her breath within an Ideology by deciding not to stray from her beliefs when confronted with a situation. For example, a dragon who possesses the Ideology &quot;Do Not Kill&quot; would refresh her breath in said ideology when she chooses to spare the man that was to be publicly executed.<br /> <br /> I'm sort of on the fence on this one. By including Ideologies we open up the option to use ANY NOUN to describe a source. But it doesn't seem as functional as the others. Are there any thoughts on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The risk with this is that it becomes &quot;the ideology of whatever I was going to do anyway&quot;. But before we go any further what is the thematic neiche you want Ideologies to fill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T19:58:00-08:00","id":24131,"title":"","content":"<b>@ReeaperFrost</b><br /> Unfortunately as Greenhorn and True Heart are Philosophies they are being discarded in the philosophy rewrite, as the new Y-Splats will emphasize styles of government. I could see perhaps writing a &quot;hapless&quot; pseudo-philosophy that represents characters that haven't settled into their style yet.<br /> True Heart is currently on the fence. I can make it work, but it will take some doing. Any which way it will be independent of Philosophy.<br /> <br /> <b>@TheKingsRaven</b><br /> On personally damaging the Province:<br /> Sounds good. I'll make sure to present specific cases so that it's clear that the sin means &quot;Actions that impede The Greater Good&quot; not &quot;Any Petty Infraction&quot;<br /> <br /> On Ideologies:<br /> Well what I wanted to emphasize was that--in addition to her obligations as an Oroboros--a dragon is still responsible for herself and her beliefs. As I think on it, though, the Virtue mechanic handles that idea sufficiently and it doesn't need the support.<br /> &quot;What I was going to do anyway&quot; is dangerous not only because it's likely to happen, but because THAT WOULD BE A VALID IDEOLOGY! So let's just toss the idea and stick to the School House Rock definition of nouns.<br /> <br /> On Demanding Sources:<br /> While I can see the logic of making a Province's scope more demanding as Furnace rises, and while I can predict how we would similarly impose such Furnace penalties on a Hoard, I'm just not sure how we'd apply the idea to Maidens. Your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T20:35:38-08:00","id":24151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=24131#post24131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>@ReeaperFrost</b><br /> Unfortunately as Greenhorn and True Heart are Philosophies they are being discarded in the philosophy rewrite, as the new Y-Splats will emphasize styles of government. I could see perhaps writing a &quot;hapless&quot; pseudo-philosophy that represents characters that haven't settled into their style yet.<br /> True Heart is currently on the fence. I can make it work, but it will take some doing. Any which way it will be independent of Philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be helpful to have a &quot;catch-all&quot; for Dragons who don't care to dominate or set up a government style management. Granted this will be a pain on their Breath upkeep but they can exist just as Ghost Wolves and Unaligned exist. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T02:10:32-08:00","id":24248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=24131#post24131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I can see the logic of making a Province's scope more demanding as Furnace rises, and while I can predict how we would similarly impose such Furnace penalties on a Hoard, I'm just not sure how we'd apply the idea to Maidens. Your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's pretty easy. In fact there's two different ways but my prefered solution is to do both of them.<br /> <br /> 1) All Maidens have a &quot;qualification&quot;, why it's worth singling them out.<br /> <br /> At low furnace &quot;eh, I kinda like them&quot; is qualification enough.<br /> <br /> At medium furnace they need to have two+specality or three dots in a skill that catches your eye. An appropriate Merit (Striking Looks). Or maybe they have to be a literal virgin.<br /> <br /> At high furnace they need 4/5 dots. A rarer or more potent merit. Or have stats that reinforces their intangible qualification, such as a virtue or striking looks that plays to medieval stereotypes of virginal purity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2) It's how much control you have over them.<br /> <br /> At low levels you just need to be part of their social circle.<br /> <br /> At medium levels they must depend on you. You pay their bills, are their manager or something, and they know this.<br /> <br /> At high levels they basically live in your giant-dragon-palace and can't step outside without your permission. Total control, though gilding cages is recommended. If your Maidens don't look happy and well cared for that reflects badly on your Honor as a dragon. Who'd trust someone who can't keep his house in order to run a city?<br /> <br /> <br /> This could mean that at high levels you're mechanically distanced from your Maidens; so to prevent that a possiblity is for Maidens to have a trait (probably their maximum Breath) that directly scales with how long you can keep them for and how desirable they might be to other Dragons. Though I must say I like the idea that as you get older you loose interest in your old Maidens but still won't give them up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another question btw; in Dragon who are the metaphorical barbarians?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-06-2013, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T16:43:29-08:00","id":24742,"title":"","content":"I like 2 best. It fits with the bigger... BIGGER! mentality as an expression of &quot;bigger&quot; control. It'll also give a better reason for me to include a 'towering' section in the first chapter.<br /> <br /> Who are the barbarians? That is a very good question. If we think of Dragons as feudal kings, then the ones pounding on their walls COULD be dragons from other Dens, mortals drawn to the Oroboros Heart, or even the knights of Saint George. We could also use the Deep Ones for this purpose (They were swallowed up by the original dragons of old and they reside within the hearts of every Oroboros... though sometimes they escape), but I was reserving them for something else. They fit, though, because their motivations are completely foreign to the Oroboroi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:10:48-08:00","id":24799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=24742#post24742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like 2 best. It fits with the bigger... BIGGER! mentality as an expression of &quot;bigger&quot; control. It'll also give a better reason for me to include a 'towering' section in the first chapter.<br /> <br /> Who are the barbarians? That is a very good question. If we think of Dragons as feudal kings, then the ones pounding on their walls COULD be dragons from other Dens, mortals drawn to the Oroboros Heart, or even the knights of Saint George. We could also use the Deep Ones for this purpose (They were swallowed up by the original dragons of old and they reside within the hearts of every Oroboros... though sometimes they escape), but I was reserving them for something else. They fit, though, because their motivations are completely foreign to the Oroboroi.</div> </div> </div> </div>hum... I'm tempted to say &quot;anything that is not a Dragon is treated as a Barbarian&quot; but that seems to be a bit of a cop out. The Forsaken have the Pure, Bale Hounds, and Spirits (God help any Dragon who gets in their crossfire) and the rest have theirs. <br /> <br /> Mortals in Dragon represent both a resource and a threat (not so much like any other nWoD game) and could be used as such. Other Dragons however, would not be counted as &quot;Barbarians&quot; due simply to the fact the other party is a Dragon (though the term could be used as an insult if a Dragon's Honor starts to reach a noticeably low point) unless said party was a Devourer. The Deep One tie the place of normal humanity as a threat but it depends on how they are used.<br /> <br /> The Ancient Dragons (Those who weren't killed off when humanity took over or Oroboroi who've reach 6+ on their power stat) wouldn't be counted as barbarians as so much as hurricanes and on par of other natural disasters.<br /> <br /> So it's a bit of a toss up between Mortal Hunters, Devourers, and the Deep Ones. I can easily see Dragons referring to the two as Barbarians but thematically, I think it fits the Deep Ones more so than Mortal Hunters due to the fact that most Dragons accept at some level that a Hunter is going to attempt to kill them to take their place at some point and have an amount of some respect for an individual who does that (granted, it's not going to stop a dragon from killing those that fail). Deep Ones and Hunters who are attempting to destroy a heart would not have the same respect. <br /> <br /> In short: If something or someone is attempting to hasten the race's extinction, then it would be called a &quot;Barbarian&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T00:04:35-08:00","id":24971,"title":"","content":"On a different note, I had a cool idea for Edicts in the new edition.<br /> One of the major criticisms for Edicts was the empty dots between laws, which only serve to increase the effect rating of a proclamation (essentially giving it one more use within the scene). My hotfix for this issue was an idea I called Ordinances, wherein a character could specify on purchasing an even dot a 'specialty' target for her Edict, which would further increase the effect rating if subjected to a proclamation.<br /> <br /> I had a better idea just now, though, and I wanted to pitch it.<br /> <br /> Instead of the Law-Empty-Law pattern, dots purchased in an Edict would serve a specific purpose. From 1 to 10, that purpose is:<br /> <br /> Veto-Law1-Law2-2Combo-Law3-BreathGate-Law4-3Combo-Philibuster-Freeform<br /> <br /> I'll walk through each below:<br /> <br /> <b>Veto</b><br /> When an Oroboros learns the first dot of an Edict, she acquires the universal law of Veto for that Edict. She may now detect whenever someone or something is under the effect of a proclamation in the Edict, and can make a proclamation herself to reverse said effect. For example, someone enthralled by one of the laws of Assembly might be freed from the supernatural compulsion by another Oroboros proclaiming Veto with Assembly 1.<br /> Veto starts off very limited in its application as effect rating is likely to be quite low. However, as knowledge in the Edict grows it becomes a very potent shield for constituents against an enemy Oroboros.<br /> <br /> <b>Law 1</b><br /> The Oroboros may choose one of the laws available within the Edict (I'm thinking I'll set up a spread of 5 for each, reducing the total number of Edicts but making each more versatile). Each law is roughly equivalent in potency and--compared to other templates--stands as a level 2 power. Knowing the law, the Oroboros may make proclamations using said law.<br /> <br /> <b>Law 2</b><br /> With the third dot, the Oroboros obtains a second law from the remaining ones available. At this point, the system is identical to the one in the Second Stage PDF except for the addition of Veto.<br /> <br /> <b>2Combo</b><br /> The Oroboros may now proclaim both laws in a single action by spending two Breath, rather than breaking the proclamations into separate actions. This has the advantage of proclaiming two laws at the same Effect Rating.<br /> Any combination of Two laws is moderately useful and equivalent to another system's level 4 power.<br /> <br /> <b>Law 3</b><br /> Just like Law 2.<br /> <br /> <b>BreathGate</b><br /> Each Edict requires a particular kind of Breath to be utilized, such as Breath from a Province in the case of Assembly. But once an Oroboros reaches dot 6 within her Edict, that restriction is lifted and she may use Breath of any type to make proclamations in said Edict.<br /> <br /> <b>Law 4</b><br /> The Oroboros learns one more law within the Edict. Note that it is impossible to learn all the laws within a single Edict. This shortcoming can be circumvented with a Graft, but that's a topic for another post<br /> <br /> <b>3Combo</b><br /> Just like 2Combo, only now the Oroboros may choose to proclaim three of her laws in a single action by spending three Breath. Again, this has the advantage of proclaiming three laws at the same Effect Rating (which by the way is quite high by dot 8).<br /> Any combination of Three laws is extremely useful and equivalent to another system's level 8 power.<br /> <br /> <b>Philibuster</b><br /> For 1 Breath per turn, the Oroboros may prevent any other dragon from making proclamations in the Edict, including Veto proclamations.<br /> <br /> <b>Freeform</b><br /> Ever read Scion: God? You know how the final dot of epic attribute allows the character to take narrative control of the scene, within the purview of the attribute described? Well Freeform law proclamation is like that. For 10 Breath, the player may describe--within the general theme of the Edict in question--exactly how she completely deconstructs a conflict (or creates one). Have fun with this, it's a level 10 power.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T10:14:13-08:00","id":25213,"title":"","content":"Not sure honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T14:34:12-08:00","id":25350,"title":"","content":"I think that mortals, both hunters and not, who aren't ruled by a Dragon is the best out of that list. But that makes it hard for a Dragon to justify it's tyranny as protecting people from barbarians without looking completely deluded. The ideal would be that dragons can plausibly claim to be protectors while hunters can make perfectly solid counter-arguments that Dragon's are just greedy tyrants.<br /> <br /> Though it might be possible to tie it into the idea of looming extinction. Back in ye-olde days (and even today in parts of Africa) other humans basically were a pillaging barbarian horde even if they were perfectly civilised in their own homes. Having a Dragon was a good deal, now, not so much. In essence the species as a whole lost the Mandate of Heaven when the world became safer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T14:49:44-08:00","id":25354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=25350#post25350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that mortals, both hunters and not, who aren't ruled by a Dragon is the best out of that list. But that makes it hard for a Dragon to justify it's tyranny as protecting people from barbarians without looking completely deluded. The ideal would be that dragons can plausibly claim to be protectors while hunters can make perfectly solid counter-arguments that Dragon's are just greedy tyrants.<br /> <br /> Though it might be possible to tie it into the idea of looming extinction. Back in ye-olde days (and even today in parts of Africa) other humans basically were a pillaging barbarian horde even if they were perfectly civilised in their own homes. Having a Dragon was a good deal, now, not so much. In essence the species as a whole lost the Mandate of Heaven when the world became safer.</div> </div> </div> </div>'<br /> Quite. I also imagine that while a few Barbarian groups call themselves &quot;Barbarians&quot; with pride, these tend to be the more intellectual &quot;tribes&quot;, ie The People Who Know What Real Barbarians Were. These are the people who write dissertations on Ghenghis Khan's modern ideals of government and freedom of religion, the foundation of France by the Franks, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> I can easily see Barbarians being a deconstruction of the Fantasy Barbarian ideal-they have abilities relating to the primal and untamed parts of human nature, but part of that human nature also means that when it comes down to it, they're people like anyone else. You just don't speak their language, and from their views, you're greedily hogging all the resources they need to thrive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:43:47-08:00","id":25523,"title":"","content":"After hearing about edicts it reminds me about nobilis powers where they can literately make anything they want to happen as long as its based around their one embodiment which to me edicts kinda sound a lot like that for instance your projectile edict lets you turn anything into a projectile like bottles of water or a pillow having the punch of a shotgun so why not use this to make your voice into a projectile and yes I was thinking of skyrim right now<br /> <br /> Or better yet why not project your thought to another person effectively making a telepathy but with no way to read the guy your message just sent mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T21:23:14-08:00","id":25585,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=25350#post25350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it might be possible to tie it into the idea of looming extinction. Back in ye-olde days (and even today in parts of Africa) other humans basically were a pillaging barbarian horde even if they were perfectly civilised in their own homes. Having a Dragon was a good deal, now, not so much. In essence the species as a whole lost the Mandate of Heaven when the world became safer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. It's arguable that the ye-olde days are not so much different from the world of today (at least, in WoD's viewpoint). Sure, the old barbarian hordes of yesteryear have fallen to the wayside, but now you have crime, corruption, and various other problems that may have a Dragon say &quot;Enough is enough!&quot; and attempt to take command. On the lower end, you have gang warfare where a Dragon can most certainly take the position of a benevolent tyrant while on the higher end, you can emulate Shadowrun's Dunkelzahn and have the people love you so much that they keep electing you as their representative.<br /> <br /> The sociological niche is still there (and so by proxy is the Mandate of Heaven) even if it isn't being expressed in the classical way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=25350#post25350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that mortals, both hunters and not, who aren't ruled by a Dragon is the best out of that list. But that makes it hard for a Dragon to justify it's tyranny as protecting people from barbarians without looking completely deluded. The ideal would be that dragons can plausibly claim to be protectors while hunters can make perfectly solid counter-arguments that Dragon's are just greedy tyrants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, that is the ideal and given the current state of the World of Darkness, it really isn't that hard to pull off. Using CJC's examples, you can have some new disease start attacking her patents, her horde getting robbed (or something stealing the music and running off with it), Maiden getting kidnapped (happens a lot in real life mexico. It's worse in WoD), etc.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I love to see groups of hunters and dragons accuse each other of being tyrants while being guilty of the same thing. Makes good drama. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T05:43:52-08:00","id":25751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=25585#post25585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends. It's arguable that the ye-olde days are not so much different from the world of today (at least, in WoD's viewpoint). Sure, the old barbarian hordes of yesteryear have fallen to the wayside, but now you have crime, corruption, and various other problems that may have a Dragon say &quot;Enough is enough!&quot; and attempt to take command. On the lower end, you have gang warfare where a Dragon can most certainly take the position of a benevolent tyrant while on the higher end, you can emulate Shadowrun's Dunkelzahn and have the people love you so much that they keep electing you as their representative.<br /> <br /> The sociological niche is still there (and so by proxy is the Mandate of Heaven) even if it isn't being expressed in the classical way.</div> </div> </div> </div> The neiche <i><b>is</b></i> still there but it's shrinking. It's being pushed to inner city gang-warfare hellholes and poorer countries.<br /> <br /> In the real world ye-olde days are very different to today. The of dying of starvation or violence are virtually nil for the modal average person in any first world nation. Even the impoverished have a very good chance of getting enough food to survive. In some WoD games it might be worth ignoring that, but in Dragon, with the themes of extinction and heavenly mandate, I'd embrace it.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of room for a dragon today, but like the rainforests their niche is shrinking rapidly. The day it vanishes completely is probably the day they'll finally go extinct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=25585#post25585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using CJC's examples, you can have some new disease start attacking her patents, her horde getting robbed (or something stealing the music and running off with it)</div> </div> </div> </div> The question you have to ask is, would you put up with her eating the occasional person in exchange for her protection? Heck, would you even put up with her managing your life and refusing to let you leave? (Whether you could escape if you tried is a whole other question)<br /> <br /> Now if I was a man from the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:War_deaths_caused_by_warfare.svg\" target=\"_blank\">Jivaro</a> I would take that deal because it massively lowers my chance of death. However, as someone with very low chance of being murdered a dragon would look completely delusional if they thought the occasional human-snack was justified.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically, I'm now thinking that when Dragons build their domains in places where the murder rate is sky high they have an easily managed and loyal population. Anything else is a high risk, their niche isn't gone but it's shrinking and you don't get any rich trading city-states eager to accept a dragon overlord any more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T15:16:33-08:00","id":34111,"title":"","content":"Started working on major revisions; I'm going to be producing sections piecemeal and then releasing snippets (well... chapters) for examination. This is one among many developmental strategies I'm borrowing from Onyx Path (this being the blog-esque feedback style) to finally finish this project!<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I was thinking about what ExplodingFrogs said in the previous discussion about customization of True Form. One of the big problems with Degree of Divinity as written is the mandatory physical characteristics. It directly contradicts the declaration that an Oroboros' divinity is self-defined. So I came up with this:<br /> <br /> <b>Currently:</b> Tail, Teeth, Size, and to some extent Scales are traits that have been absorbed by Degree of Divinity.<br /> <br /> <b>New:</b> At character creation, the player selects three Ablutions to be DoD Ablutions (this is separate from the Ablutions that receive dots). These three are always manifest at a level equal to the Oroboros' current Degree of Divinity. In other words, they are traits that begin to express themselves as the Oroboros manifests other features.<br /> <br /> For example, one player might pick Wings, Claws, and Venoms as DoD Ablutions when constructing a Coatl.<br /> <br /> Benefits to this change include greater system flexibility, especially during character creation. It also makes it easier to remember what DoD actually does (every five points manifest, get a point manifest in each of your DoD Ablutions). It is not without drawbacks, though, the two I can think of being really strange-looking dragon combinations and terminology confusion (I suppose we could come up with a separate name to call these DoD Ablutions to prevent getting them mussed with regular Ablutions... maybe Divinities?).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TL, DR</b><br /> DoD Ablutions (or Divinities) are Ablutions that the player has flagged as being characteristic of their dragon's true appearance. Rather than being used like powers, they are always manifest at a level equal to the dragon's current DoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T20:13:57-08:00","id":34258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development#post20836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A major overhaul to the Ethics system. Ethics is kaput, being replaced with a more GMC friendly mechanic called Honor. All 'sins' on the list trigger degeneration rolls regardless of where the Dragon's current Honor may fall (In GMC, these are dragon-specific breaking points that are NOT removed after they occur, ensuring they can occur repeatedly if the player does not correct his course</div> </div> </div> </div>Why &quot;Honor&quot;? I rather liked the suggestion of &quot;Mandate&quot; that was being tossed around in the old threads; it suggests the ancient Chinese Mandate of Heaven, which resonates well with &quot;Dragons-as-metaphor-for-power&quot; and the &quot;Storytelling game of Divine Right&quot;. &quot;Honor&quot;...no offense, but it doesn't sound much better than &quot;Ethics&quot;, arguably sounds worse, and doesn't have any thematic connection to the splat that I can see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development#post20836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A major overhaul to the Dreamtide: IE, it's going to be removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that the Dreamtide didn't work very well as it was executed, I think that a different kind of dream/thought/archetype realm could suit Dragon very well. I'd had an idea a couple weeks ago about a dream-world that gradually overlaid and subsumed a Dragon's perceptions of the world the deeper he went into it, with Furnace limiting how deep he could ultimately go. It's initially a more symbolic and mythical view of the world, but as you go deeper the symbols overtake the &quot;reality&quot; until you're not interacting with individual people, places, and things anymore, but abstractions of the larger concepts and institutions and ideas they participate in.<br /> <br /> So, in the low levels (someone needs to come up with terminology for this place) you're interacting with a business executive, and see chains leading from him to those who he controls and who control him. You can manipulate those chains and screw around with the hierarchy of the office, or at least how people perceive it. At higher levels, the businessman himself is merely an abstraction for the local branch of his company, and the chains are the connection between other branches. Higher still, and he's an abstraction for the entire corporation, or even the very <i>concept</i> of corporations and big business, and the chains are everything that company/concept touches on. Follow one of those chains and drop back to the &quot;normal&quot; world, and you could find yourself miles away or even on another continent, standing in front of something that was closely connected on an abstract level (a superior, another office, a rival company, Wall Street) but that was separated by vast physical distance.<br /> <br /> If you use this, I recommend this be pretty much the <i>only </i>social magic in a Dragon's toolkit apart from raw charisma and intimidation. This would make it easy for Dragons to manipulate the beliefs and ideals of large groups of mortals, but much harder to deal with them one-to-one. It would also make it very easy for Dragons to forget that mortals actually, you know, <i>exist</i> at the individual level, outside of the context of the faceless masses. Given the themes of the game, these seem like good things for the system and setting to encourage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T20:54:33-08:00","id":34278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=34258#post34258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why &quot;Honor&quot;? I rather liked the suggestion of &quot;Mandate&quot; that was being tossed around in the old threads; it suggests the ancient Chinese Mandate of Heaven, which resonates well with &quot;Dragons-as-metaphor-for-power&quot; and the &quot;Storytelling game of Divine Right&quot;. &quot;Honor&quot;...no offense, but it doesn't sound much better than &quot;Ethics&quot;, arguably sounds worse, and doesn't have any thematic connection to the splat that I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used the term Honor to differentiate it from Mandate because when the new setup was first conceived it was a resource mechanic, wherein Breath was generated by betraying a trust. I've since simplified that into the much more function system described earlier in this thread.<br /> Honor works for me because losing honor for causing a scandal sounds grammatically correct. I can still see all sins being described as 'betrayals of the Mandate', but it is not the mandate itself that is damaged by such a betrayal, it is the dragon's standing.<br /> <br /> I dunno, think about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=34258#post34258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that the Dreamtide didn't work very well as it was executed, I think that a different kind of dream/thought/archetype realm could suit Dragon very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, what you are describing sort of fits my vision of the Network Edict. Perhaps some psychopompus should be infused into that Edict to simulate the effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Dreamtide, including all of its denizens except dreamers, will be replaced with Jormungandr's Treasury, a pocket dimension within the heart of every Oroboros filled with riches, blood, and monsters.<br /> Have you ever played the tactical battle game Disgaea? In the third and fourth installment a mechanic called Character World is introduced. Long story short, inside of every demon is an entire reality filled with more demons. That's sort of what I'm picturing for each Oroboros Treasury.<br /> <br /> The general idea is that every Heart carries with it baggage: previous owners, suppressed memories and deep-seated fears, and the ancient monsters swallowed by the Heart's first owner.<br /> The Treasury is going to serve as an interlude solo setting for characters who have perished, giving them a chance to resurrect without removing the danger of death and without reducing the concept to a flat mechanic. It'll also be possible to reach the Treasury voluntarily, though I haven't worked out what purpose that might serve yet (possibly the destruction of deep-seated fears, like acrophobia?).<br /> <br /> I'm really fond of this idea because the Treasury doesn't need to be real: it could just be a phenomenon that occurs when the Oroboros brain is deprived of oxygen by death. It's also plays on the pseudoscientific concept that because the heart has nerve tissue and all nerve tissue is capable of recording thought impressions the fears and demons of the Oroboros Heart's previous owner are literally transplanted into the player.<br /> But I came up with it, so I'm biased. I'd really appreciate a second set of eyes on the idea, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T21:56:38-08:00","id":34293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=34278#post34278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used the term Honor to differentiate it from Mandate because when the new setup was first conceived it was a resource mechanic, wherein Breath was generated by betraying a trust. I've since simplified that into the much more function system described earlier in this thread.<br /> Honor works for me because losing honor for causing a scandal sounds grammatically correct. I can still see all sins being described as 'betrayals of the Mandate', but it is not the mandate itself that is damaged by such a betrayal, it is the dragon's standing.<br /> <br /> I dunno, think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But &quot;Honor&quot; doesn't tie in to the themes of Dragon. Look at Humanity, either the Promethean or the Vampire version. Look at Memory. Look at Wisdom. The name of the trait is evocative of the game's theme and tone. &quot;Mandate&quot; works in this way for Dragon in a way that &quot;Honor&quot; does not.<br /> <br /> Also, you could argue that the Mandate <i>is,</i> in fact, being damaged: the divine right to rule is contingent upon ruling wisely and well, and will be withdrawn from a ruler who misuses it. In ancient China, that was how dynasties fell: it was believed that an Emperor who fucked up badly enough had &quot;lost the Mandate&quot;, and Heaven demanded (often via some form of natural disaster) that he be overthrown and a new Emperor take his place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=34278#post34278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, what you are describing sort of fits my vision of the Network Edict. Perhaps some psychopompus should be infused into that Edict to simulate the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, the chains are only one form of symbolism that came to mind. It's not necessarily about networking; it's about perceiving and interacting with the world on an increasingly symbolic, abstract, conceptual scale. Traveling between different branch offices of a multinational conglomerate, for example, could take the form of walking between rooms of an ornate palace representing the company as a whole. Killing a dove could foster widespread discord, gang wars, or even international warfare depending on the scale at which the Dragon is operating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=34278#post34278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dreamtide, including all of its denizens except dreamers, will be replaced with Jormungandr's Treasury, a pocket dimension within the heart of every Oroboros filled with riches, blood, and monsters.<br /> Have you ever played the tactical battle game Disgaea? In the third and fourth installment a mechanic called Character World is introduced. Long story short, inside of every demon is an entire reality filled with more demons. That's sort of what I'm picturing for each Oroboros Treasury.<br /> <br /> The general idea is that every Heart carries with it baggage: previous owners, suppressed memories and deep-seated fears, and the ancient monsters swallowed by the Heart's first owner.<br /> The Treasury is going to serve as an interlude solo setting for characters who have perished, giving them a chance to resurrect without removing the danger of death and without reducing the concept to a flat mechanic. It'll also be possible to reach the Treasury voluntarily, though I haven't worked out what purpose that might serve yet (possibly the destruction of deep-seated fears, like acrophobia?).<br /> <br /> I'm really fond of this idea because the Treasury doesn't need to be real: it could just be a phenomenon that occurs when the Oroboros brain is deprived of oxygen by death. It's also plays on the pseudoscientific concept that because the heart has nerve tissue and all nerve tissue is capable of recording thought impressions the fears and demons of the Oroboros Heart's previous owner are literally transplanted into the player.<br /> But I came up with it, so I'm biased. I'd really appreciate a second set of eyes on the idea, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the ideas could be merged, actually: every Heart is much &quot;bigger&quot; in the dream-world than you'd expect, because of all the conceptual and emotional baggage attached to them.<br /> <br /> Of course, as a consequence of this, it's at least notionally possible to use the dream-world to visit any other Dragon's Heart, by virtue of the fact that at a sufficient level of abstraction, you're dealing not with any individual Heart but with the archetypal &quot;Dragon's Heart&quot;...<br /> <br /> Of course, reaching this level of abstraction is probably impossible except at the highest Furnace levels.<br /> <br /> Another consequence is that, by dealing so extensively in abstractions and concepts and archetypes, the dream-world can serve to suggest at Dragons having some kind of connection to the Supernal Realms without ever actually touching on Mage or Atlantis. Or not. It depends on what the players and Storyteller feel like reading into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T14:25:16-08:00","id":38881,"title":"","content":"Some further elaboration on how the dream-world might work, and also some ideas on Dragon's Integrity/Honor/Mandate/whatever and Willpower recovery mechanics.<br /> <br /> <b>Mythic Reality</b><br /> <br /> So I think that a good name for the dream-world might be the Mythic World, or maybe just the Mythos. Fits with the overall symbolic/archetypal/abstract feel.<br /> <br /> At the lowest level, it functions as Dragon's form of supernatural senses: the Ouroboroi's answer to Mage Sight, Auspex, what have you. It's symbolic perceptions overlaid onto the ordinary world: a murderer's hands drip with the blood of his victim(s), someone driven by greed has coins for eyes to symbolize their materialistic view of the world, bureaucrats are literally shackled to and by the institutions they work for, and so on. Naturally, supernatural phenomena are represented as well. This doesn't allow the dragon much in the way of actual influence except insofar as their newly-granted insights give them more information to work with.<br /> <br /> To enter the higher levels, a dragon <i>must </i>be in True Form. They can't enter in human form or partially transformed. On the other hand, doing so costs absolutely nothing; they can do it anytime, anywhere...provided that they're willing to take the risk of assuming True Form first. In the higher levels of the Mythos, symbols and concepts overtake reality; the dragon vanishes from the ordinary world upon entry.<br /> <br /> Everything in the higher levels of the Mythos is an abstraction of a concept, idea, or archetype that touches on the the things of the ordinary world. These abstractions can be interacted with to produce real results. This won't result in buildings being torn down or anything (unless the dragon somehow manages to implant that notion in a construction company), since the abstractions are a product of living beings' thoughts and feelings, but the effects can be profound nonetheless.<br /> <br /> For example, killing a businessman-abstraction representing a particular corporation might lead to the loss of that company's &quot;spirit&quot;, its zeitgeist, its &quot;corporation-ness&quot;--whatever it might be on paper, it's not a corporation any more. The people composing it just don't have any sense of shared identity or loyalty or purpose. They're just a bunch of guys who happen to work in the same building. It might recover, developing a new direction, a new &quot;company spirit&quot;. (And anyone aware of the loss--as the abstraction's killer almost certainly would be--would be in a unique position to shape this new vision.) Or it might just fall apart, regardless of how well it was doing before.<br /> <br /> Or forging an alliance with the abstraction of a neighborhood could leave all the people in that neighborhood feeling vaguely well-disposed toward the dragon, even if they've never met. Perhaps even somehow...obligated. (Or perhaps expecting some kind of obligation from the dragon. That could be interesting.)<br /> <br /> Or compelling fear and worship from an appropriate abstraction could start a cult centered on the dragon. (Or even an inappropriate abstraction: imagine a cult composed of, say, all the used car salesmen in the area...)<br /> <br /> The point being, messing around with abstractions affords dragons widespread social influence, but very little in the way of fine control, especially at the individual level. I also think that perhaps this should be their only form of supernatural social-fu: it gives them a unique niche, and fits in with the themes of rulership and divine right. A king commands nations, not individual peasants.<br /> <br /> Even if they have other social tricks, I think they should be variations on that general theme. Dragons are primal, elemental forces: their powers should have a simple, direct, forceful feel to them, without much in the way of complexity. Influencing crowds with raw charisma and blinding terror? A-OK. Subtle, one-to-one social manipulation? No way.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> The Mythos has varying levels of abstraction. The higher you go, the more archetypal and universally relevant the abstractions you're dealing with become. For example, you might be talking to an actual businessman at the lowest level, overlaid with appropriate symbols of the kind of person he is. Then you shift to True Form (ignoring for the purposes of this example the logical consequences of turning into a fucking dragon mid-conversation) and enter the next level of the Mythos. Now the businessman you're talking to is an abstraction of his entire branch office. Go higher. Now he represents the entire company. Higher still. Now he's all corporations, everywhere. Even higher. Now he's the very concept of Big Business, or Commerce, or Wealth.<br /> <br /> How high you can go is determined by your Furnace. This is mostly so that starting dragons can't become King of the New World Order after a few interactions with suitable archetypes. (Although abstractions have game traits, and archetypes that big-time would probably be biting off more than said starting dragon could chew. Still and all.)<br /> <br /> To leave the Mythos, you have to pass through all the levels of abstraction between you and the ordinary world--you can't be chatting it up with Death Personified and then pop instantly back into the real world.<br /> <br /> Distance in the higher levels of the Mythos is a function of conceptual relation rather than spatial separation. Take the office-businessman from our earlier example. The building you're in could represent the corporation as a whole; going into another room and exiting the Mythos could find you in an office of the same company on the other side of the country. It can be a handy way to travel. Bearing in mind, of course, that you're in True Form when you're in the higher Mythos and can't assume human form until you leave. You need to be careful about what's on the &quot;other side&quot;. (&quot;Breaking news! An honest-to-God firebreathing dragon materialized in front of the Eiffel Tower this morning. More information as soon as we figure out just what the hell is going on.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Also, traveling long distances through the higher Mythos can provoke dreams of a dragon's True Form in the individuals touched on by the concepts they pass through. This becomes more and more likely the higher the level of abstraction, if only because of how <i>many</i> are touched on by major archetypes. These dreams may or may not convey a vague sense of the dragon's intended real-world destination.<br /> <br /> Usually, only concepts and archetypes held by currently living (or, well, unliving, in the case of vampires and lucid ghosts and such) beings are present in the Mythos. The Heart is an exception to this rule; every Heart contains the symbols and archetypes not only of the present bearer, but of all Antecedents as well. It comprises a small Mythos unto itself, called the Treasury. A dragon enters the Treasury automatically upon (non-Final) death, but the Treasury may be accessed as with any other part of the higher Mythos, with one exception: even dragons with Furnace too low to enter the higher Mythos can enter their own Treasury.<br /> <br /> At a sufficiently high level of abstraction, all Hearts are connected by the archetypal Dragon's Heart. They are no different from any other Mythos phenomenon in this respect. This means that a dragon with sufficiently high Furnace can visit another dragon's Treasury, and from there emerge into the ordinary world at the location of their Heart. This may or may not be a level attainable in the normal course of play. (That is to say, if there's a Dragon equivalent to archmastery, it may be restricted to such an evolved template.)<br /> <br /> <b>Mandate, Majesty, and Monstrosity</b><br /> <br /> Dragons don't have Virtues or Vices. They're not human any more, and the keystones of their psychology have changed as dramatically as their forms. Instead, they have Majesty and Monstrosity, the glory of the divine god-king and the rapaciousness of the tyrannical god-monster.<br /> <br /> Majesty is the nature of the authority a dragon holds. It's how they relate to their subjects. It doesn't have to be a specific position--it's more about the <i>style</i> of authority than the particular role. Do they bark out orders like an army drill sergeant? Do they have advisers? Do they lead by example? Or by raw charisma and force of personality? What persona do they try to project, in their role as leader? What kind of Province are they trying to build? What role do they want their subordinates to play? What principles of rule do they strive to uphold?<br /> <br /> When a dragon lives up to the principles of their Majesty in a meaningful way, they gain 1 Willpower. When they take significant risks to do so, they earn a full Willpower refresh.<br /> <br /> Monstrosity is how a dragon abuses their power. It's the indulgence of dark hungers, the exercise of authority to TAKE what they want, and damn the consequences, the clawed boot stomping on a human face, forever. Do they bully subordinates? Do they take protection money? Do they demand worship? Do they literally get away with murder?<br /> <br /> When a dragon abuses their authority in their characteristic fashion, they gain 1 Willpower. When they do so in an extravagant, destructive fashion, they earn a full Willpower refresh. (What I mean by &quot;extravagant&quot; and &quot;destructive&quot; is stuff like demanding exorbitant tribute or human sacrifice or executing incompetent subordinates or making their subjects genuinely fear for their lives. Banal corruption like taking bribes and kickbacks or blackmail earns 1 Willpower; you need to get into full-on Evil Overlord territory for the full refresh.)<br /> <br /> Dragons don't have Integrity or Morality. They have the Mandate instead. Mandate breaking points don't change from dragon to dragon like Integrity does; the Mandate is something that <i>all </i>dragons must uphold as part and parcel of their divine right to rule.<br /> <br /> However, Dragons might still have their own set of &quot;five questions&quot;. These would be tools to help figure out the details of Majesty and Monstrosity.<br /> <br /> The roll for a Mandate breaking point is Resolve + Presence. A dragon experiencing a breaking point isn't struggling to maintain mental clarity, but rather to show their worth as a ruler.<br /> <br /> The following circumstances modify breaking point rolls:<br /> <br /> Acting in the best interests of one's subjects and/or Province (+2)<br /> Mandate 8-10 (+2)<br /> Punishing a traitor (+2)<br /> Eliciting awe/reverence/deep respect from subjects (+1)<br /> Inciting terror in enemies (+1)<br /> Inflicting retribution for disrespect (+1)<br /> Mandate 7-8 (+1)<br /> Upholding established laws, promises, agreements, etc. (+1)<br /> Mandate 4-5 (-1)<br /> Inciting terror in own subjects (-2)<br /> Mandate 2-3 (-2)<br /> Unnecessary violence (defined specifically as &quot;given this particular goal/set of circumstances, you could have gotten what you wanted without resorting to violence.&quot;) (-2)<br /> Mandate 1 (-3)<br /> Selfish, arbitrary commands (-3)<br /> Allowing one's subjects and/or Province to suffer through inaction (that is, you could have done something about it, but didn't) (-4)<br /> Undermining rightful authority (-4)<br /> Acknowledging a mortal as superior (-5)<br /> Allowing disrespect from a mortal (-5)<br /> Breaking laws, promises, and agreements you set yourself (-5)<br /> Causing widespread chaos and disruption (-5)<br /> <br /> Breaking points should fall into one of the following categories:<br /> <br /> A dragon is a Ruler. A dragon is In Charge. If the dragon's authority is undermined? That's a breaking point. If they allow disrespect and insubordination to go unpunished? That's a breaking point, too. If it's clear that no one respects the dragon or recognizes their authority? Breaking point.<br /> <br /> One who rules under the Mandate is as much representative of the state as person. They must conduct themselves as such. If the dragon breaks the laws of their Province, whatever those may be, that's a breaking point. Even (especially) if they established those laws. Breaking their word is a breaking point. Exceeding their rightful authority (somewhat nebulous, but basically: whether formally or otherwise, the dragon is recognized to have authority in their Province, but even the most unrestricted authority has a point at which they overstep their bounds) is a breaking point.<br /> <br /> A ruler's purpose is to maintain peace, prosperity, and order in their domain. Anything that significantly disrupts the day-to-day functioning of the dragon's Province is a breaking point, whether or not they were directly responsible.<br /> <br /> Things that are <i>not</i> breaking points:<br /> <br /> Violence, destruction, and killing are not, in and of themselves, breaking points. If it falls under a dragon's authority and won't disrupt the workings of the Province, they can do it. (In fact, <i>failure</i> to commit violent acts could well be a breaking point--say, in the case of blatant insubordination, or extreme threats to the Province.) Violence-related circumstantial modifiers will tend to make the breaking point roll worse when it does happen, but it doesn't actually cause them.<br /> <br /> Selfish and immoral behavior. You can be a completely awful person and still be a good (for certain values of &quot;good&quot;) leader. In other words, gaining Willpower from Monstrosity is not automatically a breaking point. Again, though, the relevant circumstantial modifiers will make breaking point rolls a lot more likely to fail when they do occur.<br /> <br /> Breaking the Masquerade. (Or whatever term Ouroboroi use. You know what I mean.) This isn't especially relevant, because it'll usually fall under one of the breaking point categories by default (probably &quot;disruption in the Province&quot;), but for whatever it's worth, it's not a Mandate violation in and of itself. The secrecy of the Ouroboroi is strictly a social construct.<br /> <br /> Eating another dragon's Heart. This isn't a breaking point, because there's no roll. Any dragon who commits such a heinous act immediately loses a dot of Mandate.<br /> <br /> Ideas for Conditions resulting from breaking point rolls:<br /> <br /> These don't have mechanics. They're just ideas and flavor at the moment.<br /> <br /> Outrage: Your wounded pride drives you to acts of monstrous fury. (I swear I wasn't thinking of the Pokemon move. I didn't even notice until after the fact.)<br /> Shame: You have been judged, and found wanting.<br /> Despair: You have lost sight of your higher purpose. What place does a monster like you have in the world of man?<br /> Paranoia: Assassins in the shadows and barbarians at the gates! Your enemies are everywhere. The whole world undermines your rule.<br /> Justified: You did what you had to do.<br /> Aloof: You are above these pathetic creatures.<br /> Surrounded By Fools: I really feel that this is self-explanatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T15:25:11-08:00","id":38917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38881#post38881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the lowest level, it functions as Dragon's form of supernatural senses: the Ouroboroi's answer to Mage Sight, Auspex, what have you. It's symbolic perceptions overlaid onto the ordinary world: a murderer's hands drip with the blood of his victim(s), someone driven by greed has coins for eyes to symbolize their materialistic view of the world, bureaucrats are literally shackled to and by the institutions they work for, and so on. Naturally, supernatural phenomena are represented as well. This doesn't allow the dragon much in the way of actual influence except insofar as their newly-granted insights give them more information to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you mean to say that the Oroboros is always within the reach of the Mythos, at least to some extent, and manifesting their divinities (raising the DoD) draws them further into the realm?<br /> I will assume this is NOT what you mean for the rest of the post, though I can see the benefit in such a system I'm hesitant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38881#post38881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To enter the higher levels, a dragon <i>must </i>be in True Form. They can't enter in human form or partially transformed. On the other hand, doing so costs absolutely nothing; they can do it anytime, anywhere...provided that they're willing to take the risk of assuming True Form first. In the higher levels of the Mythos, symbols and concepts overtake reality; the dragon vanishes from the ordinary world upon entry.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I very much like. Actually, I'd like it if it requires True Form and Circling, the rotational flight/sprinting that opens a door for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38881#post38881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything in the higher levels of the Mythos is an abstraction of a concept, idea, or archetype that touches on the the things of the ordinary world. These abstractions can be interacted with to produce real results. This won't result in buildings being torn down or anything (unless the dragon somehow manages to implant that notion in a construction company), since the abstractions are a product of living beings' thoughts and feelings, but the effects can be profound nonetheless.<br /> ...<br /> The point being, messing around with abstractions affords dragons widespread social influence, but very little in the way of fine control, especially at the individual level. I also think that perhaps this should be their only form of supernatural social-fu: it gives them a unique niche, and fits in with the themes of rulership and divine right. A king commands nations, not individual peasants.</div> </div> </div> </div>This this a million times this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38881#post38881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they have other social tricks, I think they should be variations on that general theme. Dragons are primal, elemental forces: their powers should have a simple, direct, forceful feel to them, without much in the way of complexity. Influencing crowds with raw charisma and blinding terror? A-OK. Subtle, one-to-one social manipulation? No way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about this. I still think Assembly is a good Edict and I haven't moved into the Edict once-over yet (working on Ablutions at the moment). They really don't have any &quot;Look into my eyes&quot; powers as is, so I don't think it will be a big point of contention. In general, though, all supernatural prowess that doesn't come from Ablutions are sort of wide-shot as is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38881#post38881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How high you can go is determined by your Furnace. This is mostly so that starting dragons can't become King of the New World Order after a few interactions with suitable archetypes. (Although abstractions have game traits, and archetypes that big-time would probably be biting off more than said starting dragon could chew. Still and all.)<br /> Distance in the higher levels of the Mythos is a function of conceptual relation rather than spatial separation. Take the office-businessman from our earlier example. The building you're in could represent the corporation as a whole; going into another room and exiting the Mythos could find you in an office of the same company on the other side of the country. It can be a handy way to travel. Bearing in mind, of course, that you're in True Form when you're in the higher Mythos and can't assume human form until you leave. You need to be careful about what's on the &quot;other side&quot;. (&quot;Breaking news! An honest-to-God firebreathing dragon materialized in front of the Eiffel Tower this morning. More information as soon as we figure out just what the hell is going on.&quot;)<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Usually, only concepts and archetypes held by currently living (or, well, unliving, in the case of vampires and lucid ghosts and such) beings are present in the Mythos. The Heart is an exception to this rule; every Heart contains the symbols and archetypes not only of the present bearer, but of all Antecedents as well. It comprises a small Mythos unto itself, called the Treasury. A dragon enters the Treasury automatically upon (non-Final) death, but the Treasury may be accessed as with any other part of the higher Mythos, with one exception: even dragons with Furnace too low to enter the higher Mythos can enter their own Treasury.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I was picturing it the other way around... the Mythos is inside of each dragon's Treasury.<br /> That is: When a dragon is aware of an organization or entity that can be abstracted in this manner, it forms a structure within that dragon's Treasury. Think of it like a corporate headquarters with each floor representing a further level of Abstraction. To ascend the building an Oroboros needs to get clearance from the Mythos. Higher Furnace translates to a higher clearance level.<br /> Since multiple Oroboroi can interact with the same organization, the structure is shared between them and simultaneously exists in multiple Treasuries. Breaking into another Oroboros treasury through a Mythos structure is quite an endeavor, though, and not for the faint of Furnace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38881#post38881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At a sufficiently high level of abstraction, all Hearts are connected by the archetypal Dragon's Heart. They are no different from any other Mythos phenomenon in this respect. This means that a dragon with sufficiently high Furnace can visit another dragon's Treasury, and from there emerge into the ordinary world at the location of their Heart. This may or may not be a level attainable in the normal course of play. (That is to say, if there's a Dragon equivalent to archmastery, it may be restricted to such an evolved template.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This I do not agree with. I think a stronger statement is made by saying that dragon Hearts are NOT part of this structure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38881#post38881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mandate, Majesty</b><br /> <br /> Dragons don't have Virtues or Vices. They're not human any more, and the keystones of their psychology have changed as dramatically as their forms. Instead, they have Majesty and Monstrosity, the glory of the divine god-king and the rapaciousness of the tyrannical god-monster.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what to say about this, I'll need to think on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38881#post38881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragons don't have Integrity or Morality. They have the Mandate instead. Mandate breaking points don't change from dragon to dragon like Integrity does; the Mandate is something that <i>all </i>dragons must uphold as part and parcel of their divine right to rule.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's basically what I had in mind. Thank you for the legwork on that chart; I'm still adjusting to GMC and it really is helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T16:23:42-08:00","id":38945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38917#post38917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you mean to say that the Oroboros is always within the reach of the Mythos, at least to some extent, and manifesting their divinities (raising the DoD) draws them further into the realm?<br /> I will assume this is NOT what you mean for the rest of the post, though I can see the benefit in such a system I'm hesitant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. When I say it's Dragon's answer to Mage Sight, I mean exactly that: the lower Mythos isn't so much a realm unto itself as it is a set of symbolic perceptions overlaid on the ordinary world. The upper Mythos is either a separate realm or so abstract that the ordinary world ceases to be directly relevant (I prefer to leave that deliberately unclear), so upon engaging with that &quot;level&quot; of Mythos, the dragon vanishes from the ordinary world. And they can't engage with the upper Mythos without being in True Form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38917#post38917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This I very much like. Actually, I'd like it if it requires True Form and Circling, the rotational flight/sprinting that opens a door for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like that notion myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38917#post38917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure about this. I still think Assembly is a good Edict and I haven't moved into the Edict once-over yet (working on Ablutions at the moment). They really don't have any &quot;Look into my eyes&quot; powers as is, so I don't think it will be a big point of contention. In general, though, all supernatural prowess that doesn't come from Ablutions are sort of wide-shot as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to get the splat's themes and history and framework down long before we tackle the actual powers or the mechanics thereof. Fit the powers to the fluff, not the other way around. If that makes sense? It's something one of the developers of Exalted mentioned once, IIRC--the Charms are actually the very last thing they tackle.<br /> <br /> It's a bit premature to be thinking about specific Edicts, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38917#post38917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I was picturing it the other way around... the Mythos is inside of each dragon's Treasury.<br /> That is: When a dragon is aware of an organization or entity that can be abstracted in this manner, it forms a structure within that dragon's Treasury. Think of it like a corporate headquarters with each floor representing a further level of Abstraction. To ascend the building an Oroboros needs to get clearance from the Mythos. Higher Furnace translates to a higher clearance level.<br /> Since multiple Oroboroi can interact with the same organization, the structure is shared between them and simultaneously exists in multiple Treasuries. Breaking into another Oroboros treasury through a Mythos structure is quite an endeavor, though, and not for the faint of Furnace.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disadvantage of this approach is that this setup is extremely similar to the Astral Realms of Mage--mages enter their personal Astral Space, the Oneiros, through meditation at a Hallow, and follow their personal Astral Path into the Temenos (collective unconscious) and the Dreamtime (the dreams of the world itself). Dragons, in this setup, enter their personal Treasury dream-worlds and navigate from there to the higher Mythos.<br /> <br /> While the Mythos is intended to at least potentially be an alternative perspective of Astral Space (and, for the matter, the Skein of Changeling), I don't think the parallels should be so direct. Having the Treasury be a sort of pocket-Mythos tied to the Heart differentiates them more.<br /> <br /> Also, while I've used the phrase &quot;levels&quot; to express the idea of different degrees of abstraction, I actually envision the transition between them being a lot more subtle and fluid than that term implies. I'm not sure how to articulate it, but your model seems somehow more...closed-in? Rigidly defined? Regimented? Restricted? It doesn't lend itself as easily to the image of a dragon flowing between archetypes and concepts almost without noticing. If that makes sense? Like I said, I'm having trouble finding the right words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38917#post38917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This I do not agree with. I think a stronger statement is made by saying that dragon Hearts are NOT part of this structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. The Heart <i>is</i> pretty special. I was hesitant to make that statement anyway, but it seemed like a logical conclusion given the established properties of the Mythos. It's easy enough to say that Hearts are an exception to the rule (indeed, most rules.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T10:57:36-08:00","id":39485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38945#post38945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's important to get the splat's themes and history and framework down long before we tackle the actual powers or the mechanics thereof. Fit the powers to the fluff, not the other way around. If that makes sense? It's something one of the developers of Exalted mentioned once, IIRC--the Charms are actually the very last thing they tackle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ordinarily I would agree with you, but the majority of our template's thematic structure is already in place. We're down to debating supernatural settings and in Embers the supernatural setting is not the core focus of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38945#post38945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disadvantage of this approach is that this setup is extremely similar to the Astral Realms of Mage--mages enter their personal Astral Space, the Oneiros, through meditation at a Hallow, and follow their personal Astral Path into the Temenos (collective unconscious) and the Dreamtime (the dreams of the world itself). Dragons, in this setup, enter their personal Treasury dream-worlds and navigate from there to the higher Mythos.<br /> While the Mythos is intended to at least potentially be an alternative perspective of Astral Space (and, for the matter, the Skein of Changeling), I don't think the parallels should be so direct. Having the Treasury be a sort of pocket-Mythos tied to the Heart differentiates them more.</div> </div> </div> </div>But doesn't externalizing the Mythos make it too much like the Shadow? I believe we're going to run into this issue no matter what direction we take, and the idea of placing every important concept of reality within the confines of the Heart just makes the Oroboroi so magnificently self-centered.<br /> &quot;Everything important in the world is a component of MY Heart&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38945#post38945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while I've used the phrase &quot;levels&quot; to express the idea of different degrees of abstraction, I actually envision the transition between them being a lot more subtle and fluid than that term implies. I'm not sure how to articulate it, but your model seems somehow more...closed-in? Rigidly defined? Regimented? Restricted? It doesn't lend itself as easily to the image of a dragon flowing between archetypes and concepts almost without noticing. If that makes sense? Like I said, I'm having trouble finding the right words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was picturing it more like rivers in the Underworld. The word you were looking for is 'Deliberate', they wouldn't be able to transition without intent.<br /> Perhaps Checkpoint isn't the right description. What if the concentration of concept is something that experiences a sort of mystic environmental intensity (GMC does a fantastic job portraying hostile environments). As an Oroboros traverses more abstracted Mythos, the energy of those concepts tears away at her like the scorch of a desert sun, and only having a higher Furnace allows her to survive in these places.<br /> Then any Oroboroi could wander into more abstracted regions without being aware of their misstep, but those with low Furnace would be forced to turn back or perish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T19:45:56-08:00","id":39745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=38945#post38945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disadvantage of this approach is that this setup is extremely similar to the Astral Realms of Mage--mages enter their personal Astral Space, the Oneiros, through meditation at a Hallow, and follow their personal Astral Path into the Temenos (collective unconscious) and the Dreamtime (the dreams of the world itself). Dragons, in this setup, enter their personal Treasury dream-worlds and navigate from there to the higher Mythos.<br /> <br /> While the Mythos is intended to at least potentially be an alternative perspective of Astral Space (and, for the matter, the Skein of Changeling), I don't think the parallels should be so direct. Having the Treasury be a sort of pocket-Mythos tied to the Heart differentiates them more.<br /> <br /> Also, while I've used the phrase &quot;levels&quot; to express the idea of different degrees of abstraction, I actually envision the transition between them being a lot more subtle and fluid than that term implies. I'm not sure how to articulate it, but your model seems somehow more...closed-in? Rigidly defined? Regimented? Restricted? It doesn't lend itself as easily to the image of a dragon flowing between archetypes and concepts almost without noticing. If that makes sense? Like I said, I'm having trouble finding the right words.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting spin on the matter is allowing the current owner of the Heart see and experience what past owners have done with it while in the Mythos. This may be cramping on Mummy's territory of memory and whatnot but this is a game about leadership and tyranny so simply having the memories isn't as big of a thing compared the effects of those past actions on the population of the time. It would also help if you reach the a pocket where the effects of the player's actions are shown with an unfiltered lens. That would help to underline the horror setting of Embers.<br /> <br /> an quick example between the difference between a Mummy and a Dragon would be a Mummy would be far more interested on where she was on June of the 1935 year and what happened to the relic she was holding while past actions that may have helped/harmed her cult members/local landscape at that time would be summed up as &quot;inconsequential&quot;. They are after all, mortals and there are always more in an Arisen game.<br /> <br /> On the other end of the spectrum, a Dragon (hopefully) would take the opposite approach. It doesn't really matter what the past owner of the Heart was doing but rather how he treated his province/subjects in terms of getting it and allow him to incorporate the lessons of the past into how he manages his day to day activities. <br /> <br /> A good way to raise a Dragon's morality rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 12-30-2013, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T21:34:11-08:00","id":39771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=39485#post39485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ordinarily I would agree with you, but the majority of our template's thematic structure is already in place. We're down to debating supernatural settings and in Embers the supernatural setting is not the core focus of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. It seems I misunderstood were you are in the development process.<br /> <br /> I do have some ideas on the subject of how Edicts work, but I haven't had a chance to get them organized yet.<br /> <br /> The short version is that (assuming the present model is roughly similar to the previous version of Dragon) I think the number needs to be cut down; they shouldn't be based on skills, and so there's no need to have one for every skill. There should be a relatively small number, each based on/themed after some fundamental/primal force or concept. They should be simple, forceful, and direct, and there should be a way to combine them for greater complexity. (Like syllables of Dragon Shouts, really.)<br /> <br /> Also, re: the &quot;dead dots&quot; issue: Who says they need to go up to five dots? If each Edict has three major effects, then have it be three dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=39485#post39485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But doesn't externalizing the Mythos make it too much like the Shadow? I believe we're going to run into this issue no matter what direction we take, and the idea of placing every important concept of reality within the confines of the Heart just makes the Oroboroi so magnificently self-centered. &quot;Everything important in the world is a component of MY Heart&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, after sleeping on it I think I may have come up with compromise that has a lot of potential:<br /> <br /> The Mythos is within the Treasury.<br /> <br /> The Treasury is within the Mythos.<br /> <br /> Both seem to be true. Both seem to be false. We cannot know.<br /> <br /> Here is the way of it: to consume the Dragon's Heart is only the first step for one who would shed their mortality and become Ouroboros.<br /> <br /> Upon swallowing the last bite, the dragon-to-be loses consciousness. He vanishes from the mortal world. He awakens in the labyrinth of the draconic soul we know as the Treasury.<br /> <br /> Here he will wander the maze, facing his Antecedents and the trials born of their thoughts and memories, their dreams and nightmares, until at last he finds his way to the very center of the Treasury, the heart of the Heart.<br /> <br /> There is a final rite of passage here. I'm not sure what it is. Maybe it varies from dragon to dragon, or Heart to Heart. Maybe it's a gate, or a mystic portal. Maybe it's the divine fire that burns away the last of his mortal impurities. Maybe it's a pool, pure and clear and deep, that he must dive into.<br /> <br /> Whatever it is, he passes through. In so doing, he assumes True Form for the first time. And then, he finds himself in the Mythos.<br /> <br /> Once in the Mythos, he may return to the ordinary world, shifting between degrees of abstraction without need for the Treasury.<br /> <br /> This ordeal repeats whenever the dragon is (non-permanently) killed. He may also enter the Treasury from the &quot;outside&quot;, as with any other Mythos phenomenon. This is the only way to enter the Treasury in True Form.<br /> <br /> There are no greater abstractions encompassing the Heart. Each individual Heart manifests as its own distinct abstraction on all levels of the Mythos, somewhere among the abstractions derived from its current resting place. (This is an exception to the normal rule of real-world location having no bearing on location in the Mythos.)<br /> <br /> No dragon can enter another dragon's Treasury.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=39485#post39485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the concentration of concept is something that experiences a sort of mystic environmental intensity (GMC does a fantastic job portraying hostile environments). As an Oroboros traverses more abstracted Mythos, the energy of those concepts tears away at her like the scorch of a desert sun, and only having a higher Furnace allows her to survive in these places.<br /> Then any Oroboroi could wander into more abstracted regions without being aware of their misstep, but those with low Furnace would be forced to turn back or perish.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like an excellent idea to me. It also provides an excuse to leave the fate of the True Dragons in doubt--no Ouroboros could say for certain that a few might not have survived in the uppermost reaches of the Mythos where no lesser dragon could follow.<br /> <br /> (Assuming that you're going with the idea of True Dragon predecessors of the Oroboroi, as Vree suggested in the old thread. Otherwise substitute &quot;pre-Collapse ancients&quot; for &quot;True Dragons&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":743,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","user":"Exploding Frogs","date":". 12-31-2013, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T13:41:01-08:00","id":40707,"title":"","content":"Sorry to double-post, but I managed to get those ideas on Edicts I mentioned above in something vaguely resembling order, and I think they're more or less presentable now.<br /> <br /> So like I said, I think that Edicts should based on a handful of primal forces. The dice pool should probable be something like Furnace+Willpower+Edict, or something similarly evocative of how they come from raw power and divine right inherent to being a dragon rather than any mortal Skills or Attributes.<br /> <br /> (Maybe toss Mandate in there somewhere? Although that has the downside of making low-Mandate dragons inherently less powerful, which doesn't seem right; there should be advantages to upholding the Mandate, yes, but the temptation of forbidden power as a trope is rather undermined if breaking it leads to weakness. Hmm. Maybe the higher of Mandate and Furnace? That would make flouting the Mandate seem more and more appealing as the dragon grows more and more powerful, which plays well into the metaphor of dragons-as-rulers. The young, ambitious, and idealistic prince who becomes more and more jaded and corrupt when he sits the throne himself...)<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> The Laws an Edict grants should be fairly simple and direct, although powerful. They're not subtle, at least not in the sense of being delicate tools wielded with precision and care. (They can be subtle in the sense of being hard to detect; it's just that their actual effects are more like being hit with a sledgehammer than being chipped away at with a chisel. If that makes sense.)<br /> <br /> Greater complexity can be achieved by combining Laws, both within the same Edict and with Laws from other Edicts.<br /> <br /> I have a few ideas for what some of the Edicts might be, and how combining them might work:<br /> <br /> Edict of Heaven: The name refers to the concept of Providence, &quot;Heaven's Will&quot;, the idea that if Heaven wants a thing to happen, this is a thing that <i>must be.</i> It's the edict of fate and fortune, omens and prophecy. It works a bit differently from Mage or Changeling-style Fate, though.<br /> <br /> When you give a prophecy with the Edict of Heaven, you're not foretelling the future. You are declaring--<i>commanding</i>, even--that &quot;this event is a thing that is going to happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it is so.<br /> <br /> The world <i>makes </i>it so. <i>How</i> is not up to you. If you say that there's going to be a bridge over a particular river when next you need to cross? That bridge is going to be there. It might be a fallen tree. It might be a construction project that <i>just</i> finished when you show up. (Or even isn't finished, but the bridge is done enough for you to get across, and that's all you need.) A spirit could use Influences to freeze the river's surface in that spot, for whatever arcane reasons spirits do anything. Could be an enemy luring you into a trap. (You never specified that the bridge was going to lead to anything <i>good, </i>after all.) Beavers could have built a dam. Debris could have floated, drifted, fallen, and blown into that spot over time until it accumulated into a mass that could support your weight.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter <i>how</i> it happens. One way or another, that bridge is going to be there.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, this works by encouraging events that help the outcome you've chosen, that move toward it, and hindering events that oppose it. By default, this is stuff like circumstantial modifiers to rolls. So the construction crew might get bonuses or even automatic successes on any rolls to make, implement, and overcome obstacles to building a bridge on that particular spot, and penalties or even automatic failures--maybe even dramatic failures!--for trying to bring the project to a halt or move it elsewhere. Anything influencing the crew would likewise benefit or suffer--funding flows like the river they're bridging, supportive lobbyists are incredibly persuasive on this one point, obstructive bureaucrats are effortlessly bypassed. And this applies not just to the construction crew, but to anything and everything in the world that might result in there being something bridging the river when you get there.<br /> <br /> Obviously it would get boring fast if the Storyteller had to roll for every random force or entity that has the slightest impact on your goals, so unless this affects significant characters he can usually just handle it in the narrative. (Unless you can come up with a system to abstract all of that down to just one or two dice rolls, in which case go for it.)<br /> <br /> Combining other Edicts with the Edict of Heaven allows other &quot;incentives&quot; and &quot;penalties&quot; to be applied, as appropriate to that particular edict. You can also use the Edict of Heaven with another Edict to change the time and place a given Law will take effect--effectively, you're telling the world &quot;at thus-and-such time, at this place, under these circumstances, this Law shall take effect.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edict of Earth: This is the Edict of the physical world, the mortal world, the earthly world. It allows control over matter, natural forces and disasters, and the world we live in in general. It does <i>not</i> allow control over living things, except insofar as it can impact them via weather, radiation, kinetic force, and suchlike.<br /> <br /> Laws of the Edict of Earth normally have a relatively limited range of effect. This can be expanded by combining them with the appropriate Edicts.<br /> <br /> Edict of Eternity/The Eternal Edict: This is the Edict of time. As the name implies, it doesn't allow much in the way of time travel or other cross-temporal shenanigans; it is much more centered around preservation and stasis, exempting things important to the dragon from the ravages of time. It also has some influence over age and transition--you can age things into dust or make changes to them that would normally only come with lots of time (like fossilization). Basically, if time is a river, then the Eternal Edict lets you see it clearly and halt its flow or speed it up, but not to go back or instantly jump forward.<br /> <br /> The Eternal Edict can extend the duration of other Edicts' Laws, assuming they have one and it isn't already &quot;permanent&quot;. It also allows for &quot;skipping ahead&quot; in a Law with progressive effects over time.<br /> <br /> Edict of Blood: This is the Edict of living things and the connections between them, both biological and metaphysical. The &quot;tree of life&quot;, blood relations, inheritance (<i>not</i> Inheritance, dear god) both genetic and material, bloodlines, interactions, obligations, oaths and promises, bindings. It generally does not allow direct control over living things but rather over these connections--thus a dragon doesn't mutate the local animals or control their bodies like meat puppets, but alters the ties of predator and prey and parasite to twist their normal behavior and send plagues upon his enemies. He doesn't mind-control humans, but rather binds them in oaths and laws and contracts.<br /> <br /> The Edict of Blood can allows other Edicts to target living things through these connections and relations. It can also allow them to spread from their original target through these connections--a contagious blessing or curse that ultimately affects many more than the dragon could easily target himself.<br /> <br /> There are three more Edicts that I have more vague ideas on. They're really just a set of themes associations, some of them very shaky. I haven't yet come up with even a vague outline of how they'd work out in play. I'm not even sure if they're worth using. See what you make of them:<br /> <br /> Edict of Flame: Creation, beginnings, change, growth, transformation, revelation, inspiration, emotion, being, power, souls, Breath<br /> <br /> Edict of Undoing: Destruction, negation, nonbeing, death, decay, corrosion, entropy, chaos, things falling apart, the center cannot hold<br /> <br /> Edict of Void: Mystery, obfuscation, the unknown and unknowable, shadows, darkness, confusion, the occult, Twilight, the Shadow, the Underworld, spirits, ghosts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T09:47:58-08:00","id":41164,"title":"","content":"Very interesting..Do you have any additional thoughts on how the Edicts should reflect the Philosophies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T10:00:04-08:00","id":42337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=41164#post41164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting..Do you have any additional thoughts on how the Edicts should reflect the Philosophies?</div> </div> </div> </div>They shouldn't. Edicts are a core power, an inherent part of being a dragon. A splat's factions are social constructs and thus don't get to control access to traits and abilities inherent to the splat's condition.<br /> <br /> That is to say, you can't be a dragon and not have a Method. That's just plain impossible. You're a dragon<i> because</i> you have a Method. That's why it makes sense that Method determines what Ablutions a dragon favors, something that could be extended to Edicts. (Or not. We could just as easily go with favored Edicts being either a thing that doesn't exist because they all cost the same, or something the individual player chooses during chargen independently of Method or Philosophy.)<br /> <br /> You <i>can</i>, on the other hand, be a dragon and not be part of a Philosophy. They're a social construct that a dragon can choose to be a part of, or not. Thus the benefits of Philosophies should be unique to each Philosophy. Which means non-members can't use them. Which means they can't be universal abilities fundamental to the nature of a dragon, because how the hell would they control access? Even if it was something that wasn't immediately instinctive, sooner or later someone outside the Philosophy would figure it out.<br /> <br /> Look at Vampire. Invictus Oaths, Carthian Law, Coils of the Dragon, and the variants of blood sorcery aren't Disciplines. They aren't part of a universal, standardized system of powers that all vampires get access to and even the most exotic variations run on. Each is effectively a distinct subsystem of its own that only vampires of the right Covenant get access to. (There are mechanical similarities to the existing systems, chiefly because they <i>work</i> and the writers are sensible enough to not reinvent the wheel, but also marked differences.)<br /> <br /> If Philosophies are to grant any special powers at all, this is the model they should follow. Maybe the Imperators, with their emphasis on direct autocratic rule, have some kind of weird Hoard-based magic where the symbols of luxury and power are translated into actual wealth and authority. Maybe the Idols are particularly skilled at manipulating their subjects' attitudes towards them via the Mythos, or can &quot;draw down&quot; Mythos abstractions to become the embodiment of an ideal, with appropriate social effects.<br /> <br /> Another approach is the way that Demon: the Descent's Agendas work. In Demon, following an Agenda gives you a permanent, constantly renewing Condition that earns you Beats for stirring up plot and/or trouble in an Agenda-characteristic fashion, and can also be periodically resolved for a useful Agenda-relevant bonus. Since anyone can go and see them in the free Kickstarter preview, I think it should be okay to reproduce them here:<br /> <br /> Condition: Prepared for Anything<br /> <br /> A Watcher is always planning and preparing, analyzing edge cases and counter measures and<br /> performing statistical analyses \u2014 all in her head. Other demons are frequently impressed by the<br /> Inquisitors\u2019 preparedness for events they believe nobody could have predicted, but which the Inquisitors<br /> would point out was a simple matter of statistics.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Beat: The Inquisitor gains a Beat when the character poses a question to one or more members of his<br /> ring that leads them to reconsider or change their course of action. \u201cWhat if we try going in through the<br /> roof?\u201d or \u201cHow did the angel know we\u2019d switched cars?\u201d are possible examples.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Resolution: The character can make a leap of logic, connecting disparate clues into a revelatory truth.<br /> Resolve this Condition to gain information from the Storyteller about how the current situation \u2014 how<br /> two plot threads tie together, what a good next step would be, or something that the character saw but<br /> just didn\u2019t connect until now. If no such element presents itself, the player can instead resolve this<br /> Condition to gain a +3 on any Mental Skill roll (Embeds and Exploits included).<br /> <br /> Condition: Angel Empathy<br /> <br /> While most Unchained emotionally distance themselves from their angelic past to some extent,<br /> Integrators don\u2019t. Instead, many spend at least some time actively trying to remember what angelhood<br /> was like. For this reason, devoted Idealists have greater insight into the psychology of the angel than<br /> other Agendas, which they may call upon to their advantage.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Beat: Take a Beat when the character puts the ring at risk or makes the ring vocally or actively<br /> suspicious of his motives.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Resolution: The character can place himself in an angel\u2019s mindset, understanding its actions and plans<br /> by his own memories and analysis of its behavior. Upon resolving this Condition, the player gains a +3<br /> bonus to any roll to evade, outwit, persuade, or learn the bane/ban of an angel. This bonus does not<br /> apply to combat rolls made against angels, however.<br /> <br /> Condition: An Eye for Disorder<br /> <br /> A talented Saboteur quickly picks up a keen eye for the seams where the world is stitched together and<br /> knows just what to say or do to make the houses of cards around her collapse.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Beat: Gain a Beat when the character draws attention to herself by destroying, unsettling, or<br /> destabilizing a system. The attention doesn\u2019t have to be from the God-Machine or its agents, nor does it<br /> have to be immediately dangerous, but it should at least be inconvenient or cause some conflict.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Resolution: The character knows just what to do to turn harmony into dissonance. This may be just<br /> the words needed to start a fight, what buttons to press to set off alarms, or where in the machinery to<br /> toss her shoe to cause it to start tearing itself apart. After performing an action intended to create<br /> chaos, the player enjoys a +3 bonus on the relevant Skill roll.<br /> <br /> Condition: I Know Someone<br /> <br /> The character is a member of the Tempters and probably an associate of one of their secret societies.<br /> Through this membership, he has access to the Decadents\u2019 extensive network of friends and favors<br /> owed, giving him threads to pull all over the city.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Beat: Gain a Beat when the character delegates a task, talks someone into taking a risk on his behalf,<br /> or otherwise avoids getting his hands dirty directly.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Resolution: The character knows someone everywhere. With a single phone call or a word in the right<br /> ear, the character can gain instant VIP treatment. He enjoys a +3 bonus to a Social roll where VIP status<br /> would be a significant benefit, such as being admitted into an establishment that caters to a restricted<br /> clientele, cutting red tape, or similar.<br /> <br /> Getting Beats from Agenda Conditions (including by resolving them) provokes a Cipher roll as well. (The Cipher is...well, it's complicated, but suffice it to say that every demon is on a personal journey of self-discovery, and gaining Beats from involvement with demons, angels, and/or the God-Machine can provoke a roll to see if they've had a moment of insight, allowing them to get information from the Storyteller about the next step in that journey.) I'm not sure how significant this is to balancing Agency Conditions: are the Conditions enough on their own, with the Cipher rolls being a &quot;bonus&quot;, or are the Cipher rolls a big part of what makes them &quot;worth it&quot;? Because in the latter case, Philosophy Conditions (should they be implemented) would need something extra. Maybe a persistent effect just for having the Condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:51:24-07:00","id":107504,"title":"","content":"Sorry to ask but is this project still up or has it been shelved for now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2295-coderr","name":"CodeRR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T12:02:33-07:00","id":107591,"title":"","content":"It's been shelved for now as I am currently in my last year in college. I can't speak for CJC so I am assuming stuff is going on his life as well.<br /> <br /> If there is interest, I may see about resurrecting this project over the summer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T18:26:51-07:00","id":116255,"title":"","content":"I still want to play this, if an opportunity presents itself.<br /> <br /> While I enjoy debating rules or adding tweaks as much as the next person, a finished RPG that isn't being played is a bit like a mounted fish on the wall. It looks nifty but doesn't really do anything. You'd have to see it in action to truly be able to appreciate its beauty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T00:15:42-07:00","id":116388,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u201cWriting a book is an adventure. To begin with it is a toy and an amusement. Then it becomes a mistress, then it becomes a master, then it becomes a tyrant. The last phase is that just as you are about to be reconciled to your servitude, you kill the monster and fling him to the public.\u201d</span></span></b><br /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T10:42:19-07:00","id":116576,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I thought I was there at the end of Second Stage development.<br /> I am experiencing a more and more constricted schedule as time goes on and this fan project is plummeting on my list of priorities.<br /> I have at least three other projects to complete before I can give time to DtE.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to accelerate the production of the project, you can contribute in the following ways:<ul><li>Do a full write-up for a philosophy. We're replacing the five in the book with four new ones:<ul><li>Imperators (Rule by Law)</li> <li>Paragons (Rule by Example)</li> <li>Viziers (Power behind the throne)</li> <li>Idols (Rule by Celebrity)</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Philosophies need to answer the following questions:<ul><li>How the Dragon rationalizes her membership in the Oroboroi</li> <li>How the Dragon manages her Province</li> <li>How the Dragon manages mortals in general</li> <li>How the Dragon interacts with others of her kind</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can work on one of these:<ul><li>Write some laws for an Edict, or write up a new Edict. It is important when writing laws for Edicts that they fit together to make a more potent effect. That is: a Law should work as a two dot power independently, or as a four dot power when combined with another law from the same Edict. It helps to write out possible combinations</li> <li>Draw some illustrations. Illustrating the book is the most time-consuming component of making a fan project.</li> <li>Create some characters with rigorous origins to go into the Storytelling chapter.</li> <li>Develop GMC notes for the existing mechanics. Breath already has corrections to be GMC compatible, but other systems (especially Experience) are in need of corrections.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I'm sorry I can't work faster on this project, but I have more pressing matters to attend to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T21:28:43-07:00","id":187693,"title":"","content":"I know I'm late to the party, but count me still interested. Been watching this game for a while, and somehow just now found the bailout draft wasn't the latest version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T21:55:12-07:00","id":197491,"title":"","content":"I am working on the project, but slowly and between other endeavors. Regrettably I have not given it as much love as I would like, though I've recently had a surge of inspiration.<br /> <br /> The biggest way to help the project currently is to provide me with information about GMC experience, since I don't use GMC myself and so I haven't purchased Blood and Smoke. I need to know the experience rates for Blood Potency and Disciplines in Blood and Smoke so that I can price Dragon's GMC experience table accordingly.<br /> <br /> On another note, I have decided to give the Oroboroi a small stipend of masquerade protection. Most splats do this with memory loss (like Lunacy and Disbelief), but Embers does something a little different. A mortal who encounters a dragon will remember it with crystal clarity, but any time he tries to tell his tale no one believes him. If he attempts to reproduce the dragon with a description or illustration, the result is an ordinary reptile (usually an alligator). This protection, called the Miasma (I like the word, and since the Dreamtide is gone... well, no sense letting it go to waste) does not apply to technology. Specifically: a photograph or recording will capture the true image of an Oroboros; it is not fool-proof.<br /> <br /> <br /> Glad you're on board, WarDragon. Let us know if you have any thoughts on the version as it is, and what you'd like to see changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T23:12:37-07:00","id":197589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The biggest way to help the project currently is to provide me with information about GMC experience, since I don't use GMC myself and so I haven't purchased Blood and Smoke. I need to know the experience rates for Blood Potency and Disciplines in Blood and Smoke so that I can price Dragon's GMC experience table accordingly. </div> </div> </div><u>One Experience is made out of five Beats.</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each time your character fulfills one of the following criteria, take a Beat. Certain criteria have limits: for example, you may only gain one Beat for a Dramatic Failure in a scene.<ul><li>If your character fulfills an Aspiration, take a Beat. At the end of the game session, replace the Aspiration. Choosing a new Aspiration is an excellent activity between games or to handle before the next game session. <b>(NdJesuncolo: Aspirations are simple statements of what a character/player wants his character to happen, like &quot;make</b> <b>Gabriel drink his Vitae&quot;</b><b> &quot;Find information on the hunters&quot; &quot;Encounter a ghost&quot; &quot;Break the Masquerade&quot;. You get</b> <b>three Aspirations, and when you resolve one, you take a Beat and replace the Aspiration.</b></li> <li>Some rolls and powers may impart Conditions on your character. Each Condition has criteria for resolution, usually requiring a difficult choice for the character. If resolved, take a Beat. You may only take one Beat for a Condition in a given scene.</li> <li>Once per scene, if you fail a roll, you may opt to take a Dramatic Failure instead. If you do so, take a Beat. Certain Conditions can have you take an automatic failure as part of their resolutions; you may make these failures Dramatic and take two Beats.</li> <li>If your character takes damage in one of her last (rightmost) Health boxes, take a Beat.</li> <li>The Storyteller can choose to award a Beat for any exceptional example of roleplaying, tactics or character development. If this involves more than one character,<br /> all of them should receive the Beat.</li> <li>At the end of any game session, take a Beat.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><br /> Plus, you generally take a Beat when social influence either mundane (by simple persuasion) or supernatural (Majesty, Domination), makes your character do something he doesn't desire.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Costs</b><br /> <b>Merit:</b> 1 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Skill Specialty:</b> 1 Experience<br /> <b>Skill:</b> 2 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Attribute:</b> 4 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 3 Experiences per dot (It's the new Morality)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 1 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Power stat:</b>5 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Rituals:</b> 1 Experience per dot (though I personally use 1 Experience flat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T23:13:08-07:00","id":197590,"title":"","content":"I'm playing catch up but anyway I can help, I will.<br /> Just let me know what is the highest priority, ok?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T01:10:47-07:00","id":197671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=197589#post197589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><u>One Experience is made out of five Beats.</u>[/LIST]<br /> Plus, you generally take a Beat when social influence either mundane (by simple persuasion) or supernatural (Majesty, Domination), makes your character do something he doesn't desire.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Costs</b><br /> <b>Merit:</b> 1 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Skill Specialty:</b> 1 Experience<br /> <b>Skill:</b> 2 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Attribute:</b> 4 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 3 Experiences per dot (It's the new Morality)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 1 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Power stat:</b>5 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Rituals:</b> 1 Experience per dot (though I personally use 1 Experience flat)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, B&amp;S Humanity only costs 2 Experiences/dot and vampire Disciplines cost 3 or 4 Experiences, depending on if they are Clan Disciplines or not.<br /> Admittedly this makes them very cheap, since they do more work than an Attribute dot. I see no problem with applying this cost directly to Dragon Ablutions, since they are generally weaker similar to pre GMC Vampire.<br /> <br /> If there is something to take away from B&amp;S it is that a lot more powers have been made free-to-use with bonuses if you choose to spend Vitae on them.<br /> For example, Vigor, Resilience and Celerity are now added to Strenght, Stamina and Defense as permanent bonuses (instead of needing to be activated with Vitae for a turn/scene) - but you can spend Vitae to boost them for one action for extra benefit (Resilience gives Armor for its rating for a turn, Celerity boosts Initiative or movement speed for one action etc.)<br /> <br /> So for example some Ablutions would probably look more like this under GMC philosophy:<br /> <br /> <b>Inferno: </b>The dragon can belch up fire that deals Lethal damage. (no cost) If 1 Breath is spent, the damage becomes Aggravated.<br /> <br /> <b>Wings: </b>The dragon can soar or fly at no cost. If 1 Breath is spent, he gets some nifty effects (aerial tricks,mitigating wind penalties, mitigating aerial battle penalties (ie. can fly and fight in the air at the same time instead of flight consuming his normal action) etc.)<br /> (Or, if flying seems too powerful:<br /> Soaring at 1 dot. Full flight at 2 dots. Hovering at 3 dots...There are )many possibilities)<br /> <br /> Part of me likes that you have to spend less time managing resource pools now and only spend them when it matters.<br /> I really love the Ablutions and wouldn't dream of throwing them off balance, but this particular GMC conversion probably wouldn't mess them up too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T01:33:38-07:00","id":197695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=197671#post197671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is something to take away from B&amp;S it is that a lot more powers have been made free-to-use with bonuses if you choose to spend Vitae on them.<br /> For example, Vigor, Resilience and Celerity are now added to Strenght, Stamina and Defense as permanent bonuses (instead of needing to be activated with Vitae for a turn/scene) - but you can spend Vitae to boost them for one action for extra benefit (Resilience gives Armor for its rating for a turn, Celerity boosts Initiative or movement speed for one action etc.)<br /> <br /> So for example some Ablutions would probably look more like this under GMC philosophy:<br /> <br /> <b>Inferno: </b>The dragon can belch up fire that deals Lethal damage. (no cost) If 1 Breath is spent, the damage becomes Aggravated.<br /> <br /> <b>Wings: </b>The dragon can soar or fly at no cost. If 1 Breath is spent, he gets some nifty effects (aerial tricks,mitigating wind penalties, mitigating aerial battle penalties (ie. can fly and fight in the air at the same time instead of flight consuming his normal action) etc.)<br /> (Or, if flying seems too powerful:<br /> Soaring at 1 dot. Full flight at 2 dots. Hovering at 3 dots...There are )many possibilities)<br /> <br /> Part of me likes that you have to spend less time managing resource pools now and only spend them when it matters.<br /> I really love the Ablutions and wouldn't dream of throwing them off balance, but this particular GMC conversion probably wouldn't mess them up too bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind adding GMC blocks for Ablutions. However, I feel doing this for Edicts might break some of the elegance of their intention. Considering Edicts are much more active than Ablutions, and even involve directly speaking the words, I believe it's still appropriate for them to require Breath to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> The book block is being maintained as user-friendly as possible, so players will be able to use it with or without GMC as they please after this phase of development is released.<br /> <br /> Oh, which reminds me. There was another thread on here about aquatic combat, which got me thinking about how disorienting it would be to actually be in combat in a 3D environment such as the open ocean or in the air. I'd like to develop rules for submerged and airborne scenes to better serve the benefit of certain ablutions like Wings (I've also planned an Edict law that deactivates gravity on a certain number of combatants, such would complement the new system).<br /> <br /> Any ideas? Gator the Unread has a good start with surface swimming:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/191846-the-world-of-darkness-and-water\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/191846-the-world-of-darkness-and-water\"> The World of Darkness and Water - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/191846-the-world-of-darkness-and-water\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/191846-the-world-of-darkness-and-water </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I cannot, for the life of me, find anything in the World of Darkness about being in water, other than a specialty of Athletics. So, I made my own rules, but I'm not </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> but I was mulling over how to simulate disorientation. After all, one wrong move and you might lose which direction is up, especially while underwater.<br /> <br /> My first gut thought was that suffering damage would result in temporary blindness (or rather, tapping into the blindness mechanic to simulate the confusion) until the character rights herself. Of course such disorientation would only occur if the character was out of her natural element (a terrestrial). Still, I'm not sure that's a viable system, because it gives a ridiculous advantage to the aquatic/avian combatant. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T01:55:17-07:00","id":198716,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone!I really liked the idea of a world of darkness Dragon-storytelling game,and as I see Shock and CJC have a really busy schedule,so from now on I'm going to help you progress with this project as much as I am able to.Been working on philosophies at the moment,and all I can say for now is that each philoshophy should influence the dragon's view on the world,physically and metaphorically.For example,imperators are the classic model of the &quot;Justice at all costs&quot; in their province,but that defines their very personality as well,in their long/short term relationships.Being hard on others,they're being harder on themselves,and similarly for the other philosophies as well.I'll be in touch and inform whenever I have something appropriately prepared to present.See ya soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3496,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","user":"Pandalfino","date":". 07-18-2014, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:08:06-07:00","id":198721,"title":"","content":"Welcome aboard, FallenEco and Pandalfino! (Sorry for the late welcome FallenEco, I spaced)<br /> <br /> I'm ecstatic to hear that somebody's working on the new philosophies, because frankly I'm not very good at writing Y Splats! (Let's be honest, we all read my interpretation of the original Volcano model philosophies and they were awful).<br /> <br /> I did start a little bit on the new ones, but I sort of absorbed Idols into the Paragon philosophy. Here's what I have so far, maybe it'll give you some inspiration (It's the blurbs from the first chapter).<br /> I'm not particularly attached to any of this, so feel free to change whatever you find doesn't fit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Imperator</b><br /> An Imperator is a general and everyone she interacts with are soldiers marching to battle. She is stern with her allies, who she commands with unquestionable authority. She is ruthless with her enemies, destroying them utterly body and soul. The whole world is against an Imperator, but she will not lay down her sword at the opposition. No, she is mobilizing her forces to strike a decisive blow. Failure is not an option.<br /> <br /> <b>Paragon</b><br /> A Paragon needs to be needed. A Paragon craves attention. A Paragon must be a beacon of respect in her community. She seeks to control the world around her with careful politics and benevolence\u2026 or at least the kind of benevolence that looks good to an audience. All the world is a stage, and she leads by example. Supporting cast receive her love, but those that upstage her disappear.<br /> <br /> <b>Savant</b><br /> There is no better teacher on Earth than an Oroboroi Savant. Recognizing the fleeting nature of their existence and that of life itself, a Savant seeks to educate the mortal masses so that they might carry on once the Oroboroi element has vanished from the world. Ignorance is poison and must be stamped out, by force if necessary.<br /> <br /> <b>Vizier</b><br /> There is power in puppetry. There is protection in sitting beside the throne, rather than upon it. The Viziers change the world by feeding manipulation through a paparazzi face. A Vizier has her fingers in everything; like the proverbial oil tycoon there is no business that is safe from the coils of her reach. While on the surface she may seem plain, she is the most powerful political force in a room.<br /> <br /> <b>Caitiff</b><br /> An Oroboros that rejects her membership is a Caitiff, a coward and a criminal who wanders the world without attachment. Such is not an easy life; other Oroboroi are inherently untrusting of a dragon without borders, and rightly so. Without a province, unmarried, or hoard to sustain her a Caitiff is forced to turn to\u2026 unnatural appetites.<br /> <br /> <br /> I already like your Imperator definition more than what I came up with!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:44:49-07:00","id":198755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=197589#post197589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u>One Experience is made out of five Beats.</u>[/LIST]<br /> <br /> Plus, you generally take a Beat when social influence either mundane (by simple persuasion) or supernatural (Majesty, Domination), makes your character do something he doesn't desire.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Costs</b><br /> <b>Merit:</b> 1 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Skill Specialty:</b> 1 Experience<br /> <b>Skill:</b> 2 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Attribute:</b> 4 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 3 Experiences per dot (It's the new Morality)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 1 Experience per dot<br /> <b>Power stat:</b>5 Experiences per dot<br /> <b>Rituals:</b> 1 Experience per dot (though I personally use 1 Experience flat)</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to do a bit more research on the matter but I feel that a large part of Dragon's Beats come from how the Province is doing. Mostly if the people are Spooked, Restless, Riotous, Revolutionary (The last part is storming the castle to put the Dragon's head on a pike). Other conditions would for the people would be Cowed, and Subdued. Demon's Hunted condition would also work wonderfully if a Dragon is facing a threat of assassination rather than simply being attacked by a lynch mob.<br /> <br /> I feel the need to crack open Damnation City for a bit and see what I can grab from the Ambiance and Attitude section. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T04:30:55-07:00","id":198796,"title":"","content":"I do not use GMC rules,but I am somewhat familiar with them.You are right about the Beats being synonymous with the province's well-fare.I'd suggest that the Heart could inflict Conditions as well,and the Dragon Realm as well(Treasury-Mythos-I would call it Astral as I am fond of the Atlantean Lore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:45:16-07:00","id":200242,"title":"","content":"As I had said,I would present something when it was aproppriate(at least),and thus far I have been re-examining the Imperator philosophy.What you are about to see,was made in around 30 minutes,so if you do not like something,it will be subject to changes according to your feedback and opinion!<br /> <br /> <b>Imperators-Rule by Law</b><br /> <br /> Since the beginning of time and the great explosion that led to the creation of our universe,the cosmos has been moving silently and eternally in the flow of certain principles,seen but not understandable to the human logic.The only common truth human beings can recognize in this,is that all was created to exist.Leave out one of the great cosmic laws and the world will crumble into nothingness.Laws-unwritten rules at first,helped the first man survive,create communities and become the dominant species to rule the entire planet,where other stronger species succumbed into oblivion.If it wasn't for those guiding lights and the ones who stepped in front and have the strength of will to impose them,humanity would have surrendered itself to nothingness as well.<br /> <br /> Without laws,everything is chaos.And chaos,called the hidden hand of God by some,is the opposite of order-the opposite of the steadiness that nurtures life itself.In chaos,there is no control.And what we cannot control,as shown by history itself,may very well become the source of our destruction.In chaos,no civilization or province can endure and an Imperator knows that better than anybody else.Embraced with the responsibility to avoid this anarchy,Imperators strive to embody and disseminate those sacred principles,to all those in her province.To be the law one must first understand it,and thus put aside personal interest for the greater benefit.That kind of confidence makes them prudent,but also swift and sure to their judgement.Justice and order must be preserved,and many of the Imperators go to the extreme to make sure that happens.Injustice won't be tolerated,and one who disagrees with that,should do well to hide it in the presence of an imperator,lest she finds herself at the end of her wrath.Many who do not,bitterly regret the decision they made.<br /> <br /> As personalities,Imperators tend to reflect their philosophy tenet in everyday aspects of their life,being strict to the point of absolute in their opinions,seldom though without any solid grounds to back them up.This kind of behavior marks them as cold and cruel many of the times,and inevitable arguments rise-especially with those they hold dear,being over-protective over them,or too arbitrary with conflicts of course,rising in return.That's not to say they are devoid of emotions,or that they cannot be sensitive and tender,only that they choose wisely when to express themselves that way.They do not let rush decisions and sentiments get the better of them,and as cold as that may seem to an outsider,an Imperator knows that is the way to a just society.The strictness and the punishments they inflict are not only on others but on themselves as well,surprisingly most of the times.They do not shy away from the wrong calls they may have made.Being a ruler,one must first rule himself and discipline comes very high among Imperators.That makes them perfectionists,and many of them find themselves on the edge of obsession,with many young Imperators developing some sort of O.C.D. in their early years.That makes for perfect Finders and Challengers,though other methods may embrace the philosophy as well.A Slayer,may for example come up with more violent solutions to uphold the law,while an Inheritor learns how to impose her will,with sheer dominant looks and a single word suffising to bring almost everyone to heel by breaking their spirit.<br /> <br /> Imperators fear the unknown,and thus learn quickly to observe facts and then acting,becoming as squared-logic as they can be(really annoying to other philoshophies most of the time!).Their constant vigilance makes them rarely surprised to danger,but the lack of facts can be their downfall,as without them any warning is most of the times discarded as gibberish.<br /> Surely,being orthologistically obsessed hardly makes them the best of company,but one that follows an Imperator soon adheres to the feeling of safety when she's around her.That's what is required first and foremost by a ruler,right?<br /> <br /> <br /> Favored Attributes:Wits,Resolve,Composure<br /> Common Skills:Politics,Intimidation,Investigation<br /> Common Merits:Trained Observer,Common Sense,Danger-Sense<br /> Concepts:Charismatic General,Ruthless police-officer,Authoritarian Professor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3496,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","user":"Pandalfino","date":". 07-18-2014, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T16:33:03-07:00","id":200505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pandalfino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200242#post200242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I had said,I would present something when it was apropriate(at least),and thus far I have been re-examining the Imperator philosophy.What you are about to see,was made in around 30 minutes,so if you do not like something,it will be subject to changes according to your feedback and opinion!(Sorry in advance for the lack of paragraphs!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to throw in a couple tweaks... have a look.<br /> <br /> <b>Imperators-Rule by Law</b><br /> <br /> <i>After the spark, Zhu Long--dragon of the south--looked upon the universe and came to understand its principles; an inescapable set of laws to which all matter was forced to obey. These laws were beacons of warmth, remnants of the spark that sought to create, balance, and destroy. Beyond their scope was nothing more than a swirling abyss of nothing. Seeing fractal beauty in this patten, Zhu Long looked to the creatures that spawned from the spark. They too seemed to follow the pattern--those with rules thrived and those without collapsed into oblivion. Zhu Long decided that the greatest gift he could share was the knowledge of this universal truth, which he witnessed as he watched the spark. The Imperators are his heirs and share his aspiration--the supply and enforcement of law.</i><br /> <br /> Without laws, everything is chaos--the very brink of abyssal oblivion. In chaos, there is no control. In what cannot be controlled waits destruction. This is the core belief of the Imperators. Imperators strive to embody and disseminate these sacred principles. To be the law one must first understand it, thus one must put aside personal interest for the greater benefit. This confidence fills them with both prudence and vengeance. Justice and order MUST be preserved, even if such involves extreme measures or violence. Injustice will not be tolerated; those who disagree will face the wrath of an Imperator and her army.<br /> <br /> Imperators reflect their philosophy in their everyday routine and composure, being strict and stubborn to the point of implacability. This behavior marks them as cold and cruel; though an Imperator is not incapable of emotion she is very calculated in social exchanges, carefully suppressing her mental state to maintain authoritative control. They do not let sentiments get the better of them and their decisions are rarely rash; an Imperator knows that an appropriately tuned poker face is essential to negotiation. This is a useful skill as a member of the Oroboroi, her self-discipline has taught her when using Ablutions would be frivolous and she knows to deal with mortal witnesses sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> The strict expectations an Imperator holds do not only apply to her subjects but to herself as well. She requires excellence in all matters, anything less leaves cracks in her walls through which chaos might slip. After all, it was the laziness of the earliest Oroboroi that led to their downfall. Imperators fear the unknown and thus learn quickly to observe before acting. The danger of counterattack must always be assessed. Their constant vigilance leaves them rarely surprised, but an unreliable network can be their downfall.<br /> <br /> Imperators favor hoards as their primary means of replenishing Breath: sufficient wealth can bribe even the most principled of dignitaries and can hire an impressive force of mercenary might. Weapons are a popular choice, as they can always be plucked from the collection in a pinch. As for an Imperator\u2019s province, it in many ways resembles a police state. Security and safety are more important than personal freedoms; the boundaries of the province are heavily monitored by an Imperator (or her trusted subordinates) and those entering and residing are subject to her forceful regime. Imperators are of the opinion they know what\u2019s best for everyone, and being dragons they have the power to impose that opinion on others. Imperator provinces favor traditional geographic boundaries, such as city blocks.<br /> <br /> Being obsessed with protocol makes for unpleasant friendships; other Oroboroi are often annoyed with the seemingly unnecessary precautions that an Imperator enlists. Still, they run a tight ship and that security can be comforting, especially against the paranoia of Heart loss. An Oroboros may be driven to den with an Imperator after she suffers a serious military setback, such as loss of territorial claim or even injury from a mundane source like a mugging. An Imperator can supply the structure necessary to reduce crime in a province and has the dedication to assist in the vicious pursuit of a wrongdoer.<br /> \u200b<br /> Favored Attributes: Wits,Resolve,Composure<br /> Common Skills: Politics, Intimidation, Investigation<br /> Common Merits:Trained Observer, Common Sense, Danger-Sense<br /> Concepts: Charismatic General, Ruthless police-officer, Authoritarian Professor, Local Judge, Hospital Administrator<br /> <br /> <br /> I liked your core idea, but I wanted to make the personality a little more general and include some key points on Oroboroi lifestyle, such as reaction to the Collapse (fear of Chaos) and reaction to other members of their species (den formation circumstances).<br /> <br /> Also (sorry to bug), could you give me the books and page numbers of those merits? I\u2019d like to list it on the page in the new version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T19:14:55-07:00","id":200652,"title":"","content":"Yeah,the alterations you did were pretty well done.You summed it up beautifully ! I did not list parts of their Oroboroi nature as I 'll need some feedback on your vision for them(General info and changes,new dangers,the general Oroboroi psychology and stuff like that)so I can include the way they gather breath as you mentioned for example and other stuff as well.As for the merits,(do not feel sorry,my pleasure to help)they are from the God-machine chronicle rules update for the Nwod corebook.<b>Trained observer page 164,Danger-Sense page 162,Common sense page 161---&gt;World of Darkness-The God Machine Rules Update</b><br /> <br /> P.S.I happen to have a few ideas on the Oroboroi abilities and generally lore and origins as well.Whenever(and if)you may want to hear them or share opinions on those inform me mate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3496,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","user":"Pandalfino","date":". 07-17-2014, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:16:26-07:00","id":200698,"title":"","content":"...And now I have a template for the Savant Philosophy. Thank you, <i>zmaj\u010dek!</i><br /> <br /> Actually, giving my thoughts on the Teachers/Savants, it would be a good idea to catch up on the Breath restoration options...what makes a Maiden (say a TA) different from a Province, (say her/his students).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 07-18-2014, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T22:00:11-07:00","id":200739,"title":"","content":"The second philosophy I've been thinking of is the Paragon one.I am hesitant though about combining paragons and idols.In leading by example,I instinctively think about the altruist,the one who will get into the same difficulties as any member of his province,the person who leads but not commands.Surely,attention could be one of the reasons behind giving an example,but I think it is too absolute to include all who lead by example into this category.I would keep the Idols separated,with them being the rulers considering their province a theatrical stage with them being the directors and more often the protagonists.If we are to keep Paragons the way they are I'd say they rule by celebrity,and Savants the ones that lead by example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3496,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","user":"Pandalfino","date":". 07-18-2014, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T00:47:27-07:00","id":200828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200698#post200698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And now I have a template for the Savant Philosophy. Thank you, <i>zmaj\u010dek!</i><br /> <br /> Actually, giving my thoughts on the Teachers/Savants, it would be a good idea to catch up on the Breath restoration options...what makes a Maiden (say a TA) different from a Province, (say her/his students).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, there are three traditional sources of Breath in the game (I call the sources Assets in the manual). A dragon spends points in an asset to draw Breath, just as if she were spending Willpower. When all the available points of an asset are depleted, she cannot draw more Breath from it until she spends some time with that asset (usually a scene), at which point all of the points affiliated are replenished. As for the assets themselves:<br /> <br /> A hoard is a purely physical asset: the Oroboros draws nourishment from the economic and sentimental value of the objects. For a hoard, the dots of asset refer to the net size/net worth of the objects.<br /> <br /> Example hoards: Musical Instruments (3 dots), Bottle Caps (1 dot), Medieval Weaponry (5 dots). The Musical Instruments might be on display in a single room of the Oroboros' residence, and while possibly considered eccentric the collection is not unreasonable. The bottle caps might be confined to a single container, such as a jar or box, and could be reasonably explained away as a hobby. The Medieval Weaponry hoard, however, is so tremendous and rare that it collects in piles all around the Oroboros' residence, similar to the mythical hoards of gold that might be depicted in draconic imagery. Hoards of sizes larger than five become even more ridiculous, and by 10 dots they rival Smaug's oceans of gold from the Hobbit (Note to self, list the Hobbit under sources).<br /> <br /> <br /> A maiden is a purely social asset: the Oroboros draws nourishment from the subject's talent and also from the act of 'caging' the subject, be it by hindering advancement in her career or legitimately towering her away from society. For a maiden, the dots of asset refer to the extent of the Oroboros' attachment to the maiden and consequently the degree to which the maiden is isolated.<br /> <br /> Example maidens: Jessica [That singer at the parlor] (3 dots), Jim [Who serves me Coffee] (1 dot), Francis [My towered princess] (5 dots). Jessica could have the potential to make a measurable career out of her talents, but the Oroboros that claims her as a maiden purposely polices talent scouts AWAY from her so that she will stay with the parlor. Jim is a friendly, but possibly only politely so, acquaintance that the Oroboros insists on interacting with every time they meet, though there is no active sabotage of his career. Francis, on the other hand, has become so dear to the Oroboros that she has been removed from society--or 'towered'--her only interactions are with the Oroboros, other maidens that have been towered, and possibly other Oroboroi in the den (the last is quite unlikely). At even higher dots the towering becomes more and more extreme, and by 10 dots the only living being the maiden is allowed to see and interact with is the Oroboros handler.<br /> In the case of your TA, this might involve purposely losing paperwork related to the TA's advancement or in extreme cases even sabotaging his thesis.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Province is the compromise between the two, being partly social and partly physical: the Oroboros draws nourishment from the betterment of a society or sub-culture. This often involves staking claim to the sub-culture, either openly or at least mentally, and then working to improve its stature in the world. Province asset dot ratings are a combination of size and prosperity.<br /> <br /> Example provinces: The Coffee Shop (3 dots), Theater in the Park (1 dot), The City on the Bay (5 dots). 3 dots in a province represents significant emotional investment in the property; the Oroboros is determined to see it succeed. In the case of the coffee shop, the Oroboros likely makes it her business to ensure sales are always high and customers are always satisfied with their purchase and experience. 1 dots represents a passing fancy in the topic. For the theater in the park, perhaps holding a season ticket and soaking in the atmosphere of the scene is enough. 5 dots represents an extreme dedication to the region; for the city of San Francisco the Oroboros likely works diligently to ensure emergency service is never interrupted, tourism is flourishing, and the soul of the community is kept healthy and expanding. Provinces of higher dots increase in geographic scope, and at 10 dots can represent entire continents. It might seem like provinces are the hardest Breath asset to replenish, but considering their size individual refresher visits can be quite brief (stopping in for a cup of coffee and a chat would be enough to replenish the Coffee Shop asset).<br /> In the case of your students, giving a lecture would probably be enough to refresh the asset, but to grow its dot rating the Savant Oroboros would really have to strive to inspire the students, to the point that they would spread her message to others.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is another asset as well, which all Oroboroi are entitled to utilize. That is the asset of the Heart itself. It has a rating equal to the dragon's dots of Furnace and can be refreshed by spending time within hearing distance of its beat. As such, even if the dragon somehow has purged her other assets she always has at least one source of Breath.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If by chance an Oroboros cannot access her assets for some time, due to theft or geographic distance, she may still refresh them by two means: Consuming livestock will clear up a single point of Breath, and consuming human flesh will refresh an entire asset of the dragon's choice (It is best to empty the big ones with this, as it is a violation of the Mandate).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To spend Breath, an Oroboros reflects on the asset with which it is affiliated and draws strength (no, not &quot;S&quot;trength!) from the bond she shares with the asset.<br /> I should also clarify on fossilization, as it relates to the Breath an Oroboros must spend each day. The furnace is strained by hiding and revealing divinities and must be stoked with sentimental fuel to compensate. Thus each day the Oroboros must spend an amount of breath equal to the HIGHEST degree of divinity she achieved the previous day (each degree of divinity represents 5 points manifest, so if she got up to 15 points manifest the previous day she must spend 3 Breath to resist fossilization). It might sound steep, but considering how quickly Breath can be recovered this is designed intentionally as a deterrent against all-out burnout.<br /> So what happens if she doesn't pay? For each point of Breath the Oroboros owes but does not spend with her first meal of the day, she suffers a point of fossilization... by which I mean she loses a DOT of Health. These dots can only be recovered by the expenditure of experience; the Oroboros literally has to rip away the damaged tissue and then grow replacement tissue using the furnace.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm considering re-introducing Ideologies as an asset for Breath recovery, mainly because I think they would work well with the idea for Caitiffs I have rolling around in my head. For ideologies, the Breath is refreshed when the Oroboros refrains from action because it would conflict with her beliefs. Like a ban, these ideologies become increasingly difficult to avoid the higher their dot rating becomes (so players can't just take the ideology &quot;what I was going to do anyway&quot; as a quick Breath reserve; it has to be something the Oroboros would legitimately pause to consider).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I also have a reply for Pandalfino but I'm going to place it in a separate post.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Come to think of it, given the creation myth I will be attaching to the game it is entirely appropriate to return the Ideology asset to the game and mention it as the primary source of Breath for the VIZIERS, who are highly opinionated about the world and how nations should be run, or possibly the IMPERATORS who are so dedicated to justice. That would give five types of assets total: Province, Maiden, Hoard, Ideology, Heart. It has a nice symmetry, don't you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  Afterthought 07-18-2014, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T00:57:16-07:00","id":200834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pandalfino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200739#post200739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second philosophy I've been thinking of is the Paragon one.I am hesitant though about combining paragons and idols.In leading by example,I instinctively think about the altruist,the one who will get into the same difficulties as any member of his province,the person who leads but not commands.Surely,attention could be one of the reasons behind giving an example,but I think it is too absolute to include all who lead by example into this category.I would keep the Idols separated,with them being the rulers considering their province a theatrical stage with them being the directors and more often the protagonists.If we are to keep Paragons the way they are I'd say they rule by celebrity,and Savants the ones that lead by example.</div> </div> </div> </div>After your Imperator post I came up with an excellent creation myth involving the five dragons of the five directions (I know they weren't all actually DRAGONS, but for our purposes they are). Each philosophy is related to one of these five dragons and is based on where the dragon was located in relation to the spark (the big bang). It is my desire, therefore, to have the fundamental principles of these philosophies be polarized based on being positioned on opposite sides of the spark.<br /> <br /> Viziers are to the west and thus follow Bai Long, the dragon of the west whose core virtue is rationality. Bai Long was blinded by the spark and those abhors the spotlight; Viziers are comrades among the people instead of throne-borne aristocracy.<br /> <br /> Across from them are the Paragons who follow Quing Long, the dragon of the east whose core virtue is idealism. This is why I was picturing them as smiling heroes of the people.<br /> <br /> As for the Savants, they follow Xuan Long, the dragon of the north whose core virtue is resourcefulness. Being across from the Imperators and Zhu Long (the dragon of the south whose core virtue is passion), Savants are driven by the desire to spread chaos (that chaos taking the form of Anarchy). What better way to drive people to rebel than to give them the knowledge to see they are being manipulated?<br /> <br /> Finally, the Caitiffs follow Huang Long, the dragon of the center who became the spark herself (her virtue was honesty). I'll write out the stories like the first later to explain this, but for now let's just say that because Huang Long became the universe, the dragons that follow her are principled and also terrified of their own destiny which spells death by martyrdom on the horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  Better format 07-18-2014, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T01:33:00-07:00","id":200854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200828#post200828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, there are three traditional sources of Breath in the game (I call the sources Assets in the manual). A dragon spends points in an asset to draw Breath, just as if she were spending Willpower. When all the available points of an asset are depleted, she cannot draw more Breath from it until she spends some time with that asset (usually a scene), at which point all of the points affiliated are replenished. As for the assets themselves:<br /> <br /> A hoard is a purely physical asset: the Oroboros draws nourishment from the economic and sentimental value of the objects. For a hoard, the dots of asset refer to the net size/net worth of the objects.<br /> <br /> Example hoards: Musical Instruments (3 dots), Bottle Caps (1 dot), Medieval Weaponry (5 dots). The Musical Instruments might be on display in a single room of the Oroboros' residence, and while possibly considered eccentric the collection is not unreasonable. The bottle caps might be confined to a single container, such as a jar or box, and could be reasonably explained away as a hobby. The Medieval Weaponry hoard, however, is so tremendous and rare that it collects in piles all around the Oroboros' residence, similar to the mythical hoards of gold that might be depicted in draconic imagery. Hoards of sizes larger than five become even more ridiculous, and by 10 dots they rival Smaug's oceans of gold from the Hobbit (Note to self, list the Hobbit under sources).</div> </div> </div> </div>How about animals? Lord knows of the tales of people holding unnecessary amounts of animals in their homes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200828#post200828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A maiden is a purely social asset: the Oroboros draws nourishment from the subject's talent and also from the act of 'caging' the subject, be it by hindering advancement in her career or legitimately towering her away from society. For a maiden, the dots of asset refer to the extent of the Oroboros' attachment to the maiden and consequently the degree to which the maiden is isolated.<br /> <br /> Example maidens: Jessica [That singer at the parlor] (3 dots), Jim [Who serves me Coffee] (1 dot), Francis [My towered princess] (5 dots). Jessica could have the potential to make a measurable career out of her talents, but the Oroboros that claims her as a maiden purposely polices talent scouts AWAY from her so that she will stay with the parlor. Jim is a friendly, but possibly only politely so, acquaintance that the Oroboros insists on interacting with every time they meet, though there is no active sabotage of his career. Francis, on the other hand, has become so dear to the Oroboros that she has been removed from society--or 'towered'--her only interactions are with the Oroboros, other maidens that have been towered, and possibly other Oroboroi in the den (the last is quite unlikely). At even higher dots the towering becomes more and more extreme, and by 10 dots the only living being the maiden is allowed to see and interact with is the Oroboros handler.<br /> In the case of your TA, this might involve purposely losing paperwork related to the TA's advancement or in extreme cases even sabotaging his thesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I love due to the inherent horror within it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200828#post200828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of your students, giving a lecture would probably be enough to refresh the asset, but to grow its dot rating the Savant Oroboros would really have to strive to inspire the students, to the point that they would spread her message to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good inspiration would be Noam Chomsky. He is undoubtedly a master in his field and able to articulate messages that resonate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T02:19:49-07:00","id":200939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200834#post200834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Savants, they follow Xuan Long, the dragon of the north whose core virtue is resourcefulness. Being across from the Imperators and Zhu Long (the dragon of the south whose core virtue is passion), Savants are driven by the desire to spread chaos (that chaos taking the form of Anarchy). What better way to drive people to rebel than to give them the knowledge to see they are being manipulated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't considered using the Savants to fulfil the role of the Anarchs (more accurately the Brujah). I envisioned them a little differently. Where Imperators rule (Control) by Law, I saw the Savants as acting through infomation. Propaganda, misinformation and gossip in addition to the standard teachings. Still, a slight adjustment and they can still 'rule' (free) people through Knowledge.<br /> They just do so through different means. Now it seems the best way to describe their methodology is to rule through <i><b>Trust</b></i>. Plus it handling answers my question of which is more appropeite for a Savant; Maidens or Provinces.<br /> Teach to Control. Overthrow the Reigme. Viva la Revolution! I'm happy to offer guidance.<br /> <br /> &quot;Did you know that cell phones cause cancer? It might be safer to just use landlines and pay phones...&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;You can't go downtown at night! Don't you know how many muggers are there?&quot;</i><br /> &quot;Are you ok? You should try to lay low for a while, that guy is in a gang. That's what the coloured rag means&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;I'm so sorry, the Family's put a hit out on you. But it is ok, I'll look after you. For as long as you stay here with me.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> It is not a Game of Divine Right if you can't see yourself as the King/Queen in your own mind.<br /> <br /> Will keep working on it. It's a bit of a change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T03:01:53-07:00","id":200966,"title":"","content":"This is the Paragon philosophy from my pov,I hope you like it(though I may edit it later).This time however,I demand an introductory text alteration about the philosophy progenitor(Yes,this I will leave to you CJC)<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Paragons-Rule by Example</b><br /> <br /> Leadership is an attitude.It is about values and priorities measured in actions,not empty words or hollow statements.To be a Paragon is to embrace that attitude.For her,leadership comes across as a state of being,a way to approach life.Paragons act where others would consider even talking,placing themselves in the eye of the storm,thus displacing the fear and hesitation of those around them.Enacting the influence their actions make as self-leaders,they do not look for followers;they make followers look for them.It is through the uniqueness of their own dreams that Paragons become a fountain of hope and inspiration for those around them,pushing themselves to the limit to prove that only through affecting,one can face life.<br /> <br /> Paragons are well-known as passionate and warm-hearted people,with the word &quot;over&quot; accompanying almost every adjective they are adressed with.They also tend to be caring and tender,choosing to believe in others more than they should.Living life to its fullest,they embrace every experience like it's their last.Fearing that the time they have in front of them is not enough(quite an irony for an Oroboros),they become anxious and obsessed with time itself.Driven into frustration,they have several outbursts targetting the wrong people.Hot-headed as they can be,Paragons frequently empathise with the people in their province,grasping a hold of the situation at hand quickly and act even faster,running the danger of recklessness all too often,drawing unwanted attention so they can save time.That underlines them as risky,though in endangering themselves they find themselves in the receiving end of the trust of their social circles.<br /> <br /> Testing themselves is part of their everyday life;that is the way confidence is built and transmitted.Confidence is hope and the gravest sins indifference,and selfishness.It was those two that led Dominion to its end,claim the Paragons,and the abuse of power.Paragons now know there is difference between commanding and leading,and those that fail to comprehend it are pitied,ignored or even dealt with by force.Altruism and charity are nobleties forgotten in today's world,and Paragons know that the clock is ticking for the few remaining embers as well,so they give it all they can,in hope of humanity repaying the debt on itself.After all,most of the Paragons find comfort in themselves,for without inner strength they would not have gone far from the start.<br /> <br /> Paragons spend a lot of time among people,motivating them and nurturing enduring ideals in their hearts and minds.Needless to mention that most often they replenish Breath out of the sheer respect bred by their maidens,though objects with certain emotional value make for great hoards as well.Their provinces most often have a loose organisation,and a warm atmosphere with friendly faces popping up more often than any other place.That does not imply they lack safety;people have learned to step up after the Paragon,and idealism does not allow room for cowardice.Paragons are the first to confront anyone who does not abide or trying to disrupt peace in their close environment.Geographically,Paragons' preferences lie in suburban or even rural areas,where communities are close and people have an easier time trusting one another,resembling more of a family and the warmth Paragons revel in.<br /> <br /> Their passion and energy,bears a strong impact and most of the times gets fellow Oroboroi divided;you either love a Paragon or Hate her.In a Den however,even the latter come to the aid of the Paragon during a crisis,knowing that he may very well be the first to lay his life in the line for them,and the last to back down from a threat.Reliability is the synonym for them in Oroboroi circles,and that bears enough gravity for Paragons to have the first say in a Den.After all,True leadership comes in the form of service.<br /> <br /> Favored Attributes:Resolve,Stamina,Presence<br /> Common Skills:Athletics,Expression,Persuasion<br /> Common Merits:Iron Stamina,Iron Will,Inspiring<br /> Concepts:Modern-day hero,Rich philanthropist,Charitable priest,Loving kindergartner<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T03:13:55-07:00","id":200967,"title":"","content":"Wow Pandalfino, your Paragon is perfect!<br /> <br /> Here is the story of the five original dragons. You will recognize Zhu Long's as his is unchanged.<br /> <br /> <b>Imperators, followers of the Fire Dragon of the South</b><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">After the spark, Zhu Long--dragon of the south--looked upon the universe and came to understand its principles; an inescapable set of laws to which all matter was forced to obey. These laws were beacons of warmth, remnants of the spark that sought to create, balance, and destroy. Beyond their scope was nothing more than a swirling abyss of nothing. Seeing fractal beauty in this pattern, Zhu Long looked to the creatures that spawned from the spark. They too seemed to follow the pattern--those with rules thrived and those without collapsed into oblivion. Zhu Long decided that the greatest gift he could share was the knowledge of this universal truth, which he witnessed as he watched the spark. The Imperators are his heirs and share his aspiration--the supply and enforcement of law.</span></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> <b>Paragons, followers of the Wood Dragon of the East</b></span><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">After the spark, Quing Long--dragon of the east--looked upon the universe and was enraptured by the flash; he watched as the brilliant light permeated every object and organism, imbuing it with magnificence. Fascinated, Quing Long began to correlate the brightest lights with the greatest potential; it was the light that made life so special. Quing Long was particularly intrigued by the trees, whose sole purpose appeared to be the spread of life, light, and beauty. He saw promise in this beauty\u2026 the promise of a universe at peace, following the example of trees in bloom. Quing Long decided that the greatest gift he could share was this perspective, which he gained after witnessing the spark. The Paragons are his heirs and share his wisdom--the need to lead by example.</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Savants, followers of the Water Dragon of the North</b><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">After the spark, Xuan Long--dragon of the north--looked upon the universe and saw beauty in its chaos; he was astounded that even the tiniest variation in circumstance could have widespread consequence. Like the waters of a stream grinding great boulders into dust, Xuan Long saw chaos as a force that could topple even the greatest of beings. To control chaos\u2026 to shape and direct it to one\u2019s own whim\u2026 to accept it as the inescapable champion of reality\u2026 he recognized such was the ultimate expression of enlightenment. Xuan Long decided that the greatest gift he could share was the knowledge of this universal truth, which he witnessed as he watched the spark. The Savants are his heirs and share his aspiration--the breeding and acceptance of chaos.</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Viziers, followers of the Metal Dragon of the West</b><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">After the spark, Bai Long--dragon of the west--looked upon the universe and was blinded by the flash; he was left groping in the dark and in despair over the loss. Deprived of the sense he used his snout to detect his surroundings, experiencing the universe through odor like no other dragon could. Bai Long was offended by the smell of gold, it reeked of entitlement and sloth. Conversely he was drawn to the smelting odor of iron. It was the scent of the common man. It was the scent of determination. Bai Long saw hope in these beings\u2026 the hope that he might someday witness the universe through his eyes and not his nose. For only the blind truly know what the blind need most. Bai Long decided that the greatest gift he could share was this perspective, which he gained after witnessing the spark. The Viziers are his heirs and share his wisdom--the need to relate to the common man.</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Caitiffs, inheritors of the Earth Dragon of the Center</b><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Huang Long--dragon of the center--looked upon the darkness and despaired at its emptiness. All that was and all that ever would be was herself and her four brothers. The others seemed content with the arrangement, but Huang Long sorrowed at the circumstance. She longed to nurture, but the extent of reality\u2019s potential had already been spent on her and her dragon kin. The only hope of creating anything else waited in the destruction of one of her siblings. But Huang Long was honorable: she could not bring herself to harm any of them. Instead, she made the supreme sacrifice. Praying to the light within her Heart, she erupted in a cataclysm of creation: the spark, and from her formed the entirety of the universe. The earth, the stars, the trees, the rocks, mankind--all are a piece of the center dragon Huang Long. Caitiffs in particular are inheritors of her spirit; despite her absence they receive the message of Huang Long, the call to their supreme duty. It is the duty of each Caitiff to sacrifice herself for the sake of the universe. But knowing that this death is inevitable, and that is must come of their own volition, is enough to drive a Caitiff to despair. It is no wonder they flee their destiny.</span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T09:57:41-07:00","id":201229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200834#post200834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After your Imperator post I came up with an excellent creation myth involving the five dragons of the five directions (I know they weren't all actually DRAGONS, but for our purposes they are). Each philosophy is related to one of these five dragons and is based on where the dragon was located in relation to the spark (the big bang). It is my desire, therefore, to have the fundamental principles of these philosophies be polarized based on being positioned on opposite sides of the spark.</div> </div> </div> </div>REALLY loved it!!!Probably one of the best creation myths I've heard in any Pen n Paper RPG so far.Keep at it bro!What's more,I think we should make the bonuses for a philosophy apply to certain rolls,e.g. Imperators gain the 9-a rule/+2 on rolls directly involving upholding-enforcing the law,Paragons the same on rolls directly involving motivating,inspiring,enduring stuff to set an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T10:33:54-07:00","id":201261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pandalfino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=201229#post201229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> REALLY loved it!!!Probably one of the best creation myths I've heard in any Pen n Paper RPG so far.Keep at it bro!What's more,I think we should make the bonuses for a philosophy apply to certain rolls,e.g. Imperators gain the 9-a rule/+2 on rolls directly involving upholding-enforcing the law,Paragons the same on rolls directly involving motivating,inspiring,enduring stuff to set an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... maybe not a bonus in the traditional sense.<br /> <br /> The new version's edicts are only going to have 3 levels (I'm pitching the empty levels and increasing the EXP cost like what was suggested earlier in the discussion) but they're also going to have specialty-esque tack-ons called Ordinances. When an Oroboros makes a law proclamation within the scope of her ordinance, the effect rating of the proclamation is increased by two (So if said Oroboros had Husbandry 3 and an ordinance for dogs, her first proclamation would have effect rating 3, or 5 if she used it on dogs). Perhaps each philosophy--in addition to giving one free dot in an Edict--could supply a static ordinance related to the gift of the founding dragon... one that applies to ALL of her Edicts.<br /> In addition, I think that for GMC compatibility holding up the truths of the founder is grounds for gaining a beat.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...Which gives me another idea... Since Effect Rating is Edict + DoD and Edict can only climb to 3 now, perhaps there should be a Breath dump option to increase the effect. Like say, a normal proclamation is free but each point of Breath spent increases the ER by one (subject to Breath per turn limits). That would work well with GMC as well, which seems to have made energy requirements optional.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that you liked the creation myth. It feels like Embers is finally getting the depth of setting that it needed (admittedly my fault, but I'm glad it's being fixed). I hope others enjoy this too, enough to intrigue them into playing the template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:19:18-07:00","id":208984,"title":"","content":"It's Christmas in July!<br /> <br /> I was getting close to the halfway point in my sweep and I decided I'd like to share what I've got so far, today, as a gift for the people following the project.<br /> Thus, I give the CIJ draft (It's an acronym for Christmas In July): the first three chapters of the book!<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B31Gud9WnwZXTHU1OE8wSDVEQWM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B31...it?usp=sharing</a></b><br /> <br /> As you'll notice, I started out strong with the formatting and then ran into some issues. Some of the pages may have unfortunate arrangements because of this, and the pages that have numbers are most certainly going to be the wrong numbers. Rest assured the final version I assemble will have much better presentation than this, including sub-section headings in the footers.<br /> <br /> Also, if you go into the first and second chapter you will see my mediocre artwork has begun to work its way into the document! If you don't like them... well, you can always commission a professional for artwork and send me the information. Be sure you get their copyright release, though, I don't want to get into a tangle over something like that.<br /> <br /> You'll also note that only two of the Philosophies are finished, internal page references are broken, and there are some typos. This sort of thing happens when a book gets cut in half.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Points of interest:</b> I've adjusted Ablutions so that the use of Breath is optional. By contrast to earlier versions of the template they may seem VERY powerful, and in fact they probably are. I'm tired of balancing dragons against other creatures, I'm only interested in balancing dragons against each other. You'll also note that the number of Edicts has gone down significantly: it is quite an endeavor making sure each law is compatible with each other law. I felt it better to have ten good Edicts instead of twenty-five mediocre ones. You may also notice repeated mention of the Einherjar. They're a new critter I came up with to fill the gap left by the removal of the Bloody Chalice conspiracy; they're essentially restless dead that possess living beings to pursue their unfinished business. Unfortunately such possession causes the body to begin decay as if deceased. I've also made some allusions about what the Treasury will be like, but I'm not ready to discuss specifics yet.<br /> Finally, there are still three Philosophies that haven't been written; they're marked in the bookmarks as WIP and you'll see there's really nothing on them yet. If somebody could produce write-ups for one or all of these like Pandalfino did (I know FallenEco is working on Savants), that would be awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> Enjoy! And again, sorry about the haphazard formatting, I ran into a time crunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T22:43:17-07:00","id":209083,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of tweaking my idea about Savants and trust; think that is a better fit for the Viziers.<br /> Don't worry; I've got my replacement which ties up all my odd ideas about the Savants in a neat little bow. Should have it up within in a week. Added bonus, I've some notes about the Viziers so I can get started on the next one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T03:24:19-07:00","id":209253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=208984#post208984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may also notice repeated mention of the Einherjar. They're a new critter I came up with to fill the gap left by the removal of the Bloody Chalice conspiracy; they're essentially restless dead that possess living beings to pursue their unfinished business. Unfortunately such possession causes the body to begin decay as if deceased. I've also made some allusions about what the Treasury will be like, but I'm not ready to discuss specifics yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Revenants? Could be interesting but overall, the horror in Dragon seems to be on how big your hoard is, where your Maidens are, etc. In short, It's thieves, not Werewolves or Changelings that keep Dragons up at night. It's the people coming to take their shit and if they don't get their crap back within a certain amount of time, the Heart starts taking it's pound of flesh (flesh being turned to Stone).<br /> <br /> After all, As much as The Hobbit is a stable of fantasy literature, it is at it's core, a Heist novel. People hear of a great treasure owned by some guardian and come together to steal it and piss it off in the process.<br /> <br /> Though I may be ripping off Mummy too much with that line of thought but it's what I have at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 07-26-2014, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T04:30:23-07:00","id":209264,"title":"","content":"Oh good, I was worried I'd double post.<br /> <br /> I thought I should share my ideas/notes for the Viziers just in case someone else wants to write them. Most of it is how they differ from Savants, seeing as how they can be disturbingly close conceptually. The Viziers (puppet-master/adviser) and the Savants (revolutionary/teacher) can appear to be different points in the same philosophical cycle. This is not so.<br /> <br /> The big one is that Viziers rule by proxy (if they rule at all), while Savants 'rule' by legacy (or to put it in more obscure terms, <b>meme</b>).<br /> <br /> What this actually entails has sort of already been mentioned, having been discussed on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=198721#post198721\">pages 4 (splat outline)</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=200834#post200834\">5 (virtue)</a>. The bottom line has not though. To put it in the simplest terms I can; Savants are not the philosophy of scholars and Viziers are not the philosophy of con men. They <i>can </i>be but it is not inherent. Remember that their virtues (Rationality for<br /> Viziers, Resourcefulness for Savants) does not directly support these roles. So instead, I looked at how these roles support their respective virtues.<br /> <br /> It's simple really, Viziers are planners, schemers, working their networks of information and wealth two steps ahead of everyone, proactively pursuing their agenda. They are careful to keep their goals grounded in reality. Which also makes it easier to deal with your average Joe Blow, since they keep abreast of such affairs. If I had to anolog Viziers with another groups splat, it would be Demon's Tempters.<br /> <br /> Think of the proverb: '<b>give a man a fish and you feed him for a day; teach a man to fish and you feed him for a lifetime'</b>.<br /> Vizier's give the fish because it efficently solves the immedite problem and reinforces the man's dependance upon the Vizier (or at least his web of influence).<br /> Savant's teach the man to fish...and asks said man 'why didn't the other [Vizier/Dragon] teach him?'<br /> <br /> And so the seeds of the revolt are sown.<br /> <br /> Sorry, delved a little deep to get accurate influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T12:59:30-07:00","id":211574,"title":"","content":"I haven't read everything in the new book, but here are my thoughts on some of what I've seen so far.<br /> <br /> I don't really like the Caitiffs. At least not the name (surely we can do better than stealing from VtM?) and their being considered a Philosophy of their own. They seem a lot more like the absence of a Philosophy. Also, the connection to Huang Long being through honesty and humility makes Caitiffs seem &quot;better&quot; than the other Philosophies--like they're the only ones who have the right idea, while the other Philosophies are hobbled by delusions of grandeur and a need to hang on to at least <i>some</i> of their old glory. Given that the whole game centers around dragons as metaphors for rulership, elevating the ones who run away from the power and responsibility of being Oroboros--who made the decision to become Oroboroi, but couldn't cope with the consequences of that choice--seems rather...incongruous. Even more so to associate those dragons who run away from what they are, who try to be human even as their methods of sustaining themselves is the most animalistic and monstrous of all, with &quot;honesty&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I kind of slipped into &quot;in-character&quot; voice there--while I don't like the Caitiff as presented, I don't actually have the contempt for them that the last couple of sentences might imply. They're a valid character option, but I don't think they should be a Philosophy unto themselves.)<br /> <br /> Perhaps it would be better for Huang Long to be associated with something else--or perhaps no Philosophy at all, as the Yellow Dragon was often considered to be &quot;above&quot; the other directional beasts in some way in Chinese folklore. This being the case, if a Philosophy ends up being created for him/her/it, it probably shouldn't relate to &quot;honesty&quot; or &quot;humility&quot;--if anything, arrogance would probably be a characteristic flaw. &quot;Stability&quot; would be more appropriate, as well as more resonant with the original myths.<br /> <br /> I also am somewhat leery of Savants being associated with anarchy--my original conception of them owed much to the Confucian ideal of the scholarly <i>junzi</i>, or &quot;gentleman&quot; (an &quot;ideal man&quot;, probably of high rank, whose understanding of propriety and correctness not only in people but in the workings of society and the world gives rise to a peaceful and orderly society) and Plato's concept of the philosopher-king.<br /> <br /> Honestly, chaos and anarchy strike me as something that the enemies of the Oroboroi would be more likely to endorse than the Oroboroi themselves. Even a the leader of a rebellion doesn't want rebellion in his own ranks. One must remember, also, that the end goal of a rebellion is the replacement of a corrupt order (or at least, one with which the rebels disagree) with a better (less disagreeable, from the rebels' perspective) order. (Generally, one that has the rebels on top.) It's not an endorsement of disorder, or a condemnation of the rule of law.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Four (or Five) Beasts are not actual in opposition to one another, in terms of North-South/East-West or any other arrangement. They represent the cycle of seasons the five elements, the general climate and terrain in those directions in ancient China, and the astrological influences of their respective regions of the sky, all of which were complimentary rather than oppositional. (This is a thing in Chinese philosophy in general--opposites are seen as complimentary parts of the same thing, rather than two separate and intrinsically opposed things. Dualism is more characteristic of Western philosophy.)<br /> <br /> All this in mind, the dualistic opposition comes across as kind of forced, at least to me.<br /> <br /> Dragons also need a major antagonistic force. Something that shakes things up, shocks them out of their routines, forces them out of their comfort zone, makes them do interesting, story-worthy things that break out of the mold of &quot;survive, maintain Province&quot;. All the Chronicle books are based on this logic: the Strix are a threat that completely upends the vampiric playing field, the Idigam are an Outside Context Problem that none of the tribes of the Uratha are equipped for, Mysteries (otherwise known as Really Weird Shit) just will <i>not</i> leave Mages alone, nor they Mysteries, the angels and Infrastructure of the God-Machine are literally everywhere...so what do Dragons have? Neither the Einherjar nor the Knights of the Bloody Chalice are a good fit for this, IMHO: they're both just variations on the premise of Hunter, and a principally human antagonist just doesn't come across as the massive threat that the Strix, the Idigam, and the God-Machine are to vampires, werewolves, and demons and mortals respectively. Without something like that, the game just isn't as compelling.<br /> <br /> We need an antagonist that's tied into the mythology of the Oroboroi, but that isn't <i>of</i> the Oroboroi. Something so powerful and inimical to dragonkind that mortal enemies will call a truce and work together to survive it. Something that has ties to dragons, has an interest in them, has a history with them...something that makes them feel what an ordinary human feels when faced with a dragon in True Form. Frantic. Desperate to survive. Fragile. A feeling of &quot;no this can't be happening they're not supposed to be real they're just stories <i>oh god I don't want to die!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> That kind of antagonist.<br /> <br /> Without that sort of looming threat, Dragon is much less compelling as a game unto itself, as opposed to something you read for the ideas, raid for mechanics, and crossover with other games. YMMV, of course; this is just how I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T13:42:21-07:00","id":211612,"title":"","content":"I agree with the heart of what you wrote Frogs. Certain aspects of the project feel like non-sequiturs to me.<br /> <br /> Associating Savants with chaos was a big one for me. So I volunteered so I could find a way to make it work.. I've made it work by going in a different direction. They are more Daoists (Taoists?) than Anarchs in my write up, which works with both intention of opposition and the inspirational material.<br /> <br /> As for a driving antagonist? I completly agree. Even better, we have the starting point for that story. The Collapse is still there. There should be stories about it, how the Oroboroi lost the Mandate of Heaven. How they were driven from their kingdoms, their homes, away from their very Hearts...<br /> <br /> Thing is, I haven't got a suitably awesome idea yet. Mind you I have flirted with theide of the True Hearts being a villain splat. But that is more VII than Strix. I'd keep the 5 Devils though, as a Belial's Brood/Pure group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:11:35-07:00","id":211649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211574#post211574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read everything in the new book, but here are my thoughts on some of what I've seen so far.<br /> <br /> I don't really like the Caitiffs. At least not the name (surely we can do better than stealing from VtM?) and their being considered a Philosophy of their own. They seem a lot more like the absence of a Philosophy. Also, the connection to Huang Long being through honesty and humility makes Caitiffs seem &quot;better&quot; than the other Philosophies--like they're the only ones who have the right idea, while the other Philosophies are hobbled by delusions of grandeur and a need to hang on to at least <i>some</i> of their old glory. Given that the whole game centers around dragons as metaphors for rulership, elevating the ones who run away from the power and responsibility of being Oroboros--who made the decision to become Oroboroi, but couldn't cope with the consequences of that choice--seems rather...incongruous. Even more so to associate those dragons who run away from what they are, who try to be human even as their methods of sustaining themselves is the most animalistic and monstrous of all, with &quot;honesty&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I wasn't taking it from VtM, I was using it by its definition: <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">a contemptible or cowardly person. I also made the definition a little less severe in the &quot;Christmas in July&quot; PDF than it was in the thread... I'm not sure which version you're referencing.<br /> <br /> The quick definitions are flexible; I was just trying to give a seed that someone else could elaborate on. If you want to develop an alternate Philosophy for Huang Long (or an explanation for why she has no Philosophy), I would be happy to use it.<br /> <br /> Also remember: even the absence of a philosophy is a philosophy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211574#post211574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also am somewhat leery of Savants being associated with anarchy--my original conception of them owed much to the Confucian ideal of the scholarly <i>junzi</i>, or &quot;gentleman&quot; (an &quot;ideal man&quot;, probably of high rank, whose understanding of propriety and correctness not only in people but in the workings of society and the world gives rise to a peaceful and orderly society) and Plato's concept of the philosopher-king.</div> </div> </div> </div> This phrase brings to mind how Qin Shi Huangdi buried Confucian scholars alive because they were a threat to his power. The Savants are affiliated with Anarchy because an educated populace is dangerous; this does not mean that a populace educated by a dragon is a threat of anarchy against her. Propaganda is a powerful social control; that's what I meant. Controlled anarchy, like a controlled explosion, can be as effective in mining power as dynamite is in mining mineral resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211574#post211574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, chaos and anarchy strike me as something that the enemies of the Oroboroi would be more likely to endorse than the Oroboroi themselves. Even a the leader of a rebellion doesn't want rebellion in his own ranks. One must remember, also, that the end goal of a rebellion is the replacement of a corrupt order (or at least, one with which the rebels disagree) with a better (less disagreeable, from the rebels' perspective) order. (Generally, one that has the rebels on top.) It's not an endorsement of disorder, or a condemnation of the rule of law.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is an unfortunate stigma on Chaos; Chaos can be as beneficial as Law when considered as a force of creation. For example, the positioning of &quot;Goldylocks&quot; planet orientation is effectively an exercise in Chaos: minute variable alterations result in circumstances through which wonderful things--including life--become possible. Chaos breaks the harsh, cold calculation of physics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211574#post211574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, the Four (or Five) Beasts are not actual in opposition to one another, in terms of North-South/East-West or any other arrangement. They represent the cycle of seasons the five elements, the general climate and terrain in those directions in ancient China, and the astrological influences of their respective regions of the sky, all of which were complimentary rather than oppositional. (This is a thing in Chinese philosophy in general--opposites are seen as complimentary parts of the same thing, rather than two separate and intrinsically opposed things. Dualism is more characteristic of Western philosophy.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't actually depict the four directional dragons as being in opposition of each other. They each simply drew a different conclusion from the Spark due to their perspective at the time of its occurrence. Just as you might draw two different ideas from the same tree observed in Winter and Summer, these dragons each observed a beautiful event of creation under different conditions.<br /> If your comment about opposition is in relation to the Stereotypes listed at the end of the available philosophies, I provide these explanations:<br /> -Stereotypes of other Y-Splats are universally negative in World of Darkness books.<br /> -Considering the game is set in San Francisco, the characters are bound to apply a United States American interpretation to the ideas they encounter. Thus becoming aware of these five dragons that were present at the big bang, they would likely come to the conclusion that these creatures were opposed as such is the closest to their human perception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211574#post211574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All this in mind, the dualistic opposition comes across as kind of forced, at least to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elaborate, please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211574#post211574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragons also need a major antagonistic force. Something that shakes things up, shocks them out of their routines, forces them out of their comfort zone, makes them do interesting, story-worthy things that break out of the mold of &quot;survive, maintain Province&quot;. All the Chronicle books are based on this logic: the Strix are a threat that completely upends the vampiric playing field, the Idigam are an Outside Context Problem that none of the tribes of the Uratha are equipped for, Mysteries (otherwise known as Really Weird Shit) just will <i>not</i> leave Mages alone, nor they Mysteries, the angels and Infrastructure of the God-Machine are literally everywhere...so what do Dragons have? Neither the Einherjar nor the Knights of the Bloody Chalice are a good fit for this, IMHO: they're both just variations on the premise of Hunter, and a principally human antagonist just doesn't come across as the massive threat that the Strix, the Idigam, and the God-Machine are to vampires, werewolves, and demons and mortals respectively. Without something like that, the game just isn't as compelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't gotten to the thick of the Einherjar yet, which will be presented in the Storyteller Chapter (Chapter 4, not in the &quot;Christmas In July&quot; PDF). They can't be killed. Yeah, you can kill their body, but the soul just goes back to the Treasury until it can infest something else. ...But I suppose you're right.<br /> <br /> Jormungandr is the threat that the Oroboroi know is coming, so what is an appropriate threat that is out of their depth? I hesitate to say a Phoenix (Technically the Phoenix is the female of the dragon's species according to Chinese mythology: an entity that is 66% Yin to contrast the dragon's 66% Yang) since that's once more applying western duality to an eastern concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211574#post211574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need an antagonist that's tied into the mythology of the Oroboroi, but that isn't <i>of</i> the Oroboroi. Something so powerful and inimical to dragonkind that mortal enemies will call a truce and work together to survive it. Something that has ties to dragons, has an interest in them, has a history with them...something that makes them feel what an ordinary human feels when faced with a dragon in True Form. Frantic. Desperate to survive. Fragile. A feeling of &quot;no this can't be happening they're not supposed to be real they're just stories <i>oh god I don't want to die!</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the problem. In classical mythology, the only threats to dragons were great heroes. Any great hero I would attempt to fabricate as an antagonist would fall under your complaint about Hunter in different clothes. In fact, that's what I was going for with the Einherjar; they're heroes that failed against the dragon and keep coming back to try and kill its descendants (those who received the Heart after). The only other threat I can come up with that generates that sort of dread is the dark bargainers, but they are not inherently hostile as written and I don't wish to change them.<br /> The creation story involves the light of life filling the universe. What is a proper contrast? The darkness of death. I think Einherjar are the best bet at creating this sort of fear, especially if we establish that they are being driven by some sort of exodimensional force. Perhaps if they were cast in a different light (I get the feeling much of your contempt for the new material comes from the Stereotypes section of the Philosophies, which I admittedly wrote quickly because I realized they had gone overlooked).<br /> <br /> I eagerly await your exploration of each of these matters in further detail.<br /> <br /> <br /> FallenEco, I like your notes on the differences between Savants and Viziers; I will keep these in mind if I have to write any of the Philosophies (but hopefully it will not come to that!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:50:07-07:00","id":211758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211612#post211612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Associating Savants with chaos was a big one for me. So I volunteered so I could find a way to make it work.. I've made it work by going in a different direction. They are more Daoists (Taoists?) than Anarchs in my write up, which works with both intention of opposition and the inspirational material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much approve; some other archetypes informing my initial ideas for the Sages/Savants was that of the Old Master as well as that of the cryptic yet insightful stranger who gently nudges you towards enlightenment, both of which dovetail very nicely with Taoist ideas. I look forward to seeing what you come up with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211612#post211612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, I haven't got a suitably awesome idea yet. Mind you I have flirted with theide of the True Hearts being a villain splat. But that is more VII than Strix. I'd keep the 5 Devils though, as a Belial's Brood/Pure group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the original Philosophies work very well as Pure/Belial's Brood/Scelesti style antagonists. It's something I suggested in the thread on the old forums:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Another way to integrate the current Embers Philosophies into the rewrite would be to make them an antagonist faction, centering around different forms of tyranny and oppression: Oroboroi who refuse to learn from the Collapse and want to indulge in being dread god-monsters to the mortal cattle. (As opposed to the protagonist Philosophies, which apply lessons learned in the Collapse toward a mutually beneficial relationship with their subjects; even the Imperators are interested in authoritarian rule as a means to make a nation great rather than to parasitically leech off of the populace and luxuriate in their own power.<br /> <br /> Ideas on how this would work with each Philosophy:<br /> <br /> Ash: &quot;Obey me, or be destroyed. Don't think I mean it? Neither did this guy, and now he's going to be an example.&quot;<br /> <br /> Blood: Control their subjects with tangled webs of conflicting loyalties and obligations, playing them off of one another and preventing them from rising up.<br /> <br /> Bone: Aggressively maintain the status quo, on the one hand maintaining everything in reasonable condition (&quot;the trains run on time&quot;) but on the other crushing innovation and change.<br /> <br /> Sweat: Ruthless taskmasters who relentlessly drive their subjects to create monuments to their glory and takes away what few luxuries they are permitted in the form of tribute and taxes.<br /> <br /> Tears: Sadists on a power trip who love seeing their subjects squirm. Pointlessly abuse power specifically to cause suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some other things that I think need to change:<br /> <br /> * The jade weakness. Oroboroi aren't werewolves; it doesn't fit any of the mythic or folkloric associations for them to have a particular substance they are vulnerable to. <i>Particularly </i>not jade, which was thought by the ancient Chinese to be a pure/noble/divine substance, in much the same way that dragons were themselves thought to be pure, noble, and divine beings. It's not mandatory for a WoD splat to have a substance that is especially harmful to them; it's only used if it fits the folklore from which the splat is drawn.<br /> <br /> * The pseudo-scientific and pseudo-historical explanations for splat traits and powers. Much like midichlorians, they're answers to questions no one asked, and they actually hurt suspension of disbelief. Don't explain how the Heart works as a blood-pumping organ. Don't go into involved explanations of the physical space taken up by the Heart and Furnace. Don't explain where every bit of terminology came from in-universe. This is a game about <i>fire-breathing dragons</i>, for Pete's sake. I guarantee you that if you leave these things unexplained, <i>no one will notice or care</i>. And the explanations you've used clash horribly with all the talk of divine right, tyrannical god-monsters, and the soul of the world.<br /> <br /> * Relatedly, the organ removal in exchange for higher Furnace. Firstly, see above re: pseudoscience. Second, there's no basis for it in myths and stories about dragons. Third, it presents a serious obstacle to role-playing and encourages roll-playing (players should not have to expend mechanical resources to have their characters <i>express emotion</i>.) Fourth, it excessively penalizes Furnace increase; the Heartbeat is more than sufficient on its own.<br /> <br /> * Typhoon. Myths and stories of dragons credit them with influence over the weather, but this is generally portrayed as being something entirely under their control. This is clearly a matter of Ablutions and Edicts, not uncontrollable side effects of high Furnace.<br /> <br /> * Mandate is not nearly as divorced from human morality as advertised. The higher ranges should have more to do with being unquestionably In Charge and having a well-maintained province than being benevolent or beloved by the people; the lower ranges should be more about abandoning a ruler's dignity, authority, and self-respect than about being a petty dictator. Petty dictators can be competent rulers (witness Machiavelli's <i>The Prince</i>), and someone can be loved by the people and still be running the country into the ground.<br /> <br /> * Philosophies are an X-splat kind of power, not a Y-splat kind of power.<br /> <br /> * Sparti. First, the correct word is Spartoi. Second, it's probably too powerful: creating supernaturally skilled humans out of thin air on demand? Really? Third, it comes across as vaguely cartoonish. I'd suggest something like turning &quot;the fertile soil&quot; into a metaphor for &quot;a pregnant woman&quot;, thereby forcing dragons to wait for their Spartoi to grow to adulthood. Or maybe a metaphor for &quot;a human with great potential&quot;, thus making it into the equivalent of Ghouls, Stigmatics, or Sadikh, and setting hard limits on how many Spartoi a dragon can create.<br /> <br /> * Grafts. They're not especially thematic; they seem more like leftovers from the earlier versions of the game than anything else.<br /> <br /> * The general portrayal as the Oroboroi as <i>instrinsically</i> and <i>unavoidably</i> doomed to extinction. Give players reason to hope for their characters' future! Let there be a promise of Ascension or Apotheosis: a semi-mythical ascent to the condition of the True Dragons of old, shrouded in mystery, rumor, and outright misinformation but promising salvation for those who can attain it.<br /> <br /> * Deep Ones. They don't fit in a game about dragons, either in style and tone or in function. They need to go.<br /> <br /> * Less defined backstory. The New World of Darkness doesn't have a history <i>per se</i>. It has stories and rumors and urban legends. The origins of supernatural entities are vague and uncertain, never spelled out in detail in the books, so that each individual chronicle can come up with their own origins. There is no Caine for the vampires, no Antediluvians, no Enoch. Or if there is, it's just one of many, many stories they tell of where they came from, and who can say whether it's the truth? Atlantis is an allegory for <i>the world used to be different before the Fall</i>, not a history of a literal island-nation of mages that existed way back when. The Uratha begin every story they tell with &quot;This story is true.&quot;, after the fashion of many orally-transmitted cultures. That doesn't mean that the stories are literal histories of events that happened, but rather that they articulate the truths the Uratha live by through metaphor and symbolism. The Oroboroi should be no different. They know that once upon a time, dragons ruled the world; they know that now, they must hide from mankind. They have an inkling that their power was stolen from greater beings even as they themselves stole their power from their Antecedents. They feel the Mandate of Heaven deep in their bones. They gather scraps of memory, dream, and nightmare from the Treasury, yet who can say what of that is true or false, and what of the true is history and what is allegory? Scatter stories of their origins throughout the book, but feel free to let the details contradict one another: only the broad strokes of it are consistent. The rest is for the players and Storyteller to decide at the gaming table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:17:50-07:00","id":211882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some other things that I think need to change:<br /> <br /> * The jade weakness. Oroboroi aren't werewolves; it doesn't fit any of the mythic or folkloric associations for them to have a particular substance they are vulnerable to. <i>Particularly </i>not jade, which was thought by the ancient Chinese to be a pure/noble/divine substance, in much the same way that dragons were themselves thought to be pure, noble, and divine beings. It's not mandatory for a WoD splat to have a substance that is especially harmful to them; it's only used if it fits the folklore from which the splat is drawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, dragons (lowercase d) are pure/noble/divine entities. The jerks that killed them and ate their hearts are not. That is why Jade is so harmful to the Oroboroi and even inhibits their ability to portray divine traits.<br /> Additionally, a supernatural allergen assists in the reduction of the Marty Stu complex.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The pseudo-scientific and pseudo-historical explanations for splat traits and powers. Much like midichlorians, they're answers to questions no one asked, and they actually hurt suspension of disbelief. Don't explain how the Heart works as a blood-pumping organ. Don't go into involved explanations of the physical space taken up by the Heart and Furnace. Don't explain where every bit of terminology came from in-universe. This is a game about <i>fire-breathing dragons</i>, for Pete's sake. I guarantee you that if you leave these things unexplained, <i>no one will notice or care</i>. And the explanations you've used clash horribly with all the talk of divine right, tyrannical god-monsters, and the soul of the world</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly you don't care to read these things. So skim. The information is there if it is wanted. Some people happen to enjoy scientific explanations in literature, and some people enjoy fluff in general. Aren't these contradicting origins myths like you called for below? Also, it's not pseudoscience, it's theoretical biology. If a creature were to develop an organ, how and why would that organ change in the way it does? I do extensive research on everything I write and this is no exception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Relatedly, the organ removal in exchange for higher Furnace. Firstly, see above re: pseudoscience. Second, there's no basis for it in myths and stories about dragons. Third, it presents a serious obstacle to role-playing and encourages roll-playing (players should not have to expend mechanical resources to have their characters <i>express emotion</i>.) Fourth, it excessively penalizes Furnace increase; the Heartbeat is more than sufficient on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly you didn't understand the goal of this particular system; the expenditure is only required when characters do not carry the organs on their person. These furnace mechanics are present to increase the body horror of the game and help distance people from the opinion that this is D&amp;D World of Darkness, which it is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Typhoon. Myths and stories of dragons credit them with influence over the weather, but this is generally portrayed as being something entirely under their control. This is clearly a matter of Ablutions and Edicts, not uncontrollable side effects of high Furnace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragons control the weather, but Oroboroi do not. Your complaint about this contradicts later complaints that I did NOT deviate from myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Mandate is not nearly as divorced from human morality as advertised. The higher ranges should have more to do with being unquestionably In Charge and having a well-maintained province than being benevolent or beloved by the people; the lower ranges should be more about abandoning a ruler's dignity, authority, and self-respect than about being a petty dictator. Petty dictators can be competent rulers (witness Machiavelli's <i>The Prince</i>), and someone can be loved by the people and still be running the country into the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div> I literally only changed the words of the Mandate levels from 'Ethics' to 'Mandate'. As I said, I was in a hurry to make &quot;Christmas in July&quot; and things got overlooked. The real changes to mandate are the mechanics of Betrayals in lieu of Sins, which each bear equal footing and repeated triggering for both GMC and non-GMC games. My descriptions of what each stage of Mandate is 'like' are nothing more than fluff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Philosophies are an X-splat kind of power, not a Y-splat kind of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're wrong. X-Splats refer to a dragon's physical nature, while Y-Splats define how she rationalizes the world around her. I don't care if Edicts break the mold of what a faction should grant to a character; <b>DtE</b> is <b>different</b>. Proclamations are a dragon literally enforcing her will on the fabric of reality; they have nothing to do with how she acquired her Heart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Sparti. First, the correct word is Spartoi. Second, it's probably too powerful: creating supernaturally skilled humans out of thin air on demand? Really? Third, it comes across as vaguely cartoonish. I'd suggest something like turning &quot;the fertile soil&quot; into a metaphor for &quot;a pregnant woman&quot;, thereby forcing dragons to wait for their Spartoi to grow to adulthood. Or maybe a metaphor for &quot;a human with great potential&quot;, thus making it into the equivalent of Ghouls, Stigmatics, or Sadikh, and setting hard limits on how many Spartoi a dragon can create.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I studied classical mythology, it was spelled Sparti. The relation in etymology to Sparta was used by the Greeks to imply the origins of those peoples, as all life in Greek myths originated from some form of autochthonous source. I represented the Sparti/Spartoi to the letter of the myth (which you scolded me for straying on with Typhoon), but the fact is there ARE limitations. Making a Sparti costs an Oroboros Willpower dots (just like ghouling), how is it any different? Also, how many teeth do your dragons have?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Deep Ones. They don't fit in a game about dragons, either in style and tone or in function. They need to go.</div> </div> </div> </div> Gee, doesn't that make them the unknowable enemy you were so adamant about adding to the template? You may not see the connection, but the Deep Ones represent forgotten gods (I even went so far as to state this directly in the &quot;Dragon and the Deep One&quot; Myth. Since the dragons in this game are gods as well, the deep ones stand as a lingering question about what being forgotten really means. Did they always look the way they do? Why do they have to make bargains? Are the Oroboroi going to end up the same way? They are entirely appropriate, both in style and tone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Less defined backstory. The New World of Darkness doesn't have a history <i>per se</i>. It has stories and rumors and urban legends. The origins of supernatural entities are vague and uncertain, never spelled out in detail in the books, so that each individual chronicle can come up with their own origins. There is no Caine for the vampires, no Antediluvians, no Enoch. Or if there is, it's just one of many, many stories they tell of where they came from, and who can say whether it's the truth? Atlantis is an allegory for <i>the world used to be different before the Fall</i>, not a history of a literal island-nation of mages that existed way back when. The Uratha begin every story they tell with &quot;This story is true.&quot;, after the fashion of many orally-transmitted cultures. That doesn't mean that the stories are literal histories of events that happened, but rather that they articulate the truths the Uratha live by through metaphor and symbolism. The Oroboroi should be no different. They know that once upon a time, dragons ruled the world; they know that now, they must hide from mankind. They have an inkling that their power was stolen from greater beings even as they themselves stole their power from their Antecedents. They feel the Mandate of Heaven deep in their bones. They gather scraps of memory, dream, and nightmare from the Treasury, yet who can say what of that is true or false, and what of the true is history and what is allegory? Scatter stories of their origins throughout the book, but feel free to let the details contradict one another: only the broad strokes of it are consistent. The rest is for the players and Storyteller to decide at the gaming table.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you griping about here? The creation myth? It's a mythical interpretation of the big bang, it's not a concrete definition of reality. Are you talking about the Dragon and the Deep One? That's a myth about why the Oroboroi remove their Hearts, there's not evidence whether it's true or not. As for the collapse, it is heavily implied that there were MULTIPLE collapses; in fact each generation of Oroboroi is a collapse of the previous generation. It's a metaphor for a political coup.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tell you what: if you want to change something in the book, write a paragraph <b>as it would appear in the manual</b> and I'll consider it. I put out the &quot;Christmas in July&quot; update to give people material to chew on while I work on my other projects (many of which are more important than this) and I don't have time to keep rewriting the book each time it doesn't fit someone's tastes. There are players that like the Deep Ones. There were players that liked the old Philosophies. There were players that liked the Dreamtide. I have to pick and choose who to disappoint and who to please, and each time I do so I have to start over from the beginning of the book and make sure everything self-references correctly, both in layout and in force of intent. So fine, if you want to change the content, then you WRITE the content you want changed and I'll change it.<br /> <br /> And I'll repeat it, just so I'm clear: I don't mean write a backseat discussion about what should be changed. Write the change, in paragraphs, in the form it will appear in the PDF. If I like what you wrote, I'll copy and paste it into the document. If I don't, well, then you'll know what it's like to have your efforts thrown away repeatedly.<br /> <br /> I'm tired of getting paragraphs and paragraphs referencing manuals I don't own and telling me to rewrite the whole book 'like they did'. If you feel this way, I invite you to take what you like from <b>Dragon the Embers</b>, throw out what you don't like, and start a splinter template. Alternatively, you can wait until I've finished the manual and then you can write a supplement that fixes all the problems you perceive (Call it an errata, call it the Innsmouth Chronicles, call it whatever you like).<br /> <br /> Let this be perfectly clear: I want to have a finished form of Dragon the Embers. I am NOT rewriting the book again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T19:41:51-07:00","id":211955,"title":"","content":"Suffice it to be be said that I'm in the course of reading the PDF myself and will be posting my findings when my schedule no longer has me more swamped than the Florida Everglades, but this bears response: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211882#post211882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly you don't care to read these things. So skim.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is my vehement and exasperated duty to inform you that this is neither how &quot;don't like, don't read&quot; works nor <i>ever</i> a legitimate response to criticism, especially not a criticism <i>that I raised myself about the last draft of the book.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'll repeat it, just so I'm clear: I don't mean write a backseat discussion about what should be changed. Write the change, in paragraphs, in the form it will appear in the PDF. If I like what you wrote, I'll copy and paste it into the document. If I don't, well, then you'll know what it's like to have your efforts thrown away repeatedly.<br /> <br /> I'm tired of getting paragraphs and paragraphs referencing manuals I don't own and telling me to rewrite the whole book 'like they did'. If you feel this way, I invite you to take what you like from <b>Dragon the Embers</b>, throw out what you don't like, and start a splinter template. Alternatively, you can wait until I've finished the manual and then you can write a supplement that fixes all the problems you perceive (Call it an errata, call it the Innsmouth Chronicles, call it whatever you like).<br /> <br /> Let this be perfectly clear: I want to have a finished form of Dragon the Embers. I am NOT rewriting the book again. </div> </div> </div>CJC, if I wanted to read &quot;bet you couldn't do better!&quot; as a response to criticism I would still be hanging around fanfiction boards.<br /> <br /> I don't.<br /> <br /> If you have a problem with criticism and iteration then you're welcome to hand the project off to somebody else until you feel up to the task of refining your work in response to perceived issues with it, but if you could go without replicating the more memorably petulant lines of people at least a decade your junior that would be absolutely fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-28-2014, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T20:26:27-07:00","id":211997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211955#post211955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CJC, if I wanted to read &quot;bet you couldn't do better!&quot; as a response to criticism I would still be hanging around fanfiction boards.<br /> <br /> I don't.<br /> <br /> If you have a problem with criticism and iteration then you're welcome to hand the project off to somebody else until you feel up to the task of refining your work in response to perceived issues with it, but if you could go without replicating the more memorably petulant lines of people at least a decade your junior that would be absolutely fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say &quot;Bet you can't do better&quot;, I said &quot;Rewrite it, don't tell me to rewrite it&quot;. I am absolutely handing over the reins, because I'm tired of working on a project I am no longer invested in. I am telling people to fix it, rather than tell me how to fix it, because five years down the line shows that clearly <b>I</b> can't fix it.<br /> <br /> So yes, I'm handing over the reins. Give me what you want in the book, and I'll assemble the book. Or cut me out of the picture completely. Or let me finish the flawed book and then fix it with an errata. That is the gist of what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T20:33:08-07:00","id":212002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211997#post211997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the gist of what I said.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the gist of what you said is &quot;I'm tired of participating in discussions in which my work is criticized, make your own version of the game if you don't like what I've done.&quot; Which is essentially &quot;Bet you couldn't do better,&quot; especially when you make an entire paragraph going on about what other people are doing and particularly when this comes on the heels of a multi-block response to criticism of your handiwork.<br /> <br /> The appropriate means of handing over the reins is to say &quot;I'm starting to have trouble staying invested in/finding time for the project and thus would like to hand the reins off to somebody with more time/greater enthusiasm for it. Would anybody like to take over?&quot; This is basic I-statement-You-statement tone stuff.<br /> <br /> Being that I'm still very much a peripheral element, that would seem to leave Shock, Frogs, and Vree as the main candidates for new dev(?), along with whoever else wants the position. Anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-28-2014, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T22:01:59-07:00","id":212072,"title":"","content":"Truth be told, CJC has been the one to shoulder the majority of the load of the burden on this project so it's about time to give him a bit of a rest while he works on other things in the meantime.<br /> <br /> I'll see what I can come up with in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T23:01:45-07:00","id":212154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * The jade weakness. Oroboroi aren't werewolves; it doesn't fit any of the mythic or folkloric associations for them to have a particular substance they are vulnerable to. <i>Particularly </i>not jade, which was thought by the ancient Chinese to be a pure/noble/divine substance, in much the same way that dragons were themselves thought to be pure, noble, and divine beings. It's not mandatory for a WoD splat to have a substance that is especially harmful to them; it's only used if it fits the folklore from which the splat is drawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall the justification for the Jade weakness due to the fact that a Oroboroi walking around in True Form is a pain to kill and as a result, something needs to put fear in their eyes when they see their enemies use it. Jade was selected due it's connection to the Orient in which most of the game is based off of. If we wish to scrap that, we could go with obsidian as a flavor material and justify the fluff better. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The pseudo-scientific and pseudo-historical explanations for splat traits and powers. Much like midichlorians, they're answers to questions no one asked, and they actually hurt suspension of disbelief. Don't explain how the Heart works as a blood-pumping organ. Don't go into involved explanations of the physical space taken up by the Heart and Furnace. Don't explain where every bit of terminology came from in-universe. This is a game about <i>fire-breathing dragons</i>, for Pete's sake. I guarantee you that if you leave these things unexplained, <i>no one will notice or care</i>. And the explanations you've used clash horribly with all the talk of divine right, tyrannical god-monsters, and the soul of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That much detail about the Heart is necessary given it is the object that the Oroboroi base their existence around. However, I would save it for a Storyteller's section or an appendix at the end of the book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Relatedly, the organ removal in exchange for higher Furnace. Firstly, see above re: pseudoscience. Second, there's no basis for it in myths and stories about dragons. Third, it presents a serious obstacle to role-playing and encourages roll-playing (players should not have to expend mechanical resources to have their characters <i>express emotion</i>.) Fourth, it excessively penalizes Furnace increase; the Heartbeat is more than sufficient on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed Heartbeat should be good enough. This oddly seems more akin to Mummy than Dragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Typhoon. Myths and stories of dragons credit them with influence over the weather, but this is generally portrayed as being something entirely under their control. This is clearly a matter of Ablutions and Edicts, not uncontrollable side effects of high Furnace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. I kinda see Typhoons as anger impulses. Same way a powerful man may effect an entire house by simply being angry, a Dragon affects the world around him. Either way, This could stick around or it can be knocked off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Mandate is not nearly as divorced from human morality as advertised. The higher ranges should have more to do with being unquestionably In Charge and having a well-maintained province than being benevolent or beloved by the people; the lower ranges should be more about abandoning a ruler's dignity, authority, and self-respect than about being a petty dictator. Petty dictators can be competent rulers (witness Machiavelli's <i>The Prince</i>), and someone can be loved by the people and still be running the country into the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any ideas on what each level should focus on?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Philosophies are an X-splat kind of power, not a Y-splat kind of power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Sparti. First, the correct word is Spartoi. Second, it's probably too powerful: creating supernaturally skilled humans out of thin air on demand? Really? Third, it comes across as vaguely cartoonish. I'd suggest something like turning &quot;the fertile soil&quot; into a metaphor for &quot;a pregnant woman&quot;, thereby forcing dragons to wait for their Spartoi to grow to adulthood. Or maybe a metaphor for &quot;a human with great potential&quot;, thus making it into the equivalent of Ghouls, Stigmatics, or Sadikh, and setting hard limits on how many Spartoi a dragon can create.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So an bloodline. Interesting. Could be be a source where one could convert a Maiden into something more...Perhaps a delayed development that requires months to process. Could leave the powers as is and require the development process to be extended for months at a time, making it a very sized able investment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Grafts. They're not especially thematic; they seem more like leftovers from the earlier versions of the game than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that was my idea. I felt the need to have a bit of body horror in Dragon and the idea of someone burning a body to use their bones for artifacts is pretty gruesome but sounds more Promethean/Vampire. Any ideas on filling the void?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The general portrayal as the Oroboroi as <i>instrinsically</i> and <i>unavoidably</i> doomed to extinction. Give players reason to hope for their characters' future! Let there be a promise of Ascension or Apotheosis: a semi-mythical ascent to the condition of the True Dragons of old, shrouded in mystery, rumor, and outright misinformation but promising salvation for those who can attain it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I thought that was implied. After all, the Horror of Dragon shares the same Horror of Wrath: the Oblivion. Just on a more macro scale. I believe Vree made the suggestions about how some Dragons ascend and reproduce. They travel between realms. A few tales could be about how offspring are left in this one and just what those offspring are capable of. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Deep Ones. They don't fit in a game about dragons, either in style and tone or in function. They need to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deep Ones function much akin to nature realizing that there are two alpha predators and one of them needs to go. One is reproducing at a fast rate while the other simply isn't. The Deep Ones as a whole can kick the bucket but that still leaves the void for an antagonist splat that needs to replace them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=211758#post211758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Less defined backstory. The New World of Darkness doesn't have a history <i>per se</i>. It has stories and rumors and urban legends. The origins of supernatural entities are vague and uncertain, never spelled out in detail in the books, so that each individual chronicle can come up with their own origins. There is no Caine for the vampires, no Antediluvians, no Enoch. Or if there is, it's just one of many, many stories they tell of where they came from, and who can say whether it's the truth? Atlantis is an allegory for <i>the world used to be different before the Fall</i>, not a history of a literal island-nation of mages that existed way back when. The Uratha begin every story they tell with &quot;This story is true.&quot;, after the fashion of many orally-transmitted cultures. That doesn't mean that the stories are literal histories of events that happened, but rather that they articulate the truths the Uratha live by through metaphor and symbolism. The Oroboroi should be no different. They know that once upon a time, dragons ruled the world; they know that now, they must hide from mankind. They have an inkling that their power was stolen from greater beings even as they themselves stole their power from their Antecedents. They feel the Mandate of Heaven deep in their bones. They gather scraps of memory, dream, and nightmare from the Treasury, yet who can say what of that is true or false, and what of the true is history and what is allegory? Scatter stories of their origins throughout the book, but feel free to let the details contradict one another: only the broad strokes of it are consistent. The rest is for the players and Storyteller to decide at the gaming table.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've gone through more than a few rewrites with people telling us &quot;there is no back story at all! focus on the back story!&quot; so now we got one that kinda works for what we have. This isn't saying it's great but ultmatly, it's good for a place holder until more people can throw more creative stuff at the wall and we can start introducing mysteries and counter claims.<br /> <br /> In short, it works for now and it's good enough to base a &quot;Father Wolf/Atlantis&quot; story for now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T23:18:49-07:00","id":212164,"title":"","content":"...I'm sorry I snapped. It was just so nice when Pandalfino posted the new Philosophies, because all I had to do was plug them into the document. When people started suggesting that <i>I</i> take charge of the changes again, I just flipped out. It's just too much work for me, I can't do it anymore.<br /> <br /> I'm especially sorry for being aggressive towards Frogs, I wasn't trying to be nasty but it's hard not to when frustrated.<br /> <br /> It's best that Shock take charge for a while.<br /> <br /> Also... if it's not to much to ask...<br /> When you suggest a change, could you post it in a way that it could be plugged directly into the book? That would make actually assembling the document 647% easier.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you in advance for understanding that sometimes a guy has a bad day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T04:28:45-07:00","id":212334,"title":"","content":"Understood. Just take a few days to recharge your batteries ok?<br /> No need to work yourself up over this CJC. The contributions can and will wait until you are ready for them. And you don't have to be in charge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T00:39:28-07:00","id":213268,"title":"","content":"Where do I have to read for the most up to date version?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind, I found it. Let's see if I be can be of any help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 07-30-2014, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T10:29:43-07:00","id":219254,"title":"","content":"I should apologize, too. It would probably have been better to point out the things I liked about what you had as well as what I thought should change, rather than a relentless litany of &quot;this needs changing/doesn't make sense/doesn't feel right&quot;. For instance, I skimmed the Edicts section and very much liked what I saw. Some of the names could be changed--I think that Polygraphy, for instance, would work much better as Truth--but apart from that it was really cool; it perfectly captures the &quot;feel&quot; of <i>commanding</i> the world to shape itself to your will.<br /> <br /> I think part of the problem was that I was rushing things; I was pointing out what I saw as problems, but not really taking the time to present alternatives<i>, </i>or even the reasons for <i>why</i> I thought they were problems. I'm not sure if what I come up with in the next week or two will be something that can just be copy-pasted into the doc, but I'll try to make sure that it will at least be more useful than a long list of &quot;needs changed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T22:26:56-07:00","id":222828,"title":"","content":"Okay... I've been thinking about this for a while, and it seems like the Oroboroi's mechanics are okay: they're GMC compatible now, the Edict laws play off of each other relatively well, tells have been reduced in complication to make them more fun and interesting to use, Breath has been adapted to be both unique and a driving force at emphasizing core concepts of the game, and Mandate has had its sins simplified and made GMC compatible (Granted the fluff around mandate is bad, but at the moment all of the fluff is bad, I'm just talking mechanics here).<br /> <br /> This means we can (and should) focus our energies on the thematic components of the game. As it stands, we need:<ul><li>2.5 more Philosophies, depending on how we settle the Caitiff dilemma</li> <li>An enrichment of Antagonists, including a superstitious threat antagonist</li> <li>A firm decision on which B-Splats to keep, which to discard, and how to make them work mechanically</li> <li>A decision on whether or not to bother with the Treasury/realm invisible for dragons, and a precise definition of what said realm should include and more importantly what it should not include</li> <li>More myths about dragons, including conflicting mythology</li> </ul>The problem is, that's a tough list, and when we try to do the whole list at once things get lost, people get frustrated, and the project grinds to a halt. So we're going to set most of the list aside and focus on one thing at a time (writing philosophies excluded because we've been having good fortune with that thus far).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So the first thing I want to focus on is the Antagonists, since they will have an impact on the way the entire manual is written.<br /> <br /> Here are the antagonists we've developed for Dragon so far, in no particular order, followed with a brief description of each. Some of them have already been shot down, but I thought I'd mention them again in case they serve as inspiration for something else.<br /> <br /> <b>Chimerae/Chimeras:</b> Animals that eat an Oroboros Heart and turn into monsters. To be honest, I completely forgot about these guys, which is why they didn't get mentioned in the CIJ half-book. There's a lot of confusion about how these things would work; would they be mindless man-eating maws? Or sinister manipulators like their Oroboroi cousins. Animal instinct coupled with human intelligence is a very scary prospect, and the game practically encourages the creation of Chimerae with the Husbandry Edict. Still, I don't think they're the terrifying threat that would drive enemies to join forces.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of the Bloody Chalice:</b> The knights were really nothing more than blood-bathing immortals, with the exception that they actively bled through their skin in the presence of supernatural beings. Their purpose was to discourage overuse of Ablutions by presenting the hunter threat, but they became increasingly unnecessary as the project progressed. At the moment, they are not in the document and not slated for reintroduction.<br /> <br /> <b>Volcano Philosophies:</b> Frogs proposed using the original five philosophies as an antagonistic force, and it isn't a bad idea. As written most are single-minded and more than a bit malicious; they'd work well as a Pure-style antagonist if developed properly, but I'd need help to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Einherjar:</b> The Einherjar are sort of like the knights, only less organised and more persistent. They are freebound souls that possess injured parties and imbue them with superhuman strength, but also initiate their natural rigor and decay. In short, they're revenants. What makes them scary is that they are persistent; kill an Einherjar in a host body and it'll just possess somebody else to attack again. I think these guys have the potential to be the terrifying threat, but they'd need work to do so. They do fit the &quot;hero determined unto death&quot; niche, which would be naturally frightening to dragons as heroes are generally the only ones that slay dragons in mythology.<br /> <br /> <b>Deep Ones:</b> The Deep Ones, or dark bargainers, are essentially a grim prophecy of what will become of the Oroboroi once all of their reverence has turned to rot; they are the fate of fallen gods, clinging to existence by clinging to the warmth of other beings (by trading favors for organs). Deep Ones might have the ability to be an absolutely terrifying antagonist, the type of which Frogs was seeking, but at the moment they share much of the mechanics an Oroboros does and so they aren't particularly mysterious... at least in that sense.<br /> <br /> <b>Shayatin/Chthonic Ghuuls:</b> The Shayatin were really written as a complement to the Deep Ones; they're beasts that go around eating the corpses of memory (in the Dreamtide version of the game) or the wandering souls of dangerous Einherjar (in the Treasury version of the game). As such, they aren't villains so much as they are uncomfortable allies, much like spirits are to Werewolves. They are NOT a good fit for the terrifying antagonist and their inclusion is dependent on both the inclusion of the Deep Ones and that of the Treasury itself. In short, they're new to the pile and thus first off the pile if we've got thematic problems with the intangible/mystical half of the game.<br /> <br /> <b>Dracoliches:</b> These are what I came up with today, and the reason I am posting. I've been thinking about what else might threaten a dragon to the point of terror, and I came upon nature itself. An illness, especially a contagious one with limited or painful treatment (or none at all) can bring down even the greatest of beasts. So I thought about <i>White Nose Syndrome</i> and how it's killing bats. And I thought about the mold monsters in Fallout New Vegas. Mold killing a body and controlling it like a puppet is pretty scary; possibly superstitious terror scary. Essentially, an Oroboros succumbs to the mold and then it uses their body to take a joy ride, flaunting Ablutions and Edicts as it looks for more bodies to pollinate. What makes it a draco<b>lich</b>? Well the mold isn't actually a dragon, so as it attains degrees of divinity the flesh fetters and then falls off until it's little more than a mossy mass of skeleton and tendons.<br /> If the mold angle doesn't work for this sort of rotting danger, perhaps this notion could be incorporated into the Einherjar to make them less hunter and more terrifying revenant.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> To speak shortly, Nightmares are essentially Freddy Krueger: they transform, do scary things like shatter bones, and leaving lasting injuries on their victims even when they wake (at least in the Dreamtide version). They were really included as a means of fleshing out the Dreamtide, and are mechanically similar to ghosts and spirits (though their energy and their health are the same stat, so using energy actually harms them). They'd be easy to keep or remove, depending on the verdict on the Treasury.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... that's what we've got so far. Frogs is correct, we need something that will fill an Oroboros with blind terror... are there any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T23:17:18-07:00","id":222849,"title":"","content":"Just wondering what happens if a supernatural were to eat a dragons heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T23:21:55-07:00","id":222850,"title":"","content":"Nothing good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T00:19:36-07:00","id":222890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=222828#post222828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... that's what we've got so far. Frogs is correct, we need something that will fill an Oroboros with blind terror... are there any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Working off the idea I had before, My idea for a new Antagonist would be a group/creature who steals a Dragon's horde. As powerful as Dragons are, they are effectively the Godzilla of nWoD. Not much can put them down and simply put, not much can terrifying them (other than, of course, another Dragon). <br /> <br /> However, they are extremely vulnerable to having their Hoards/Maidens/etc messed with. A high powered Dragon who's crap is stolen is going to be turned into stone very quickly unless he gets it back and it get's worse the higher up the power level you go.<br /> <br /> Ideally Antagonists in question would be outside the &quot;I'm a human going for a trickster way of getting my heart&quot; and tied somehow into the theme of Dragons fading beyond the world.<br /> <br /> Need to see if I can get somewhat creative with this as it would result too many &quot;Run home and defend your hoard!&quot; encounters where it ceases to be an RPG and more of tower defense game on it's own. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T04:09:29-07:00","id":223120,"title":"","content":"The superstitious threat antagonist should surely be the original dragons. Say the originals were not all wiped out. Say some are sleeping or escaped to another world and could potentially seek to return. This would be a doomsday level scernario for the Ourouburi dragons. The superstitions would be, one day the original dragons will return and eat the usurper pretenders. It ties into the existing mythology, the theme of extinction and the symbol of eating itself.<br /> <br /> Whether its used or not is up to storytellers. I guess it would be a little like the Antidelivuons from the original Masquerade but I think it fits Embers well tonally. You also wouldn't need to make up any new mechanics for it since its more a plot device than a straight up antagonist, but if you did want to stat up an original Dragon, the mechanics for it can be used from the ones you've already got.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think you need a new anatognist who steals a dragon's horde. That should be what other dragons do. Weaker dragons (PCS) should be teaming up to plan epic heists on powerful dragons. That should be a key part of the game.<br /> <br /> I would say Embers right now supports the following types of games.<br /> <br /> High powered heists, Supernatural slugests, personal horror due to the controling aspects and the body horror aspect, politics.<br /> <br /> Thats a pretty good spread.<br /> <br /> As for anatognists I think it should be kept stream-lined and I would personally focus on the following and discard the rest (for now).<br /> <br /> A human faction: I have an idea for this, thats less medieval knights and more Cheiron from Hunter mixed in with spilcers from Bioshock. Humans that have transformed their bodies in gross ways Individually not powerful enough to stand toe to toe but as a group they could be a potential threat to weaker dragons.This could reflect the body horror aspect of dragons.<br /> <br /> Other dragons: I think the original philosophies as excuses for being tyranical monsters would work really well as a dragon anatagonist. Honestly though, I think its going to be pretty easy to set up dragon vs dragon scernarios as is. Having groups that become seduced by the power they wield would serve well to reflect the thin line between domineering tyrant and controlling monster. The PCs veer more towards the former, enemy dragons have crossed that line into monsters. The original philisophies could serve as a &quot;code&quot; that some actively adhere to. In my mind other dragons should be the &quot;default&quot; enemy really.<br /> <br /> The Deep Ones: I am a fan of these and think they work well as a contrast to dragons. Monsters that are extremely hard to kill (perhaps requiring a plot device or inter-realm travel if you keep that) to do so but can be bargained with and sacrificed to. I would combine this idea with Dracoliches. Dracoliches would be dragons outright possessed by Deep Ones. This would work as a merger between the two, a voluntary one. Perhaps this could incorporate the earlier idea of having gross apendages, bulbous looking eyes in the middle of shoulders. (Visually I thinking a bit like Nightmare from Soul Caliber or some of the resident evil monsters). These would work similarly to dragon's existing tells with the more powerful ones being harder to hide.<br /> <br /> <b>Chimerae/Chimeras</b>: I am actually a fan of this idea. Maybe its an animal thats fed, part of a heart rather than the whole thing. They would then seek to eat more. These could also be created by other dragons and used as watch-dogs and fill the role of ghouls to some extent. Sentient and intelligent but not human would work well.<br /> <br /> I would personally focus on these 3 enemys with chimeras being a weird add on.<br /> <br /> I have some time this weekend and will try to do a full write up of these if people like the ideas.<br /> <br /> I am also partial to the idea of mostly human heros being able to fight dragons but honestly can't think of any ideas that would well. Perhaps this idea is best being shelved. It is really &quot;fantasy-y&quot; perhaps the idea of humans killing dragons by hitting their weakspot should be spent on maidens rejecting their bonds and attacking their masters instead.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 08-09-2014, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:43:11-07:00","id":223255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=222890#post222890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Working off the idea I had before, My idea for a new Antagonist would be a group/creature who steals a Dragon's horde. As powerful as Dragons are, they are effectively the Godzilla of nWoD. Not much can put them down and simply put, not much can terrifying them (other than, of course, another Dragon).<br /> <br /> However, they are extremely vulnerable to having their Hoards/Maidens/etc messed with. A high powered Dragon who's crap is stolen is going to be turned into stone very quickly unless he gets it back and it get's worse the higher up the power level you go.<br /> <br /> Ideally Antagonists in question would be outside the &quot;I'm a human going for a trickster way of getting my heart&quot; and tied somehow into the theme of Dragons fading beyond the world.<br /> <br /> Need to see if I can get somewhat creative with this as it would result too many &quot;Run home and defend your hoard!&quot; encounters where it ceases to be an RPG and more of tower defense game on it's own.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How about the idea that they're the Ourboroi's successors, in a sense; a Greater Template that hasn't taken shape yet, and wants to take the power of Dragons so they may be fully born into the world?<br /> <br /> The idea is that they're not inherently evil (if they win they'll develop their own Karma Scale, with attendant Don't Be A Dick riders), but they're at least subconsciously aware they are not yet complete, and all other considerations are secondary to filling their internal emptiness via Horde theft to anchor their identities.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not the only thing they do, just the most reliable (because Hordes are already infused with powerful mythic resonance). Other things they do include creating urban mythology around themselves, finding other resonant objects to obtain and anchor themselves, and eat dreams to find pieces of the beings they will become.<br /> <br /> They can also be allies with the Deep Ones, on and off, to help them be remembered and reborn...but for the most part, they're a rare but increasingly known danger, because they want you to know who they are. They don't, not yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T08:36:15-07:00","id":223296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When making a Dragon character, that character receives a fleeting two dots to place in Edicts, and one such dot must always be placed in the Edict that matches the dragon\u2018s Philosophy. These first two dots reflect the dragon\u2018s introduction to her new worldviews, and the influences that come with such worldviews. To review: Imperators begin with a dot of Fire, Paragons begin with a dot of Wood, Savants begin with a dot of Water, Viziers begin with a dot of Metal, and <b>Caitiffs begin with a dot of Earth</b>. </div> </div> </div>Is this still the case? Because a non-Philosophy (or Unaligned or Ghost Wolf or Court-less) probably shouldn't give this kind of benefit. Perhaps they could have a single dot to put wherever they want. I think a new Philosophy should take Earth, but I have yet to read the Philosophies, and I'll try to understand what might be cool IMHO.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Vampires, that would be Blood Potency. For Werewolves, it\u2018s Primal Urge, Mages would subtract<br /> their Gnosis, and anything that possesses <b>Preternatural Potency</b> gets to use that trait to resist these powers.<br /> Supernatural Objects also have a type of <b>Preternatural Potency</b>, referred to in this book as its Artifact rating.<br /> An object\u2018s \u2015Artifact\u2016 is equal to the number of Merit points associated with the object. Being possessed of<br /> an Artifact rating grants the object two benefits against Edicts </div> </div> </div>It's called <b>Supernatural Tolerance</b>. Can you change it, please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 08-09-2014, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T09:54:04-07:00","id":223340,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Edict explaination was a bit long, so I shortened it a bit and make it more synthetic. Note that I changed the name of the &quot;combination&quot; for law into <b>Law corollaries</b>.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Edicts and Laws</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Part of their divine right of the dragons is the ability to impose things on matter by force-of-will, and Edicts are the way a dragon can enforce them. Their words are charged by their majesty, and are given the possibility to re-weave the fabric of reality at their command. It\u2019s good to be a king.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Each Edict is accompanied by three laws, with each Law bearing its own unique purpose. Laws enable the Oroboroi to perform one particular action in the vein of the Edict. Every dot in an Edict unlocks one Law in any order. Everytime an Oroboroi learns his first Law of an Edict, he learns the Law\u2019s Veto (see below). Activating a Law or Veto is an Instant action, and it\u2019s called <i>\u201cproclamation\u201d.</i></span></span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">When the dragon knows at least two Laws of an Edict, he can purchase a Law corollary. A Law corollary take two Laws and roll them into a single proclamation; the laws may be proclaimed in a single Instant action and at the same Effect Rating but the mechanics are otherwise unchanged. This way, it\u2019s possible for the dragon to reach up to three Laws and three Law corollaries.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Edicts decrease in power every time they are used within the same scene, and this is reflected by the Effective Rating (similar to how manifest Ablutions are). The Effective Rating begins each scene equal to the dots known in the Edict. Every time a proclamation is resolved, the Edict\u2018s Effective Rating is reduced by 1. </span></span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Ordinances work as Skill Specialities for Edicts, but the Philosophy of the Oroboroi grants him a peculiar Ordinance that applies to all Edicts. It might describe a type of target (such as \u201cSquirrels\u201d for the Husbandry Edict) or a specific situation (such as \u201cRaining\u201d for the Water Edict).</span></span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Effective Rating of an Edict can be increased in four ways:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">+1 to the Effective Rating per Breath spent.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">+2 to the Effective Rating if the proclamation meets the condition of an Ordinance the Oroboros owns.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">+2 if the Oroboros uses the Draconic 3 Merit to proclaim it</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Always adds the current Divinity of the dragon.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">These are only temporary boosts, and the Effective Rating still decreases when the Edict is used, regardless of any empowerment the dragon applied. A Law the reaches a natural Effective Rating of 0 ceases to function for the rest of the scene. When calculating the natural Effective Rating, don\u2019t count Divinity. You can track the current Effect Rating of an Edict by checking off the boxes under the dots as proclamations are made.<br /> When making a Dragon character, that character receives a fleeting two dots to place in Edicts, and one such dot must always be placed in the Edict that matches the dragon\u2018s Philosophy. These first two dots reflect the dragon\u2018s introduction to her new worldviews, and the influences that come with such worldviews.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Imperators:</b>One dot in Fire</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Paragons:</b> One dot in Wood</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Savants: </b>One dot in Water</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Viziers: </b>One dot in Metal</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Caitiff: </b>One dot in Earth</span></span></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:01:54-07:00","id":223521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=222849#post222849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering what happens if a supernatural were to eat a dragons heart.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=222850#post222850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's sort of like swallowing napalm for beings that are already supernatural.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=222890#post222890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Working off the idea I had before, My idea for a new Antagonist would be a group/creature who steals a Dragon's horde. As powerful as Dragons are, they are effectively the Godzilla of nWoD. Not much can put them down and simply put, not much can terrifying them (other than, of course, another Dragon).<br /> <br /> Ideally Antagonists in question would be outside the &quot;I'm a human going for a trickster way of getting my heart&quot; and tied somehow into the theme of Dragons fading beyond the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223255#post223255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the idea that they're the Ourboroi's successors, in a sense; a Greater Template that hasn't taken shape yet, and wants to take the power of Dragons so they may be fully born into the world?<br /> <br /> The idea is that they're not inherently evil (if they win they'll develop their own Karma Scale, with attendant Don't Be A Dick riders), but they're at least subconsciously aware they are not yet complete, and all other considerations are secondary to filling their internal emptiness via Horde theft to anchor their identities.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not the only thing they do, just the most reliable (because Hordes are already infused with powerful mythic resonance). Other things they do include creating urban mythology around themselves, finding other resonant objects to obtain and anchor themselves, and eat dreams to find pieces of the beings they will become.<br /> <br /> They can also be allies with the Deep Ones, on and off, to help them be remembered and reborn...but for the most part, they're a rare but increasingly known danger, because they want you to know who they are. They don't, not yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223120#post223120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The superstitious threat antagonist should surely be the original dragons. Say the originals were not all wiped out. Say some are sleeping or escaped to another world and could potentially seek to return. This would be a doomsday level scernario for the Ourouburi dragons. The superstitions would be, one day the original dragons will return and eat the usurper pretenders. It ties into the existing mythology, the theme of extinction and the symbol of eating itself.<br /> <br /> Whether its used or not is up to storytellers. I guess it would be a little like the Antidelivuons from the original Masquerade but I think it fits Embers well tonally. You also wouldn't need to make up any new mechanics for it since its more a plot device than a straight up antagonist, but if you did want to stat up an original Dragon, the mechanics for it can be used from the ones you've already got.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like both of these ideas: Gravitas's ancient dragons gives a real &quot;Looming Jormungandr&quot; vibe that I think the game would easily accommodate, while a 'newcomer god' threatens from the other side of the spectrum.<br /> ...Unfortunately, the only modern gods I can think of at the moment are lolcats... perhaps somebody else can come up with something good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223120#post223120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you need a new anatognist who steals a dragon's horde. That should be what other dragons do. Weaker dragons (PCS) should be teaming up to plan epic heists on powerful dragons. That should be a key part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree here as well; if we do write up a new usurper (that isn't a lolcat) the focus should be on snatching the dragon's Heart, not her assets. In a way, this new entity would already be in the thoughts of the mortals (being a media icon on the verge of tremendous worship power), so it wouldn't need to rob an Oroboros for mystical sustenance. That's a player motive, just as Gravitas said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223120#post223120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say Embers right now supports the following types of games.<br /> <br /> High powered heists, Supernatural slugests, personal horror due to the controling aspects and the body horror aspect, politics.<br /> <br /> Thats a pretty good spread.<br /> <br /> As for anatognists I think it should be kept stream-lined and I would personally focus on the following and discard the rest (for now).<br /> <br /> A human faction: I have an idea for this, thats less medieval knights and more Cheiron from Hunter mixed in with spilcers from Bioshock. Humans that have transformed their bodies in gross ways Individually not powerful enough to stand toe to toe but as a group they could be a potential threat to weaker dragons.This could reflect the body horror aspect of dragons.<br /> <br /> Other dragons: I think the original philosophies as excuses for being tyranical monsters would work really well as a dragon anatagonist. Honestly though, I think its going to be pretty easy to set up dragon vs dragon scernarios as is. Having groups that become seduced by the power they wield would serve well to reflect the thin line between domineering tyrant and controlling monster. The PCs veer more towards the former, enemy dragons have crossed that line into monsters. The original philisophies could serve as a &quot;code&quot; that some actively adhere to. In my mind other dragons should be the &quot;default&quot; enemy really.<br /> <br /> The Deep Ones: I am a fan of these and think they work well as a contrast to dragons. Monsters that are extremely hard to kill (perhaps requiring a plot device or inter-realm travel if you keep that) to do so but can be bargained with and sacrificed to. I would combine this idea with Dracoliches. Dracoliches would be dragons outright possessed by Deep Ones. This would work as a merger between the two, a voluntary one. Perhaps this could incorporate the earlier idea of having gross apendages, bulbous looking eyes in the middle of shoulders. (Visually I thinking a bit like Nightmare from Soul Caliber or some of the resident evil monsters). These would work similarly to dragon's existing tells with the more powerful ones being harder to hide.<br /> <br /> <b>Chimerae/Chimeras</b>: I am actually a fan of this idea. Maybe its an animal thats fed, part of a heart rather than the whole thing. They would then seek to eat more. These could also be created by other dragons and used as watch-dogs and fill the role of ghouls to some extent. Sentient and intelligent but not human would work well.<br /> <br /> I would personally focus on these 3 enemys with chimeras being a weird add on.<br /> <br /> I have some time this weekend and will try to do a full write up of these if people like the ideas.<br /> <br /> I am also partial to the idea of mostly human heros being able to fight dragons but honestly can't think of any ideas that would well. Perhaps this idea is best being shelved. It is really &quot;fantasy-y&quot; perhaps the idea of humans killing dragons by hitting their weakspot should be spent on maidens rejecting their bonds and attacking their masters instead.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also agree that the volume of antagonists we currently have for the template is much too tremendous for the needs of the game. Whichever entities don't make the cut for the core book can be introduced in a supplement. I definitely agree that Chimerae need to be part of the main book, though, simply because the question &quot;What if 'X' eats a Dragon Heart&quot; is certain to come up, as it has many times before.<br /> Hmmm... do you suppose other supernatural beings turn into Chimerae after eating a Heart? : D<br /> The weird &quot;eyes everywhere&quot; phenomenon is actually the visual cue I used for Devourers (dragons that eat more than one Heart), so we probably shouldn't use it for Dracoliches too... but I really like the idea of the Dracolich being a dragon fused with a Deep One... or perhaps subjected to the same loss of worship these old gods suffered.<br /> I worry that humans with weird powers will be perceived as simply pseudo-Hunters with magic beans; while it might be nice to explore them in a side book (Dragon the Embers: Dragonslayers?) perhaps we should leave them out of the core. The same could be said about the Knights and the Einherjar; they'd all fit together nicely in a sort of &quot;Humans that hunt dragons for sport&quot; manual, but they might distract focus in the core book. ...Which is a bummer, because that means I have to rewrite the intro story for Chapter Two. Hmmm... perhaps something with the Dark Bargainers...<br /> I'm beginning to wonder if revisiting the Volcano Philosophies in the core book is necessary. Considering what you've said and what we have so far, there really doesn't need to be a tremendous difference in ideology to trigger conflict between dragons. Hey, even dragons of the same Philosophy probably rob each other on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223296#post223296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this still the case? Because a non-Philosophy (or Unaligned or Ghost Wolf or Court-less) probably shouldn't give this kind of benefit. Perhaps they could have a single dot to put wherever they want. I think a new Philosophy should take Earth, but I have yet to read the Philosophies, and I'll try to understand what might be cool IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Philosophy of the Center will receive a dot of Earth as they follow the lessons of the Earth Dragon. Whether or not the Caitiffs will be that Philosophy is questionable, but yes, if they become a factionless then a new Philosophy will take their place and take the Earth Dot as their Edict bonus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223296#post223296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT:<br /> It's called <b>Supernatural Tolerance</b>. Can you change it, please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, I knew they finally assigned an official term. I just forgot what it was. Fixed in my version, will be fixed in the next PDF release.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223340#post223340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Edict explaination was a bit long, so I shortened it a bit and make it more synthetic. Note that I changed the name of the &quot;combination&quot; for law into <b>Law corollaries</b>.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I used most of this, but kept the point-box visual and clarified that the first law learned is always Veto, not Veto plus an additional law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  Added a little space between quotes to make the post less cluttered. 08-09-2014, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:05:33-07:00","id":223648,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think cutting human hunters from the core would probably be for the best. Maybe a section on humans being dangerous because they are indirectly the source of a dragon regaining breath and the dangers of maidens fighting back or people ignoring the dragon would suffice. Perhaps a story of a dragon goes to his maiden after his hoard has been raided, only for her/him to spurn him and leave. Weakened and out of breath (ha!) he/she starts to fossilse.<br /> <br /> I have followed this project on and off over the past year and would be happy to write up something on Deep Ones, Dracholices, Chrimea or Dragons as antagonists. Though I could do with a link to the current document so I can re-read the current write up and see how things stand. on the Deep Ones and refresh myself with some of the material.<br /> <br /> I think I will make a start on Chrimea tomorrow and then if you guys like what I've done and want me to write up some of the other enemy types from there just let me know.<br /> <br /> Its nice to see this game enter into its final development stages after all the work you guys have put into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:19:50-07:00","id":223653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cool. I used most of this, but kept the point-box visual and clarified that the first law learned is always Veto, not Veto plus an additional law. </div> </div> </div>Can you Veto a Veto as a Dodge action? Just to know.<br /> Plus, if your Dragon has two Edicts with his two dots, does that mean that he only has Vetos? Vetos are ok, but they are useful only against dragons and people who use Edicts. It seems to me a little lackluster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:01:04-07:00","id":223679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223648#post223648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have followed this project on and off over the past year and would be happy to write up something on Deep Ones, Dracholices, Chrimea or Dragons as antagonists. Though I could do with a link to the current document so I can re-read the current write up and see how things stand. on the Deep Ones and refresh myself with some of the material.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B31Gud9WnwZXTHU1OE8wSDVEQWM/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a link to the Christmas in July half-book, which I released on July 25th of this year. It's got the GMC compatible Edicts and Ablutions, two Philosophies, and a mess of fluff in the first and second chapter that needs work. Since it's only the first half of the book, all mentions of antagonists are in the first chapter and remain vague blurbs. Once we've settled on what we want to threaten the dragons I'll try to work on Chapter Four.<br /> Other than that, we are still working off the material from the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B31Gud9WnwZXa1k2elNGV2oza0U/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Second Phase PDF</a>. As I release more material I will post links both in the run of the thread and in the first post, so if you take a break and come back you can check the first post for any new PDFs associated with the production of the core book (instead of having to fish through pages and pages of replies!).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223653#post223653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you Veto a Veto as a Dodge action? Just to know.<br /> Plus, if your Dragon has two Edicts with his two dots, does that mean that he only has Vetos? Vetos are ok, but they are useful only against dragons and people who use Edicts. It seems to me a little lackluster.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, yes, two one-dot Edicts will only have the Veto law. I know it's a little lackluster, but I was trying to give the opening to the Edict more semblance to a one-dot power. Perhaps such is not necessary; it may be better to give Veto AND one of the Laws with the first dot. I'd like to hear the opinions of others on this matter.<br /> And vetoing a veto sounds awesome. Provided the Effect Rating can be raised to match, it could lead to some deliciously frustrating dragon encounters. I would say it remains an instant action, but undoes a portion of the other Veto's effect. I'll work that into the Veto's description the next time I'm working with the document.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:38:32-07:00","id":223700,"title":"","content":"I changed Wood a little bit. Allergen is now a bit more streamlined, and I added an appropriate Tilt for GMC. Harvest got merged into Bloom, Bloom has become more synthetic and I created a new Law in replacement of Harvest. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Allergen</b><br /> <b>Attribute:</b> The lower of Stamina or Intelligence<br /> &quot;Let the pollen cloud their mind&quot;<br /> The proclaiming Oroboros triggers a spray of pollen from all nearby plant sources. Anyone within range suffers an immediate sneezing and coughing fit, even if they are not particularly allergic to outdoor irritants. This law requires plants to be nearby in order to have an effect. The plants affected gain the highly allergenic pollen permanently; new beings entering the area suffer the same fit but are permanently acclimated to the irritant once they finish sneezing and coughing.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Stamina/Intelligence + Wood + Furnace<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Oroboros triggers the pollen spray, but subjects herself to the allergic fit.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Within a number of yards equal to the Effect Rating, hyper-allergenic pollen clouds the air. Anyone within this cloud suffers a sneezing and coughing fit, suffering 1 point of bashing damage per turn of combat, and must roll Stamina + Resolve -3 or lose the action. A creature that successfully acts for three consecutive turns from contesting the allergen becomes immune to the allergen for the entire scene. This fit lasts for a number of turns equal to the Effect Rating of the proclamation.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The duration is improved by 3 turns.<br /> <br /> [GMC: Apply the Poisoned (moderate) Tilt, but add that the failed Stamina + Resolve -3 to resist the poison makes the creature lose the action for failing to sneeze and cough the allergen out]<br /> <br /> <b>Bloom</b><br /> <b>Attribute:</b> The lower of Resolve or Manipulation<br /> &quot;Let them grow strong, reaching for the light.&quot;<br /> The proclaiming Oroboros seeds the growth of plant matter, sprouting a bed of flowers as well as a number of saplings equal to the Effect Rating within the target region. If any plants are already within the area, they are sped along their natural lifespan, grow strong and lively, and eventually can lead dying plants to rot and die.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve/Manipulation + Wood + Furnace<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Oroboros accidentally kills the plant or suffers 2 bashing damage while trying to kill vegetation.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens.<br /> <b>Success:</b> All plants in the area (see the <b>Targets</b>)or specific plants can either grow from seed to young plant, mature plant, and eventually to death and decay, at choice of the Oroboros. The plants don't need an appropriate terrain to grow, and can grow roots into stone, concrete and similar harsh terrains. The Oroboros can grow the plant so greatly that they can be used for narrative purpose to create means to reach impervious places expending 1 Breath. A plant that bears fruit can be enchanted using 1 Breath to sprout a magical fruit capable of healing 1 bashing or lethal damage per Furnace dot. A single plant can only bear one fruit of this kind.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: When using the Law to grow plants, the Dragon can choose to turn it into a hndering terrain, halving the Speed and inflicting -2 to Initiative to everyone inside except for the Dragon itself. When used for growing the magical fruit, the fruit will heal the Effective Rating instead of his Furnace (if higher).<br /> <br /> <b>Land sense</b><br /> <b>Attribute:</b>The lower of Wits or Composure<br /> &quot;Let the nature be my eyes&quot;<br /> The proclamation makes the Oroboros' senses open to the surrounding nature. He can see, smell and hear through the vegetation, and know the terrain better, to find dangers and avoid them, or know how to best fight it.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits/Composure + Wood + Furnace<br /> <b>Success:</b> The Oroboros gains information from the landscape within 50 yards per Effective Rating. He gains knowledge of the position of every single creature within the range of the Law, gains +3 to Perception rolls, +2 to Initiative and +1 to all actions while inside the affected area. The Oroboros is also protected by ambushes, as plants perceive everyone in the area which is not in a state of Twilight or incorporeal. The dragon doesn't need to roll for surprise, and simply rolls Initiative like he won the surprise roll. Concealing magic can defeat the land sense with a Clash of Wills, using the rating of the concealing power + Supernatural tolerance (or 3 if the power rating is undefined) versus Wood + Furnace.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Oroboros gains rote action to Perception rolls, +3 to Initiative and +2 to all actions while inside the affected area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 08-10-2014, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T19:02:18-07:00","id":223761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223521#post223521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually really like both of these ideas: Gravitas's ancient dragons gives a real &quot;Looming Jormungandr&quot; vibe that I think the game would easily accommodate, while a 'newcomer god' threatens from the other side of the spectrum.<br /> ...Unfortunately, the only modern gods I can think of at the moment are lolcats... perhaps somebody else can come up with something good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking along the lines of the <a href=\"http://thefearmythos.wikia.com/wiki/The_Fear_Mythos_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Fear Mythos</a>, Slenderman and his &quot;pantheon&quot; of internet urban legends everyone knows is false. For those of you who don't feel the need to trawl the wiki I linked, they're the main villains and focuses of a shared Lovecraftian metafictional universe.<br /> <br /> In the New World of Darkness...it's still false. It's going to be mostly false even if the, to borrow a Keats term here, Rough Beasts are to be truly born, they still work on a comparable-to-mortal scale. But the legends, of what they can and cannot do, anchor them, help them figure out who they are and what their role in the world is.<br /> <br /> Naturally, it's easier to steal that role from someone else, and the dying Dragons may not be needing it any more soon (may, because I'm pretty sure you accepted the idea that new Hearts can be created with heroic effort at some point to emphasize the Ouroboroi raging against their extinction). So they might as well help themselves to a role of rulership and dominance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T21:35:30-07:00","id":223847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223761#post223761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was actually thinking along the lines of the <a href=\"http://thefearmythos.wikia.com/wiki/The_Fear_Mythos_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Fear Mythos</a>, Slenderman and his &quot;pantheon&quot; of internet urban legends everyone knows is false. For those of you who don't feel the need to trawl the wiki I linked, they're the main villains and focuses of a shared Lovecraftian metafictional universe.<br /> <br /> In the New World of Darkness...it's still false. It's going to be mostly false even if the, to borrow a Keats term here, Rough Beasts are to be truly born, they still work on a comparable-to-mortal scale. But the legends, of what they can and cannot do, anchor them, help them figure out who they are and what their role in the world is.<br /> <br /> Naturally, it's easier to steal that role from someone else, and the dying Dragons may not be needing it any more soon (may, because I'm pretty sure you accepted the idea that new Hearts can be created with heroic effort at some point to emphasize the Ouroboroi raging against their extinction). So they might as well help themselves to a role of rulership and dominance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also for some reason their counterpart are way worse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T07:50:30-07:00","id":224100,"title":"","content":"What if the &quot;chronicle&quot; enemy is a bunch of original Dragons that survived the first Collapse, and that hate the Oroboroi (which I understand they are called this way because the oroboros eats iself, so the original dragons aren't considered Oroboroi) fiercely for killing the other original dragons?<br /> <br /> They might even not ever removed their Hearts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T09:18:37-07:00","id":224201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=224100#post224100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the &quot;chronicle&quot; enemy is a bunch of original Dragons that survived the first Collapse, and that hate the Oroboroi (which I understand they are called this way because the oroboros eats iself, so the original dragons aren't considered Oroboroi) fiercely for killing the other original dragons?<br /> <br /> They might even not ever removed their Hearts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original Dragons would most likely play the role of nWoD Kaiju of the Godzilla/Pacific Rim variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T09:54:23-07:00","id":224216,"title":"","content":"Yep, and I think THAT could certainly be a proper enemy for Oroboroi. Oroboroi are pretty powerful, and a bunch of experienced Oroboroi in badass dragon form might be strong enough to stand, even if for a small period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T14:40:58-07:00","id":224491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=224216#post224216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, and I think THAT could certainly be a proper enemy for Oroboroi. Oroboroi are pretty powerful, and a bunch of experienced Oroboroi in badass dragon form might be strong enough to stand, even if for a small period.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How bout something like that novel worm where they had some seriously great monsters.<br /> here is the link <a href=\"http://parahumans.wikia.com/wiki/Endbringer\" target=\"_blank\">http://parahumans.wikia.com/wiki/Endbringer</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T00:38:27-07:00","id":224917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=224216#post224216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, and I think THAT could certainly be a proper enemy for Oroboroi. Oroboroi are pretty powerful, and a bunch of experienced Oroboroi in badass dragon form might be strong enough to stand, even if for a small period.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth mentioning that the hate that they have for the Oroboroi is buried somewhere in there is the lessor hate for humanity.<br /> <br /> There might be a handful sleeping those dark dreams in the depths of the sea but if they rise, they will most certainly won't be keeping humanity around if they wake. They've already made that poor choice before.<br /> <br /> If the Oroboroi are akin to kings, governors and emperors, the Elders (my running name for them right now) are akin to what the Oroboroi fear most which is a walking Act of God rampaging around their turf and hunting them specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T04:27:07-07:00","id":224973,"title":"","content":"...if anyone was wondering, yes I do have a write up for the Savants and yes, I am late putting it forward.<br /> <br /> Computer is having slight problems. Repair in progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:22:13-07:00","id":225099,"title":"","content":"No worries, FallenEco. Good things are worth waiting for. : )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking... since we now have three different types of dragons (instead of the original two; elders and usurpers) we should probably come up with some official terminology to differentiate them.<br /> <br /> The <b>Oroboroi</b> are the usurpers, self consuming to maintain a power that they are not suited to handle.<br /> <br /> The five dragons of the five winds already have &quot;Long&quot; in their name, which covers the eastern interpretation. To add a bit of west to it, I want to tack on Zmeu, a Romanian dragon-esque entity that has a penchant for abducting fair maidens. So the five original dragons that predated the universe will be referred to as <b>Long Zmeu</b> (Singular) or <b>Long Zmei</b> (Plural).<br /> EDIT: Looked it up for pronunciation, Zmeu is pronounced <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Zh-MAY-ew. Thanks to Merrie Haskell for the clarification. (source: </span></span></span>http://blog.merriehaskell.com/tag/zmeu/ )<br /> <br /> As for the dragons that were dethroned, I believe <b>Nidhoggr</b> is an appropriate moniker as Jormungandr is their poster child. I've used the term in literature before and I'm quite fond of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> If we are all in agreement that the Nidhoggr should be the terrifying threat, we should begin developing them as a fully fleshed antagonist. Mechanically I propose they use the quick character rules I posted in another thread (Six Attributes, Three Skills), though with attribute bounds of 1-5 instead of 0-3 for the low-end ones. ...Or is it bad form to supply the terrifying antagonist with mechanics?<br /> <br /> Thematically? Well... I'll let you guys work on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 08-11-2014, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T09:01:19-07:00","id":225112,"title":"","content":"CJC have you seen the Wood Edict remake I did? Any comment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T12:18:51-07:00","id":225216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223700#post223700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I changed Wood a little bit. Allergen is now a bit more streamlined, and I added an appropriate Tilt for GMC. Harvest got merged into Bloom, Bloom has become more synthetic and I created a new Law in replacement of Harvest. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Allergen</b><br /> <b>Attribute:</b> The lower of Stamina or Intelligence<br /> &quot;Let the pollen cloud their mind&quot;<br /> The proclaiming Oroboros triggers a spray of pollen from all nearby plant sources. Anyone within range suffers an immediate sneezing and coughing fit, even if they are not particularly allergic to outdoor irritants. This law requires plants to be nearby in order to have an effect. The plants affected gain the highly allergenic pollen permanently; new beings entering the area suffer the same fit but are permanently acclimated to the irritant once they finish sneezing and coughing.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Stamina/Intelligence + Wood + Furnace<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Oroboros triggers the pollen spray, but subjects herself to the allergic fit.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Within a number of yards equal to the Effect Rating, hyper-allergenic pollen clouds the air. Anyone within this cloud suffers a sneezing and coughing fit, suffering 1 point of bashing damage per turn of combat, and must roll Stamina + Resolve -3 or lose the action. A creature that successfully acts for three consecutive turns from contesting the allergen becomes immune to the allergen for the entire scene. This fit lasts for a number of turns equal to the Effect Rating of the proclamation.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The duration is improved by 3 turns.<br /> <br /> [GMC: Apply the Poisoned (moderate) Tilt, but add that the failed Stamina + Resolve -3 to resist the poison makes the creature lose the action for failing to sneeze and cough the allergen out]</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like that it does damage; wood is the element of life and there are much better Edicts to use for the purpose of inflicting harm. Also, sneezing and coughing are rarely severe enough to leave a lasting impact, even bruises (It's have to be a very violent reaction and even then, the choking does more damage than the coughing). The blind effect of the original version was actually intended to reduce the damage the dragon will suffer during the effect, since fighting blind is worse than rolling chance dice. Overcoming the allergen with a roll is nice, but I think it might work better with cumulative rolls, and with those counting up to the effect rating. By which I mean, after five successful actions (actions not impaired by the pollen because the Stamina + Resolve - The Proclaiming Dragon's Furnace roll succeeded) they adjust to the pollen and become immune for the scene, but the successful actions need not occur in a row.<br /> As for the penalty for sneezing and coughing--full blindness unless the aforementioned Stamina + Resolve - Furnace roll succeeds in which case it is treated as substantial darkness (I don't have the WoD core book on hand, but I think it's -3 to act, -3 sight perception).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223700#post223700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bloom</b><br /> <b>Attribute:</b> The lower of Resolve or Manipulation<br /> &quot;Let them grow strong, reaching for the light.&quot;<br /> The proclaiming Oroboros seeds the growth of plant matter, sprouting a bed of flowers as well as a number of saplings equal to the Effect Rating within the target region. If any plants are already within the area, they are sped along their natural lifespan, grow strong and lively, and eventually can lead dying plants to rot and die.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve/Manipulation + Wood + Furnace<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Oroboros accidentally kills the plant or suffers 2 bashing damage while trying to kill vegetation.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens.<br /> <b>Success:</b> All plants in the area (see the <b>Targets</b>)or specific plants can either grow from seed to young plant, mature plant, and eventually to death and decay, at choice of the Oroboros. The plants don't need an appropriate terrain to grow, and can grow roots into stone, concrete and similar harsh terrains. The Oroboros can grow the plant so greatly that they can be used for narrative purpose to create means to reach impervious places expending 1 Breath. A plant that bears fruit can be enchanted using 1 Breath to sprout a magical fruit capable of healing 1 bashing or lethal damage per Furnace dot. A single plant can only bear one fruit of this kind.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: When using the Law to grow plants, the Dragon can choose to turn it into a hindering terrain, halving the Speed and inflicting -2 to Initiative to everyone inside except for the Dragon itself. When used for growing the magical fruit, the fruit will heal the Effective Rating instead of his Furnace (if higher).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the hindering terrain, and I believe that should be incorporated into the base effect, rather than an exceptional bonus. I do not like that it absorbed Harvest, however; this law was mainly for the purpose of generating raw materials for the Wood Edict and for producing storytelling-based advantages, such as a tree to hide behind or climb (or to filter the toxic air around a volcano or in a post-apocalyptic wasteland).<br /> Letting an Oroboros benefit multiple times from the golden fruit in a scene breaks the Breath balance, since it's much more energy effective to grow and eat a bushel of golden fruit than it is to use the furnace to repair wounds (1 Breath for Furnace Lethal removed against 2 Breath for one Lethal removed). The limit of benefiting once per scene from the fruit circumvents this. Also, by making it only a single fruit the Oroboros cannot assist her friends with the proclamation; there's never enough to help more than one person. And finally, the Edict cannot backfire if the plant only grows one fruit; in the original version of Harvest a hostile target could--if knowledgeable of Oroboroi magic--steal one of the fruit from a tree and benefit himself. This is especially easy if the Oroboros is depending on old growth to produce the tree--most parks will produce areas of effect that could spawn dozens of golden fruit.<br /> I believe Bloom and Harvest need to remain separate laws.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=223700#post223700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Land sense</b><br /> <b>Attribute:</b>The lower of Wits or Composure<br /> &quot;Let the nature be my eyes&quot;<br /> The proclamation makes the Oroboros' senses open to the surrounding nature. He can see, smell and hear through the vegetation, and know the terrain better, to find dangers and avoid them, or know how to best fight it.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits/Composure + Wood + Furnace<br /> <b>Success:</b> The Oroboros gains information from the landscape within 50 yards per Effective Rating. He gains knowledge of the position of every single creature within the range of the Law, gains +3 to Perception rolls, +2 to Initiative and +1 to all actions while inside the affected area. The Oroboros is also protected by ambushes, as plants perceive everyone in the area which is not in a state of Twilight or incorporeal. The dragon doesn't need to roll for surprise, and simply rolls Initiative like he won the surprise roll. Concealing magic can defeat the land sense with a Clash of Wills, using the rating of the concealing power + Supernatural tolerance (or 3 if the power rating is undefined) versus Wood + Furnace.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Oroboros gains rote action to Perception rolls, +3 to Initiative and +2 to all actions while inside the affected area</div> </div> </div> </div>I see that you're going for a Boneyard feel with this, and I can imagine one of the possible combinations with Land Sense: the remote trigger of a pollen burst. However, this law conflicts with one of the primary features of the Edict system: each Edict has a fixed target regardless of the law proclaimed. For Wood, that target is a space with yard radius equal to the effect rating, or rather an area in square yards equal to <b>Pi * ER^2</b>. Land Sense breaks this pattern, and HAS to break this pattern to be worthwhile. However, that makes combinations with it rough, because the limited size of the other two Laws force repeated uses to make Land Sense viable, especially with Bloom.<br /> What's worse, the potency of Land Sense remains much larger than the other two Laws combined: a level 1 proclamation of Land Sense covers more than the entire area of a level 10 proclamation of Bloom. This is a problem, since players can pay experience to learn how to perform two proclamations in a single instant action (a Law Corollary). If they were to combine Bloom and Land Sense, they would only be able to see within the confines of the Bloom space, which they could see anyway because it has to be within the range of their voice to form. It's also a problem for Land Sense because the only component being controlled by the effect rating is essentially nullified for all combinations.<br /> I'm not saying that Land Sense isn't awesome; I am saying that it doesn't work as a starting level Law. In a high-octane supplement (one that supplies powers for 6+ dots), I could see listing Land Sense as a viable Law (perhaps with a prerequisite of Wood 4).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T13:53:49-07:00","id":225293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=225099#post225099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries, FallenEco. Good things are worth waiting for. : )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking... since we now have three different types of dragons (instead of the original two; elders and usurpers) we should probably come up with some official terminology to differentiate them.<br /> <br /> The <b>Oroboroi</b> are the usurpers, self consuming to maintain a power that they are not suited to handle.<br /> <br /> The five dragons of the five winds already have &quot;Long&quot; in their name, which covers the eastern interpretation. To add a bit of west to it, I want to tack on Zmeu, a Romanian dragon-esque entity that has a penchant for abducting fair maidens. So the five original dragons that predated the universe will be referred to as <b>Long Zmeu</b> (Singular) or <b>Long Zmei</b> (Plural).<br /> EDIT: Looked it up for pronunciation, Zmeu is pronounced <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Zh-MAY-ew. Thanks to Merrie Haskell for the clarification. (source: </span></span></span>http://blog.merriehaskell.com/tag/zmeu/ )<br /> <br /> As for the dragons that were dethroned, I believe <b>Nidhoggr</b> is an appropriate moniker as Jormungandr is their poster child. I've used the term in literature before and I'm quite fond of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> If we are all in agreement that the Nidhoggr should be the terrifying threat, we should begin developing them as a fully fleshed antagonist. Mechanically I propose they use the quick character rules I posted in another thread (Six Attributes, Three Skills), though with attribute bounds of 1-5 instead of 0-3 for the low-end ones. ...Or is it bad form to supply the terrifying antagonist with mechanics?<br /> <br /> Thematically? Well... I'll let you guys work on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Help with terms.<br /> <br /> The Ancestors: The Dragons who put the universe together and set down the Mandate. (I use the term Ancestors due to every culture's respect of them but most notably the cultures of Asia really hammer home the idea of respecting those who came before over everything else). Typically did their job, had kids (The Elders), told their kids how to do their jobs, and vanished.<br /> <br /> Elders/Tyrants: The Ancestor's kids. Did well for a time but eventually got lazy and tyrannical and most ditched the Mandate. Proto-kingdoms wracked by world wide storms and disasters. Stability eventually became a thing of the past and humans kept rebelling due to it. Some Elders saw the writing on the wall and bolted to other realms while others entered deep sleep under the sea. Most however, were eventually consumed by the humans who would take on their shapes and take their place.<br /> <br /> Usurpers/Oroboroi: The human/dragons we now know and love.<br /> <br /> Also, here is an idea that why the Oroboroi can't really breed and can solve that problem: Humans are not meant to hold the Mandate. Their inheritance of it is an aberration and while the Universe follows the primal law set forth by the Ancestors (&quot;He who does not uphold the Mandate will suffer the wrath of those who can&quot;), It still doesn't really expect the Oroboroi to rise to the expectations laid forth by the Ancestors.<br /> <br /> In short, while most of the Elders were lazy and tyrannical, they were still foremost Dragons. The Universe had a clear place for them set. Humans entering the positions complicates things as they are rising above their station in a way that the Universe gives them the squint eye.<br /> <br /> To quote Scott Card: &quot;Some Kingdoms can't be conquered, only inherited&quot;.<br /> <br /> If a Usurper starts to reach an high Furnace level, while achieving what the Mandate describes, I can see the Universe giving way and allowing him/her to breed.<br /> <br /> Of course, the trouble is trying to find another Usurper who has done the same...<br /> <br /> Edit- as for the Elders themselves.<br /> <br /> The issue with them is akin to bring any Kaiju into nWoD game. How do you accurately portray a creature who is as large as a skyscraper and can crush a car flat just by stepping on it without getting bogged down with mechanics?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 08-11-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T15:16:12-07:00","id":225346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=225293#post225293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with them is akin to bring any Kaiju into nWoD game. How do you accurately portray a creature who is as large as a skyscraper and can crush a car flat just by stepping on it without getting bogged down with mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well why not present them as godzilla where they are apathetic towards everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T15:41:22-07:00","id":225356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=225346#post225346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well why not present them as godzilla where they are apathetic towards everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda goes against the mood and story. Almost all of the Elders would despise Oroboroi for both personal (Saw their offspring's/mate's heart torn out by humans during the collapse) and metaphysical reasons (&quot;These upstarts killed my family and now are dancing around acting like me?!&quot;).<br /> <br /> In short, they are much akin to the Idigam. Old enemies of your race before time which are just now starting to rise and still nurse old grudges.<br /> <br /> To humanity, it's less personal and more Godzilla-like. Almost all of the Elders would, of course, burn every last human to cinders if they could but it's the Oroboroi who are their primary target. A good tactic for an Elder to use would to be to start incinerating every last human in a territory of a Oroboroi to flush him/her out. <br /> <br /> Same way one might burn a forest to flush out a wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 08-11-2014, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T15:42:21-07:00","id":225359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=225293#post225293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit- as for the Elders themselves.<br /> <br /> The issue with them is akin to bring any Kaiju into nWoD game. How do you accurately portray a creature who is as large as a skyscraper and can crush a car flat just by stepping on it without getting bogged down with mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short Answer: When dealing with Kaiju, the Kaiju use game stats and the players are treated like a swarm. Yep, that means every time the Kaiju takes an action to reduce the size of the swarm, somebody dies.<br /> <br /> Long Answer: I was actually toying around with something like this, building a system based off the damage reduction True Form used to supply and a &quot;Scale&quot; mechanic which was actually an Exalted homebrew by Requim_Jeer (Source: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/38075-homebrew-subsystem-scale-and-scope\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...cale-and-scope</a>).<br /> <br /> Scale is a measure of half the character's longest dimension in yards (We'd do the calculations and throw them alongside a size chart). When a character is a scale larger than her attacker, all damage she would sustain is downgraded by one grade and all damage she would inflict is upgraded by one grade.<br /> <br /> Swarm Size Damage (Bashing) -&gt; Bashing -&gt; Lethal -&gt; Aggravated -&gt; Health Dots -&gt; Reduce Swarm Size (Instant Slay)<br /> <br /> This means that, eventually, beings are so small that a single attacker becomes insignificant; the attackers must work in tandem (becoming one game entity) to increase their scale to the point where they would be viable as a swarm, and even then they only inflict fleeting damage. The Oroboroi are the exception, of course, because as they manifest Ablutions they become increasingly enormous, somewhat rivaling the scale of a giant monster.<br /> <br /> If Scale is too much of a pain to track, we could instead do multiples of seven (since the WoD core only covers creatures up to size 7). Anything within sizes 1-7 is Scale 1, everything in sizes 8-14 is Scale 2, and so forth. Since skyscrapers are only like... size 60, the Kaiju would only be Scale 9. That's still enough to squash human beings like ants (Compared to Scale 1, it's a damage decrease of 8 and damage increase of 8, meaning a bashing attack would fly off the charts), but a Divinity 8 Oroboros would be able to squeeze into the chart (With an average size of 48, that makes them Scale 7. Their agg damage will be bashing, but they'd only take agg damage from the Kaiju's bashing attacks. If Godzilla decides to breathe fire, though... bye bye Oroboros!).<br /> <br /> There's always problems when the size ratings go through the roof... if we're going to have the Elders/Nidhoggr be as massive as this we'll need to supply structure to the mechanics or make it a narrative affair (When fighting something that big, you don't fight it as an entity but as individual parts, such as a leg or the head).<br /> <br /> <br /> On the matter of terminology, as I thought about it Zmeu is actually a better fit for the usurpers than it is for the Ancestors... perhaps we'll throw it in the slang for eastern European Oroboroi and leave the Ancestors as just <b>The Long</b> or <b>The Five</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  Typos, whoops 08-11-2014, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:50:46-07:00","id":225409,"title":"","content":"Two abilities come to mind for the Nidhoggr to have.<br /> <br /> 1. Mental Supremacy: All powers meant to influence or outright attack the mind simply fail. These are not beings that can be forced or intimidated. They are walking demigods with most having the history of control, and subjugation. They <i>can</i> be reasoned with and some can be persuaded to leave you alone but it's gonna take some digging in the Nidhoggr's history to even open up a conversation before it decides to crush you flat.<br /> <br /> 2. Heart Seeking: In the distant past, the Nidhoggr had offspring and mates who's hearts were plundered during the collapse where were later passed down to modern day Oroboroi. A Nidhoggr has a connection (abide a weak one) to a heart that used to belong to his/her mate and/or offspring. As a result, A Nidhoggr can lock on to a single Usurper and can trash a city looking for that person.<br /> <br /> The Nidhoggr doesn't know where exactly the Heart is but can follow an instinctual tugging which will eventually lead to it's prize.<br /> <br /> If the Usurper leaps across realms, the Nidhoggr's connection will lead to the closest doorway into that Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 08-11-2014, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T01:11:16-07:00","id":225743,"title":"","content":"Another problem with Kaiju, is that...what about Miasma? What about the secrecy of Oroboroi? Does a Kaiju have Miasma? How can they manage to be so unseen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T01:52:35-07:00","id":225763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=225743#post225743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another problem with Kaiju, is that...what about Miasma? What about the secrecy of Oroboroi? Does a Kaiju have Miasma? How can they manage to be so unseen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've thought about that earlier today and the solution is actually quite simple. Over the course of modern human history as we know it, the Nidhoggr come infrequently. Most of the time, they're asleep or in other realms and prior to humanity getting connected to the internet, communication was pretty damn hard (Lord knows how many primary sources have gone up in flames). A Egyptian town could be attacked, it's resident Oroboroi's heart torn asunder, and the Nidhoggr would vanish back into the sea before the rest of the empire would realize something was up. At best, they would chalk it up to bandits, a natural disaster, or even the Gods just getting pissed at them (ironically, the last wouldn't be too far off).<br /> <br /> To be completely honest, the destruction of Pompeii would make an great historical setting of where a Nidhoggr is waking from Mt Vesuvius and the residential Oroboroi have to deal with it.<br /> <br /> In short, a good reason why the Nidhoggr haven't been discovered/messed with is less having to do with the Miasma and more to do with the fact of the long periods (Centuries long) between both their attacks and the rest of the world learning about the town's destruction which in all honestly would be chalked up to a natural disaster of some sort.<br /> <br /> Though now the world is connect to the internet so I would guess that would only be a matter of time before a Nidhoggr awakens and heads to a major city.<br /> <br /> On that note, I would suspect San Fran would have a Nidhoggr buried within it's depths. The &quot;Big One&quot; is overdue after all.<br /> <br /> If secrecy was required of the Nidhoggr, I would think they are more than capable of shape shifting to a human form and managing an human organization but they aren't subtle creatures by nature. If they are planning secrecy, it would be isolating a town's communication network, shutting down the power, and then hunting the residential Oroboroi down in the guise of a natural disaster.<br /> <br /> edit- A more modern take would be the eruption at Mt Saint Helens in which a Nidhoggr awakened, killed everyone in the area, honed in on a Oroboro's heart who was caught in the blast, and then vanished. <br /> <br /> God only knows what lies in Yellowstone..<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 08-12-2014, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T09:36:50-07:00","id":226049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=225763#post225763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If secrecy was required of the Nidhoggr, I would think they are more than capable of shape shifting to a human form and managing an human organization but they aren't subtle creatures by nature. If they are planning secrecy, it would be isolating a town's communication network, shutting down the power, and then hunting the residential Oroboroi down in the guise of a natural disaster.<br /> <br /> edit- A more modern take would be the eruption at Mt Saint Helens in which a Nidhoggr awakened, killed everyone in the area, honed in on a Oroboro's heart who was caught in the blast, and then vanished.<br /> <br /> God only knows what lies in Yellowstone..</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Nidhoggr hide their movements in natural disasters. Hurricane Katrina and Hurricane Sandy? Nidhoggr attacks. Mortals in the region are too panicked with survival to notice the giant monster that is killing everybody, and the few that do are subjected to the Miasma, unable to convince others of their story. Unlike the Oroboroi, Nidhoggr have control of the Typhoon phenomenon (being actual dragons), so they can trigger these events as they approach to serve as a protective smokescreen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T10:47:55-07:00","id":226101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=222828#post222828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Deep Ones:</b> The Deep Ones, or dark bargainers, are essentially a grim prophecy of what will become of the Oroboroi once all of their reverence has turned to rot; they are the fate of fallen gods, clinging to existence by clinging to the warmth of other beings (by trading favors for organs). Deep Ones might have the ability to be an absolutely terrifying antagonist, the type of which Frogs was seeking, but at the moment they share much of the mechanics an Oroboros does and so they aren't particularly mysterious... at least in that sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Okay, you sold me. I think I was thrown by the name &quot;Deep Ones&quot;; something ripped straight from Lovecraft didn't gel very well with Dragon, in my mind. (I'd suggest a different name--Deep Ones carries certain connotations that don't quite fit with your vision for them, and I suspect that I wasn't the only one who got the wrong impression from the name--but I'm not entirely sure what it should be. The Forgotten, perhaps? The Empty Ones?) But the way you describe them is a brilliant counterpoint to the themes of the Oroboroi. Personally, I'd prefer their bargaining take the form of something different than organ-trading, but thematically similar--some kind of sacrifice that diminishes the bargainer and strengthens the &quot;Deep One&quot; in exchange for...whatever it is the vengeful remnants of forgotten gods can offer.<br /> <br /> Do they only bargain with Oroboroi, or could they potentially be a source of other antagonists? Like, maybe they undermine Provinces and foment discontent and rebellion by making bargains with a dragon's subjects: pushing them to think of what life could be like without an Oroboros tyrant, and offering them the power to make that vision a reality. At a price, of course...<br /> <br /> What can they offer that's so tempting an Oroboros might deal with them? How does the bargain strengthen them? What sorts of things can they do aside from the bargain, and how does this pose a danger to Oroboroi?<br /> <br /> Maybe the &quot;power&quot; they offer comes in the form of twisting the beneficiary into a monster reflective of the worst of their inner nature, like the Witches in <i><b>Puella Magi Madoka Magica</b></i><i>.</i> Perhaps whatever they take is representative of the beneficiary's better nature, so such a transformation reflects on the outside the twisted ruin that's been made of their soul. That jives well with the symbolic nature of the Treasury, and it could be seen as a twisted version of Ablutions...<br /> <br /> What do they look like? I don't think they should be particularly uniform in appearance, but there ought to be some common themes. If their bargain really does grant a twisted version of Ablutions, maybe that's the theme--it would fit with them being the remnants of beings similar to the Oroboroi. Not that they're draconic, but that, in the absence of the fear and reverence a god is due, their once-divine forms are twisted and warped, full of rot and corruption. Maybe the vitality they bargains for manifests as their forms becoming less polluted, less tainted, more whole, more coherent--but along bizarre aesthetics reflective of their complete alienation from the world that has forgotten them. They start off as impressionistic visions of corruption and decay and bleak emptiness like that of a corpse abandoned and left to rot, and become more Lovecraftian as they (re)gain definition and vitality.<br /> <br /> What do they take? Particularly defining memories? Wishes and aspirations? The victim's Virtue? Something more vague and ephemeral, like whatever metaphysical quality it is that makes someone's fear and reverence empowering to the Oroboroi? Identity/sense of self/self-definition? Something that leaves the victims empty and hollow in some mystical sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:33:49-07:00","id":226139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226101#post226101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Okay, you sold me. I think I was thrown by the name &quot;Deep Ones&quot;; something ripped straight from Lovecraft didn't gel very well with Dragon, in my mind. (I'd suggest a different name--Deep Ones carries certain connotations that don't quite fit with your vision for them, and I suspect that I wasn't the only one who got the wrong impression from the name--but I'm not entirely sure what it should be. The Forgotten, perhaps? The Empty Ones?) But the way you describe them is a brilliant counterpoint to the themes of the Oroboroi. Personally, I'd prefer their bargaining take the form of something different than organ-trading, but thematically similar--some kind of sacrifice that diminishes the bargainer and strengthens the &quot;Deep One&quot; in exchange for...whatever it is the vengeful remnants of forgotten gods can offer.<br /> <br /> What do they take? Particularly defining memories? Wishes and aspirations? The victim's Virtue? Something more vague and ephemeral, like whatever metaphysical quality it is that makes someone's fear and reverence empowering to the Oroboroi? Identity/sense of self/self-definition? Something that leaves the victims empty and hollow in some mystical sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>They could bargain for memories; I've got experience writing about memories lost through choice (Witches spend their own memories to bend reality in my literature) and it's an easy theme to explore (Especially with the &quot;Forgotten Glory&quot; aspect of Embers that was coupled with &quot;Divine Right&quot;). Characters might willingly part with memories that are painful, not realizing that all experiences, including the bad ones, serve as the foundation of personality. The prospect of parting with painful memories and gaining power in exchange is quite addictive, and by the time someone realizes they've fallen into the trap they're already too far down the rabbit hole to escape. They become no different than the bargainers, reaching for memories to try and reclaim the humanity they've thrown away. Devil May Cry 4 is also a good source for this kind of horror.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226101#post226101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they only bargain with Oroboroi, or could they potentially be a source of other antagonists? Like, maybe they undermine Provinces and foment discontent and rebellion by making bargains with a dragon's subjects: pushing them to think of what life could be like without an Oroboros tyrant, and offering them the power to make that vision a reality. At a price, of course...<br /> <br /> What can they offer that's so tempting an Oroboros might deal with them? How does the bargain strengthen them? What sorts of things can they do aside from the bargain, and how does this pose a danger to Oroboroi?<br /> <br /> Maybe the &quot;power&quot; they offer comes in the form of twisting the beneficiary into a monster reflective of the worst of their inner nature, like the Witches in <i><b>Puella Magi Madoka Magica</b></i><i>.</i> Perhaps whatever they take is representative of the beneficiary's better nature, so such a transformation reflects on the outside the twisted ruin that's been made of their soul. That jives well with the symbolic nature of the Treasury, and it could be seen as a twisted version of Ablutions...</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree that other entities, including mortals, should be just as vulnerable to a Forgotten's bargains (We'll stick with Forgotten until we come up with a better name, or we'll give them <b>Shayatin</b> and throw the ghuuls out).<br /> The bargains strengthen the Forgotten by giving them memories to anchor on to, even if they aren't their own memories. The Forgotten are essentially empty shells, any existence that they have is meaningless because it lacks permanence; their actions have no identity on which to anchor. So they collect the memories of others to form a new identity; monstrous and mutated though it may be.<br /> Ablutions specific to the Deep Ones didn't work as a mechanic, but perhaps the bargains are Ablutions themselves... maybe even Ablutions borrowed from the Forgotten's repertoire. Since they're hollow beings, the cold of pulling majesty from their soul corrupts the beneficiary's end of the arrangement, luring them into more bargains as it warps and distorts their own self-image.<br /> What if a Deep One breaks off a piece of its own body and implants it into the victim with which it makes a bargain? The result would be a permanently manifest Ablution (with dots equal to the extent of the memory sacrificed), but one that resembles the Deep One rather than the being's own personality? Might make a nice substitution for Grafts with the whole Body Horror angle... we could even have them BE Grafts and describe the bargains with merit dots.<br /> I'm not sure if such Ablutions would contribute to Degree of Divinity, or if they'd just be mutated limbs like Nightmare from Soul Calibur (Poor Siegfried, don't you know you shouldn't touch Soul Edge?!).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226101#post226101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do they look like? I don't think they should be particularly uniform in appearance, but there ought to be some common themes. If their bargain really does grant a twisted version of Ablutions, maybe that's the theme--it would fit with them being the remnants of beings similar to the Oroboroi. Not that they're draconic, but that, in the absence of the fear and reverence a god is due, their once-divine forms are twisted and warped, full of rot and corruption. Maybe the vitality they bargains for manifests as their forms becoming less polluted, less tainted, more whole, more coherent--but along bizarre aesthetics reflective of their complete alienation from the world that has forgotten them. They start off as impressionistic visions of corruption and decay and bleak emptiness like that of a corpse abandoned and left to rot, and become more Lovecraftian as they (re)gain definition and vitality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deep Ones appeared in an aquatic sense was to emphasize the brine and shiver of their state; they are perpetually icy lifeforms and fish tend to portray such quite well. We can easily rewrite the Forgotten to have any manner of visage, including a wildly variable one (I was actually picturing an amalgam of fish morphology just as a dragon is an amalgam of reptile morphology). I like that making bargains makes them more whole, more alive, and yet more bizarre... it also gives the Storyteller a way to visually distinguish a successful bargainer from a failed bargainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:09:58-07:00","id":226266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226139#post226139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could bargain for memories; I've got experience writing about memories lost through choice (Witches spend their own memories to bend reality in my literature) and it's an easy theme to explore (Especially with the &quot;Forgotten Glory&quot; aspect of Embers that was coupled with &quot;Divine Right&quot;). Characters might willingly part with memories that are painful, not realizing that all experiences, including the bad ones, serve as the foundation of personality. The prospect of parting with painful memories and gaining power in exchange is quite addictive, and by the time someone realizes they've fallen into the trap they're already too far down the rabbit hole to escape. They become no different than the bargainers, reaching for memories to try and reclaim the humanity they've thrown away. Devil May Cry 4 is also a good source for this kind of horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Perhaps memory is only one of the sorts of things they can take? I think that what they take should be more of a symbol for what they're really taking, that whether it's memory or emotion or Breath or soul or senses or some vague &quot;life force&quot; that's being bargained for, what they're really taking is...identity, vitality, self-determination, strength, I'm not sure what word I want. The Forgotten are rotting corpses of what they used to be; they take the things that a person has that make them a <i>person</i>, not a corpse or an automaton. The fire of life, that makes what has it a being that <i>acts</i>, instead of an object that <i>is acted upon</i>. The flame that casts the shadows, instead of the shadows cast or the wall they are cast upon.<br /> <br /> Experience, perhaps. Experience of the world, the ability <i>to</i> experience the world, to see and touch and think and feel and want and judge and act. To leave a mark on the world. To <i>live</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm taking a lot of cues from the Actuals in Nobilis, come to think of it. For instance, I think this passage does a good job of getting across the essential <i>feel</i> of the Forgotten and what it is they lack, what it means that they're empty and hollow:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobilis: the Essentials: Field Guide to the Powers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are the soulless forerunners of the True Gods -- the movement that is like life, before it learned to live; the thinking that is like personhood, before it learned to be people. They are the dead things that invented life.<br /> <br /> They are born hollow; they are empty...<br /> <br /> ...Alone they were lifeless. They were as meaningless words spoken from nothing to nothing to no purpose. They were as models without the concept of referents. They were the dead that moved...<br /> <br /> ...The Actuals are creautres of straight white limbs, pillars of ivory; the writhing, wriggling presence of impossibility. The breath that isn't breath, membranes of clear substance, and the jittering of moments fit incompletely into Time. They are mechanical worms and insects that writhe together in the endless dark of their blindness, their deafness, their inability to touch or smell or taste or know. They strive a meaningless striving to consume, to grow, and most of all to <b><i>wake</i></b><i>...<br /> <br /> ...</i>Their bodies in our world are interpreted forms; they make no biological sense. Often they make some mythical sense -- thornbush-creatures, or creatures made from spreading blankets of needle-like spines, or protoplasm, or creatures of endlessly branching wires -- but they may also be pure mandalas of flesh...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226139#post226139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree that other entities, including mortals, should be just as vulnerable to a Forgotten's bargains (We'll stick with Forgotten until we come up with a better name, or we'll give them <b>Shayatin</b> and throw the ghuuls out).</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Shayatin is the &quot;proper&quot; name for them, and the Forgotten and the Empty Ones are common sobriquets? Like how the Strix are also called the Owls and the Nemeses and the Birds of Dis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226139#post226139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bargains strengthen the Forgotten by giving them memories to anchor on to, even if they aren't their own memories. The Forgotten are essentially empty shells, any existence that they have is meaningless because it lacks permanence; their actions have no identity on which to anchor. So they collect the memories of others to form a new identity; monstrous and mutated though it may be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <i>Yeessss. </i>I really, <i>really</i> like what's starting to take shape here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226139#post226139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ablutions specific to the Deep Ones didn't work as a mechanic, but perhaps the bargains are Ablutions themselves... maybe even Ablutions borrowed from the Forgotten's repertoire. Since they're hollow beings, the cold of pulling majesty from their soul corrupts the beneficiary's end of the arrangement, luring them into more bargains as it warps and distorts their own self-image.<br /> What if a Deep One breaks off a piece of its own body and implants it into the victim with which it makes a bargain? The result would be a permanently manifest Ablution (with dots equal to the extent of the memory sacrificed), but one that resembles the Deep One rather than the being's own personality? Might make a nice substitution for Grafts with the whole Body Horror angle... we could even have them BE Grafts and describe the bargains with merit dots.<br /> I'm not sure if such Ablutions would contribute to Degree of Divinity, or if they'd just be mutated limbs like Nightmare from Soul Calibur (Poor Siegfried, don't you know you shouldn't touch Soul Edge?!).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they should use the same mechanics as Ablutions, but I do think they should be conceptually similar, in that they're a physical transformation that reflects the person transformed in some way. But where Ablutions have a feel of burning away the mortal dross to express the god-beast-king within, the powers granted by the Forgotten feel more like...like someone's inner self, their spirit, their <i>soul </i>has gone so horribly, viscerally <i>wrong</i> that their body twists and warps to match.<br /> <br /> For this reason, I don't think they should be grafted on. It should be like when Palpatine's face finally twists into that of the Emperor from the original trilogy. It should be like when Tetsuo's mutations finally go completely out of control in <i>Akira</i>. It should be like when Zemus's poisonous hate coalesces into Zeromus.<br /> <br /> I also think that maybe Forgotten-granted transformations can get a bit more abstract and mystical than Ablutions--to compare them to the powers of Oroboroi, maybe they sort of blur the line between Edicts and Ablutions. Sometimes there's no direct connection between the physical trait and the power it grants: the physical transformation symbolizes an abstract power, like an empty dark hole in the chest for a transformed that can drain Breath or Willpower or &quot;life energy&quot;, or weirdly twisted limbs on one who can warp space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":743,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","user":"Exploding Frogs","date":". 08-12-2014, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T14:02:13-07:00","id":226338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They could bargain for memories; I've got experience writing about memories lost through choice (Witches spend their own memories to bend reality in my literature) </div> </div> </div>Reference, please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T15:26:36-07:00","id":226436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226338#post226338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reference, please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My pulp (as in cheap paperback, not gritty mystery) Sword and Sorcery series <b>Pocket Star</b>. Each of the three books in the series touches on Witchcraft in some way (as opposed to the tamer magic of Sorcery), though the one that supplies the most definition is <b>Tales of My Brother</b>. Unfortunately as it is the first book I ever published it suffers some significant &quot;greenhorn&quot; flaws (which I am working on a rewrite to fix, though admittedly progress is slow). The strongest book in the series is <b>Flowers for Isolda</b>, admittedly because it is the latest, but that book has a particularly dark plot and it's a little heavy to start with. So I recommend that--if you're interested--you should look into <b>Empty Moon</b>, which you can find on Amazon.com.<br /> I highly recommend looking inside the book with the preview option before you decide you want to buy, or reading the first chapter for free <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/walrustuskpublications/empty-moon\" target=\"_blank\">on my sad and neglected blog</a>. There isn't a whole lot of witchcraft in the first chapter (except for Helru, but he will prove entirely mysterious until late in the book).<br /> ...And I've swung completely off topic. Sorry about that.<br /> EDIT: Removed link to Amazon.com, this is a discussion about <b>Dragon</b>, not an advertisement platform! Shame on me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=226266#post226266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Perhaps memory is only one of the sorts of things they can take? I think that what they take should be more of a symbol for what they're really taking, that whether it's memory or emotion or Breath or soul or senses or some vague &quot;life force&quot; that's being bargained for, what they're really taking is...identity, vitality, self-determination, strength, I'm not sure what word I want. The Forgotten are rotting corpses of what they used to be; they take the things that a person has that make them a <i>person</i>, not a corpse or an automaton. The fire of life, that makes what has it a being that <i>acts</i>, instead of an object that <i>is acted upon</i>. The flame that casts the shadows, instead of the shadows cast or the wall they are cast upon.<br /> Experience, perhaps. Experience of the world, the ability <i>to</i> experience the world, to see and touch and think and feel and want and judge and act. To leave a mark on the world. To <i>live</i>.<br /> EDIT: I'm taking a lot of cues from the Actuals in Nobilis, come to think of it. For instance, I think this passage does a good job of getting across the essential <i>feel</i> of the Forgotten and what it is they lack, what it means that they're empty and hollow:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you have exactly captured what I'm picturing here! Now we just need to work out a way to explain this in our own words for the document.<br /> And yeah, Shayatin is as proper as Oroboros is for the usurpers; in context Forgotten or the Empty Ones are viable pronouns to describe them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they should use the same mechanics as Ablutions, but I do think they should be conceptually similar, in that they're a physical transformation that reflects the person transformed in some way. But where Ablutions have a feel of burning away the mortal dross to express the god-beast-king within, the powers granted by the Forgotten feel more like...like someone's inner self, their spirit, their <i>soul </i>has gone so horribly, viscerally <i>wrong</i> that their body twists and warps to match.<br /> <br /> For this reason, I don't think they should be grafted on. It should be like when Palpatine's face finally twists into that of the Emperor from the original trilogy. It should be like when Tetsuo's mutations finally go completely out of control in <i>Akira</i>. It should be like when Zemus's poisonous hate coalesces into Zeromus.<br /> <br /> I also think that maybe Forgotten-granted transformations can get a bit more abstract and mystical than Ablutions--to compare them to the powers of Oroboroi, maybe they sort of blur the line between Edicts and Ablutions. Sometimes there's no direct connection between the physical trait and the power it grants: the physical transformation symbolizes an abstract power, like an empty dark hole in the chest for a transformed that can drain Breath or Willpower or &quot;life energy&quot;, or weirdly twisted limbs on one who can warp space.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... dread powers? I guess we could define a list of features that the bargaining mortal/Oroboros can acquire from a bargain and then let the Storyteller mix and match them based on what the mortal/Oroboros parts with. For example, the list might include:<ul><li>Steal Health</li> <li>Steal Breath</li> <li>Steal Willpower</li> <li>Simulate Ablution</li> <li>Simulate Edict Law</li> <li>Simulate Weapon w/combat feature (Like Deadly Wound)</li> <li>Something else...</li> </ul>For example, perhaps a bargain gives the mortal/Oroboros three tendrils on the palm of her left hand. When she grasps the head of another being with these tendrils, they steal 2 Willpower and trigger the Truce Law of Assembly at Effect Rating 1 (And ONLY that Law; the tendrils are the result of a class 3 bargain).<br /> Or am I being too specific with this? Do the bargains need to have hard mechanics or should they remain aloof?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I follow you on the whole &quot;Darkness within&quot;. Since that's a primary component of the low-perception end of the Treasury (Close to the Daylight world), it dovetails well with the rest of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":"08-12-2014, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T19:31:02-07:00","id":226709,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, the concept of the Internet &amp; other forms of globalization, (and more importantly the reflections thereof in the Treasury), create more connections for the <b>Nidhoggr</b> to follow.<br /> Hence why they would start waking up more often now. There is simply more ways to the Hearts in the minds of the people.<br /> <br /> And every Heart lost, connection severed, throne/dominion/province fallen pushes the Nidhoggr away from the Daylight world...and one step closer to being truely Empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T12:53:48-07:00","id":227269,"title":"","content":"Okay, so to recap:<br /> <br /> We've got two leading antagonists at the moment, the <b>Nidhoggr</b> and the <b>Shayatin</b>. Here's a summary of what we've discussed about each.<br /> <br /> <b>Nidhoggr</b><br /> Nidhoggr, or the Elders, are natural-born dragons that survived the usurpation of the Oroboroi by fleeing to the corners of the world and the corners of reality (the ocean floors and the depths of the Treasury). They are giant, they are powerful, and they are PISSED! Nidhoggr have one goal: to reclaim the stolen Hearts of their relatives, and they even possess the ability to sense such Hearts from great distance. When seeking the heart of a relative, a Nidhoggr gains +3 to the Heartbeat perception and may sense the Heart even from beyond the confines of the Oroboros' lair.<br /> Nidhoggr attack like any Kaiju would, by knocking down buildings and generally squishing everything in their path. As natural-born dragons they are completely in control of the Typhoon effect and use it to their advantage by hiding their actions under the veil of natural disasters. Any humans who happen to notice them during the torrential storms or terrible eruptions are subject to the Miasma just as if they had witnessed an Oroboros; no one will believe their story.<br /> A sufficiently powerful Oroboros might be able to do battle with a Nidhoggr, but they are usually too large to confront directly. These terrifying antediluvian beasts need to be attack en masse if there is any hope of driving them back to the corners they crawled out from.<br /> <br /> <b>Shayatin</b><br /> Shayatin, or the Forgotten, are beings abandoned by reality, clinging to their last tethers of warmth that grant them meaning. Lacking memory and personality they are little more than objects to be tread upon by the world around them. But the Shayatin desire form, desire an identity on which they may anchor meaning to their actions. They are filled with the dark power of void and are willing to trade this darkness for the shining treasure of <i>potential</i>.<br /> It is believed by the Oroboroi in particular that the Shayatin were once great gods as the dragons are themselves, but their pursuit of power stripped away everything that defined them until they were little more than empty husks, squirming like amoeba in the vast expanses of the Treasury. In this way they are beings worthy of pity; a grand divinity reduced to a bottom feeder by hubris. However, Shayatin are rarely satisfied with their position.<br /> When a Shayatin makes a bargain with another being (usually a mortal or an Oroboros), it offers to unlock the power of that being's own darkness in exchange for a piece of their reality: a sense, a memory, a defining event in their past... anything the Shayatin might use to construct a new identity. The bargaining being gains the malevolent might of their own darkest desires, while the Shayatin gains one more piece of warmth it may use to cobble together a viable identity. As a Shayatin makes bargains it receives form as payment, filling its empty skin with ideas and limbs until it is a veritable horror of form and rage. These beings are never satisfied, however; no matter the number of bargains they make they always desire more form, more identity to fill the gaps in their perforated soul. Any who encounters one of these beings must beware, lest they too fall to the same empty fate.<br /> An empty Shayatin has much power to offer, but is relatively easy to bargain with. As the Forgotten collects more identity they become increasingly talented negotiators, demanding more and more for less. Sufficiently filled Forgotten may even simply take what they want by force.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think these two antagonists are awesome, and they may be enough to suit the core book. Still, do you think we need one more thorough antagonist? Other than humans, of course, but I'll discuss dragonslaying later [including the fabrication of an Ascalon with which a mortal might kill an Oroboros].<br /> <br /> If not, we can move on to the next item on the list, B-Splats. I'll wait to see what other people have to say on our antagonists and then I'll summarize the B-Splats we've come up with to date, just as I did with the Antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T13:58:31-07:00","id":227323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=227269#post227269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think these two antagonists are awesome, and they may be enough to suit the core book. Still, do you think we need one more thorough antagonist? Other than humans, of course, but I'll discuss dragonslaying later [including the fabrication of an Ascalon with which a mortal might kill an Oroboros].</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not.<br /> <br /> The Elders fill the void of &quot;There's a storm coming&quot; part of a chronicle which are basically plot devices unto themselves while the Forgotten Ones fill the need of &quot;miscreants and rebels&quot; to a point.<br /> <br /> However, I kinda feel like there is a niche missing. an &quot;antagonist&quot; who isn't an antagonist per say but is much akin to how Werewolf packs treat spirits.<br /> <br /> An non-dragon example would be the game Tropico where one can (or simply ignore) political factions from environmentalists to religious to loyalists.<br /> <br /> The idea is that leaders come to you for issues/demand to be solved and you can proceed to work to their request (and gain their support), or simply ignore them and let them get angry and eventually rebel if they get pissed off enough which then proceed to become antagonists unto themselves.<br /> <br /> However, looking at this, I kinda get the feel that this is leaning towards Vampire's territory a bit too much and since these are going to be almost always human, I think we can save this discussion for later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 08-13-2014, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T13:03:25-07:00","id":228400,"title":"","content":"Given the lack of conv, I would say to move on to B-splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T13:45:29-07:00","id":228443,"title":"","content":"Well, what you were describing made me picture other Dragons, actually, before I realized you were talking about human beings. With another dragon, you either compromise by forming a Den with them or you risk them stealing your Assets when they inevitably overlap. With mortals, though, you keep them happy or they revolt, damaging your assets in the process. Both are worth exploring in the Storytelling and Antagonists chapter, but I don't think we need another supernatural entity to fill that slot, at least for the core book.<br /> <br /> As for the B-Splats, we currently have four:<br /> <br /> <b>Dragonborn:</b> Akin to wolf-blooded, the Dragonborn are mortals with Oroboroi heritage, be it parents, grandparents, or great-grandparents (though no further than that, the usurper potency does not last many generations severed from its power source). Dragonborn start with some extra talent as described in the merit and they benefit from the prospect of gaining higher Furnace upon their coronation (based on a roll of the merit dots, again as described in the merit). They are otherwise normal human beings.<br /> <br /> <b>Brood-Bonded:</b> Similar to a Vampire's Ghoul, a Brood-Bonded consumes a piece of the Oroboros Heart and gains the ability to learn Ablutions that his dragon benefactor knows (or rather, he learns how to borrow Ablutions from her). Being Brood-Bonded will extend the mortal's lifespan but also spells death (or at least serious medical complication) if the Heart changes owners. Oroboroi that undertake the ritual share degeneration/breaking points with their bonded mortal.<br /> <br /> <b>Pilot Lights:</b> Pilot Lights are just like Brood-Bonded except all of the drawbacks have been removed; they are born with one ninth of a dragon Heart in their body. As written, they require the joining of two True Heart Oroboroi (which may not be in the game come the closure of the third development phase, so if we're keeping them we may need alternate criteria for the creation of a Pilot Light). The only major drawback a Pilot Light faces is that some dragons wish to cut them up and use their Heart fragments to cobble together a new Heart. I'll discuss ideas for this B-Splat later in the post.<br /> <br /> <b>Spartoi:</b> Spartoi are sown men, they spring into being when a dragon plants one of her teeth as if it were a seed. Spartoi have above-average talents and can make use of Edicts; they also serve as a mouthpiece through which their creating Oroboros may proclaim her own Edicts. Outside that, they spring to life fully grown and thus have no credentials, credit rating, social security number, or identity of any sort. Physically, Spartoi are close clones of their creator.<br /> Alternatively, the Spartoi can be taken more figuratively (as proposed by Frogs), sown into the 'soil' of an expectant mother to bless the child with draconic talent. I'll discuss ideas for this B-Splat later in the post.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so we've got four B-Splats and most game lines only have one, and some of them supply more value to the game than others. Time for some constructive pruning.<br /> Starting with the <b>Spartoi</b>, I know exactly why they didn't turn out well in the CIJ half-book. I was trying to make an &quot;Edict&quot; equivalent to the Brood-Bonded, but it just doesn't work in practice. Edicts are significantly more powerful than Ablutions are, and their thematic stance as a dragon's stubbornness bending reality should not extend to third parties (Dark Heroes are of course the exception, but let's not get into that now). The more I thought about them as an entity the more I realized THEY are actually just another form of Dragonborn. In fact, all Dragonborn are just the result of a dragon planting a piece in soil (yes, it's an uncomfortable metaphor, but it's a common one in Greek mythology). To that end, I propose that the Dragonborn merit absorb the Spartoi's origins (but not its functions, as it is mechanically unbalanced) as a possible explanation for owning the Dragonborn merit (That is, a Dragonborn could be the result of a human-Oroboros union or could be completely unrelated to the Oroboros, her power planted within a mother before the child was born). We could call the merit Spartoi (to create a little distance from TESV Skyrim) and we might even keep the 'proclaiming Edicts through the child' option as a drawback to characters taking this merit.<br /> <br /> As for the <b>Pilot Lights</b>, they're just so... well, overpowered. I was thinking about it, and perhaps Pilot Lights should be the result of combining the Dragonborn and Brood-Bonded merits: if a character uses all seven of their starting dots to purchase Brood-Bonded 5 and Dragonborn 2, they are actually a Pilot Light, born with a fragment of a dragon Heart and possessing the ability to learn and manifest some Ablutions. This change has several advantages: first it lets us rate Pilot Light at a much higher Merit rating than the system usually allows, second it eliminates the need for True Heart Oroboroi to be involved in the creation of a Pilot Light (They just happen sometimes from a dragon-human union or a Spartoi blessing), third it gives Players a motivation to actually conduct Spartoi blessings, and fourth it folds in some duplicate mechanics to save space in the second chapter.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, if we take those two points into consideration the number of B-Splats goes down from 4 to 2.5, with one being the 'kinfolk' style B and the other being the 'retainer leech' style B. Does anybody have any opinions to share on these? Is 2.5 Bs still too many? Or is it too few? I'm eager to hear the opinions of others on this matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T18:06:07-07:00","id":228607,"title":"","content":"That sounds significantly more streamlined and user friendly to me. I was thinking that we don't need 5 playable templates in a book devoted to 1.<br /> In other words, I completely approve.<br /> <br /> Pilot Lights in particular did not seem likely to survive 3Dev in their current form. True Hearts are starting to feel more and more like the kind of thing that would set off alarm bells. I might not tie them directly to Nidhoggr, but I can certainly see in setting rumours that if you stay 'True' too long you start to become Nidhoggr.<br /> <br /> But back on topic, GMC increased the number of merit dots available to starting characters to 10. So Dragonborn/Spartoi and Brood-Bonded would be more common in GMC compatible games and 'Pilot Lights' are smaller investments. Just food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T20:46:07-07:00","id":228701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=228607#post228607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pilot Lights in particular did not seem likely to survive 3Dev in their current form. True Hearts are starting to feel more and more like the kind of thing that would set off alarm bells. I might not tie them directly to Nidhoggr, but I can certainly see in setting rumours that if you stay 'True' too long you start to become Nidhoggr.</div> </div> </div> </div>A True Heart may become an &quot;Elder&quot; at rank 10 but they aren't Nidhoggr. Nidhoggrs are pissed because of the Collapse (both out of shame for their failure to uphold the Mandate and anger on humanity pillaging their offspring, friends, and the like).<br /> <br /> It would be a interesting rumor but has as much credibility as a modern day Quebecer being pissed at the British because the French lost the battle of Trafalgar.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T22:15:32-07:00","id":228784,"title":"","content":"I never said it was true, just that it would be interesting. What becomes of a True Heart doesn't matter in game as much as what people think becomes of a True Heart. If people think the Crown is failing, they will act in such a way that the Crown will fail. Perception in the eyes of the people can turn the tides of history. The Oroboroi should know this all too well.<br /> <br /> Which makes them repeating this mistake all the more delicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T22:25:48-07:00","id":228793,"title":"","content":"I hate to lay a penny on the tracks at this point, but I notice there's a bit of a thematic hole in Dragon's genetics:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dragon_(Beowulf)\" target=\"_blank\">Where the hell is Beowulf's final foe?</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T00:03:03-07:00","id":228849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=228793#post228793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to lay a penny on the tracks at this point, but I notice there's a bit of a thematic hole in Dragon's genetics:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dragon_(Beowulf)\" target=\"_blank\">Where the hell is Beowulf's final foe?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The real question comes into context of the fact that Beowulf was a king after he slew Grendel's Mother (which begs the question, did Beowulf consume her Heart?) and throws into question if the fight between Beowulf and the Dragon was simply nothing more than Usurper politics.<br /> <br /> And if they both died, what did Wiglaf do with the Hearts?<br /> <br /> <br /> edit: Found this picture while on Deviantart. Thought it might go well with high powered games.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://th05.deviantart.net/fs71/PRE/i/2014/217/f/2/new_tenant_by_themefinland-d7twlkd.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 08-15-2014, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T15:42:03-07:00","id":229641,"title":"","content":"I think 2.5 B-Splats is the way to go and I think your solution concerning pilot lights works well. I'll try to write up crimera this weekend which would round out the B-Splats to Dragonborn, Brood-mates, Pilot lights and Chrimera; with Chrimera being essentially animal Brood-mates. I think Chrimera should be a viable alternative to a human brood-mate but be quite alien despite being intelligent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:27:53-07:00","id":229685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=229641#post229641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 2.5 B-Splats is the way to go and I think your solution concerning pilot lights works well. I'll try to write up crimera this weekend which would round out the B-Splats to Dragonborn, Brood-mates, Pilot lights and Chrimera; with Chrimera being essentially animal Brood-mates. I think Chrimera should be a viable alternative to a human brood-mate but be quite alien despite being intelligent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for doing so. The thing that I was thinking about is how do we define the alien mindset of Dragonborn and the like. We've are basically already running wild with the &quot;Reptilians&quot; conspiracy myth. Add stories of coverups of mentally disturbed offspring of people in power (particularly after said offspring murders or engages in other crime) and you drama ripe for incorporation into Dragon.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T13:00:18-07:00","id":230458,"title":"","content":"@Satchel: Grendel's mother was probably an Oroboros, and so the dragon that Beowulf did battle with was probably a Nidhoggr (considering the overt damage it inflicted in its assault), based on Shock's interpretation. This might be an interesting topic to cite in literature inspirations, or maybe as flavor mythology somewhere in the manual (or both).<br /> <br /> I wasn't expecting the B-Splat discussion to go this smoothly, and short of clarifications on the Chimerae it looks like we're about done with that item. But, before moving on to the next problem ticket I want to take some time to discuss some fringe mechanisms in the Oroboroi condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Typhoon:</b> It was mentioned that Typhoon is inappropriate because when dragons are depicted as weather spirits they have control of this capacity. I was justifying the 'wild weather' as a strictly Oroboroi shortcoming, and now that we have official terminology I thought I would clarify.<br /> Nidhoggr can and do control the weather to their whim. In short, they may trigger a Typhoon effect (GMC hazardous environment) any time they please, at a rating likely based on their rank (But not equal to their rank, because even low-end Nidhoggr should be able to make reasonably dangerous weather phenomenon to cover their tracks). Conversely, the usurper Oroboroi control the weather subconsciously, almost making it a secondary backlash mechanic like Heartbeat. There are of course advantages for weather exploding when a usurper dragon gets into a rage, but its unpredictability is dangerous.<br /> I was trying to make Typhoon the Dragon equivalent of Frenzy: an Oroboros doesn't lose control of herself but rather the weather around her. Is there a better way to present this system to make that intention more clear? Perhaps the phenomenon should be severed from the Furnace mechanic. Any help with this would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Jade Allergy:</b> Frogs also mentioned that Jade is a pure substance and dragons should not be maimed by this substance. Again, this is a matter that is assisted by the clarification of terminology: Nidhoggr are not bothered by Jade in the slightest, but the usurpers are. I think if we explain that the act of stealing the Hearts in the first place contaminated the Oroboroi with the blood of treachery the Jade pill would be easier to swallow. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <b>Vomiting Up Organs versus Devouring:</b> Devouring the Hearts of other Oroboroi has consistently been one justification for increasing a character's Furnace. It's the easy button for growing power. The problem is, devouring doesn't actually SEEM like an easy button, because the normal way to grow Furnace was never clarified. I tried to fix this in the CIJ half-book by making standard Furnace growth a body and psychological horror; an Oroboros must rip out the very things that make her human in order to grow her divinity, or keep them at the cost of her species as she greedily snuffs out other dragons for power. In practice, though, Frogs is correct that such a system encourages roll-playing instead of role-playing. So we need an alternative. How do we present the idea that a dragon turning to Heart devouring is a means of avoiding hardship? I think the 'vomit up your mortal soul' thing is good, but we need a different way to present it in the manual.<br /> Maybe emotions aren't the way to go. Maybe it needs to be the same kind of loss someone making a bargain with the Forgotten would suffer?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry Shock, I can't use that image in the book for a few reasons: it doesn't have initials clearly visible on the piece, I don't know the artist's name, and I don't know if you got permission for its inclusion. Again, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  Cool image not making it into the manual 08-16-2014, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T13:23:44-07:00","id":230472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=230458#post230458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Sorry Shock, I can't use that image in the book for a few reasons: it doesn't have initials clearly visible on the piece, I don't know the artist's name, and I don't know if you got permission for its inclusion. Again, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a problem. I am mostly using it to hammer the concept of what a mortal feels while facing a high powered Dragon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T13:33:21-07:00","id":230481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=230458#post230458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vomiting Up Organs versus Devouring:</b> Devouring the Hearts of other Oroboroi has consistently been one justification for increasing a character's Furnace. It's the easy button for growing power. The problem is, devouring doesn't actually SEEM like an easy button, because the normal way to grow Furnace was never clarified. I tried to fix this in the CIJ half-book by making standard Furnace growth a body and psychological horror; an Oroboros must rip out the very things that make her human in order to grow her divinity, or keep them at the cost of her species as she greedily snuffs out other dragons for power. In practice, though, Frogs is correct that such a system encourages roll-playing instead of role-playing. So we need an alternative. How do we present the idea that a dragon turning to Heart devouring is a means of avoiding hardship? I think the 'vomit up your mortal soul' thing is good, but we need a different way to present it in the manual.<br /> Maybe emotions aren't the way to go. Maybe it needs to be the same kind of loss someone making a bargain with the Forgotten would suffer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the system writer a lot of other folks are, so I've been keeping quiet, but I would like to chime in here. Personally, I'm of the mind that a discount in experience cost, skipping training time altogether, and the role-play value of forever diminishing your species, should be enough to show it's an &quot;easy button,&quot; and I was not a fan of the organ-vomiting thing. It's the equivalent of using steroids instead of putting in more hours in the gym, or buying a degree from a diploma-mill instead of earning it at a respectable school. Giving in to your rage and tapping the dark side of the Force rather than practicing the discipline of a Jedi. You get your power quickly and easily, while another person gets similar or better results by putting in time and sweat.<br /> <br /> If you really think another cost beyond that to raise Furnace is needed, I could see two possible ways... either you're refining your divinity and thus growing more remote from ordinary humans (taking a penalty on social rolls as you have trouble connecting and others think you're just stuck up), or having to give up an Asset to fuel the fire. Consuming part of your Hoard, retreating from a Province and letting it lie fallow as you focus inward, the emotional wrench of letting a Maiden go...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T03:42:16-07:00","id":231263,"title":"","content":"Hey, i know ive never said anything before but I'd lean in favour of consuming your assets. Eating your hoard is easy, but adding your ideology to the sins list, stealing the maidens talent could work. Don't know how you would consume a province though. In terms of typhoon, it think it would work tied to honour: noble dragons are in control, while monstrous ones arent. On jade, I think the emphasing the whole not rightful owners would help. I never really got that impression from any of the books.<br /> EDIT: the artists name is themeFinland, btw","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-Failure is always an option<br /> roseerifnosi","edited":{"userid":115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/115-dahqueendiva","user":"DahQueenDiva","date":". 08-17-2014, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/115-dahqueendiva","name":"DahQueenDiva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T07:44:17-07:00","id":231494,"title":"","content":"Hey guy. Long time no see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T13:05:45-07:00","id":231893,"title":"","content":"Welcome back Demo!<br /> <br /> Okay, so consensus seems to be that Furnace growth should be tied to 'liquidating' Assets. I think this is excellent because it re-emphasizes the selfishness of a Devourer; they're eating the Hearts of other dragons because they can't bear to do away with their own Assets.<br /> <br /> I have a few follow-up questions before I start working this into the document:<br /> <br /> 1.) Should Asset loss to grow Furnace be a dot-by-dot matter or a binary All-or-Nothing sacrifice? Would a dragon be able to retreat slightly from her Province to pay the needs of her growing Furnace or would she need to intentionally dissolve the community?<br /> <br /> 2.) Should Asset loss have a specific number of dots required to raise Furnace? If so, should that requirement be the new Furnace rating attained? That is, to earn Furnace 3 without devouring a Heart an Oroboros must liquidate three dots of Assets?<br /> <br /> 3.) If Assets are lost through other means (death of a maiden by a third party, theft of Hoard), should the Oroboros still be able to grow Furnace through that loss? I'm leaning towards 'no' because the Oroboros must harvest the raw benefit of the Asset through its destruction (steal the talent of the maiden, collapse the Province, consume the Hoard, shred the Ideology).<br /> <br /> 4.) Should shredding Ideologies place them on the sin list as discussed? If so, it might make playing the game more interesting as Furnace grows, because the Oroboros effectively accumulates bans as she naturally grows her Furnace.<br /> Alternatively, should the dissolution of ANY Asset add a sin to the Mandate? For example, if an Oroboros steals the talent of her Maiden she can no longer interact with that maiden, such is a violation of her personal mandate. Mind, such would only work if Asset depletion is all-or-nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even just typing it out, it seems like All or Nothing sacrifice is the way to go, along with requiring a certain number of Asset dots lost to build the Furnace. This creates an interesting inversion for <b>Dragon</b> as compared to other lines: building Furnace the <i>standard</i> way results in more Energy per turn, but a LOWER maximum Energy (That is, until the dragon recovers from the loss with the pursuit of a new Asset... possibly one stolen from another Oroboros).<br /> <br /> <br /> Any further thoughts on this, or shall we move to the Treasury (IE the big, BIG thematic enchilada)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:05:21-07:00","id":231939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=231893#post231893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) Should Asset loss to grow Furnace be a dot-by-dot matter or a binary All-or-Nothing sacrifice? Would a dragon be able to retreat slightly from her Province to pay the needs of her growing Furnace or would she need to intentionally dissolve the community?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first part ties into part 2 of what you asked. The second part is a rather simple affair to answer: Dragons shouldn't be dissolving their community but rather have it be self sufficient long enough to get what she needs to get done so I favor &quot;slightly retreat&quot; option. After all, if things fall apart right after a Dragon stops being completely involved, it's a sign of weakness, not strength.<br /> <br /> But this would be more up to the players to do the cost/benefit analysis. Retreat now and risk looking weak in exchange for greater power, or hold on for a later time where things have calmed down enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=231893#post231893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.) Should Asset loss have a specific number of dots required to raise Furnace? If so, should that requirement be the new Furnace rating attained? That is, to earn Furnace 3 without devouring a Heart an Oroboros must liquidate three dots of Assets?</div> </div> </div> </div>My view is Asset loss is dot by dot analysis and a specific number of dots are needed to raise a Furnace to a new level. My rule current rule of thumb is that Asset Loss * 2 = your new Furnace level. so a Furnace level 1 would require 2 Assets to eat and Furnace level 4 would require 8. Time also needs to be factored in but I'm unsure how long of a period it should take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=231893#post231893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3.) If Assets are lost through other means (death of a maiden by a third party, theft of Hoard), should the Oroboros still be able to grow Furnace through that loss? I'm leaning towards 'no' because the Oroboros must harvest the raw benefit of the Asset through its destruction (steal the talent of the maiden, collapse the Province, consume the Hoard, shred the Ideology).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on my part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=231893#post231893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4.) Should shredding Ideologies place them on the sin list as discussed? If so, it might make playing the game more interesting as Furnace grows, because the Oroboros effectively accumulates bans as she naturally grows her Furnace.<br /> Alternatively, should the dissolution of ANY Asset add a sin to the Mandate? For example, if an Oroboros steals the talent of her Maiden she can no longer interact with that maiden, such is a violation of her personal mandate. Mind, such would only work if Asset depletion is all-or-nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be interesting. Of course some players might be annoyed with being &quot;locked&quot; into a Ideology but most games have consequences for leaving a group be it Tribe, or Court. <br /> <br /> An interesting way to set it up is that it's a violation of the Mandate for a Oroboros to consume his/her own Assets but it's perfectly fine to consume someone else's. Racks up the tension and paranoia. Of course, the Mandate would cover any and all Dragons within a Den. This is Dragon: the Embers, not Monopoly.<br /> <br /> As for All or Nothing loss, I do have some reservations about it (Mostly about salvaging dots but looking at it now, it seems like an easy thing for players to abuse) but I think we can go with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=231893#post231893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even just typing it out, it seems like All or Nothing sacrifice is the way to go, along with requiring a certain number of Asset dots lost to build the Furnace. This creates an interesting inversion for <b>Dragon</b> as compared to other lines: building Furnace the <i>standard</i> way results in more Energy per turn, but a LOWER maximum Energy (That is, until the dragon recovers from the loss with the pursuit of a new Asset... possibly one stolen from another Oroboros).<br /> <br /> <br /> Any further thoughts on this, or shall we move to the Treasury (IE the big, BIG thematic enchilada)?</div> </div> </div> </div>None right now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:30:59-07:00","id":232075,"title":"","content":"So, what I missed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T18:20:41-07:00","id":232174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=232075#post232075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot. We started in on developing the new Philosophies (Pandalfino wrote two great ones, FallenEco is working on a third, and we have two to go), I released a &quot;Christmas in July&quot; half-book with the GMC compatible Ablutions and Edicts (There's a link to it in the first post of the thread), I sort of blew my top, we settled down, and now we're straightening out the thematic elements of the game (Antagonists, B-Splats, Fringe Mechanics, Realms Invisible, and Supplied Mythology).<br /> <br /> <b>Quick overview of things that are different but not in the CIJ half-book:</b> the dragons of old are now called Nidhoggr to reduce confusion between them and the Oroboroi, and they present a seriously terrifying threat (they want the Hearts of their relatives back, and they attack under cover of natural disasters). Also, the Deep Ones are now called the Forgotten and their bargaining is much more existential (They're trying to capture the quantifiable definition of life to make themselves real). Pilot Lights are now the combination of having both the Dragonborn Merit and the Bond of Brood Merit, Dragonborn can also be created when an Oroboros blesses an expectant mother (they're called Spartoi in such an instance), Chimerae are animals subjected to the bond of Brood (Gravitas is working on that), and... Oh, the part in the CIJ about sacrificing organs to raise Furnace has been vetoed, we're going with Asset dissolution instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want to wait just a little longer before we move into the Treasury, just to make sure everybody has time to process what has been discussed so far and put in their thoughts. If you want to jump in on the thematic discussions, I recommend starting on Page 7 and reading through... this post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T03:02:09-07:00","id":232631,"title":"","content":"This might be a bit newbie, but what <i>is</i> the treasury? I get that it reflects the worth of stuff, but I'm not sure what purpose it serves. Can you eat stuff in it for breath? How do changes to one realm change the other? I'm kinda imagining smaug's ocean of golden, but across the whole world, with golden, jewel incrusted living idols to represent big businesses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-Failure is always an option<br /> roseerifnosi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/115-dahqueendiva","name":"DahQueenDiva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T10:13:09-07:00","id":232965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=232174#post232174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot. We started in on developing the new Philosophies (Pandalfino wrote two great ones, FallenEco is working on a third, and we have two to go), I released a &quot;Christmas in July&quot; half-book with the GMC compatible Ablutions and Edicts (There's a link to it in the first post of the thread), I sort of blew my top, we settled down, and now we're straightening out the thematic elements of the game (Antagonists, B-Splats, Fringe Mechanics, Realms Invisible, and Supplied Mythology).<br /> <br /> <b>Quick overview of things that are different but not in the CIJ half-book:</b> the dragons of old are now called Nidhoggr to reduce confusion between them and the Oroboroi, and they present a seriously terrifying threat (they want the Hearts of their relatives back, and they attack under cover of natural disasters). Also, the Deep Ones are now called the Forgotten and their bargaining is much more existential (They're trying to capture the quantifiable definition of life to make themselves real). Pilot Lights are now the combination of having both the Dragonborn Merit and the Bond of Brood Merit, Dragonborn can also be created when an Oroboros blesses an expectant mother (they're called Spartoi in such an instance), Chimerae are animals subjected to the bond of Brood (Gravitas is working on that), and... Oh, the part in the CIJ about sacrificing organs to raise Furnace has been vetoed, we're going with Asset dissolution instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want to wait just a little longer before we move into the Treasury, just to make sure everybody has time to process what has been discussed so far and put in their thoughts. If you want to jump in on the thematic discussions, I recommend starting on Page 7 and reading through... this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. That's quite a bit. Oh, careful with the Dragonborn. It's the recent DnD race.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:04:13-07:00","id":233471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DahQueenDiva</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=232631#post232631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be a bit newbie, but what <i>is</i> the treasury? I get that it reflects the worth of stuff, but I'm not sure what purpose it serves. Can you eat stuff in it for breath? How do changes to one realm change the other? I'm kinda imagining smaug's ocean of golden, but across the whole world, with golden, jewel incrusted living idols to represent big businesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a newb question at all; we're still working out what exactly the Treasury will entail. In fact, that's the next item on the docket for thematic adjustment.<br /> <br /> Here's what we have so far, and keep in mind most of this is flexible at this point:<br /> <br /> <b>The Treasury:</b> The Treasury, or rather the soul of the world, is a state of non-euclidean perception and reality that all dragons (from the Longs and Nidhoggr to the usurper Oroboroi) may enter by circling anticlockwise like a low-pressure system. In essence, circling lightens the soul, allowing it to drift into this higher perception.<br /> How the Treasury appears varies greatly by how much a dragon lightens her soul, and if she dives more deeply than her Heart can handle the light and power of this realm will burn her like fire.<br /> On its shallowest end, the Treasury reveals the inherent value of material goods (Assets), much like you have described; the world becomes awash in piles of riches. A dragon sees locations and people by how much she might benefit from taking them as Assets; Maidens wear apparel indicative of the kind of talent they might muster, the quality of a structure reflects its utmost potential (rather than its current state of dilapidation). If you picture a medieval filter painting over the standard reality that pretty much sums up the shallows.<br /> Go a little deeper and mortals start depicting personality traits physically across their body. At this state the dragon still maintains local scope but interacts with the surface thoughts of beings rather than their direct consciousness. Time is compressed here; a day's worth of interaction will translate to a single scene when the dragon returns from the Treasury. The world also twists; buildings begin to represent the organizations that are housed within them. Picture the Dark World from <u>A Link to the Past</u>, that was big inspiration for me for this depth.<br /> Even deeper and the individuals begin to vanish, amalgamating into massive \u2018idols\u2019 that represent the organizations in which they are involved. Space begins to warp at this perception; buildings that were separated by great geographic distance but closely related by ties of business and nepotism might be within walking distance of each other at this level of perception, or perhaps even connected by flesh and sinew. Walls and rivers begin to bleed, lightning courses through the air, and the sky takes on the appearance of myocardial tissue as a dragon at this perception is actually within the world Heart. At this stage, the dragon might accumulate months of interactions which compress to a single scene when returning from the Treasury. Killing one of these great Idols (Many of which are Kaiju-grade size, by the way) could very will shatter the organizations they represent).<br /> <br /> These time compressions are a peculiar thing; when the dragon returns the actions she has taken will not have yet occurred, but will play out over the days and months to follow. For this reason, a dragon may use the Treasury to ensure everything is in place to her advantage in the immediate future.<br /> <i>Alternatively, the time compressions might work retroactively, this is a key point I\u2019d like to discuss as we elaborate on the Treasury</i>.<br /> <br /> A few key notes: At the deepest depths of the Treasury, an Oroboros might encounter the Great Wyrm, which is the embodiment of the Oroboroi. Let\u2019s just say it\u2019s not a good idea to pick a fight with this thing. On the other end is Saint George, the greatest Dragonslayer, who is an embodiment of the humanity the Oroboroi cling to. These two unstoppable forces are in constant conflict and it\u2019s generally a bad idea to get caught in the crossfire.<br /> Also, Oroboroi who die awaken in the deepest depths of the Treasury and must find ways to \u2018leaden\u2019 their soul so they might return to their earthbound perception. This often involves collecting \u2018sparks\u2019 (name tentative) to restart their corporeal heartbeat so that they can regenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T02:17:08-07:00","id":233974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=233471#post233471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few key notes: At the deepest depths of the Treasury, an Oroboros might encounter the Great Wyrm, which is the embodiment of the Oroboroi. Let\u2019s just say it\u2019s not a good idea to pick a fight with this thing. On the other end is Saint George, the greatest Dragonslayer, who is an embodiment of the humanity the Oroboroi cling to. These two unstoppable forces are in constant conflict and it\u2019s generally a bad idea to get caught in the crossfire..</div> </div> </div> </div>Saint George seems a bit too westernized for a manifestation of an abstract concept that is supposed to encompass all of humanity. Granted, the icon of western dragon slaying should be down but shouldn't that much as the focus.<br /> <br /> as for general feel, I like it but I feel it's missing something. Following our current line of ideas from Asian cultures, they place extremely high reverence for ancestors and rule of law (Chinese legalism and Confucianism being it's apex in my limited understanding) so this is something that the Treasury needs to reflect. Granted the Oroboros don't revere the Nidhoggr and vice versa but it's the Nidhoggr who largely fucked up in the first place. The Treasury, at it's lowest depth, should show how the universe worked when Dragons followed the Mandate while at the same time, how fucked up it currently because of past and current generations of Dragons haven't been doing their jobs. <br /> <br /> <br /> An metaphor would be akin to finding a chest of gold within a fleet of sunken spanish galleons. A single relic within the vast crumbling tomb complex. An ember of divine right against the backdrop of fading glory.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:21:22-07:00","id":234120,"title":"","content":"If lower depths represent both a pre-collapse existence and material corporations etc, then the heart could be a place of possibility, where ideas exist in a pure state and actions have a domino effect. Its the place where the original oroboroi came from, so they might have left a mark. Nidhoggr slumber on top of the idols of great businesses. In contrast, its surrounded by an infinite wasteland, devoid of any chance to change or advance. The size of the heart might be tied to the dragons: with each destroyed heart it shrinks and dims","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-Failure is always an option<br /> roseerifnosi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/115-dahqueendiva","name":"DahQueenDiva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T20:10:58-07:00","id":236118,"title":"","content":"Hello a question if you don't mind,but what does Embers mean, what does it mean to the oroboros. A couple of examples Lost for changelings is what they call themselves because they just escaped a mad realm with even madder gods to a world no longer theirs for most likely a copy cat has taken their place and if not their family's probably thinks them as dead and most is at the tipping point to insanity. Awakening for mages is not only the process of a mortal becoming a Mage it is when ones soul see's through the lie and see's the supernal truths. Curse for mummies is their condition, it is that they have to be undead slaves to dark gods for the rest of time, most of the Arisen would call that heresy but that's mostly because most of them barely have enough memory to remember their names. And Requiem to vampires is simply their Damnation, the hunger for blood, the never seeing daylight again, to see everything that you love and care fore rot and decay to dust and ash when you become a monster. Anyway sorry for rambling but again I ask you,what does Embers mean, what does it mean to the dragons<br /> <br /> P.S sorry for bad grammar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 08-20-2014, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T20:56:30-07:00","id":236144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236118#post236118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello a question if you don't mind,but what does Embers mean, what does it mean to the oroboros. A couple of examples Lost for changelings is what they call themselves because they just escaped a mad realm with even madder gods to a world no longer theirs for most likely a copy cat has taken their place and if not their family's probably thinks them as dead and most is at the tipping point to insanity. Awakening for mages is not only the process of a mortal becoming a Mage it is when ones soul see's through the lie and see's the supernal truths. Curse for mummies is their condition, it is that they have to be undead slaves to dark gods for the rest of time, most of the Arisen would call that heresy but that's mostly because most of them barely have enough memory to remember their names. And Requiem to vampires is simply their Damnation, the hunger for blood, the never seeing daylight again, to see everything that you love and care fore rot and decay to dust and ash when you become a monster. Anyway sorry for rambling but again I ask you,what does Embers mean, what does it mean to the dragons<br /> <br /> P.S sorry for bad grammar</div> </div> </div> </div>Embers is a state of being for the Usurpers as a whole. I figure most would try to avoid the issue in casual conversation as it reminds them of their race's precarious existence but it does come up (usually when a Heart is destroyed but on the rare occurrence where one is created/recovered) and usually invoked in times of deep significance where an event involves most (if not all) of the Dragons in an area. Negative events such as another splat getting tired of their shit and is hell bent on genocide of the species (not just aiding a mortal to take their place but Genocide.), Nidhoggr awakening, and the such will get the motif dropped but also positive events. A long lost heart being discovered, a new heart being created, the wasteland of the Treasury being pushed back enough to be noticed. Dragons may chew and nip at the said newcomer but in their hearts and souls, they celebrate the fact that one more is among them.<br /> <br /> In short, Embers is both a negative and positive term for Dragons but most of all, a very significant one. Negative because it implies that their race is on the threshold of getting snuffed out. Positive because Embers means there is still fire left. There still is hope to reignite the flame. They aren't all gone. And as anyone who has handled fire before knows, it just takes a few embers to start the fire anew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 08-21-2014, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T21:39:58-07:00","id":236174,"title":"","content":"I like the Treasury doe I have some questions<br /> <br /> From the sound of it the Treasury will have Idols which I guessing will be the spirt-like inhabitants of the realm, does anyone have ideas how their mechanics going to work and how they interact with the materiel world?<br /> <br /> From my view the Treasury sounds a lot like the Shadow, anyway to make it make more clearer?<br /> <br /> Can other supernaturals enter the Treasury and if they can how they look at it (especially mages)?<br /> <br /> And from the splat mythology wouldn't the Treasury be the heart of one of the Longs?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't their be something like a gate or something, I like the circling idea and you should keep it but imagine this for a second imagine you see a guy stop out of nowhere and started circling and then disappears that this not make much sense<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S sorry for the poor grammar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 08-21-2014, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:22:34-07:00","id":236190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236174#post236174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Treasury doe I have some questions<br /> <br /> From the sound of it the Treasury will have Idols which I guessing will be the spirt-like inhabitants of the realm, does anyone have ideas how their mechanics going to work and how they interact with the materiel world?<br /> <br /> From my view the Treasury sounds a lot like the Shadow anyway to make it make more clearer?<br /> <br /> Can other supernaturals enter the Treasury and if they can how they look at it (especially mages)?<br /> <br /> And from the splat mythology wouldn't the Treasury be the heart of one of the Longs?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't their something of a gate or something, I like the circling idea and you should keep it but imagine this for a second imagine you see a guy stop out of nowhere and started circling and then disappears that this not make much sense<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S sorry for the poor grammar</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the Treasury is mostly CJC's work and I would like to get a response from him about commenting any further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T04:49:21-07:00","id":236330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236190#post236190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the Treasury is mostly CJC's work and I would like to get a response from him about commenting any further.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok gott ya <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T10:15:49-07:00","id":236642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236174#post236174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Treasury doe I have some questions<br /> <br /> From the sound of it the Treasury will have Idols which I guessing will be the spirt-like inhabitants of the realm, does anyone have ideas how their mechanics going to work and how they interact with the materiel world?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Idols that were described are amalgamations of the population of the society that constitutes their parts. In the material world, these 'beings' are organizations, clubs, companies, and other lifeless ideas that are given life by the sum of their parts. As such, an Idol doesn't move in on the Daylight world because it already exists in the daylight world; its state as a living being is a personification that lets an Oroboros approach it from a different angle. Whereas in the Daylight world dealing with an organization can be a real hassle what with meeting appointments, swarms of lawyers, and various bureaucratic hurdles to cross; by contrast a dragon interacting with the organization as a living entity in the Treasury evades these complications and comes straight to the core of the matter.<br /> When one of these idols is wounded, the damage bleeds back into the real world over the course of several months (Time is compressed at that depth of the Treasury). For example, say an Oroboros attacks an Idol and removes the arm it uses to carry its weapon. Upon returning to the real world, news would spread that the Weapons Research division of the company the idol represents is suffering serious cutbacks leading up to the closure of that wing of the business. A lab exploded and killed six workers, and they are trying to distance themselves from the scandal.<br /> Conversely, should the Oroboros persuade the idol to disarm rather than take its weaponry away by force, the company's business model might be completely rewritten (perhaps due to a change in CEO? Or perhaps a merger?) and the removal of the Weapons Research division would be a result of this change in direction rather than due to the deaths of six people.<br /> <br /> So interacting with idols is easier than trying to change an organization in person, but it is harder to predict the results. It's sort of like hitting an old radio repeatedly to get it to work instead of opening it up and finding the actual problem; you might be able to get what you want but you might break something else in the process.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236174#post236174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my view the Treasury sounds a lot like the Shadow, anyway to make it make more clear?<br /> <br /> Can other supernaturals enter the Treasury and if they can how they look at it (especially mages)?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a Mage-esque cosmology the Treasury would fall somewhere between the Primal Wilds and the Aether. However, the Treasury is the a state of perception rather than an actual place (much like Twilight is a state of perception), so being able to travel there with magic is questionable. Were you to house rule a way into the treasury, you would probably want to tie it to Prime magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236174#post236174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And from the splat mythology wouldn't the Treasury be the heart of one of the Longs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Treasury is the Heart of Huang Long, the center wind who destroyed herself to create the universe. It is also the heart of every dragon (Nidhoggr AND Oroboroi... but not the four other longs) as each dragon is herself a fragment of Huang Long. In essence, the world heart is the combined potential of every Heart within the universe, and as such it and the Treasury shrink every time a Heart is destroyed and it and the Treasury grow every time a Heart is created. This is just as DahQueenDiva suggested.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236174#post236174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't their be something like a gate or something, I like the circling idea and you should keep it but imagine this for a second imagine you see a guy stop out of nowhere and started circling and then disappears that this not make much sense</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as actions are translated up into abstraction as the depth of perceiving the Treasury increases, so to are actions translated down to practical application. A dragon interacting with the Idol of a corporation at the deepest depths of the Treasury would be seen in the real world making appointments, conversing with lawyers and receptionists, filing paperwork, and generally doing everything needed to achieve the changes she is triggering directly in the idol. So a dragon does not actually disappear when going into the treasury, she sets her body on autopilot.<br /> <br /> ...This would perhaps be easier to swallow if we removed the time compression element of the Treasury. Or perhaps the dragon does not take all the actions necessary to exact the change; maybe interacting at that level of perception drives other entities (such as members of the organization the idol represents) to take these actions in the dragon's favor, much like pawns on a chessboard. It is worth discussing further.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the moment the definition of the Treasury is in flux. I really want to discuss with everybody what works and what doesn't, and make it <b>Dragon</b>'s thing instead of my thing. I've got a bad track record with systems and thematic elements that are just <i>my</i> thing, so let's make it everybody's thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T11:08:25-07:00","id":236708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236642#post236642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Idols that were described are amalgamations of the population of the society that constitutes their parts. In the material world, these 'beings' are organizations, clubs, companies, and other lifeless ideas that are given life by the sum of their parts. As such, an Idol doesn't move in on the Daylight world because it already exists in the daylight world; its state as a living being is a personification that lets an Oroboros approach it from a different angle. Whereas in the Daylight world dealing with an organization can be a real hassle what with meeting appointments, swarms of lawyers, and various bureaucratic hurdles to cross; by contrast a dragon interacting with the organization as a living entity in the Treasury evades these complications and comes straight to the core of the matter.<br /> When one of these idols is wounded, the damage bleeds back into the real world over the course of several months (Time is compressed at that depth of the Treasury). For example, say an Oroboros attacks an Idol and removes the arm it uses to carry its weapon. Upon returning to the real world, news would spread that the Weapons Research division of the company the idol represents is suffering serious cutbacks leading up to the closure of that wing of the business. A lab exploded and killed six workers, and they are trying to distance themselves from the scandal.<br /> Conversely, should the Oroboros persuade the idol to disarm rather than take its weaponry away by force, the company's business model might be completely rewritten (perhaps due to a change in CEO? Or perhaps a merger?) and the removal of the Weapons Research division would be a result of this change in direction rather than due to the deaths of six people.<br /> <br /> So interacting with idols is easier than trying to change an organization in person, but it is harder to predict the results. It's sort of like hitting an old radio repeatedly to get it to work instead of opening it up and finding the actual problem; you might be able to get what you want but you might break something else in the process..</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, so for terms of power, low power Idols would be like be like family run stores or new businesses, moderate power Idols I would see would be like big companies but not that big like reginal organizations or stuff like that(wouldn't that include onyx path?) and big ones I would see are like organizations you see everywhere like McDonalds or the roman catholic church? Anyway like what you guys are doing so far but out of curiosity, wouldn't Idols also represent supernatural organizations like Hunter's conspiracys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T11:20:44-07:00","id":236720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236642#post236642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a Mage-esque cosmology the Treasury would fall somewhere between the Primal Wilds and the Aether. However, the Treasury is the a state of perception rather than an actual place (much like Twilight is a state of perception), so being able to travel there with magic is questionable. Were you to house rule a way into the treasury, you would probably want to tie it to Prime magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <b>really</b> need to take a look to the spoilers of Mage 2e specially this one: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/</a><br /> <br /> You'll find it both relevant to this conversation a probably a source of &quot;overlap&quot; between Dragons and Mages.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;between the Primal Wilds and the Aether&quot; isn't really a thing that makes sense since Imperial Mysteries. The Supernal Realms are a continuum of Symbol-Truths that give meaning to the whole of the universe. The Realms as seen by Mages while awakening are filtered by the &quot;viewpoint&quot; of the Watchtowers because otherwise the seer Meaning of the experience would retroactively erase the potential Mage from existence. Otherwise it's the same &quot;place&quot; although in truth is more like a point of view <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T12:29:03-07:00","id":236805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236720#post236720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <b>really</b> need to take a look to the spoilers of Mage 2e specially this one: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/</a><br /> <br /> You'll find it both relevant to this conversation a probably a source of &quot;overlap&quot; between Dragons and Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, low perception Treasury and Active Magesight are practically the same thing. Why do I keep coming up with ideas that are present in books I haven't seen yet?!<br /> That's pretty cool, though.<br /> <br /> I suppose, then, that my claim of the Treasury being between the Primal Wilds and the Aether would really be a claim that the Treasury is a kind of perception that Mages bearing the Life or Forces primary arcanum would be able to witness. Still, knowing this clarification and knowing the long-time connection between dragons and mages in mage cosmology, I could see the Treasury being interpreted as a highly concentrated form of mage sight, regardless of arcanum (or perhaps the combination of ALL arcanum). The universe is, in effect, the interior of Huang Long's body after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T12:29:04-07:00","id":236806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236720#post236720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You <b>really</b> need to take a look to the spoilers of Mage 2e specially this one: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/</a><br /> <br /> You'll find it both relevant to this conversation a probably a source of &quot;overlap&quot; between Dragons and Mages.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;between the Primal Wilds and the Aether&quot; isn't really a thing that makes sense since Imperial Mysteries. The Supernal Realms are a continuum of Symbol-Truths that give meaning to the whole of the universe. The Realms as seen by Mages while awakening are filtered by the &quot;viewpoint&quot; of the Watchtowers because otherwise the seer Meaning of the experience would retroactively erase the potential Mage from existence. Otherwise it's the same &quot;place&quot; although in truth is more like a point of view <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I would dump the Awakened cosmology and focus on hammering down the Treasury mechanics as it forces us to play by Mage's rules for things instead of defining things that best fit the theme of Dragon.<br /> <br /> For example, a Mage may conceptually (and physically) know of the Underworld but almost all sure as hell don't know about Duat and how that crap works (or even if it is part of the Underworld and isn't it's own Realm all together).<br /> <br /> In terms of Magi, the Treasury maybe a pocket Astral Realm, an Emanation Realm, Something akin to Twilight, or something that is more bizarre. But that ultimately concerns the Awakened and their obsessive need for map making.<br /> <br /> If the Treasury confounds the Awakened, then we are all the better for it. The terms &quot;Here be dragons&quot; exists for a reason.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T12:38:30-07:00","id":236812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236806#post236806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truth be told, I would dump the Awakened cosmology and focus on hammering down the Treasury mechanics as it forces us to play by Mage's rules for things instead of defining things that best fit the theme of Dragon.<br /> <br /> For example, a Mage may conceptually (and physically) know of the Underworld but almost all sure as hell don't know about Duat and how that crap works (or even if it is part of the Underworld and isn't it's own Realm all together).<br /> <br /> In terms of Magi, the Treasury maybe a pocket Astral Realm, an Emanation Realm, Something akin to Twilight, or something that is more bizarre. But that ultimately concerns the Awakened and their obsessive need for map making.<br /> <br /> If the Treasury confounds the Awakened, then we are all the better for it. The terms &quot;Here be dragons&quot; exists for a reason.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I recommended he read the blog post because I found his description on the Treasury incredibly similar to how Mage Sight works in 2e and found it interesting. The bit about Mage cosmology was also to highlight how similar his ideas were to current Mage canon. Again because I found it curious.<br /> <br /> I will refrain from discussing how I think Mages would respond to being told about Duat because is highly offtopic, but I will tell you that I don't think the Awakened would be confounded by the Treasury as described. Intrigued? certainly, specially if it keeps being so similar to how they perceive the Supernal. But hardly confounded.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In fact, if I were you I would play the similarities up, add some important twists and be all ambiguous about the true nature of the Treasury. Is it some kind of Mage Sight? Are the Dragons looking into the Supernal as Mages do only using the themes of their Heart in place of a Watchtower? Nobody knows. The Dragons don't care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","user":"Ravraxas","date":". 08-21-2014, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:00:10-07:00","id":236908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236812#post236812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually I recommended he read the blog post because I found his description on the Treasury incredibly similar to how Mage Sight works in 2e and found it interesting. The bit about Mage cosmology was also to highlight how similar his ideas were to current Mage canon. Again because I found it curious.<br /> <br /> I will refrain from discussing how I think Mages would respond to being told about Duat because is highly offtopic, but I will tell you that I don't think the Awakened would be confounded by the Treasury as described. Intrigued? certainly, specially if it keeps being so similar to how they perceive the Supernal. But hardly confounded.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In fact, if I were you I would play the similarities up, add some important twists and be all ambiguous about the true nature of the Treasury. Is it some kind of Mage Sight? Are the Dragons looking into the Supernal as Mages do only using the themes of their Heart in place of a Watchtower? Nobody knows. The Dragons don't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I apologize if I came out too strong. It's just the feeling of the combination of being invested in the project and the slight annoyance at M:tAw's tendency to shoehorn everything into it's universe which granted that is by theme and design but it get bad when GMs and Players start applying them to other game lines. It cheapens the sense of discovery to me (which is ironically what Mage tries not to do).<br /> <br /> Reguardless, I would suspect the Treasury would both confound and intrigue many Awakened in equal measure. It wasn't built for humans nor even cares for human understanding. It was built for Dragons by Dragons. Any other visitors would have to tread very lightly. <br /> <br /> Also, I've wondered about Antagonists in the Treasury. Given the lowest point of it is basically a wasteland of the former draconic golden age, I feel like the Forgotten Ones would be a great fit for it. They could've been creatures/servants left to rot after everything fell apart and started running wild, rampaging through the wasteland but I'm open to other suggestions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:06:43-07:00","id":236912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236642#post236642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just as actions are translated up into abstraction as the depth of perceiving the Treasury increases, so to are actions translated down to practical application. A dragon interacting with the Idol of a corporation at the deepest depths of the Treasury would be seen in the real world making appointments, conversing with lawyers and receptionists, filing paperwork, and generally doing everything needed to achieve the changes she is triggering directly in the idol. So a dragon does not actually disappear when going into the treasury, she sets her body on autopilot.<br /> <br /> ...This would perhaps be easier to swallow if we removed the time compression element of the Treasury. Or perhaps the dragon does not take all the actions necessary to exact the change; maybe interacting at that level of perception drives other entities (such as members of the organization the idol represents) to take these actions in the dragon's favor, much like pawns on a chessboard. It is worth discussing further.</div> </div> </div> </div>So think I got a way for that ,the myth of the sleeping dragon. So basically what i am thinking is that for an oroboros to enter the treasury he must enter a meditive trance, while he's in the trance it looks like he's in twilight but he's acutally in the treasury just at the shallows. for him to go deeper he must circle as you said to lighten his soul and go deeper, but the problem is that while he's in the treasury, his body in Daylight is in True form and he's practically in a coma which could present problems <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and just for fun what would you think the ancient draconic dialect would be based of, I would think it to be an ancient version of Chinese","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 08-21-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:16:22-07:00","id":236920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236912#post236912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So think I got a way for that ,the myth of the sleeping dragon. So basically what i am thinking is that for an oroboros to enter the treasury he must enter a meditive trance, while he's in the trance it looks like he's in twilight but he's acutally in the treasury just at the shallows. for him to go deeper he must circle for he as you said lighten his soul, but the problem is that while he's in the treasury, his body in Daylight is in True form and he's practically in a coma which could present problems</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Entering a Buddhist temple, you encounter what looks to be a statue of a Dragon in the center. You ask the monk to see the owner of the temple. The monk simply wipes the dust off the statue to show the flesh beneath.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:15:52-07:00","id":236975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=236920#post236920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Entering a Buddhist temple, you encounter what looks to be a statue of a Dragon in the center. You ask the monk to see the owner of the temple. The monk simply wipes the dust off the statue to show the flesh beneath.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that might explain how Siddhartha Gautama Bhudda sat under that tree for forty years. It also reminds me of desert varnish on stone, which is awesome.<br /> <br /> If other people like this concept, we might go with hibernation stasis for deep Treasury perceptions (where the time compression would start to apply, we'd replace it with hibernation).<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the draconic language, PaladinDemo was spearheading that initiative so he'd be the one to ask. I also found <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?230842-Fan-nWoD-Dragons-the-Imprisoned&amp;s=f0c5ec60fa0a30107a7dfc0b1d21fbb8&amp;p=4927247#post4927247\" target=\"_blank\">this on RPG.net</a>; it was developed for another Dragon fan template, but maybe we could ask the creator if we can use it for Draconic in <b>Embers</b> (The thread I linked to is nine years old, so don't post in it. If you want to pursue that as Draconic [I'm fine leaving it undefined], send the guy a private message).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:32:03-07:00","id":237280,"title":"","content":"Me and Paraduo staled out with the game over at Spoony Experiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T17:51:30-07:00","id":237579,"title":"","content":"I was reading you description of the Treasury and I was wondering , can you get Breath in the Treasury and if you could what would it look like(I'm guessing along the lines of floating orbs of fire and lightning bolts) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:52:31-07:00","id":238405,"title":"","content":"Iceblade44, I want to say no because of the importance of working with Assets to recover Breath, but really I'm not sure. I suppose dragons could find the sparks that an Oroboros requires to resurrect and consume them, refreshing their own Breath by devouring them. In such a case, yes: they would be floating orbs of lightning and fire.<br /> <br /> The thing is, sparks are a very valuable resource to entities that spend their time in the Treasury and they are almost always going to be hoarded by Idols, the Forgotten, or even the Great Wyrm. A regular dragon seeking to replenish Breath in the Treasury will find it is not worth the risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T13:41:24-07:00","id":240662,"title":"","content":"Just a quick update. I have written up a section introducing Chimera and finished a section on Bonded Chimera. Essentially animals that have been put through a similar process as Bond of Brood and mechanically function the same in terms of ablutions. I am going to write up a piece on the effects eating multiple pieces of hearts will have on this. I have yet to write up a section on Chimera that have eaten a full heart, but I have a few ideas as to how this would work. I am tempted to call these Sphinxes. These would be fully sentient creatures that have the full powers of an Ourobori and would be dangerous antagonists or potential allies. When I have my ideas down in a readable fashion I will post up what I have for comments. Sorry it has taken me so long, I have been unusally busy recently and had little free time to do much writing.<br /> <br /> On the Treasury ideas that have been raised. I like the idea of going into a coma-trance of some kind to instigate it. I don't like the different layers of reality idea. Its too similar to the proposed Mage changes. I know that was unintentional (and is a good idea!) but I think for Dragon it would not work as well. I think the Treasury would be a place that Dragons would enter to hunt for lore, bargain with Forgotten Ones directly (perhaps the only way to kill a forgotten one for good would be in this realm) or seek out to communicate with other Dragons. Perhaps if a Dragon is trapped in the Treasury for too long or their spirit form is destroyed, they would fossilise in the real world? I like the idea of presenting the Treasury as a high-risk, high-reward place to explore as an alternative to the real world but right now have not got a lot of ideas as to what the rewards from exploring would be.<br /> <br /> Overall though, I think the Treasury has a lot of potential and is worth keeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T14:09:17-07:00","id":244311,"title":"","content":"I want to give everybody a heads-up that my availability is going to evaporate starting next week. Feel free to take what we've discussed and run with it, and I'll be back... eventually!<br /> <br /> <br /> Before I go, here's some fiction for the game... perhaps an inter-chapter story or something to spruce up a particularly mechanical stretch of text.<br /> <br /> <i>He stopped, panting, out of breath. It was chasing him. He saw it at the edge of his perception; a shadow: a silhouette of the monster his religion had taught him was the Beast. His arms were covered in slashes from its claws. Still, he was alive. He let out a sigh of relief, convinced he had lost the monster.<br /> <br /> Then the floor boards began to rumble. He ran. The ground erupted in a burst of dust and splinters as fog filled the hallway. He turned a corner. A screech brought him to his knees. The fog thickened until he could hardly see. He ran his hands along the walls in panic until he came to a doorknob. Quickly he threw it open. Hurrying inside he ducked under a desk and held his breath.<br /> <br /> Quiet. The only sound was his own heartbeat. But something was... off. The beat, it had a response. Two heartbeats. Before he could scream, the beast was upon him. Driving the claw of its index finger into his chest, it ripped him open. His final vision? The beast, tearing his heart to pieces.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=240662#post240662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the different layers of reality idea. Its too similar to the proposed Mage changes. I know that was unintentional (and is a good idea!) but I think for Dragon it would not work as well. I think the Treasury would be a place that Dragons would enter to hunt for lore, bargain with Forgotten Ones directly (perhaps the only way to kill a forgotten one for good would be in this realm) or seek out to communicate with other Dragons. Perhaps if a Dragon is trapped in the Treasury for too long or their spirit form is destroyed, they would fossilise in the real world? I like the idea of presenting the Treasury as a high-risk, high-reward place to explore as an alternative to the real world but right now have not got a lot of ideas as to what the rewards from exploring would be.<br /> <br /> Overall though, I think the Treasury has a lot of potential and is worth keeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Treasury stands as a type of perception because the body of the Oroboros remains in a physical state while she goes traipsing through the heart of the world; it is not a distraction as Two World Sight or the new Mage Sight would be, as interactions that are abstracted in the Treasury become suitably grounded in the real world. As for stepping on the toes of Mage 2e, I don't think it's worth our energy to worry about overlap anymore. What you're picturing is the deepest states of perception, where the spatial relations between objects and beings becomes less important. I feel that having both (the high concept deep Treasury and the altered visions low concept Treasury shallows) would help the game rather than hurt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T21:37:27-07:00","id":244526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=244311#post244311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to give everybody a heads-up that my availability is going to evaporate starting next week. Feel free to take what we've discussed and run with it, and I'll be back... eventually!<br /> <br /> <br /> Before I go, here's some fiction for the game... perhaps an inter-chapter story or something to spruce up a particularly mechanical stretch of text.<br /> <br /> <i>He stopped, panting, out of breath. It was chasing him. He saw it at the edge of his perception; a shadow: a silhouette of the monster his religion had taught him was the Beast. His arms were covered in slashes from its claws. Still, he was alive. He let out a sigh of relief, convinced he had lost the monster.<br /> <br /> Then the floor boards began to rumble. He ran. The ground erupted in a burst of dust and splinters as fog filled the hallway. He turned a corner. A screech brought him to his knees. The fog thickened until he could hardly see. He ran his hands along the walls in panic until he came to a doorknob. Quickly he threw it open. Hurrying inside he ducked under a desk and held his breath.<br /> <br /> Quiet. The only sound was his own heartbeat. But something was... off. The beat, it had a response. Two heartbeats. Before he could scream, the beast was upon him. Driving the claw of its index finger into his chest, it ripped him open. His final vision? The beast, tearing his heart to pieces.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly:<br /> <br /> The Treasury stands as a type of perception because the body of the Oroboros remains in a physical state while she goes traipsing through the heart of the world; it is not a distraction as Two World Sight or the new Mage Sight would be, as interactions that are abstracted in the Treasury become suitably grounded in the real world. As for stepping on the toes of Mage 2e, I don't think it's worth our energy to worry about overlap anymore. What you're picturing is the deepest states of perception, where the spatial relations between objects and beings becomes less important. I feel that having both (the high concept deep Treasury and the altered visions low concept Treasury shallows) would help the game rather than hurt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice I like the fiction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T13:56:05-07:00","id":244984,"title":"","content":"I've just went through the whole thread and read every post on the treasury and this is what I think the treasury is<br /> <br /> So far I would split the treasury in at least three levels<br /> First Level: at this level the dragon has reached something like 2E Mage sight and Twilight , he sees the world through symbols and abstractions and potential, he is on the surface of the treasury but not in it. As much as this is like Mage sight it is not in my opinion for the uses it has for dragons, the difference in these two things are that Mage sight is an investigating tool, which is fine with mages as they are investigators, but dragons are not investigators,they are Rulers. No ruler is an investigator(well maybe except the Delvers) they got more important things to do, like taking control of the Middle East, kidnapping the next great Da Vinci's, collecting enough gold to make Fort Knox look like a piggy bank and Rockefeller a hot dog vendor, things like that. I see this level not a investigating tool but something a ruler always need, a social tool, a thing to help the ruler to well rule. Anyway I am rambling this a bit long, also I got an idea that at this level one could tell if something was an asset to a dragon, maybe as aura of Breath around it. This could serve as a tool for you to take your things close to your rivals or vice versa<br /> <br /> Second Level: at this level a dragon is in the heart of the world, which he would need to be in trance to enter. This is the level of the Idols, here a dragon can influence the the organizations those Idols represent and where a dragon , It is also here where time compresses and I would think where antecedents go when they die. To a dragon this level of the treasury is like what CJC described, a combination of twilight and a giant Heart. I also think their would be Breath at this level but Breath dragons can't use, I would see it as pure potential,the same energy that created the world,but it would be too pure for the oroborus for they are not the original dragons but their usurpers, instead of healing the dragons it would harm them. While it might be useless for the orobori it would not for others, I would see that antecedents would be able to use it as they are no longer(part) human but rather echoes of the Heart,for Idols it would be the thing that keeps them running, and the Nidhoggr would be able to use as they are the original.<br /> <br /> Third Level: here the Treasury stops looking like a weird version of the modern world but what it look like long ago, when Dragon-kings ruled the world through fear and whose very words were able to control and destroy thousands of lives, when the Forgotten wasn't was forgotten but gods, when instead of Embers their was Inferno, here the Treasury shows the wrecks of the great Dominion, here is the rotten core of the Heart. At this level one can find the ancient Nidhoggr, sleeping through the millennium, this where the Empty ones spend their days with oblivion. This is not a place any dragon would go lightly, for instead of the bright potential of Breath there is only decay, destruction, and hopelessness. I have not so far got any good ideas why the orobori would to this level yet so does anyone have ideas?<br /> <br /> So that is what I think the Treasury is and does anyone have ideas about it? I would love to get opinions from others, and does anyone have a cooler name than Levels,I can't think of one<br /> <br /> Oh and sorry for the bad grammar,I'm in a rush","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 09-30-2014, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T17:00:50-07:00","id":249291,"title":"","content":"Sorry for not poking my nose in here for a while CJC. It seemed like you had a good thing going and I didn't want to upset it.<br /> (I'd probably have lashed out at Frogs for that lazily-written critique or 'd have spammed too many random ideas at once and ruined everything...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> Oh, and I really liked the Oroboros symbol that you drew in the CIJ update. Very cool.<br /> <br /> I wrote up bunch of thoughts on each topic, then I tried to organize them into more helpful notes..<br /> Maybe I should wait for when you return, but I'll post some of them, and these are some of what I was working on.<br /> <br /> - Bloody Chalice Knights, new write-ups (rewrote them as a multiple choice, the true facet depending on one's GM and campaign)<br /> - Pros and cons of the new and the old Breath regain system, discussion<br /> - Edicts- flavor texts and small system tweaks (like the Language thing)<br /> - healing - system for bringing it back and making it work<br /> - more advanced Devourer/Hydrae rules, ablutions and descriptory text<br /> - True Heart/heartless fluff talk (pros-cons: how tthey revive, gain Breath, make Bonds/PLs, etcetra)<br /> - Jade small rewrite attempt (more sellable)<br /> - restoring the high-Durability Heart (to the 5-Health one how you had it in the original version)<br /> - small additions to the Treasury, history, Philosophies stuff<br /> <br /> ---<br /> I want to mention the easiest change; it's simple and I's sure you're in agreement with me.<br /> When the CIJ document says this<br /> &quot;He pays for these with his own experience, paying double the cost of the Ablution.&quot;<br /> this becomes<br /> &quot;He pays for these with his own experience.&quot;<br /> <br /> (And the Pilot Lights' text changes likewise.<br /> Every other disadvantage (no Method, borrowed etc.) remains the same so nothing else even needs to be edited.)<br /> <br /> This small rule was a vestige from mimicking old Vampire that I changed my mind about pretty quickly - and, surpise, when B&amp;S came out, it was gone from that as well.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> Spart(o)i:<br /> <br /> I think it's a neat idea.<br /> My question is, why is it sold as a merit.<br /> It seems to me like one could select this background at no cost, since it gives more drawbacks than advantages.<br /> No memories, identity, or belongings, bethralled to the first person he meets:<br /> &quot;Socially she is as fresh as a newborn child, and is likely to believe anything and everything she hears. She is inescapably loyal to the first person she meets.&quot;<br /> these seem like the hallmarks of an excellent power, but not a very good merit.<br /> <br /> When I said that I wished the Edicts had more &quot;flavor&quot; this is the kind of thing I meant though, so I dared to repurpose this as an Edict concept:<br /> <br /> <i>CADMUS' CROP<br /> <br /> The dragon can create life from nothing, summoning the aid of a personal warrior.<br /> <br /> Spartoi have 3 in every Physical Attribute, 1 in every other Attribute, and 1 dot in Athletics, Brawl, Weaponry and Firearms.<br /> <br /> Spartoi exist until the end of the scene, and then they return to the earth from whence they have come.<br /> If a dot of Willpower per person is spent by the summoning Dragon, the effect can be made permanent. (Mark the Spartolos Retainer on your character sheet.)<br /> <br /> The effect can also be delayed; the dragon places the tooth into the ground after breathing on it, and the Spartolos will rise and carry out the Dragon's will only when the trigger that the Dragon set is met (for example, an intruder entering the Lair).<br /> <br /> Spartolos<br /> Mental Attribute s: Intelligence 1; Wits 1; Resolve 1<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 3; Dexterity 3; Stamina 3<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 1; Manipulation 1; Composure 1<br /> Skills: Firearms 1; Brawl 1; Weaponry 1; Athletics 1<br /> Willpower: 2<br /> Initiative: 4<br /> Defense: 1 (reduced to 0); 2/1 Armor<br /> Speed: 11 (species factor 5)<br /> Size: 5<br /> Weapon: Sword - Damage: 2 Lethal; Dice Pool: 6<br /> Health: 8<br /> <br /> (Spartoi possess no Virtue or Vice.<br /> Instead, a Spartolos receives a point of Willpower if it bests an opponent in combat or contest.)</i><br /> <br /> ---<br /> New Breath regain system:<br /> <br /> I like it.<br /> Whether it is better for the purpose than the fuel-eating solution is going to be the topic of another discussion.<br /> <br /> Right now, I only want to add the critique that it is a bit weak on the horror element.<br /> Possessive and jealous acts could be emphasized a bit more with rules like:<br /> <br /> If a Maiden interacts with anyone else intimately, s/he stops funtioning as a Maiden.<br /> If a Hoard is moved, borrowed, even just handled by someone else, it stops functioning as a hoard.<br /> If a mortal challenges the dragon's authority on the grounds of the Province and does not get punished, or if another Dragon is allowed to move in except as a guest of the ruler and does not get chased out, or the Province stops functioning as a source of Breath.<br /> Ideologies fail to take hold if they are too positive.<br /> <br /> We can talk more about this later. I wanted to repurpose Fossilization a bit - give it a bit more mystery flair, rather than something every dragon knows and suffers from by default. That would change the scenery a bit, since the current one was pushed in a small way by adding the required daily Breath.<br /> ---<br /> Healing:<br /> This is a sketch for another possible system - still working on some of this.<br /> <br /> It might look a bit messy, because I balanced it for 1 Breath = 1 Bashing damage, <br /> Maybe this is, yknow, wrong, maybe it is better to go back to a more Vampire-like price.<br /> <br /> As written here, Dragons may lose more Breath to healing themselves than say, Vampires, but counterbalance it somewhat by a greater degree of flexibility. And their defense is definitely on par (the legendary &quot;dragon scales&quot;).<br /> <br /> <i><u>USES OF BREATH</u><br /> <br /> PROTECTIVE SKIN:<br /> <br /> First of all, the Oroboros can cancel damage as it happens (as a reflexive action). For 1 point of Breath, the dragon can cancel out one point of Bashing or Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Cancelling Bashing damage is covert; the dragon's body simply appears to be more sturdy, more resistant to harm. Cancelling Lethal wounds however is clearly supernatural, as bullets bounce off and weapons slide away from the dragon's skin. (Fortunately a bullet is too fast for the naked eye so the dragon can usually simply deny that she got hit in the first place.)<br /> <br /> (This power can protect the dragon from Exceptional Successes or Conditions like Leg Wrack or Stun, reducing the number of successes on the opponent's roll below what would be required. It can also protect her from Resistant wounds, which would be impossible to recover later with supernatural healing).<br /> <br /> Aggravated damage can not be downgraded in this manner. <br /> <br /> HEALING WOUNDS:<br /> <br /> A point of Breath recovers a point of Bashing damage.<br /> Two points of Breath recover a point of Lethal damage<br /> Five points of Breath, plus a point of Willpower can restore a point of Aggravated damage. Only one Aggravated wound can be recovered this way per day, and this includes uses of the Mend Edict she received from others), she can not do it again until the next day.<br /> <br /> REGROWING LOST BODY PARTS:<br /> <br /> Finally, the dragon can channel the same energy to mend wounds that would normally be beyond human regenerative capacity.<br /> <br /> 1 Breath can heal small, cosmetic damage: a lost tooth, a permanent scar.<br /> <br /> 2 Breath (equal to 1 Lethal damage) can regrow more significant damage such as a finger, an eye, ear or nose.<br /> <br /> 5 Breath+1 WP (equal to 1 Aggravated damage) can regrow a hand, and most internal organs (the heart is the only exception).<br /> <br /> 10 Breath+2WP (equal to 2 Aggravated damage) can regrow a whole limb. It can also regrow a head, a power only used by Hydrae (a person with only one head dies like anyone else, obviously).<br /> <br /> Should a dragon lose her body, regrowing an entire body from scratch means an expenditure of 25 Breath+5 WP (equal to 5 Aggravated damage), AND then the dragon has to restore her Health track separately, as a freshly returned body has Aggravated damage in ever Health box. This means being out of commission for about two weeks, provided that the dragon has a steady income of Breath. Dragons who have lost other sources of Breath while dead can only rely on the internal energy source of the Heart (1 Breath/day) and so the same process for them can take months.<br /> <br /> Reattachments: It takes 1 Breath to reattach a cleanly-cut body part. Larger body parts or gorier wounds that have destroyed a lot of flesh may take 2 Breath. Anything bigger requires complete regeneration as above.<br /> <br /> Cauterization: <br /> <br /> Should the tissue on a wound get burned thoroughly (cautered) for any reason, that wound can not regenerate itself for the duration of the scene (essentially becoming a Resistant wound temporarily).<br /> <br /> Lastly, features that only manifest at higher levels of divinity heal differently. A lost horn may turn into a head scar when the dragon returns to human form. These wounds in Divine form heal once the other, smaller wound heals in human form.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/224953-reaper-the-initative-they-are-coming?p=228007#post228007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Vree was helping with Dragon the Embers, the social organizations were the portion of the game that needed the most revisions, but also the portion that answered those key doubts listed (Feelings invoked, Stories facilitated, etcetera).</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean when I barged in on your 90% completed game. I wouldn't call that &quot;helping&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh CJC, I'm so sorry. xD<br /> <br /> I just wanted to share some of my enthusiasm and I made it all complicated.<br /> <br /> But it turned out really nice in the end.<br /> <br /> (I just want to mention that I'll be gone until next week starting tomorrow as well, I'll try to help more and check comments after that.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T17:46:58-07:00","id":249324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spart(o)i:<br /> <br /> I think it's a neat idea.<br /> My question is, why is it sold as a merit.<br /> It seems to me like one could select this background at no cost, since it gives more drawbacks than advantages.<br /> No memories, identity, or belongings, bethralled to the first person he meets:<br /> &quot;Socially she is as fresh as a newborn child, and is likely to believe anything and everything she hears. She is inescapably loyal to the first person she meets.&quot;<br /> these seem like the hallmarks of an excellent power, but not a very good merit.<br /> <br /> When I said that I wished the Edicts had more &quot;flavor&quot; this is the kind of thing I meant though, so I dared to repurpose this as an Edict concept:<br /> <br /> <i>CADMUS' CROP<br /> <br /> The dragon can create life from nothing, summoning the aid of a personal warrior.<br /> <br /> Spartoi have 3 in every Physical Attribute, 1 in every other Attribute, and 1 dot in Athletics, Brawl, Weaponry and Firearms.<br /> <br /> Spartoi exist until the end of the scene, and then they return to the earth from whence they have come.<br /> If a dot of Willpower per person is spent by the summoning Dragon, the effect can be made permanent. (Mark the Spartolos Retainer on your character sheet.)<br /> <br /> The effect can also be delayed; the dragon places the tooth into the ground after breathing on it, and the Spartolos will rise and carry out the Dragon's will only when the trigger that the Dragon set is met (for example, an intruder entering the Lair).<br /> <br /> Spartolos<br /> Mental Attribute s: Intelligence 1; Wits 1; Resolve 1<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 3; Dexterity 3; Stamina 3<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 1; Manipulation 1; Composure 1<br /> Skills: Firearms 1; Brawl 1; Weaponry 1; Athletics 1<br /> Willpower: 2<br /> Initiative: 4<br /> Defense: 1 (reduced to 0); 2/1 Armor<br /> Speed: 11 (species factor 5)<br /> Size: 5<br /> Weapon: Sword - Damage: 2 Lethal; Dice Pool: 6<br /> Health: 8<br /> <br /> (Spartoi possess no Virtue or Vice.<br /> Instead, a Spartolos receives a point of Willpower if it bests an opponent in combat or contest.)</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, I really like your take on the spatoi,they always felt a little off to me. Just put your tooth and you get a ghoul, didn't make much sense to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 09-04-2014, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T20:13:03-07:00","id":251200,"title":"","content":"Iceblade, you've absolutely captured what I was going for with the treasury, though I was picturing a level between Asset flagging and Idols wherein an Oroboros could interact with the uninhibited psyches of mortals (having a conversation with their surface thoughts instead of speaking with them directly). Though as I type this, there's no reason such functionality couldn't be a component of Asset flagging at the low perception.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Bloody Chalice Knights, new write-ups (rewrote them as a multiple choice, the true facet depending on one's GM and campaign)</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome back Vree!<br /> We decided we were going to keep our distance from specialized Dragon Slayers (Bloody Chalice Knights, Einherjar) in the core book, instead exploring them in a supplement later down the line. Still, if you've got something that makes them a truly indispensible antagonist, I'm sure everybody would love to have a look.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Pros and cons of the new and the old Breath regain system, discussion</div> </div> </div> </div>New System Pros: Extreme emphasis on thematic elements of the game, unique take on Storytelling Mechanics, High potential for horror, low maximum but easy replenishment makes strategic use of Breath important.<br /> <br /> New System Cons: Low maximum and maximum separated from Furnace level break the mold of Storytelling templates, fluctuating and non-experience backed Asset system might invoke ire from some players.<br /> <br /> Old System Pros: Relatively simplistic means of tracking Breath recovery, generates horror of the bizarre through the consumption of hazardous fuels<br /> <br /> Old System Cons: It was utterly ridiculous<br /> <br /> I really like the new system, particularly because it reinforces the themes of the game by making the Oroboroi attend to ruler matters in order to draw their power. I am highly resistant to the idea of revisiting the old system in more than the cursory manner it was already absorbed in the new system (Eat livestock to clear one Asset, eat a human being to clear all Assets).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- True Heart/heartless fluff talk (pros-cons: how they revive, gain Breath, make Bonds/PLs, etcetra)</div> </div> </div> </div>We're trying to de-emphasize the significance of dragons that keep Heart in chest, as someone (I believe it was Frogs or Shock) suggested the idea of dragons taking the Heart out and putting it back in as a reasonable (and possibly routine) situation. Perhaps it could be stipulated as a requirement for refreshing Breath within the Heart Asset beyond a certain Furnace rating (since Furnace effectively measures the relationship the Oroboros has with her Heart).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Jade small rewrite attempt (more sellable)</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you mean more sellable as a vulnerability or more sellable as a weapon that dragonslayers could reasonable acquire? Because your first write-up was pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- restoring the high-Durability Heart (to the 5-Health one how you had it in the original version)</div> </div> </div> </div>What made you change your mind? I'm not entirely sure the durable Heart is still necessary (the only stipulation being that a Heart cannot be destroyed by circumstance, its destruction requires intent).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to mention the easiest change; it's simple and I's sure you're in agreement with me.<br /> When the CIJ document says this<br /> &quot;He pays for these with his own experience, paying double the cost of the Ablution.&quot;<br /> this becomes<br /> &quot;He pays for these with his own experience.&quot;<br /> <br /> (And the Pilot Lights' text changes likewise.<br /> Every other disadvantage (no Method, borrowed etc.) remains the same so nothing else even needs to be edited.)<br /> <br /> This small rule was a vestige from mimicking old Vampire that I changed my mind about pretty quickly - and, surpise, when B&amp;S came out, it was gone from that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be better to place it in a GMC paragraph instead? The system is trying very hard to remain compatible with both nWoD1e and nWoD2e.<br /> Also, thank you for finding this. I don't own a copy of B&amp;S so everything I do for GMC conversion is based solely off of the free rules update.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spart(o)i:<br /> My question is, why is it sold as a merit.<br /> It seems to me like one could select this background at no cost, since it gives more drawbacks than advantages.<br /> No memories, identity, or belongings, bethralled to the first person he meets:<br /> &quot;Socially she is as fresh as a newborn child, and is likely to believe anything and everything she hears. She is inescapably loyal to the first person she meets.&quot;<br /> these seem like the hallmarks of an excellent power, but not a very good merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think it might be interesting to explore the Spartoi in this manner, it is a better distillation of myth (maintaining consistency with our other distillation of mythology) to have Spartoi be the Dragonborn: 'teeth' sown into fertile soil. It also gives the interesting prospect of Oroboroi 'blessing' pregnancies. Haven't you ever wondered why politicians are always kissing babies? XD<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said that I wished the Edicts had more &quot;flavor&quot; this is the kind of thing I meant though, so I dared to repurpose this as an Edict concept:</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the ten new Edict configurations are not flavorful enough? Do they need to be flavor-blasted? **CJC might be just a little manic at the moment**<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>CADMUS' CROP<br /> <br /> The dragon can create life from nothing, summoning the aid of a personal warrior.<br /> <br /> Spartoi have 3 in every Physical Attribute, 1 in every other Attribute, and 1 dot in Athletics, Brawl, Weaponry and Firearms.<br /> <br /> Spartoi exist until the end of the scene, and then they return to the earth from whence they have come.<br /> If a dot of Willpower per person is spent by the summoning Dragon, the effect can be made permanent. (Mark the Spartolos Retainer on your character sheet.)<br /> <br /> The effect can also be delayed; the dragon places the tooth into the ground after breathing on it, and the Spartolos will rise and carry out the Dragon's will only when the trigger that the Dragon set is met (for example, an intruder entering the Lair).<br /> <br /> Spartolos<br /> Mental Attribute s: Intelligence 1; Wits 1; Resolve 1<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 3; Dexterity 3; Stamina 3<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 1; Manipulation 1; Composure 1<br /> Skills: Firearms 1; Brawl 1; Weaponry 1; Athletics 1<br /> Willpower: 2<br /> Initiative: 4<br /> Defense: 1 (reduced to 0); 2/1 Armor<br /> Speed: 11 (species factor 5)<br /> Size: 5<br /> Weapon: Sword - Damage: 2 Lethal; Dice Pool: 6<br /> Health: 8<br /> <br /> (Spartoi possess no Virtue or Vice.<br /> Instead, a Spartolos receives a point of Willpower if it bests an opponent in combat or contest.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>If we were to build this as an Edict (Perhaps called the <b>Crop</b> edict), I'd want players to be able to make three types of Spartoi: the classic warriors (Cadmus's Crop), a group of research assistants (Tiresias's Apostles), and an entourage (Jason's Argonauts). Each would excel at a particular type of task (Physical for Cadmus, Mental for Tiresias, and Social for Jason) and would be absolutely inept at the other tasks.<br /> I could see something like this working quite well as an Edict. I'll consider including it in the core book and, if not, it should definitely go into one of the supplements to follow (Perhaps Dragonslayers?).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Breath regain system:<br /> I like it.<br /> Whether it is better for the purpose than the fuel-eating solution is going to be the topic of another discussion.<br /> <br /> Right now, I only want to add the critique that it is a bit weak on the horror element.<br /> Possessive and jealous acts could be emphasized a bit more with rules like:<br /> <br /> If a Maiden interacts with anyone else intimately, s/he stops funtioning as a Maiden.<br /> If a Hoard is moved, borrowed, even just handled by someone else, it stops functioning as a hoard.<br /> If a mortal challenges the dragon's authority on the grounds of the Province and does not get punished, or if another Dragon is allowed to move in except as a guest of the ruler and does not get chased out, or the Province stops functioning as a source of Breath.<br /> Ideologies fail to take hold if they are too positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, these things are grounds for losing dots in the Asset, actually. A Maiden's effectiveness is based on how cloistered the Oroboros keeps her. If &quot;let off the leash&quot;, the relationship between the two suffers and the Maiden becomes a less effective source of Breath. Stealing from a Hoard reduces its size, subsequently reducing the dots the Asset represents. I can agree that further emphasis on how Provinces and Ideologies lose dots is necessary; I will try to make the descriptions more clear next time I'm able to work on the project (It's going to be a few months).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to repurpose Fossilization a bit - give it a bit more mystery flair, rather than something every dragon knows and suffers from by default. That would change the scenery a bit, since the current one was pushed in a small way by adding the required daily Breath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to see what you are thinking, because the current setup for Fossilization is a very effective fear tool against wasting Breath.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written here, Dragons may lose more Breath to healing themselves than say, Vampires, but counterbalance it somewhat by a greater degree of flexibility. And their defense is definitely on par (the legendary &quot;dragon scales&quot;).<br /> PROTECTIVE SKIN<br /> First of all, the Oroboros can cancel damage as it happens (as a reflexive action). For 1 point of Breath, the dragon can cancel out one point of Bashing or Lethal damage.<br /> Cancelling Bashing damage is covert; the dragon's body simply appears to be more sturdy, more resistant to harm. Cancelling Lethal wounds however is clearly supernatural, as bullets bounce off and weapons slide away from the dragon's skin. (Fortunately a bullet is too fast for the naked eye so the dragon can usually simply deny that she got hit in the first place.)<br /> Aggravated damage can not be downgraded in this manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would much prefer that the Breath downgrades an amount of incoming damage equal to the dragon's Furnace, regardless of type. That is, a Furnace 3 dragon facing 5 Lethal damage could spend 1 Breath to give herself 'ballistic armor' against the attack equal to her Furnace, reducing the wounds to 2 Lethal 3 Bashing. This is <i>similar</i> to vampires only taking bashing from lethal sources (what with them not needing their organs and all) but less potent, reflecting the dragon's innate hardiness against harm (her scales, as it were). This might work better than the Scale system I was pitching earlier in the thread.<br /> What's different here, though, is that attacks that do aggravated damage (except Jade of course) can be shielded in this manner. As you described before, doing this to bashing wounds is covert and doing it to lethal wounds is vulgar, but using Breath to shield against Aggravated damage is downright <b>repugnant</b>. A shadow of the Dragon's true form flashes before her and literally deflects the attack: this is a real Miasma-inducing situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HEALING WOUNDS:<br /> A point of Breath recovers a point of Bashing damage.<br /> Two points of Breath recover a point of Lethal damage<br /> Five points of Breath, plus a point of Willpower can restore a point of Aggravated damage. Only one Aggravated wound can be recovered this way per day, and this includes uses of the Mend Edict she received from others), she can not do it again until the next day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you were against the ability of Breath to repair aggravated damage. What made you change your mind?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=249291#post249291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">REGROWING LOST BODY PARTS:<br /> Finally, the dragon can channel the same energy to mend wounds that would normally be beyond human regenerative capacity.<br /> 1 Breath can heal small, cosmetic damage: a lost tooth, a permanent scar.<br /> ...<br /> Should a dragon lose her body, regrowing an entire body from scratch means an expenditure of 25 Breath+5 WP (equal to 5 Aggravated damage), AND then the dragon has to restore her Health track separately, as a freshly returned body has Aggravated damage in ever Health box.<br /> <br /> Reattachments: It takes 1 Breath to reattach a cleanly-cut body part. Larger body parts or gorier wounds that have destroyed a lot of flesh may take 2 Breath. Anything bigger requires complete regeneration as above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I suppose it was the Hippocratic Edict that led you to this system. I'll need some time to process this stuff before I can respond.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One last thing... do you have any ideas or write-ups for the remaining two Philosophies (Viziers and Caitiffs)? FallenEco has Savants ready to go (or almost ready anyway), but we've got to clear up these last two Y-Splats before I can continue into Chapter 4.<br /> <br /> Also, sorry for the quote nightmare, I was trying to go through your post piece by piece and my response turned into an essay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  Thought up some greek heroes to use for the Crop Edict 09-06-2014, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T19:21:39-07:00","id":259427,"title":"","content":"(You will see a lot of EDIT signs,the reason for this with CJC gone for awhile not a lot a people would put ideas on the thread so I just decided that when I got a new idea I would put it on this post,most of it is spitballing and random ideas that i get.also sorry for the jumbled mess,)<br /> <br /> So I've been wondering this for awhile now. Dragon has plenty of antagonists, they have shayatin and the niddhogr and others but not really any common antagonists. The niddhogr are rare, and I mean very rare, and the shayatin are not as common either and they don't try to attack you as much,just bargain. And with the fact that CJC said that he's not going to add the human antagonists( like the Knights) to the PDF, it doesn't look like the oroboros have any common antagonists. Also the dragons don't have an antagonist group made of their own kind, like VtR's VII,or WtF's Pure,or MtAw's seers of the the throne, etc. so here's an idea of antagonists to fill that hole<br /> (And yes I did get some ideas from the old Saintly Devils) <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Philosophy of the Devils<br /> Celebrants of sin</b></span></div> <br /> Huang Long sacrificed herself to create the universe, her Heart became the Treasury, and her body became the world, and her blood became pure potential(e.i Breath) but there was something else,an Egg. This egg was a.shard of the time before the Spark, embedded into the great Dragon's Heart when she fell. It was a reminder of the Void that all things came, in the very center of the Treasury and there it stayed,until the Collapse. When the the usurpers killed the Elders a took there Hearts,the Egg hatched. Out of the egg came a serpent named the Great Wyrm(also called Apep,And Iblis,)and it started eating the Breath from Treasury. As it ate, the realm around it started to decay, losing the Breath which gave its power, any creature to go near it would start to Empty, losing its self to Oblivion(like the shayatin,who are the indirect servants of the Wyrm)and as it ate it grew larger. The Wyrm remembered of the time before the Spark, a time of Blackness,of the Void,and it longed for it. The Wyrm planned to devour everything that Huang Long created and return to that time of nothing but there was an obstacle in that plan, the Oroboroi. The thing is that Apep can't go into Daylight,as long as the usurpers uphold the Mandate it would never be able devour everything and return to the Void,so it made a plan. During the Dark Ages, Europe was in chaos, and at the time paradise to the dragons. The Oroboroi had not ruled so openly since the ancient era, and during this period the Wyrm whispered to them while they slept. It told them that they were gods among men,that anything they wanted was theirs to take. It told by the the right of the Heart which they took, the world belonged to them and that they should take it. During this time the first Devils were born.<br /> <br /> Devils believe it is their right to indulge in any earthly pleasure they please,they are divine are they not. Who cares about a silly Mandate, its all responsibility,no fun. They is no other expression for this than their Assets, a Devil's maidens are practically toys which they play with until they break,it's hoard made up off things that would frighten even the most jaded of people,it's ideologies what most people would call blasphemes, and there Province are basically modern Sodom,and there's the fact that many of the philosophy are Devourers. Devils are normally antagonistic to other philosophy's and vice versa,when one should past a Devil it is expected by the Mandate to eradicate the Devil, permanently. For this reason many Devils do their work in secret, except in the areas in the world where there isn't one of the orobori except for the Devil( possibly the location of a recent Niddhogr attack)which then they do it quite in the open in the form of satanic breeding cults, cannibalistic feasts and other things. And as all these things happen a serpent is slowly eating its way up, into the Daylight.<br /> <br /> <b>Edict</b>: i don't have a firm idea what the Edict should be, probably like Void or Death or something like that,i also think that it should have something negative to anyone not a Devil should use it, any ideas<br /> <b>Concepts</b>: satanic cult leader, madam of sex slaves, mayor with a very dark secret, rapist, wrathful warlord, serial killer, overly sadistic businessman, cannibal, crimelord that likes to kill to much, pirate captan, terrorist that really likes fire<br /> <br /> This is the idea I got, I am going for something like the Belials Brood.This is just an idea, there was no group of orobori that was antagonists and I liked the idea of the old Devils Philosophies, i also wanted a more emphasis on the Mandate, making it more than just a bunch of rule that a dragon must follow but something of cosmic importance. With CJC gone for a while a thought I would put on something for people to chew on. Does anyone like the idea,thoughts about it? I would love some criticism.<br /> (P.S. sorry for the bad grammar)<br /> <br /> EDIT: changed Indulgers to Celebrants<br /> EDIT2: added concepts and more text<br /> EDIT3: I have nothing else to do so I thought up some ideas for Idols. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Idols</b></span></div> <br /> Idols are the natives of the Treasury, they represent the great organizations that run the world, Businesses, Governments, Religions, all of these at their Heart contain an Idol, the epicenter of potential. During Dominion, the Idols were nothing more than slaves, doing anything for their Elder masters. The Idols resented the Niddhogr for their treatment, but thanks to the Mandate could do nothing to change that, that was until the unthinkable happened,the Collapse. With most of the Elder killed and the rest banished, the Idols had freedom, bloody horrific freedom. The Oroboroi tried to bring order to the Idols and in a way they succeeded,but the Mandate worked differently to them,allowing Idols to have more free-rein then they had before. The Idols survive by Breath the same as the Oroboroi, the organization the Idol represents is it Asset, and its only Asset. Even though the Idol is the Asset it can't control it by its own, the Idols can't leave the 2nd level of the Treasury, so it has it servants to administer its Asset, the servants are called anima. An Idols anima represent the individual parts that make up an organization, think of an Idol as a combination of the heart and brain of an organization, the anima are the rest of the organs that help keep the organization running. Anima are the Idols representatives for the 1st level and the Twilight, influencing(and sometimes for drastic measures,Possessing) the organization for the Idols behalf. It is at these two realms of perception that the Oroboroi are most likely to interact with the anima. The Idols hate the Oroboroi,they see them as most people see tax-collectors, to them the usurpers are the last barrier to freedom. The Idols normally trie to avoid the 3rd level, seeing it as a pit of decay and rot fit only for the last of the Niddhogr and the Void-touched Shayatin, it is a taboo amongst the Idols to even mention the Serpent, seeing it that if they don't recognize it, it will go away. Also I would think native language would be draconic, much like spirits language is First Tongue.<br /> <br /> Then there's the First Idol(this Idol was not the first Idol to be created but the first to rebel against their masters). Legend says that it was he that whispered to mankind the weaknesses of the Elders, it was he who told them where and who the Elders were when they masqueraded amongst mortals,it was he who told them when they were weakest,it was he who told them where they hid their Hearts. After the Collapse, he saw that he didn't help to destroy his masters but replace them, sure the Oroboroi weren't as strong as the Niddhogr but they were strong enough to chain his people again, so he devised a more permanent solution for the Dragons, the Einhejar. When a human dies against one of the dragons and become a ghost,there is chance that he will have a vision of the First Idol. He will offer the ghost a chance to kill his murderer if he will pledge fealty to the Idol, if he accepts the Idol will infuse the ghost with its own Breath, transforming the ghost into the Idols own anima. The thing is that the einhejar is more powerful than a normal anima and has an easier time of possessing humans,and when it is destroy it will return the First Idol, nursing its wounds and waiting for the chance to attack the dragon again. The only way to destroy an Einhejar is to destroy the First Idol and that's not action for one to do lightly.<br /> <br /> Other than the Oroboroi, the Idols have only one rival, the spirits of the Shadow. There has been a Cold War between the two since the dawn of time. An Idol is the Heart of an organization but then there another part,the Shadow. Spirits of the organization is its Shadow, a different thing entirely but connected nonetheless. The rivalry stems from one simple source, resources. Idols need Breath to survive and spirits need Essence to survive and both use the organization as the source those two fuels. the thing is to the minds of these entities that if the organization is producing more of one that it will not produce much of the other, and there's the Cold War. One side trying to get the best from the other while the other side is doing the same. Both sides would love to destroy the other, they had figured out early on then that would be the death sentence for the organization. Think of it as a light/darkness duality, both oppose the other but if one would destroy the other it will destroy itself. Even though for the good reasons not to, sometimes the beings go on for a full on war. The idol using its anima as soldiers while the spirit using lesser spirits bound to it as its soldiers, and woe for any unlucky bastard who get himself between the two.<br /> Also I don't like the name Crop Edict, if you ask me I would go for like Servant or Follower but its you call.<br /> Oh and still looking for a cooler name than Levels.<br /> <br /> EDIT4:i got some suggestions about terminology, I would think it would be important to state the difference between the Elders that removed their Hearts and the ones who keep theirs,so heres a suggestion,the dragons that followed the Forgottens advice and removed their Hearts are called Zmei while the ones who didn't are the Niddhogr, and collectively they are all Elders. Originally they were called Zmei but after the Collapse all the Oroboroi changed the terms. Just suggestions.<br /> <br /> EDIT5:here are some new ideas about Sovereignty,Eternal and Ladons. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sovereignty</b></span></div> <br /> I've been wondering,their was no status rank system with the Oroboroi. Dragons are rare so it makes sense that they don't have much of hierarchy, but even the rarest splats have a ranking system,the Created have the Ramble,the Arisen have Guilds,Forsaken have Tribes and Renown, the list can go on. All the Oroboroi have are Provinces,but that's more like domains from VtR or territory's from WtF. There is nothing to say who is above you and nothing to say who is below you,and for game of Divine Right that doesn't make much sense. So here is a suggested system to fix that. All Dragons have a right to rule(Mandate proves that)but some have more right than others. You see the Oroboroi are rare,very rare, so there can't be much of community among them. There Philosophies are a way how to look at world,not organizations like Covenants or Orders,so there is no status there. All they have is their Provinces which they rule as kings,but if they run across one another,what do they do? Is this newcomer his equal,certainly not, so how they determine who is the alpha and who omega? The way they this is called Sovereignty. Sovereignty are much like the werewolves's Renown,but it is different, Auctoritas can go up from 0 to 5, for you to get a dot in Sovereignty you must first pass the test of one of the Zhen(I will get to that later),for a dragon to tell how how much Dots one has in Sovereignty she must first focus her Method Sense on the Oroborus,which than the ST tells you the answer. Another way to see a dragon's Title is degrees of divinity,the Sovereignty manifest in certain ways on the degree,the patterns of her scales,the number and length of her horns,even the shade of her eyes can be signs of her level in Sovereignty, for one to see the Auctoritas they must roll Resolve+investigation or occult. Advantages of Sovereignty,one of those is that it converts to Rank to creatures from the Treasury,allowing you more authority for anything below you,and if you use GMC spirit rules, you would inflict aggravated damage to those who have less Rank than you. So a high Sovereignty dragon would have an easier time bullying around Idols than a low Sovereignty dragon. Another is a way of respect,a dragon with high Sovereignty would be a celebrity in Oroboroi circles. <div align=\"center\">Table of Titles</div> <div align=\"center\">Dot 0:Lord/Lady<br /> Dot 1:Baron/Baroness<br /> Dot 2:Count/Countess<br /> Dot 3:Marquis/Marchioness<br /> Dot 4: Duke/Duchess<br /> Dot 5: Archduke/Archduchess</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>the Eternal<br /> aka Phoenixes,Djinn</b></div> <br /> <br /> With Dreamtime gone, their is no basis for Nightmares as inhabitants of the Treasury,so these are something I think could replace them. Long ago,after the Spark, the great Longs gifted there sister's children &quot;the Zmei&quot; with their Mandate. It allowed them to rule both Daylight and the Treasury,and be worship by the newly created humans as their gods. Before they ascended into the heavens,they created the Eternal. The Eternal was supposed to act as the administers of the Mandate,testing the Elders to see if they deserved their rights. If one should be neglectful of the Mandate he would be removed. They were also the guardians of the Treasury,once lead by Jormungandr,it was their duty to protect the Treasury and to maintain the flow of Breath to and from the realm. When the Elders started abusing there right of rule,the Eternal in horror from the disgrace of the Mandate,tried to put a stop to them,but the Zmei were to strong, with their power they scattered the Eternal to the farthest corners of the four directions. According to myth,the ones that survived the assault, known as the Zhen or the True,leaded humanity against the Elders,and caused the Collapse of Dominion,that's how they tell the tale anyway. Today the Phoenixes are a strange lot,when the ones who was destroyed by Elders resurrected they found out they were changed. For one thing they were no compelled to protect the Treasury,neither were they bound to be the keepers of the Mandate, they were unbalanced. You see,the Hearts of the Oroboroi and the Niddhogr came from Huang Long,but the Eternal came from the rest of the Longs,each one had a perfect amount of energy from each of the Longs,but when they tried to stop the Elders and was destroyed,they soon found the were no longer balanced, some found they had more of one Long while others found the had more of a different Long,it was general chaos(which the newly formed Northern Eternal loved), but the Zhen(the ones who remained balanced and was still true to their purpose) were able to corral their brethren, to keep them in check they assigned each one certain Bans and Banes, allowing who ever knew them to keep the Phoenix from getting to out of control.<br /> <br /> <b>mechanics</b> okay this is how I see it,the phoenixes use GMC Spirit rules,meaning they all have ranks,they can use Numia,etc. there is also some unique things about them,one of them is that they can use Edicts. they are divide into 5 Strata(looking for a better word than Strata)four of the Strata are aligned to one of the Longs,while the last one is not aligned to any one long but to all of them. There is Strata of the North, Strata of the West,Strata of the South, Strata of the East,and then the Zhen. Those belonging to the North are knowledgeable and secretive, they seem to know every secret there is (really they don't but there close) and they know how to put those into good use,they are masters of propaganda and blackmail,with a little whisper here and a little whisper there, they can bring whole kingdoms to there feet. The ones who belong to the East are prideful and narcissistic, they think that all should bask in their glory and will do anything to get that,they are master persuaders, no one can seem to say no in their presence,for good or ill(mostly ill). Those who claim South are wrathful and tyrannical,they see world as theirs to take and they take it forcibly, who ever stands in there way they see it forfeits the right to live,which they are quite happy to take. The ones who are West are cruel and apathetic,they all have a goal and they will do anything to reach it,they are master planners,always seeming to be ten steps ahead of you(think James Moriarty). The Zhen are mysterious and insightful,they are the guardian angels of the Oroboroi, when ever you hit a crescendo,they are there watching,evaluating. Next is resurrection, the Eternal can't die,period. The process is actually much like the dragons, when ever there form is destroyed,they appear in the Treasury. From there all they have to is find a way back to their Shrines. The directional Eternal don't have much of a foothold on the Daylight, what this means that if they what to stay in Daylight they must first do something,create a Shrine. A Djinn's Shrine is its resting place,it is where they normally replenish on there Breath( e.i. At dawn everyday if the Eternal is at its Shrine it will gain a point of Breath), it is also their gateway into 2nd level Treasury(other than death). All phoenixes have to have a Shrine, without one they would dissipate into the Treasury in a matter of hours. This is law for all but the Zhen,they don't have no need for it since they are not as unbalanced as the rest. Why would a Djinn want to be in Daylight you may ask,well much of the same reasons as an Oroborus actually. You see the Eternal were created to be servants,that was their purpose. Now that most of them don't have that purpose,they seek out what they most envy,rulership. &quot;Why can't we rule?&quot; They ask,&quot;we were created by the Longs just the Oroboroi,we have as much right as them.&quot; The thing the Eternal want is to usurp the usurpers,but the Eternal is not of flesh and blood,so they have to do their ruling subtlety,Influencing,Urging,Possessing,and Claiming the people around them. The Eternal can have Assets, the number of Assets they can have is locked by their Rank,also they have to spend a number of Breath determined by their Rank,if they can not pay they dissipate into Treasury and they lose their Roost, as there is far more Eternal than Oroboroi, the phoenixes normally act as the dragons rivals and competitors in their chosen domain. This is normally the reason for the Cardinal Strata,not so for the Zhen. While the other Strata may seem more dangerous than the Zhen,it couldn't be more wrong, the source of this is a simple thing, their Tests. While a Zhens test can be beneficial and a source of power, they all come with a price. The Zhen believe it is their duty to make the Oroboroi perfect rulers, and they will take out any distractions it sees that will get in the way of that. One example, if the Zhen notices that the Oroboroi is spending to much time being with its family than running and maintaining its Province, it will use its Influences to take the family out of the equation,permanently. If the Oroborus survives the tragedy it will be rewarded(if it did exceptionally well,the Zhen might even resurrect its family,might.) if it doesn't, than the Zhen will make it disappear. For this reason when a dragon learns that a Zhen is in town, the dragon will be experiencing more sleepless nights than not. It's also important to note that if a Zhen thinks a mortal is worthy of a Heart, it will arrange circumstances for the mortal to become the owner and become one with the Oroboroi. If there is no Heart possibly available or it thinks it surpasses the average, it will set up a test to see exactly how worthy it truly is, if the mortal passes it will do the impossible, it will become a Heart. It will sacrifice its Eternal life for the mortal to become a dragon, creating a new Heart into the world.( if it does this,treat the Method as Inheritor.)<br /> <br /> The appearance of the Eternal varies, the can take on any form. The most common of those is.bird and a person but it can be anything,from squirrels to horrific monsters. The only common fact is that it is made of smokeless fire. The color of the flames depend on the Strata, South is red, North is black, East is white, West is Blue, and the Zhen is yellow.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Ladons</b></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 11-20-2014, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T08:20:19-08:00","id":337044,"title":"","content":"Hello again,been gone for a long time unfortunately,mainly due to breakage of my pc ,but I finally got my hands on the new version.From a quick view,I've seen several things I enjoyed and some that I would envision otherwise.But guys you' ve done a really good work so far.Hoping to share ideas again with you soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T20:53:57-08:00","id":337681,"title":"","content":"I'll start with a welcome back to Pandalfino, and an apology for letting the project sit fallow. I'm still not ready to return to the project, but I could have been more punctual in responding to some of these ideas.<br /> <br /> Second, I'd like to mention that we're still waiting on write-ups for the Savants, the Viziers, and the Caitiffs. If anybody wants to take a shot at developing a Y-Splat, look to the two that are already in the half-book to get an idea about what questions the Philosophy needs to answer.<br /> <br /> And now, to respond to Iceblade.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=259427#post259427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Philosophy of the Devils<br /> Celebrants of sin</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... The first paragraph of this section gives me an intriguing idea.<br /> What if the egg isn't some force of evil, but Huang Long herself? A remnant fragment of her that has hatched back into life...<br /> Here's the problem, though. Huang Long's body is the entire universe. So as this infant fragment grows, she does so by absorbing everything she touches (It could be perceived as a metaphor for the Big Crunch, if you're into cosmological models). She is contracting the Treasury and consequently all of reality as she grows. Before the first collapse, she was kept in check by the Nidhoggr, but now she grows unbounded. In fact, the stories of Jormungandr might <i>actually</i> be about Huang Long.<br /> This creates a wonderful dilemma for the Oroboroi: Huang Long sacrificed everything to create the universe. Does she deserve to exist, if it means everything else has to be consumed? Some dragons believe she does. They hate the corruption of the world they live in and yearn for the simplicity of uniting with this &quot;great mother&quot; and becoming a single being. These dragons call themselves the Phoeni (Plural, since Phoenixes just sounds... wrong), but others call them the Celebrants of Unity or, sometimes more shortly, the Saintly Devils.<br /> Dragons that subscribe to the philosophy of unity work to disassemble the forces of order in the world, thereby weakening the Idols of the Treasury and making them easier for Huang Long to absorb. These Phoeni take on the forms of great birds, rather than great lizards, to symbolize the rebirth of the great mother (Actually in some dragon mythology, Phoenix is the female of the breed with a 66% Yin composition, so this is appropriate). Obviously the Oroboroi are adamantly opposed to these Phoeni because they pose the greatest threat to their reign imaginable: the surface of Jormungandr/Huang Long and the end of the universe.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a villain like this, because it will force players to pause and consider whether their actions are justifiable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=259427#post259427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Idols</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Idols are the hearts of business just as the Treasury is the heart of the world (well, universe, but world sounds more profound) and Hearts are the heart of a dragon's reign. I like the idea of an Idol possessing its composite parts, but I feel this should be less a force of invasion and more an order of hive-mind structure. When someone joins an organization, they give up a piece of who they are to the function and control of the organization. These pieces are the Anima you describe, and the Idool uses them as it uses its own limbs, sending commands through a mental connection to get something done in the physical world, which they are unable to interact with directly. In part this is why the Oroboroi find them so useful, if an Oroboros descends into the deep perceptions of the treasury and entreats an Idol, she can cause cascading change in the physical organization it treats as its extremities. This is often easier than actually enacting change in person.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that Idols can hold grudges. It certainly sets them apart from spirits. I also agree that Idols would have grown in both population and size after the first collapse, but as a result of trophic cascade rather than slavery. Elder dragons (Nidhoggr) hunted Idols for sustenance as a wolf might hunt a stag; Idols exist in part due to delicious Breath running throughout their body. This fact is part of why humanity was in check before the Elders were usurped; any organization that would try to grow would spawn an Idol which would subsequently be hunted for sustenance.<br /> With the Nidhoggr that turned Zmei hiding in the Material world, the Idols found roles reversed, becoming predators with terrifying reach. This too was a hunt of substenance; by killing a Zmeu the Idol could absorb its Assets into its organization extremities, growing in power as a result.<br /> Zmeu being overrun by the Oroboroi simply made this hunt easier, since Oroboroi rarely delve into the depths of the Treasury.<br /> This creates a terrifying concept, that those companies that treat themselves as legal entities have a malevolent force behind them actively working to destroy you (if you're a dragon, that is).<br /> I like this too, including the connection to the Einherjar. I wouldn't include a first Idol though, or restrict Einherjar to a single idol. Rather, it is an extension of the hive mind that any Idol may apply to any of its extremities: it can convert any anima in its organization into a vessel for the vengeful Einherjar and then sick the resulting monster on its enemy. This is another scary thought; being part of an organization can turn you into a monster for the purpose of destroying a rival company? That's some great horror fuel.<br /> No need to compare or connect Idols to Spirits. The Treasury has overlap with several realms invisible from other lines, but it is best to develop as if it exists in a vacuum and let Storytellers make their own assumptions about how realms are related.<br /> So it sounds like we're dividing the Treasury into three grades of perception:<br /> 0: Sternum (Physical World)<br /> 1: Pericardium (<i>Almost</i> Physical world, people are dressed in a way that reflects their intentions and they speak in surface thoughts)<br /> 2: Myocardium (Abstract world, home of Idols that represent organizations. Spatial and Temporal Distortions of the Treasury begin here)<br /> 3: Endocardium (World before the collapse, most commonly known as Jormungandr's Treasury. Home of the Shayatin, Huang Long, and the place where dragons go to seek resurrection)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=259427#post259427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Terminology</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the distinction between Nidhoggr and Zmei. It also makes explaining the stages of a collapse more clear, particularly the first collapse. I would say that all elders called themselves Nidhoggr until some removed their hearts, and were redubbed Zmei by the remaining Nidhoggr as a derision of their cowardice.<br /> As such, there would be very few Zmei (if any) in a modern <b>Dragon the Embers</b> game, as they would have been ripe for usurpation during the second and any subsequent collapse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=259427#post259427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sovereignty</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Who is more powerful, the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom or the President of France?<br /> Each would tell you they are more important, and the Oroboroi are no different. There is no status rank system because that would mean they'd have to admit that someone has more authority than they do, and that would be against everything that defines them.<br /> There are some subtle measures of political hierarchy, though, which can be measured by a dragon's Furnace and more importantly by her Assets. I would say that the Assets mechanic covers what you're trying to do here, particularly the Province asset.<br /> <br /> As for pulling rank in the Treasury, again that's a matter for the dragon's assets. I could see perhaps having assets adorn an Oroboros the further she descends into the perception of the Treasury, and that adornment granting her an advantage when dealing with Idols and bargaining with Shayatin. When I get back to writing and produce a rough draft of the Treasury Appendix, this is something I'd like to discuss in more detail.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=259427#post259427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>the Eternal<br /> aka Phoenixes,Djinn</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like this, I'm sorry. I could see perhaps changing Nightmares into something a little more general: broken dreams turned to monsters when potential failed to coalesce into a victory in the real world. For example, the unpublished book sitting on the counter might trigger the birth of a Djinn (Nightmare) in the Treasury's Myocardium. The potential of a whirlwind booksigning tour and two sequels collapses into a black mass of horror which seeks to collapse other dreams and thereby increase in number. It's a powerful symbol for the contagious nature of depression and it would give Oroboroi a reason to hunt them (if a Maiden is spawning Djinn in the Treasury, they could turn their misery onto the Province and cause a lot of damage).<br /> The key is shattered dreams. Djinn thereby attack by raising the spirits of a victim only to knock them down when they're ecstatic. They need the hope to collapse in order to create another Djinn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=259427#post259427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ladons</b></div> </div> </div> </div>????<br /> The dragon god from Breath of Fire?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, these are great ideas Iceblade! Keep them up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T09:31:46-08:00","id":340868,"title":"","content":"Here is a little bit of the Philosophy of Savants,as I picture it.Hope you like it(feel free to enrich,modify,point out what you think needy of change and why!)<br /> <br /> &quot;What you fail to understand,you fear.In what you fear,lies salvation.Break the chains of logic,and you shall be set free.&quot;<br /> <br /> Humanity has always been a phobic race.Clinging on to religion,society and self-made guilt,they resemble larvas at the edge of a leaf,staring into the chaos underneath.Those few that make the transition to a butterfly and fly off,are the ones that are truly free.According to a Savant,ignorance is not bliss.To be complete one must embrace the unknown,for even if your logic is not enough,your emotions are.Chaos is a part of all of us-the very part that gave birth to the world itself.To disdain it,is to disdain yourself.Only through chaos can there be creation,and to be caged by self-imposed prejudism against the very law of nature is to exclaim pure hubris in the face of the universe.Order,is after all,the foolish dream of mankind,the very reason humanity is degrading minute by minute,second by second,striving against its real purpose.Chaos is not the end,it is the means,and in accepting that you're pretty much accepting the self,and your part in the vast scheme of the cosmos.A savant thus,is the key the world needs to unlock the shackles of denial and turn the tide.<br /> <br /> Mannerisms:Savants try to embody their philosophy tenet through unpredictability.They form wide arrays of behaviors,seeming emotionally unstable to those that would hardly know them,and on rare occasions even a little crazy.Their constant esoterique monologue is a trait that defines them,as they often shun themselves to break the stereotyic leader people expect to see.That way,they encourage people to act accordingly and be the first that takes the plunge.They are most often enthusiastic about their ideas,to the point of contradicting themselves,never settling down to one opinion or the other.This may get them across as opportunists,but becomes appealing as well.A savant is most likely the mysterious,liberated kind of person we 'd all love to be but lack the will to try.Not surprisingly,they draw audiences through attitude alone,being the indirect voice on the back of people's heads.Where there's a riot or a disagreement,a Savant has most likely been.'Doubt everything'they say,often creating tension just to impart a taste of how important 'living' actually is,not simply surviving.Taboos and rules are meant to be broken,and in what is forbidden lies the sweetest sin of them all.All worth living for a single moment,even if this moment never comes.Had the world started paying attention to the greater picture and not on details,none of this would have been the way they are,Savants agree.<br /> <br /> Assets:Savants most often find value in the living,as people tend to reflect that so cherished unpredictability(an object would not do that well anyways...!).Objects after all,are not meant to last forever,and may one day fade like words on the wind;their philosophy on the other hand,will not.Therefore,Maidens are the most usual means of replenishing breath.Savants tend to have an even more obsessive relationship with them than other Oroboroi do,pushing themselves to the extreme in effort of making the seeds of their beliefs bloom in the hearts of their ''dearest''.This leads to self-destructive tendencies some of the times,but again that is the thrill of the moment according to a Savant.In what concerns Provinces,Savants tend to enjoy loose-organisation circles,accepting anyone who does not pose a threat to free will,leaving the people act and think on their own;that is what they strive for,in the end.They seldom take action(usually supervising the constant uproar of mortals),and when they do they usually strike like thunder;wild and sudden.The geographical preferences for their Province,is usually random as well,though some tend to prefer rural or suburban areas where they can do more as they please,without having the authoritarian background of a vast metropolis on their mind.<br /> <br /> Den Formation:Relationships with others of their kind tend to be tense most of the times,especially with Imperators as they lie on the opposite sides of a coin.Savants are often portrayed as non-caring individuals by other dragons,unfit for royalty or leading.For all the disadvantages their rebellious nature brings,the constant judgement they ensue to others and themselves as well is honest and well-based.They most often function as the ''extra eye'' in a den,searching through words and actions to find flaws in other Dragons in order to get their own philosophy as infallible.That zeal works for the den as well,as many times has a phantom menace been noticed firstly by a Savant,and thus prevented.<br /> <br /> Character Creation:Savants base their strengths in speed of thought and action;the first to question the self is the first to access the unknown.Most useful Attributes fall between Wits,Dexterity and even Manipulation(indirect approach often helps people believe more in themselves and less in another,which is exactly what Savants envision).Talents that help Savants convey their principles range from mental to social,and include skills as Occult and Academics,as to set hardly countered arguments on the table,as well as expression or even athletics to demonstrate their point,socially or physically.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I would suggest Assembly as their core Edict,but I'll need to check on the others you guys modified,as well.Concepts could be smt like modern day Che-Guevara,punk-teen,riot leader,neo-liberal politician,rock-star etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3496,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","user":"Pandalfino","date":". 12-15-2014, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T18:42:07-08:00","id":351163,"title":"","content":"<br /> You had a great start, Pandalfino, thank you for working so hard on this for everybody.<br /> I made a couple changes, which you will find below.<br /> <br /> I wasn't really on board with the butterfly motif, sorry.<br /> <br /> ==================================<br /> <u>Savants (Modified from Pandalfino's Take)</u><br /> Humanity has always been a phobic race. Clinging to wise words that have long shed their meaning, they are like cattle perched on the precipice of a cliff, one crack of thunder away from stampeding to their own destruction. The safety of the familiar is a lie, a tradition of stagnation that leaves them rubbing sticks for a flame as the Embers before them wither and die. Man and monster share this ignorance and to a Savant there is no greater threat. Pursuit of the new is ingrained in all creatures--it is the very thing that gave birth to the world. To shun it is to cut away at the very definition of life. Safety is the foolish dream of humankind; the notion that a force can be culled, defeated, trapped in prisons of iron and stone. To learn from the world is an act of change, and change is painful. In that way, ignorance is a bliss the Savant must tear away from the world so that it can grow.<br /> <br /> <b>Mannerisms:</b> Savants try to embody their philosophy's tenets through unpredictability: they are the wild card at the poker table and the devil's advocate in the courtroom. They form fractal behavior arrays, often appearing unstable to the casual observer. There is method in this madness, however, each social peculiarity is explicitly planned to provoke thought in the other party. They are often found narrating an epic monologue, even stepping away from a conversation to carry on an apparent aside with themselves (often to the confusion and dismay of others). They view humans as comrades rather than cattle, acting as a voice to a crowd. They encourage others to follow in their footsteps, taking up arms and spurring on the cause. Savants are forcefully enthusiastic about their ideals, mainly because they cannot conceive the notion that they might be wrong. This can make them difficult to negotiate with, particularly when interacting with other Oroboroi. It also gives them the air of opportunists, as any conversation can and will be redirected to their cause. The key to working with a Savant is to convince them that your goals and their goals lead to the same destination (though perhaps not on the same route). Savants are shockingly charismatic; this comes from their confidence in their beliefs. They draw audiences through attitude alone, planting subliminal messages in the minds of everyone that crosses their path. Riots follow in their wake.<br /> <br /> <b>Assets:</b> Savants find more value in the animate than the inanimate. They tend to take on disciples and set them to work fetching data that can be plied towards the cause. These disciples therefore end up cloistered in the various dusty libraries and evidence lockers, serving as Maidens for the Savant and her cause. Savants tend to have an even more obsessive relationship with them than other Oroboroi, pushing themselves to the extreme in the effort of making the seeds of their beliefs bloom in the hearts of their ''dearest''. When a Savant takes a province, it comes in the form of loosely-knit circles, the kind that can splinter into other organizations. A Savant maintains the province mainly by convincing its constituents that all of their problems can be solved in the pursuit of her goal and her justice.<br /> <br /> <b>Den Formation:</b> Relationships with other Oroboroi tend to be tense, mainly because the Savant is such a driven individual and her rebellious nature contradicts much of what a Dragon seeks to gain with her power. It is her knowledge of rebellion, however, that makes a Savant an excellent resource in an alliance. When the Province is in an uproar; when the Maidens cry for freedom, it is the Den's Savant who knows how to set everything right again. She is, despite her quirks, a people pleaser. Who better to quell a rebellion than somebody who knows how to start one?<br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation:</b> Savants base their strengths in speed of thought and action; the first to question the self is the first to access the unknown. Most useful Attributes fall between Wits, Dexterity and Manipulation; the indirect approach is highly effective as someone who comes to a conclusion on their own is more likely to trust it (even if given a push). Talents that help Savants convey their principles range from mental to social and include skills such as Occult, Academics, Expression, and Athletics (to outrun the backlash when they get people rioting).<br /> New Oroboroi drawn to the Philosophy of the Savant find the withering fate of their new brethren distasteful, and so seek to break the rules of man so that they might challenge the rules of nature itself; the Philosophy gives them license to stir the pot and change the world, violently if necessary.<br /> Savants begin play with one dot in the Water Edict, in honor of their founder.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts:</b> Modern revolutionary, punk rocker, associate professor, professional gambler, priest, IT guy, park ranger<br /> ==================================<br /> <br /> And, here to remind myself: I need to clean up the reason why a new Oroboros might turn to the Paragon philosophy, and specify that Paragons begin with a dot of the Fire Edict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T18:54:44-08:00","id":363995,"title":"","content":"The changes you made(syntactically and thematically)were well done mate.Some of my texts may come across as sloppy(the way I see it at least),since I have no more than 20 mins to write them(REAAAALLLYYY busy schedule)but when Monday comes,I will do my best to get the other philosophies done as well.Oh,and a happy new year to all guys(&amp;lasses:P)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3496-pandalfino","name":"Pandalfino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T21:37:32-07:00","id":453791,"title":"","content":"Has there been any development on the Chimeras? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5450-the-son-of-the-swordfish","name":"The Son of the Swordfish","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T10:16:50-07:00","id":510865,"title":"","content":"No, there hasn't been any development on Chimeras... or any development at all, actually.<br /> <br /> In previous instances of lulls like this I spent the break writing new material for the book, but this time I was waiting for write-ups on the remaining two Y-Splats. Eventually I lost interest, and now it seems that the project has stalled into its grave.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you like the project and you want to resurrect it, I have the following recommendations:<br /> <br /> <b>1.) Ditch the &quot;Dragon&quot; term</b><br /> The problem with the name Dragon is one of exposure; it's <i>too</i> familiar and so prospective contributors enter the project with too many expectations of what they want to see. As such, they are frequently driven off when they do not encounter what they were looking for. If you revive the project in a new form, I recommend using a more obscure term, like <b>Zmeu (Plural Zmei)</b> [sz+MAY-OOO, plural sz+MAY-EEE]. This would of course mean reworking the lexicon of the content that already exists but it would be worth the break from the cloud hanging around the term &quot;Dragon&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>2.) Make a new &quot;The X Chronicles&quot; thread</b><br /> Dragon began its development as a nWoD fan template and it has not been able to keep pace with the changes that accompanied the God Machine Chronicle and the second edition new World of Darkness. As such, any hope for a new phase of the project will hinge on bringing the content that already exists into compatibility with the God Machine Chronicle. I tried to have my cake and eat it too by making the book compatible with both versions of the nWoD. It doesn't work. If you crack open the half-book, you'll find that the Ablutions, Edicts, and even some of the secondary characteristics (like Furnace and Breath) are at a midpoint between the old edition and new edition rules compatibility. Take out the gooey parts that are already partially compatible with the God Machine, solidify them, and then build from there.<br /> Possible titles for the chronicles:<br /> Zmeu: The Myocardium Chronicles<br /> Zmeu: The Ignition Chronicles<br /> Zmeu: The ChimeriChronicles<br /> If you really want to reignite the project, I'm sure you can come up with something better than that, it's just to get your brain storming.<br /> <br /> <b>3.) Start from Scratch</b><br /> With the half book and the second-stage development PDF, it might look like you can harvest a great deal of the written text and continue from there. You can't. While the mechanical bits are viable, the so-called &quot;fluff&quot; has consistently been the most detested portion of the document since its first PDF; it cannot be salvaged.<br /> <br /> <b>4.) If you're looking to produce a PDF, start looking for artwork early</b><br /> A big mistake I made was waiting to finish the text before starting to seek artwork. See, while you're looking for artwork to make the book look nice, everyone else is losing interest because there's no new content to read. It's better to break the project into tiny pieces and work on them all simultaneously (possibly allocating certain contributors to certain tasks) so that the people following your project consistently have content to keep them hungry. If you don't do this, when you encounter a task that you cannot perform yourself (like I did with the factions), there will be no one around to help you.<br /> <br /> <b>5.) I won't be part of the new project</b><br /> One of the problems with Dragon's third-stage development are the ghosts in its rafters, and I am the big one. When I'm around it looks like somebody is stitching together all of the pieces of the project and I just don't have the chops to do it anymore. Another lead developer shouldn't have to fret me looming overhead. Therefore if a new iteration of the project is to succeed, I cannot be involved.<br /> <br /> Best of luck. I do love this project and I hope it gets completed some day. But I'm not the guy to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T03:01:07-07:00","id":627421,"title":"","content":"Well I don't want to overcomplicate it. I just would like to have enough material to run ONE decent D:E game someday xD<br /> <br /> Something that bugged me before that I randomly thought of today:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/ezAG542.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Couldn't you make dragons have 2+ hearts? One human heart, and one dragon one. And possibly more if you collect more.<br /> Simplifies the idea, to me at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T17:27:30-07:00","id":865209,"title":"","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> I've been playing with Dragon, and I'm really liking it, but I'd like it to get more fleshed out. Is anyone working on a revitalization of this project, or should I go start my own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T18:05:41-07:00","id":865236,"title":"","content":"It's pretty much dead. There's another Dragon fansplat in the works that's pretty much complete, though. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1h-o7bWocPX_6vO9PCfVYcCyApJMTudFcZGUCOmjw1Ok/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon: The Inheritance </a>(with a development thread <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?404998-nWoD-fansplat-Dragon-the-Inheritance\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T18:26:42-07:00","id":865247,"title":"","content":"Ah, yeah, this... I read through this one and had mixed feelings about it...<br /> <br /> Mainly though, I liked the concepts played with in Embers, so I was more interested in doing something with the remains of this project. Is anyone doing that already, or should I just go ahead and start?<br /> <br /> Edit: Part of this is that I HAVE characters I've made with Embers, as well as other things I've used from it, and I want to be able to do stuff with it in the future. For that, it needs to have the finer details hashed out better and the math updated to fully work with the new Second Edition rules...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 04-14-2016, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:52:43-07:00","id":866096,"title":"","content":"If no one tells me not to in a few days, I'm probably going to go to work reviving this project. If anyone has already started work on that, let me know.<br /> <br /> Conversely, if anyone wants to help, please PM me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T17:05:18-07:00","id":866172,"title":"","content":"To my knowledge, there's been nothing done. I've been a fan, but haven't had the time or energy to delve into writing for it.<br /> <br /> Go nuts, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T17:45:18-07:00","id":866184,"title":"","content":"There's been other dragon projects that have been risen up in the time between this one's.... completion and today.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/451589-dragon-the-inheritance\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...he-inheritance</a><br /> <br /> <br /> This one I recomend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-15-2016, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T18:21:38-07:00","id":866200,"title":"","content":"As I told WarDragon, I have that PDF. I've read it. I understand it.<br /> I like a lot of the aspects and implications this one has though, and want to revive it, not just give up on this plot and use the other one.<br /> <br /> Seeing as it sounds like no one else is actually reviving this one, I'm gonna put something together to show the direction I'm taking and start up a new project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T18:49:32-07:00","id":866204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=866200#post866200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I told WarDragon, I have that PDF. I've read it. I understand it.<br /> I like a lot of the aspects and implications this one has though, and want to revive it, not just give up on this plot and use the other one.<br /> <br /> Seeing as it sounds like no one else is actually reviving this one, I'm gonna put something together to show the direction I'm taking and start up a new project.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you insist. Go ahead and make your in thread.<br /> <br /> I'm sure a number of people here can pitch in. Maybe I will. Who knows","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T00:47:03-07:00","id":866300,"title":"","content":"Waiting on permission from CJC to use his artwork...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T03:11:04-07:00","id":866329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=866184#post866184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been other dragon projects that have been risen up in the time between this one's.... completion and today.<br /> This one I recomend.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really read previous comments, do you?...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> ---<br /> Anyway, I'm sure CJC wouldn't be offended if you picked this up since he dropped leading the project for now.<br /> (if you already PMed him that's the best first step.)<br /> <br /> I consider &quot;Inheritance&quot; a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; to Embers (it continues many of the same themes, and a lot of the rules are more playable or GMC appropriate - eg. what'd be fighting <i>power</i> in Embers is usually a fighting <i>style</i> (merit) in Inheritance, which is the GMC way).<br /> I don't think I'd be interested in a revival at the current time.<br /> <br /> <i>However</i> I am massively interested what your experience was like with Embers as a player. What did you play/what rules did you try, what happened? What did you like, compared to other WoD games/other rpgs? If you read Inheritance, is there anything you think only Embers has or does better? etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T18:01:46-07:00","id":866586,"title":"","content":"Embers was completed for 1st ed nWoD. There are some GMC hacks within it that help with the translation. It's around the 3rd bout of editing of which steam ran out (again, I might add.)<br /> <br /> As it currently stands, I believe it falls under the Dark Pack legality which since the translation from White Wolf/Onyx Path gets murky. However, I'm sure that CJC will be glad for anyone else to pick up the torch again. God knows he's had to suffer under that crown enough already.<br /> <br /> edit- Also, find it oddly fitting that the core of the game theme is enduring dwindling extinction and outlasting it and we are still talking about after all these years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 04-16-2016, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T02:57:44-07:00","id":867458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=866329#post866329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't really read previous comments, do you?...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I did. I replied that I was more interested in reviving this one. I WILL say that it's occurred to me that both of these things can exist simultaneously in the same setting, so running a crossover campaign someday HAS crossed my mind...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, I'm sure CJC wouldn't be offended if you picked this up since he dropped leading the project for now.<br /> (if you already PMed him that's the best first step.) </div> </div> </div>I figure he can't get that mad if the attempt was made, but you know how some artists can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I consider &quot;Inheritance&quot; a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; to Embers (it continues many of the same themes, and a lot of the rules are more playable or GMC appropriate - eg. what'd be fighting <i>power</i> in Embers is usually a fighting <i>style</i> (merit) in Inheritance, which is the GMC way).<br /> I don't think I'd be interested in a revival at the current time. </div> </div> </div>It has stylistic differences that I'm not too in to... I kinda like the idea that the Orobori have basically stolen the powers of the first gods man created for himself, and the implications of the Dreamtide connection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>However</i> I am massively interested what your experience was like with Embers as a player. What did you play/what rules did you try, what happened? What did you like, compared to other WoD games/other rpgs? If you read Inheritance, is there anything you think only Embers has or does better? etc. </div> </div> </div>Currently, the only Dragon character I have in play is a Slayer named Jean, who got his heart by killing a baron in the French Revolution. It's a mixed-party campaign involving Vampires, so I did this interesting thing where he was originally just a bulky red dragon with an axe, but after hanging out with the Ordo Dracul for too long, he's slowly been altered by the perception of what a &quot;Dragon&quot; looks like, so he's now basically the dragon from the Ordo Dracul logo. They've had him on retainer as a monster hunter for a few decades. I like playing him because it's like having a mini-garou on standby that WON'T kill the rest of the party, it's an immortal creature that ISN'T Vampires but is still pretty open-ended, and just the general aesthetics are really nice. Also he makes a good troll on the rest of the party, especially their Primogen benefactor.<br /> <br /> I also had the PCs encounter a Deep One in their back yard, offering to trade with them, in the last campaign I ran: we'd just gotten Werewolf: Second Edition and I wanted to throw a curve-ball that wasn't being hostile to them. Dragon had a lot of good ideas sort of floating around in there.<br /> <br /> It's hard for me to really remember much about the others, because I've had a ton of characters over the years and I really didn't get enough time with them, and it's hard to find GMs who have read Dragon in the first place. I'm probably going to end up having to run a game on some forum with a transitional ruleset...<br /> <br /> The two elements that I've enjoyed coming into play are the Dreamwalking ability and the simple fact that Dragons are basically creatures of what you think about them, and therefore, it stands that you can really screw with them by just believing things about them, like &quot;he kinda looks like the logo&quot;. That was something that we figured out which had a lot of potential, which I wanted to expand upon: forget about being petrified by insults, what if people's opinions of you could alter your very form? There were alot of things like that that, when we we thought through them further, had these really interesting implications. Oh! I also like the thing where they eat to get back power, that's made them fun, especially Jean, because he's obsessed with food, and the other players didn't know what he was, and hadn't read the book, so they thought he was just obsessed with food for some other odd reason like &quot;he took gluttony as a vice&quot;. (come on guys, Gluttony hasn't been a &quot;vice&quot; for over a year.)<br /> <br /> Also, there's something pleasing about CJCs little doodles in the first and third addition...<br /> <br /> Dislikes I've had are the morality system pushing that you have to &quot;rule&quot; something, and making us have to stretch the limits to make any campaign that isn't all about them, or that has them doing anything other than trying to &quot;rule&quot; a city. Stuff like that and the simple way it's written were things that have made it hard to actually get a lot of use out of the book, as it turns off the other main GM of my RP group: he's the kind of guy who insists that Mage is &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;overpowered&quot;, but has very obviously never even read it. I also (as you've probably guessed) didn't like a lot of the changes in 3rd edition: the Treasury has no precedent in World of Darkness and the Dreamtide stuff was really interesting to play around with, and a lot of the nerfing in general felt like they'd been pandering to the people who thought it was &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;overpowered&quot; when they hadn't actually read it. Mage took the route of doubling down on those people with the 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> So... My plan is to take a mix of 2nd and 3rd edition, keep that feeling of the raw power that comes with stolen divinity, and inject that dark, visceral nature that Vampire and Werewolf seem to have going for them. For the morality thing, I was thinking of making it more generalized: you got this heart by killing someone, and it was originally acquired by murdering a god, so you teeter between the Hubris of being too confident about the power, and the Guilt that you're not living up to the potential of the Heart. For the writing thing, I was thinking of taking more cues from Vampire, which has this pervasive darkness to it, but isn't so dark that it ruins the fun and interesting setting. (I'm one of those people who thinks WoD settings are best when you can justify really inane stuff, like werewolf tea-parties between the viscous and traumatic fight sequences, because just picture a garou in a frilly pink dress, daintily sipping tea)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=866586#post866586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embers was completed for 1st ed nWoD. There are some GMC hacks within it that help with the translation. It's around the 3rd bout of editing of which steam ran out (again, I might add.)<br /> <br /> As it currently stands, I believe it falls under the Dark Pack legality which since the translation from White Wolf/Onyx Path gets murky. However, I'm sure that CJC will be glad for anyone else to pick up the torch again. God knows he's had to suffer under that crown enough already.<br /> <br /> edit- Also, find it oddly fitting that the core of the game theme is enduring dwindling extinction and outlasting it and we are still talking about after all these years.</div> </div> </div> </div>SHOCK! Do you have any notes I might use for this endeavor? Would it be possible to chatter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T03:50:16-07:00","id":867472,"title":"","content":"I felt like popping in, because I'm actually the one running the game with the above dragon as a PC. Honestly, there are a lot of things I like about the rules and plenty of things I would want to work on to alter or fix.<br /> <br /> The newer GMC morality systems could improve Dragon much like they did for the other splats (providing a Hunger system for Beast, and Werewolf Harmony in particular are my favorite uses).<br /> <br /> I also loved the concept of the Dreamtide (having already been a fan of dream-space in RPGs in general...including in Changeling and to a lesser degree in Mage), and since Beast recently arrived and gave information on concepts like the Primordial Dream, it made so much sense to me that Dragons could inhabit a similar space.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I like Dragons is that they represent the raw power, both in the mental and the physical worlds, that has the ability to dominate all. Even though I've only used Dragon twice [Once for NPCs in a game I have on hiatus and once for the ongoing game above], It became a favorite of mine that I want to continue to experiment with. I love that dragons are so powerful, but they have no way to protect themselves, like Werewolves do, from mortal observation.<br /> <br /> The one idea that I had recently was that if I was to change something about the book, it would actually be how Breath is regained. While I can see interesting ideas when it comes to eating food or strange materials to regain energy, it seemed really mundane and strange in-play. It ended up boiling down to, when we played it, something like &quot;Oh, I had some food, can I get Breath back?&quot; and to me that felt very uninteresting. I realized that I liked the concept of eating to regain energy, and unlike in Werewolf it would be something that was encouraged and not as negative. Being someone who read Fairy Tail I can't help but think it would be cooler to have Dragons eat physical properties (Ie: Lightning, Steel, Fire, ect.) and perhaps have an option to devour spiritual material (Essence, Souls, ect.) and perhaps even concepts if it doesn't step on Changeling too much. Eating essence was actually something that came up in our game as a potential option, and to make things interesting I even allowed Jean to develop a Vampiric Ablution so that he could feed on blood (though it was more painful and brutal than the subtle vampiric kiss)<br /> <br /> Otherwise I don't really have any further suggestions, but I had been interested in reviving the game for a long time after watching the development stall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5298-novap","name":"NovaP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T06:46:16-07:00","id":867534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did. I replied that I was more interested in reviving this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Want directed at you. The guy who linked it a 2nd time.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:02:40-07:00","id":867540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867534#post867534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Want directed at you. The guy who linked it a 2nd time.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My fault. I think was half suffering from a lack of sleep at the time and forgot it was already linked. <br /> <br /> Would you want me to delete it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:59:26-07:00","id":867628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867534#post867534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Want directed at you. The guy who linked it a 2nd time.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh... Neither of you have avatars, and I got you mixed up...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T12:10:10-07:00","id":867718,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SHOCK! Do you have any notes I might use for this endeavor? Would it be possible to chatter?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the notes should be on this board. I had a few PMs from the other board that didn't make it due to the change over from WW to OP forums. Basically my advice is simply understand the themes and mood at play. The main mood of Dragon is entering into a species is hovering near it's end. Empires in disrepair, enemies hounding at the gates, etc. That being said, there is hope. All is not lost, and embers can set the fire anew. I believe we pounded the point too hard of the first part of the sentence while not enough effort was put into the second part.<br /> <br /> The theme is divine right. The empire maybe in disrepair but it is still an empire. An empire with assets, levers, and buttons to change the face of the world and you're now in charge of dealing with it. You forcefully made that choice as well. Others splats can tell rightfully tell themselves that they were dragged kicking and screaming into their current state. A dragon in Embers can not (I see this as the main dividing line between Ember and Inheritance as well.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dislikes I've had are the morality system pushing that you have to &quot;rule&quot; something, and making us have to stretch the limits to make any campaign that isn't all about them, or that has them doing anything other than trying to &quot;rule&quot; a city. Stuff like that and the simple way it's written were things that have made it hard to actually get a lot of use out of the book, as it turns off the other main GM of my RP group: he's the kind of guy who insists that Mage is &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;overpowered&quot;, but has very obviously never even read it. I also (as you've probably guessed) didn't like a lot of the changes in 3rd edition: the Treasury has no precedent in World of Darkness and the Dreamtide stuff was really interesting to play around with, and a lot of the nerfing in general felt like they'd been pandering to the people who thought it was &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;overpowered&quot; when they hadn't actually read it. Mage took the route of doubling down on those people with the 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>on the morality system:<br /> <br /> For context, we went with &quot;A dragon king&quot; due to pinning down the game's concept back when it was still in it's conception phase. We took a look at the WoD like that was out at the time and asked our selves, what do these splats do.<br /> <br /> For vampire, they politic<br /> <br /> For werewolf, they hunt<br /> <br /> For mage, they explore,<br /> <br /> For the created, they journey.<br /> <br /> For changeling, they dream.<br /> <br /> For hunter, they stand watch.<br /> <br /> For giest, They guide.<br /> <br /> and you can continue this line of thought for the others as well.<br /> <br /> So with that line of thought, what does a game about Dragons do? How does a game about powerful creatures who hoard resources with tempers work in a game of horror/urban fantasy? In the end, we went with &quot;For dragon, they govern.&quot; due seeing how the mandate of heaven worked in Chinese thought and how easily playable the concept was.<br /> <br /> now back to the complaint: yes, that has been an issue has been brought up and I believe that stuff like Maidens have been suggested. I don't remember if it made it into the new ed but territory is viewed less as a brick and mortar and rather control over a person, group and/or physical place. This should be more adjustable for players.<br /> <br /> As for the Treasury: This is been an attempt to get away from saying point blank that &quot;Yes this is the Astral.&quot; and more to hammer home the Dragon's access to resources and right to rule. If it helps any, think of it as a Dragon themed part of the Astral where Dragons can change things in accordance to their wishes.<br /> <br /> As for the Deep ones: I don't know how CJC intends to see them but I viewed them as competitors and mirror/foils to Dragons. They are a force that knows the Dragons time is ending and are starting to close in to take control of the role that Dragons have. They are more deeply tyrannical than Dragons and willing to engage in the worst abuses and atrocities without a second thought. Also planned on using deep sea creatures for inspiration. This sadly, didn't get hammered out and was cut out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 04-18-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:12:52-07:00","id":867765,"title":"","content":"So, is Embers still going? I had thought (to my great disappointment) that it had been abandoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:32:26-07:00","id":867784,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how pertinent or useful at all this thought is, considering I have at best skimmed some parts of this project and I can't seem to find the comment I was going to respond to which talked about Dragon sputtering and rekindling to life again just like the themes that were planned for it but...<br /> <br /> I feel that, in line with the sort of image <i>The Embers</i> as a subtitle invokes and the suggested focus of divine right in the face of rapidly fading glory, there is a lot of inspiration in theme and symbolism to take from the Dark Souls series, in particular Dark Souls 3. It's hard to explain my exact reasoning, but I can say there's an ambience and an inherent quality to the conflict there lent by its mythological backdrop and the obscured and crumbling meaning around you that... feel proper for the kind of game Dragon <i>could be</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-18-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:45:20-07:00","id":867829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, the only Dragon character I have in play is a Slayer named Jean etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sound sweet as FU&amp;@. Thank you so much for sharing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> +1<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably going to end up having to run a game on some forum with a transitional ruleset...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you need playtesters and I'm still around at the time, I wanted to play a psycho bride (with Bond of Brood) who challenges powerful dragons/crime lords to curry favor with his half-fossilized bf who is now unable to protect his territory...after SHE had stabbed him following a lovers' spat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! I also like the thing where they eat to get back power, that's made them fun, especially Jean, because he's obsessed with food, and the other players didn't know what he was, and hadn't read the book, so they thought he was just obsessed with food for some other odd reason like &quot;he took gluttony as a vice&quot;. (come on guys, Gluttony hasn't been a &quot;vice&quot; for over a year.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I took a step back over the course of this thread, I began to take the view that too many times regaining power points becomes an obligatory task that players timeskip anyway, so I think a quick and easy way that can lead to amusing scenes like eating fuelstuff can be better than some elaborate way.<br /> <br /> Did you roll to gain Breath (as the original rules advise)? If I'd have changed something, it'd have been to have each fuel give you a fixed amount of Breath plus penalties (to skip having to pick up the dice), so I'm curious how that original rule worked for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the simple fact that Dragons are basically creatures of what you think about them, and therefore, it stands that you can really screw with them by just believing things about them, like &quot;he kinda looks like the logo&quot;. That was something that we figured out which had a lot of potential, which I wanted to expand upon: forget about being petrified by insults, what if people's opinions of you could alter your very form? There were alot of things like that that, when we we thought through them further, had these really interesting implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I thought dragon forms being created from human perception was an Inheritance thing.<br /> Was this also in Embers? Or is this something you'd like to add?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also loved the concept of the Dreamtide (having already been a fan of dream-space in RPGs in general...including in Changeling and to a lesser degree in Mage), and since Beast recently arrived and gave information on concepts like the Primordial Dream, it made so much sense to me that Dragons could inhabit a similar space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> What I didn't like was the part that you had to find humans whose dreams to enter, that made you just a dream-thief, thematically and mechanically identical to Changeling.<br /> I'm sure a dragon, with a body that half belongs to that other collective dreamrealm, can cross the boarder between realms more dynamically.<br /> <br /> What I'd have preferred was the idea that there is a sort of ancestral memory presents in humans (and other species) and a sort of instinctive fear from big lizards, a remnant from the time <br /> (and that this possibly continued forther down, which is why the Deep Ones, the sea-creatures are the Dragon's enemies).<br /> But it seemed natural to me that the Astral realms (being realms of human thought) would have such a neighbor-realm to them, where more basic thoughts and memories from from humankind's evolutionary past could reside...And that this was the home that dragons drew on.<br /> <br /> I haven't read Beast so I do not know how the Primodeal Dream works and if this was anything close to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the morality thing, I was thinking of making it more generalized: you got this heart by killing someone, and it was originally acquired by murdering a god, so you teeter between the Hubris of being too confident about the power, and the Guilt that you're not living up to the potential of the Heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds workable; dragon pride (DESERVED pride) is a trope.<br /> A dynamic sort of pride (Hubris or whatever you'll call it) sounds perfectly sound to me.<br /> <br /> (Admittedly I was one who vouched for a &quot;Mandate of Heaven&quot; type morality, but a broader one works too, I guess.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867458#post867458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the writing thing, I was thinking of taking more cues from Vampire, which has this pervasive darkness to it, but isn't so dark that it ruins the fun and interesting setting. (I'm one of those people who thinks WoD settings are best when you can justify really inane stuff, like werewolf tea-parties between the viscous and traumatic fight sequences, because just picture a garou in a frilly pink dress, daintily sipping tea)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> more questions:<br /> <br /> Each power having 5 dots and a need to spend exp for essentially +1 bonuses instead of new powers, yay or nay?<br /> For example, have you tried to put dots in Flying essentially just to improve speed? Has it ever bothered you that you're paying for +1 bonuses often instead of new powers? (I'd have listed them as weeknesses in Embers)<br /> <br /> How did you like CJC's power list? I find them a bit more simplicistic/D&amp;Dish and dreamed of more flavorful powers (Cadmus' spell that lets you create warriors in exchange for nails or blood, blessing of youth on others, weather magic and so on), I take it that they worked just fine for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T15:44:47-07:00","id":867877,"title":"","content":"Well, since people are asking, I think I'll share some of the thoughts I had right before I resigned.<br /> <br /> I did consider trying to finish <b>Dragon the Embers</b> on my own, as I had in the gaps between both the collapse of the first-stage development (when I unintentionally drove Gepetto off) and the collapse of the second-stage development (wherein I produced the document which became the Phase Two PDF). However, I was and continue to be woefully unable to wrap my head around the second edition; I was comfortable with the idea of hacks when Mirrors launched, but God Machine Chronicles swiftly transitioning into Second Edition and then the Chronicles of Darkness... it was too much for me. I couldn't keep pace, and it drove me mad (you can see my breakdown if you read the whole thread; I snapped and lashed out at everybody... unprovoked. I still regret it). I found that I could no longer shape the game to my vision. With other projects on my plate, I gave up on Dragon the Embers and crossed my fingers somebody else could take up the torch.<br /> To put this into perspective, I'd like to mention that I joined the project (which was already in motion) back when White Wolf started advertising Geist as a new game line. That was the summer of 2009; that should give you an idea of how long people have been working on this game.<br /> <br /> I was unhappy about the loss of the Dreamtide; I rather liked the idea and abandoned it from pressure of splat identity; one of the biggest criticisms at the time was overlap, and the Dreamtide shared much with Changeling even if the similarity was unintentional. The Treasury was a frantic attempt to restore some semblance of mysticism to the game. That said, I rather like the story with the five dragons and the birth of the universe, and it's equally viable as an explanation for the Dreamtide (since the Ocean Oroboros in the Astral Realm would essentially be a pool of ancient dragon blood). There was a suggestion that Dragons would enter the Treasury by circling (flying or running in concentric circles); perhaps this could be added as an entrance to the Dreamtide.<br /> <br /> Fossilization was an attempt to make the Oroboroi more fragile and it was in its first iteration when the project ended; this too was a reaction to balance criticisms. It needn't have been as integrated as it was; instead of being a reaction to insults it would work better as a reaction to the loss of Heart, and an explanation as to why the Oroboroi don't leave monstrous bodies littering the world when they die. They do, but they're statues.<br /> <b>The unfinished revision:</b> For each day an Oroboros does not make physical contact with her Heart, a piece of her body fossilizes (erase one Health dot). Fossilization can be halted by making contact with her Heart or by claiming a new Heart. It is reversed by tearing away the fossilized flesh (inflict Aggravated damage to restore dots; costs experience). This is what kills Oroboroi who have had their Heart stolen (in lieu of immediate death), which would give players the option to recover their Heart or find a new Heart if that plot plays out.<br /> <br /> As for the problem with gorging to recover Breath; that was being addressed with the new Assets system for Breath; an Oroboros stores her faith in her possessions (people [maidens], places [provinces], and things [hoards]) and draws from them when she needs to muster supernatural power. The ways to replenish (interact with the object over the course of a scene; eat people; or set back the Asset for a quick fix) were in need of some fine tuning, but I believe this to be one of the best systems introduced into the game.<br /> <br /> There were other promising changes; such as the new Y-Splats (though the 5th one wasn't shaping up and should have been pruned), the Edicts (which replaced the unwieldly &quot;power&quot; philosophies but needed more design synergy [and possibly the pruning of the elemental Edicts] ), and the more in-depth presentation of the Shayatin (formerly Deep Ones) and Nidhoggr (formerly &quot;old&quot; Dragons) as spearheaded by ExplodingFrogs. Still, the sticking points were prominent and unresolved, such as the issues with Mandate as a Morality substitute. It was easy to see where problems existed, but the solutions were not clear.<br /> I had some other ideas to improve the game that were in their early stages; I considered breaking Furnace into two separate Potency stats &quot;Earth&quot; and &quot;Sky&quot;; one for Ablutions and one for Edicts. When that didn't pan out in my head, I considered using &quot;Earth&quot; as a replacement for Mandate with breaking points referring to the psychological corruption of power distancing the Oroboros from mortals (a superiority complex). My troubles with the second edition changeover got in the way, though, and I couldn't resolve them.<br /> <br /> I urge you all to take what you like from the second and third edition and use it as a baseline for a new effort. There are things which need to be thrown away. There are things which need to be changed. For instance, Chronicles of Darkness books have a completely different format from 1st edition nWoD. Take what's here and craft it into the game you would want to play, and I will be happy that something came from the effort of all of these great people. Remember; there are ghosts in the attic and I'm one of them; I can't take an active role in development if a revival is to succeed.<br /> If I can give one last bit of advice, it would be this: read an official splat and try to answer the questions it asks within the framework of the Oroboroi. This is how I wrote the first edition, basing it off the questions which were asked (and answered) in Werewolf the Forsaken and Mage the Awakening. It really is quite helpful in structuring your approach to the fan work.<br /> <br /> [Ninja'd] Actually Vree, appearance being based on personal perception of what defines a dragon has always been a part of the splat. Having the perceptions of others control that appearance, though, is something Rockstar came up with and is an awesome idea.[/Ninja'd]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 04-18-2016, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T23:50:44-07:00","id":868231,"title":"","content":"Adding to what CJC said about starting a new splat, any of the stuff from my attempt, Dragon: the Hunted, is open for your use. I do intend to get in on this but I don't think I have the time or inspiration to carry that one all the way through without a good deal of help. So please, use the stones from my castle to help build a newer, less crumbly one. Or help me rebuild mine.<br /> <br /> If a new one is started though, if someone could send me a PM to make sure I don't miss it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:42:45-07:00","id":868499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867784#post867784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how pertinent or useful at all this thought is, considering I have at best skimmed some parts of this project and I can't seem to find the comment I was going to respond to which talked about Dragon sputtering and rekindling to life again just like the themes that were planned for it but...<br /> <br /> I feel that, in line with the sort of image <i>The Embers</i> as a subtitle invokes and the suggested focus of divine right in the face of rapidly fading glory, there is a lot of inspiration in theme and symbolism to take from the Dark Souls series, in particular Dark Souls 3. It's hard to explain my exact reasoning, but I can say there's an ambience and an inherent quality to the conflict there lent by its mythological backdrop and the obscured and crumbling meaning around you that... feel proper for the kind of game Dragon <i>could be</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you bro. Dark souls is all about the glory of the Age of Fire dying out. The world is on it's last leg, the creatures of darkness are poised to take its place.<br /> <br /> There is definite parallel to take from dark souls. Such as its Fadding glory &amp; Overwhelming responsibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T22:31:34-07:00","id":870949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867718#post867718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, there is hope. All is not lost, and embers can set the fire anew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... What? What is the &quot;hope&quot;? I thought there was no way to get new hearts, unless you're meaning something else...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You forcefully made that choice as well. Others splats can tell rightfully tell themselves that they were dragged kicking and screaming into their current state. A dragon in Embers can not (I see this as the main dividing line between Ember and Inheritance as well.) </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a major factor in Embers. It's where I got the idea for a Guilt vs Hubris morality: they TOOK power, now they must take responsibility. You do not see an Orobori who doesn't have something amazing going on, at least not a healthy one, because the simple act of taking the scarce hearts is an act of self-elevation and original sin which must be atoned for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For context, we went with &quot;A dragon king&quot; due to pinning down the game's concept back when it was still in it's conception phase. We took a look at the WoD like that was out at the time and asked our selves, what do these splats do. </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok. This is the kind of information I wanted from you guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So with that line of thought, what does a game about Dragons do? How does a game about powerful creatures who hoard resources with tempers work in a game of horror/urban fantasy? In the end, we went with &quot;For dragon, they govern.&quot; due seeing how the mandate of heaven worked in Chinese thought and how easily playable the concept was.<br /> <br /> now back to the complaint: yes, that has been an issue has been brought up and I believe that stuff like Maidens have been suggested. I don't remember if it made it into the new ed but territory is viewed less as a brick and mortar and rather control over a person, group and/or physical place. This should be more adjustable for players. </div> </div> </div>See, I'm thinking we can get away with &quot;they don't have a true role in the ecology, so their needs are less definite.&quot; and make it about a more demigod style &quot;you need to be worthy of your power&quot; type deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Treasury: This is been an attempt to get away from saying point blank that &quot;Yes this is the Astral.&quot; and more to hammer home the Dragon's access to resources and right to rule. If it helps any, think of it as a Dragon themed part of the Astral where Dragons can change things in accordance to their wishes. </div> </div> </div>Ok, understanding this a bit better, but I'm still more into the original Dreamtide stuff...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Deep ones: I don't know how CJC intends to see them but I viewed them as competitors and mirror/foils to Dragons. They are a force that knows the Dragons time is ending and are starting to close in to take control of the role that Dragons have. They are more deeply tyrannical than Dragons and willing to engage in the worst abuses and atrocities without a second thought. Also planned on using deep sea creatures for inspiration. This sadly, didn't get hammered out and was cut out. </div> </div> </div>I had what I think is a better idea of the unwritten meta: are you familiar with the plot of Starcraft 2: Heart of the Swarm? The Primal Zerg.<br /> <br /> My idea is that the Deep Ones are literally from the Deep End of the Dreamtide, where raw concept is so plentiful it downs everything else out. While Dragons cast it aside to assume stable forms, the Deep Ones swam in the chaos, becoming eyes of their own storms of chaos. They want things like emotions and Ablutions and whatever else because, to them, that is a new stable-concept to add to their ever-changing form.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867829#post867829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took a step back over the course of this thread, I began to take the view that too many times regaining power points becomes an obligatory task that players timeskip anyway, so I think a quick and easy way that can lead to amusing scenes like eating fuelstuff can be better than some elaborate way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Eating food works because it's simple enough to get a small amount, but is increasingly inconvenient in larger quantities. You can get 2000 calories a day easy, and spending another 2000 isn't too hard either. But if you burn 9 breath in 1 battle... Drink some Gasoline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did you roll to gain Breath (as the original rules advise)? If I'd have changed something, it'd have been to have each fuel give you a fixed amount of Breath plus penalties (to skip having to pick up the dice), so I'm curious how that original rule worked for you. </div> </div> </div>We didn't roll for food, because it's a bit ridiculous to roll to keep down a chicken sandwich, but we DID just have a bit where he literally poured a gallon jug of gasoline directly down his throat, like a car. Basically, I took 3 turns, rolling each time, and spending a willpower just to go through with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huh, I thought dragon forms being created from human perception was an Inheritance thing.<br /> Was this also in Embers? Or is this something you'd like to add? </div> </div> </div>This concept was implied, but not gotten into. That's something I wanted to elaborate from what's currently there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I didn't like was the part that you had to find humans whose dreams to enter, that made you just a dream-thief, thematically and mechanically identical to Changeling.<br /> I'm sure a dragon, with a body that half belongs to that other collective dreamrealm, can cross the boarder between realms more dynamically. </div> </div> </div>See, making it simpler like that is a temptation, but being able to do that might make them kind of powerful, like how Uratha can pass into the Twilight to deal with stuff: realize that they can use this to escape or be stealthy. It's fine, but it seems like something that should take more work, unless we decide that that's a power we want. Right now, that doesn't sound like a direction we want to take, but we can playtest it to see how it works...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I'd have preferred was the idea that there is a sort of ancestral memory presents in humans (and other species) and a sort of instinctive fear from big lizards, a remnant from the time (and that this possibly continued forther down, which is why the Deep Ones, the sea-creatures are the Dragon's enemies). But it seemed natural to me that the Astral realms (being realms of human thought) would have such a neighbor-realm to them, where more basic thoughts and memories from from humankind's evolutionary past could reside...And that this was the home that dragons drew on. </div> </div> </div>Uh huh, ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't read Beast so I do not know how the Primodeal Dream works and if this was anything close to it. </div> </div> </div>From what I've been told / shown, it's similar enough that Dragons might actually be related to Beasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That sounds workable; dragon pride (DESERVED pride) is a trope.<br /> A dynamic sort of pride (Hubris or whatever you'll call it) sounds perfectly sound to me.<br /> (Admittedly I was one who vouched for a &quot;Mandate of Heaven&quot; type morality, but a broader one works too, I guess.) </div> </div> </div>It's also somewhat 2 sided:<br /> Too good of a self image leads to Hubris, which leads to overreaching and an eventual fall, but also means a stronger self image for resisting the &quot;reimagining&quot; problem.<br /> Poor self-esteem, meanwhile, is a pretty serious issue for creatures which live with the Guilt of having taken power which they aren't using properly, AND makes them more susceptible into being reimagined as something worse.... Or better: Guilt has its own uses which can pull an Orobori out of their depression.<br /> The middle ground is where things are healthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each power having 5 dots and a need to spend exp for essentially +1 bonuses instead of new powers, yay or nay?<br /> For example, have you tried to put dots in Flying essentially just to improve speed? Has it ever bothered you that you're paying for +1 bonuses often instead of new powers? (I'd have listed them as weeknesses in Embers) </div> </div> </div>This has occurred to me as a problem, and yeah, it's something to be addressed, moving forward: Ablution dots should feel significant, because the first is giving you a new power, so the second should make that power twice as effective in some way, whether it's just a stronger version or something new entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How did you like CJC's power list? I find them a bit more simplicistic/D&amp;Dish and dreamed of more flavorful powers (Cadmus' spell that lets you create warriors in exchange for nails or blood, blessing of youth on others, weather magic and so on), I take it that they worked just fine for you? </div> </div> </div>Not sure which one was CJC's, but yeah, expect expansions to what Ablutions can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867877#post867877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did consider trying to finish <b>Dragon the Embers</b> on my own, as I had in the gaps between both the collapse of the first-stage development (when I unintentionally drove Gepetto off) and the collapse of the second-stage development (wherein I produced the document which became the Phase Two PDF). However, I was and continue to be woefully unable to wrap my head around the second edition; I was comfortable with the idea of hacks when Mirrors launched, but God Machine Chronicles swiftly transitioning into Second Edition and then the Chronicles of Darkness...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that hit a lot of us suddenly, and I've had mixed feelings about the new direction... Maybe now that we've all had time to get an idea of what the Chronicles of Darkness should be like, we'll be able to adapt it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To put this into perspective, I'd like to mention that I joined the project (which was already in motion) back when White Wolf started advertising Geist as a new game line. That was the summer of 2009; that should give you an idea of how long people have been working on this game. </div> </div> </div>Huh, I didn't know about that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was unhappy about the loss of the Dreamtide; I rather liked the idea and abandoned it from pressure of splat identity; one of the biggest criticisms at the time was overlap, and the Dreamtide shared much with Changeling even if the similarity was unintentional. The Treasury was a frantic attempt to restore some semblance of mysticism to the game. That said, I rather like the story with the five dragons and the birth of the universe, and it's equally viable as an explanation for the Dreamtide (since the Ocean Oroboros in the Astral Realm would essentially be a pool of ancient dragon blood). </div> </div> </div>And see, this is what I was saying was the mistake with 3rd edition: you shouldn't listen to people who haven't played your game. When people who had never played Mage railed about how first edition was &quot;broken&quot;, &quot;overpowered&quot;, and &quot;made the other books meaningless&quot; during first edition, and it was time to make the second edition, White Wolf doubled down on the core of what it was. This is what I'd like to do with Dragon: see what they don't like about tone and what misunderstandings might be there, but double down on what the game is actually about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There was a suggestion that Dragons would enter the Treasury by circling (flying or running in concentric circles); perhaps this could be added as an entrance to the Dreamtide. </div> </div> </div>Weird, but ok. I'll keep that in mind...<br /> <br /> Edit: I just had an idea. We should incorporate a sort of &quot;dream-tide magic&quot; to go with the Edicts/Purviews<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fossilization was an attempt to make the Oroboroi more fragile and it was in its first iteration when the project ended; this too was a reaction to balance criticisms. </div> </div> </div>Once again, as much as I like what Fossilization COULD be, I'll probably be pretty cold to balance criticisms, seeing as unlike those people I've ACTUALLY PLAYED THIS GAME, which was ACTUALLY INTENDED FOR PEOPLE LIKE ME AND NOT THEM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It needn't have been as integrated as it was; instead of being a reaction to insults it would work better as a reaction to the loss of Heart, and an explanation as to why the Oroboroi don't leave monstrous bodies littering the world when they die. They do, but they're statues. </div> </div> </div>I was gonna use it for what happened to the Dragons: we don't find their skeletons because dreamstuff doesn't leave that, it just turns to stone. I have this feeling that Dragons have a bit of an unreal quality to them too, like you might find ones that look like living paintings or even stained-glass, but rarely one that looks like mundane animals under close scrutiny...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The unfinished revision:</b> For each day an Oroboros does not make physical contact with her Heart, a piece of her body fossilizes (erase one Health dot). Fossilization can be halted by making contact with her Heart or by claiming a new Heart. It is reversed by tearing away the fossilized flesh (inflict Aggravated damage to restore dots; costs experience). This is what kills Oroboroi who have had their Heart stolen (in lieu of immediate death), which would give players the option to recover their Heart or find a new Heart if that plot plays out. </div> </div> </div>YES. Because that actually gives you a way to respond to heart-stealers. Granted, it means that &quot;ominous drums&quot; needs to be rewritten, but it's probably better this way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the problem with gorging to recover Breath; that was being addressed with the new Assets system for Breath; an Oroboros stores her faith in her possessions (people [maidens], places [provinces], and things [hoards]) and draws from them when she needs to muster supernatural power. The ways to replenish (interact with the object over the course of a scene; eat people; or set back the Asset for a quick fix) were in need of some fine tuning, but I believe this to be one of the best systems introduced into the game. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and I wasn't really into that change. The old system was actually interesting and felt like it had more direct potential. Also, it felt like you were trying to nerf them due to criticism by adding more unusual concepts, when they really don't need anything...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I urge you all to take what you like from the second and third edition and use it as a baseline for a new effort. There are things which need to be thrown away. There are things which need to be changed. </div> </div> </div>That's the plan, yeah. Rebuild 2nd edition with 3rd edition's patches, then redo it all from there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For instance, Chronicles of Darkness books have a completely different format from 1st edition nWoD. </div> </div> </div>Oh that... Yeah... Not even sure what they're going for there... It seems to be a bit haphazard and I was thinking of doing something a little different...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take what's here and craft it into the game you would want to play, and I will be happy that something came from the effort of all of these great people. Remember; there are ghosts in the attic and I'm one of them; I can't take an active role in development if a revival is to succeed. </div> </div> </div>Alright, you be the antecedent, I'll go ahead and assemble a den to reforge it with...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I can give one last bit of advice, it would be this: read an official splat and try to answer the questions it asks within the framework of the Oroboroi. This is how I wrote the first edition, basing it off the questions which were asked (and answered) in Werewolf the Forsaken and Mage the Awakening. It really is quite helpful in structuring your approach to the fan work. </div> </div> </div>I'll make sure to do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [Ninja'd] Actually Vree, appearance being based on personal perception of what defines a dragon has always been a part of the splat. Having the perceptions of others control that appearance, though, is something Rockstar came up with and is an awesome idea.[/Ninja'd] </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it really just follows, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=867784#post867784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that, in line with the sort of image <i>The Embers</i> as a subtitle invokes and the suggested focus of divine right in the face of rapidly fading glory, there is a lot of inspiration in theme and symbolism to take from the Dark Souls series, in particular Dark Souls 3. It's hard to explain my exact reasoning, but I can say there's an ambience and an inherent quality to the conflict there lent by its mythological backdrop and the obscured and crumbling meaning around you that... feel proper for the kind of game Dragon <i>could be</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=868499#post868499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel you bro. Dark souls is all about the glory of the Age of Fire dying out. The world is on it's last leg, the creatures of darkness are poised to take its place.<br /> There is definite parallel to take from dark souls. Such as its Fadding glory &amp; Overwhelming responsibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds good, but someone else is going to have to inject this: I don't play a lot of console games so I'm not familiar with Dark Souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 04-23-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T22:34:12-07:00","id":872129,"title":"","content":"Ok, before I start that other thread, it sounds like this is the new direction we're taking. I have a code-name for this project that's been floating around in my head, so I'ma use it now.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Dragon Rekindled: The Orobori Chronicles</span><br /> A New Direction</b></span></span><br /> Basically, we're going to be taking 2nd-edition as a base, things we liked from 3rd, and adding in new stuff that we're coming up with. The new edition will be built for compatibility with the new God Machine and Chronicles setting and rules.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd Edition</b> - It sounds like we'll be going back to the original Dreamtide storyline, because that works, using more of the old nomenclature, and building onto what was there.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd Edition</b> - The re-differentiation of schools and expansion of edicts seem to work, and there were new mechanics and ablutions that would be nice to bring in. The fact that losing a Heart isn't insta-death looks like a huge help for party-paranoia. I think the problem with 3rd edition was that there was a lot of response to unqualified criticism, but there were still some nice additions.<br /> <br /> <b>New Additions</b> - It sounds like we're going to expand on the Dreamtide origins of Dragon's powers, including things like Reimagining, &quot;Divine&quot; Power, and Dream Sorcery. Also seeing an overhaul will be the Integrity system, which will have less emphasis on &quot;being in charge&quot; and more emphasis on Guilt, Hubris, and balancing Divine powers with lingering Humanity. On top of that, we'll probably have to rewrite the Ominous Drums story eventually...<br /> <br /> <b>Research</b> - It will be very important to read up on older stories about dragons of this nature, especially since there is a strong tendency among this generation's writers to pull things from things like anime and video-games without really understanding them. For more recent fiction, I can recommend <i>The Dragon Knight</i>, <i>The Hobbit</i>, and <i>Dragonheart</i> as good sources of inspiration for talking dragons living with humans. (especially Dragon Knight, because it's directly about a human who gets magical powers and a dragon form) For older fiction, we should look at older accounts of Dragons (obviously), especially old chri</span>stian lore and grimoires.<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> Stuff like <i>Walking with Dragons</i> MAY be useful, but I WILL note that the Orobori are imagined creatures and don't have to follow real-life physics. There's also the matter of philosophy in play here: I already have ideas for pulling things in from Rene Descartes' meditations on divinity and Plato's concept of forms and purity, as well as the works of Machivelli and Anton Lavey.<br /> <br /> <b>Contemplation</b> - Standing rule: everything we get into here should be thought about in dual terms of &quot;how does this fit into the established meta?&quot; and &quot;what would happen if this was in the real world?&quot; Because that's where it will be. Even the Dreamtide is merely an extension of a real thing, because humans dream and imagine things. Don't have dragons doing insane things unless you've thought through why they make sense and how the world would react<br /> <br /> <b>God Machine</b> - The Meta will be partially re-written, both to fine tune the old stuff and to incorporate the setting with the God Machine, as well as the World Of Darkness setting in general, the interconnections of which is often under-anticipated by people who haven't read a few of the Mage and expanded-lore / mechanics books along with the core books. (trust me, once you've seen a bunch of them, it all fits together: thanks Exarchs.) As per the other books, affected mortals will see their own appendix with powerful stats.<br /> <br /> <b>Other Books</b> - I've always seen Dragons as a cross between Vampires, Werewolves, and Shape Changers, with a bit of Mage and Changeling lore in there. Like Vampires, they must feed on something relatively simple to regain their pool, but they also need to spend one a day to simply survive, and pretty much have to use it to heal themselves. Like Werewolves they have these powerful forms which are holdovers from a realm which they can go to but is now hostile to them. Like Shape Changers, their alternate forms are highly varied and the &quot;War Form&quot; doesn't make them go nuts. Mage and Changeling deal heavily in the concept of things made of concepts. Unlike the other books, however, Dragons don't have much going on in the way of boons and banes for having non-aware humans see their powers, and they're very rare, so meeting each other isn't going to be common, nor is meeting someone who knows what they are. Unlike the other stuff, Dragons were Outsiders, so Orobori don't have a pre-built niche in the Supernatural Ecology, which is something that (among the most major books) only Promethian deals with.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Formatting Thoughts</b> - The new format is a bit confusing, and as much as I like the new content, I feel like we might want to have fewer chapters which seem to ramble on: it's been increasingly hard to navigate the books when trying to find rules or build characters. I'm gonna suggest we try and be a bit less complicated than that, at least for now. Also, I REALLY like the thing that books like Scion have done, where you see an actual party being backstoried, formed, and going on an adventure in the game-world, which is then explained through the chapters. That might be really effective with Dragon, which means that we would have to write in a new story, possibly from playtesting sessions, at the expense of the old one. (as much as I like it)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>A General TODO list.</b></span></span></span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Build a Transitional Edition of Embers for use as a starting point.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Start work on the Playtesting Draft, building a complete meta, iceburg, and rewriting old mechanics.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Get feedback to see what people would build with these rules, and make sure they are either able to be made or that a clear reason is given for why they can't.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Finish the initial Playtesting Draft of Orobori Chronicles.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Run a Playtesting game with some good writers who know World of Darkness well (NOW SEEKING!)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Build the full book while running those sessions</span></li> </ol><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Remaining Questions</b></span></span></span><ul><li>Did anyone write down notes on things like the old playtests, meta-discussions, and unwritten lore?</li> <li>How do we feel about the new morality system I've put forward? Is there a better idea?</li> <li>How should the &quot;magic&quot; the Dragons brought from the Dream-Tide work? How do the Orobori enter the Dreamtide? (I'm thinking Jade is required here)<ul><li>How hard should it be to cross into the Dreamtide?</li> </ul></li> <li>How should we respond to the new format? How important is trying to replicate it?</li> <li>IS there a &quot;hope&quot;, as Shock seemed to imply, or is this really a game about people running around trying to steal Hearts from a depleting supply?</li> <li>Who's actually joining me here? I can't do this by myself.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Before I finish here...</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Is there <b>anything</b> else that we need to discuss before I go ahead and move forward?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T00:01:26-07:00","id":872178,"title":"","content":"Wow. You are the lead this project deserves; that was an excellent mission statement.<br /> <br /> With regards to your remaining questions...<ul><li>Old playtests, meta-discussions, unwritten lore<ul><li>I don't have many lingering notes from old playtests, though I can say the Ablution system worked better with a static experience cost rather than a scaling one. Since Chronicles made that baseline, it's a big win for Dragon. I'd say price them like merits; players shouldn't hesitate to spend experience on more Ablutions.</li> <li>The Asset system was built to redirect fuel recovery to the themes of the game. Since those themes were--at the time--divine right, Breath recovery became affiliated with tending to those Assets. I know you intend to remove that system (and as project lead you should not let me influence you on that matter, see... I'm haunting you), but it dove-tails well with eating to regain Breath.<ul><li>The fast approach to replenish Breath is to eat something (we shifted towards living things, like dragons munching on livestock, but drinking gasoline would still work), whereas the 'healthy' approach is tending to your possessions.</li> <li>You could discard Province as a type of Asset and just keep it as Hoard and Maiden, since so many European dragon stories involve greed and kidnapping.</li> <li>Even if you completely discard the Asset system for a more traditional energy pool, you should consider keeping Hoards and Maidens in some fashion, preferably as Breath production mechanics or merits.</li> </ul></li> <li>Unwritten Lore<ul><li>Antagonists<ul><li>Chimerae<ul><li>Chimerae are animals which consume Orobori hearts. This transforms them into beings which are essentially identical to an Oroboros (apply the Embers template to their animal stats). However, being that they are animals, their shape is defined by their own perception of what a 'dragon' should be (an apex predator).</li> <li>A chimera's idea of what makes the optimum apex predator warps them into increasingly complex monstrosities (as they see a biological advantage they perceive as useful, they incorporate it into their body).</li> <li>It also drives them to violence; Chimerae are incredibly territorial and kill humans, supernaturals, and anything else to establish their hunting grounds. Chimerae are generally made when a foolish Oroboros thinks it might be neat to have an immortal pet.</li> </ul></li> <li>Phoenixi<ul><li>Orobori who learn the story of the five dragons and the creation of the universe (or rather, the creation of the Dreamtide depending on who you ask) and are driven by sorrow or guilt to madness.</li> <li>Phoenixi believe the only course of a brighter future is to return all of the pieces of the Center Long to her and compress the universe back into her body. To this end, they gather up people, animals, and other Oroboros and 'feed' them to the Ocean Oroboros (where they are erased in the blood of the Long).</li> <li>Phoenixi generally incorporate flaming feathers into their divine appearance as it symbolizes the rebirth of the universe they seek. In the long game they are pursuing the Big Crunch, smashing all of reality back into a singularity to re-birth the Long.</li> <li>Phoenixi are only viable as an antagonist if the story of the five Longs persists in your version.</li> </ul></li> <li>Shayatin (Deep Ones)<ul><li>Forgotten Gods who lost their reality as they lost their worshippers. They are reduced to empty husks, hungry to feel again.</li> <li>There was a pantheon of gods who predated the original Nidhoggr as rulers of the world. They make up the bulk of the Shayatin.</li> <li>Shayatin attempt to piece together pieces of other people in order to regain a sense of identity. However, a collage of the traits of others is never enough and they perpetually seek to become MORE real, more present, MORE a part of the physical world.</li> <li>It is implied, though not explicitly stated, that those who bargain too much of themselves to the Shayatin join their ranks, pulled out of reality into the Dreamtide and losing their existence.</li> </ul></li> <li>Heart Devourers<ul><li>Remember, eating a Heart anchors ALL antecedents to the new heart. Hostile antecedents can begin to manifest 'tumors' on the devouring Oroboros, such as eyes or mouths. These can be ripped away but will eventually grow back (This was in the third edition, but I thought I'd reiterate it here).</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Purity of Jade<ul><li>Jade is a symbol of purity to dragons, but the stain of the first usurpations lingers on the hearts of the Orobori. This is why they are susceptible to Jade; it burns at the corruption inside of them. Nidhoggr do not share this vulnerability.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Morality System<ul><li>This is excellent, I have no notes.</li> </ul></li> <li>Dreamtide (Magic and access)<ul><li>Edicts are the ultimate form of solipsistic reality and an extension of the power a lucid dreamer exerts over her own dreams. In essence, an Oroboros (or any Dreaming god, such as one of the Shayatin) turns the physical world into her waking dream and then forces her will upon it. At least, that's what I was going for.</li> <li>When I wrote up the Dreamtide, most of the player access was based on the Playstation game Alundra by Matrix Software; it's a typical dreamwalking scenario where making contact with the sleeping party allows the dreamwalker to step into their subconcious, body and all. The stuff about the Miasma of active thought being aligned into clarity by a sleeping party was inspired by old analog televisions and rabbit-ear antennae, along with a healthy dose of psychology (since dreams are the brain's means of sorting and pruning observational stimulus for storage in long-term memory). Hopefully knowing where I was coming from with that mechanic will help you in some regard.</li> </ul></li> <li>Book Format<ul><li>Use what works with your goals, rather than a standardized form. If it helps you to cleave to the format presented--as it did with me--follow it. But do not feel constrained by it; if it interferes with your creativity you should abandon it without a second thought.</li> </ul></li> <li>Hope for Hearts<ul><li>There were two hopes for the creation of new Hearts for insertion into the Oroboros spiral of destruction:<ul><li>Butchering Pilot Lights<ul><li>Draconic offspring (or Spartoi, if you keep them) sometimes have additional chambers in their hearts. By collecting nine of these superfluous 'dragon' chambers (through serial murder), an unscrupulous Oroboros could perform a blood ritual to fashion these severed pieces into a new Dragon Heart. It was never confirmed whether this method actually worked or not; the intent was to allow the Storyteller to decide.</li> </ul></li> <li>The Primordial Dream<ul><li>Before the Dreamtide was removed in the third edition, it was intended that dragons could enter a group-guided dream and attempt to fashion a new Heart out of their own thoughts. This Heart could then be collected and brought back to the physical world.</li> <li>Living Dragons do not have sufficient attachment to make a functioning Heart, however. If players attempted this act, the Heart would corrode upon crossing the threshold into the physical world.</li> <li>There was another option, though. An antecedent, who is forever trapped in dreams, could dream of his own heart and make it real in the process. With the help of the Oroboros to whom he is anchored, this 'copy' Heart could be collected and brought to the physical world, reviving the Antecedent as a full-fledged Oroboros. Once alive again, the Heart is effectively back-in-play (There were thoughts of lingering attachment between the real and copy Heart, but they were never explored. I intended to write a supplement &quot;Hearts Fall to Earth&quot; on the matter, but abandoned the notion when I could no longer work on the core project).</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Assistance<ul><li>I can advise you on the intent of material which existed in the 1st, 2nd, or 3rd phase development, but as I stated before I cannot take an active role in the production of new material. I will not make suggestions for new content/mechanics, nor will I format documents. I am willing to ghost-write new literature (you mentioned you enjoyed Ominous Drums) but only when you are entering the finalizing stages (lore must be established for the entire book and set in concrete). This is because I was forced to revise the story several times as the game evolved and it was weakened as a consequence.</li> <li>I'm willing to supply doodles (not full-sized images, the scrappy tiny drawings like the Dragon and Phoenix fight) to fill margins. Again, I will only contribute in this way once you have confirmed you are in the finalizing stages. I recommend seeking larger artwork from other artists in the meantime.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> If you need to discuss these things and feel they would be better discussed here, I am at your disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T03:23:14-07:00","id":872259,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to see in the new version of Embers would be a system of more free-form sorcery, analogous to Werewolf's Rites. Perhaps the rationale would be that the Oroboroi can, with time and Breath, permanently materialise parts of the Dreamtide, making them real. You could make the process for making new Hearts a 'rumoured' ritual perhaps. It might be a way to bring Antecedents more into the picture, as (as you said) living Oroboroi don't have a strong enough connection to the Dream to pull it off. In order to use their sorcery, they have to appease one or more of their antecedents, something that might be difficult, especially if you claimed your Heart by killing the previous bearer. Even worse would be if the previous bearer was on good terms with his antecedents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T05:47:04-07:00","id":872300,"title":"","content":"In fact, I think that a theme of ancestor (or in this case antecedent) worship would be an interesting one. Perhaps a dragon's antecedents can interfere with him more actively than in previous editions, much like a reasonably powerful and completely cognisant ghost. Ablutions probably wouldn't have much effect except for dealing with other ephemerals but Edicts could certainly be quite powerful. Perhaps when a dragon enters the Dreamtide his antecedents can interfere with him there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T05:55:33-07:00","id":872306,"title":"","content":"Sorry, it's totally possible someone already brought this up, but the font, y'all. The light blue font. It's quite hard to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:24:18-07:00","id":872347,"title":"","content":"Something that definitely has to be addressed in the new version is the relationship of the DReamtide to the Primordial Dram, as well as Oroboroi and the Nidhoggr to Beasts and Horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:31:45-07:00","id":872479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872178#post872178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. You are the lead this project deserves; that was an excellent mission statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, um, thanks. I have experience...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Old playtests, meta-discussions, unwritten lore </div> </div> </div>AWESOME, I will keep this somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could discard Province as a type of Asset and just keep it as Hoard and Maiden, since so many European dragon stories involve greed and kidnapping. </div> </div> </div>See, here's one of the problems with these things: Assets are usually merits you must buy simply because they are useful in themselves. An Immortal being needs a Hoard to keep themselves going for a long time: it's likely that some of the early Orobori, being neigh invulnerable, would simply live like beasts in caves and do jobs in town to accumulate gold. A Province is useful in the simple fact that you can use it for so many things, especially covering up the fact that you're a supposed human who doesn't age and can turn into a Dragon. A Maiden is useful to run errands that you can't and keep you sane. I like the idea of pushing these things for the Orobori, perhaps even having the heart demand them, but they're useful ends in themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edicts are the ultimate form of solipsistic reality and an extension of the power a lucid dreamer exerts over her own dreams. In essence, an Oroboros (or any Dreaming god, such as one of the Shayatin) turns the physical world into her waking dream and then forces her will upon it. At least, that's what I was going for. </div> </div> </div>Ok, that makes sense. I was calling them &quot;purviews and invocations&quot; and describing them as &quot;Divine powers brought over from the Dreamtide.&quot; This really expands upon that. Very useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Draconic offspring (or Spartoi, if you keep them) sometimes have additional chambers in their hearts. By collecting nine of these superfluous 'dragon' chambers (through serial murder), an unscrupulous Oroboros could perform a blood ritual to fashion these severed pieces into a new Dragon Heart. It was never confirmed whether this method actually worked or not; the intent was to allow the Storyteller to decide. </div> </div> </div>I DID remember that, but it doesn't seem like a viable way to repopulate. Also, not sure how important it would be to do so.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]Before the Dreamtide was removed in the third edition, it was intended that dragons could enter a group-guided dream and attempt to fashion a new Heart out of their own thoughts. This Heart could then be collected and brought back to the physical world.[QUOTE]<br /> This is a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I intended to write a supplement &quot;Hearts Fall to Earth&quot; on the matter, but abandoned the notion when I could no longer work on the core project). </div> </div> </div>This is also a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can advise you on the intent of material which existed in the 1st, 2nd, or 3rd phase development, but as I stated before I cannot take an active role in the production of new material. I will not make suggestions for new content/mechanics, nor will I format documents. I am willing to ghost-write new literature (you mentioned you enjoyed Ominous Drums) but only when you are entering the finalizing stages (lore must be established for the entire book and set in concrete). This is because I was forced to revise the story several times as the game evolved and it was weakened as a consequence. </div> </div> </div>You know, you don't have to worry about me becoming beholden to your ideas: I have pretty high hubris, and will not hesitate to toss out whatever you throw in for something that seems better. I just wanted some antecedents around for guidance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm willing to supply doodles (not full-sized images, the scrappy tiny drawings like the Dragon and Phoenix fight) to fill margins. Again, I will only contribute in this way once you have confirmed you are in the finalizing stages. I recommend seeking larger artwork from other artists in the meantime. </div> </div> </div>Alright, well, I can work with whatever you give me on the images...<br /> <img src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/lxumcxl35/Wings_Dissolve.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872259#post872259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd like to see in the new version of Embers would be a system of more free-form sorcery, analogous to Werewolf's Rites.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17cZ1fN3qNhEKtwnuFV1dIuD-FvLYqQvNts45YAd5-0I/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You mean like this thing I've been writing?</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872306#post872306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, it's totally possible someone already brought this up, but the font, y'all. The light blue font. It's quite hard to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 04-23-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:23:56-07:00","id":872538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872479#post872479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean like this thing I've been writing?[/URL]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the stuff you've got so far but the thing is that, while I love ritual sorcery, and even more if the sorcery is fairly free-form, it often lacks flavour, making it little more than a power-gimmick which happens to take longer than the basic powers to use (*cough*, Werewolf, *cough*). Now, I respect that it might not be the best, but I was proposing the antecedents being involved as partly a way to add a little more roleplay into the thing and partly to put the Oroboroi at someone else's mercy a little. It would be entirely up to the Antecedents whether they help with the sorcery or not. Maybe it's possible without them, but more difficult? I can imagine a scene where the Oroboros attempts to convince the voices in his head to help, with some for it and some against.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd be happy to help out with the sorcery thing. Or any of the rest of Embers for that matter. if you want a hand (or a minion), give me a PM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:28:54-07:00","id":872544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872178#post872178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Hope for Hearts[*]There were two hopes for the creation of new Hearts for insertion into the Oroboros spiral of destruction:[*]Butchering Pilot Lights<ul><li>Draconic offspring (or Spartoi, if you keep them) sometimes have additional chambers in their hearts. By collecting nine of these superfluous 'dragon' chambers (through serial murder), an unscrupulous Oroboros could perform a blood ritual to fashion these severed pieces into a new Dragon Heart. It was never confirmed whether this method actually worked or not; the intent was to allow the Storyteller to decide.</li> </ul>[*]The Primordial Dream[LIST][*]Before the Dreamtide was removed in the third edition, it was intended that dragons could enter a group-guided dream and attempt to fashion a new Heart out of their own thoughts. This Heart could then be collected and brought back to the physical world.[*]Living Dragons do not have sufficient attachment to make a functioning Heart, however. If players attempted this act, the Heart would corrode upon crossing the threshold into the physical world.[*]There was another option, though. An antecedent, who is forever trapped in dreams, could dream of his own heart and make it real in the process. With the help of the Oroboros to whom he is anchored, this 'copy' Heart could be collected and brought to the physical world, reviving the Antecedent as a full-fledged Oroboros. Once alive again, the Heart is effectively back-in-play (There were thoughts of lingering attachment between the real and copy Heart, but they were never explored. I intended to write a supplement &quot;Hearts Fall to Earth&quot; on the matter, but abandoned the notion when I could no longer work on the core project).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also worth mentioning that we were suggesting that after a certain power level, dragons could breed (spawn new hearts)/enter other realms and the like but this was very much end game Imperial Mysteries stuff that never was included.<br /> <br /> It is also worth mentioning that I was planning on including hearts that end up being discovered/ejected after a certain time in the more exotic realms. Hedge, Underworld, Astral, Abyss, etc. Such creatures would be... influence to say by said realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T13:34:56-07:00","id":872613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872538#post872538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the stuff you've got so far but the thing is that, while I love ritual sorcery, and even more if the sorcery is fairly free-form, it often lacks flavour, making it little more than a power-gimmick which happens to take longer than the basic powers to use (*cough*, Werewolf, *cough*).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I haven't written in any flavor or anything yet. I should note though that rituals are rituals because someone made them that way, and don't happen with direct interaction with naturally occurring phenomena.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, I respect that it might not be the best, but I was proposing the antecedents being involved as partly a way to add a little more roleplay into the thing and partly to put the Oroboroi at someone else's mercy a little. </div> </div> </div>But only Orobori have antecedents, and I wanted this to be a non-Orobori-Exclusive thing, because non-exclusive powers are what alot of the new stuff is pushing for, and stuff for non-Orobori makes the book have more to offer outside of Orobori, as well as new antagonist concepts. What about an Occultist who knows these powers, and is hunting for a catalyst to do open portals with?<br /> <br /> I had other plans for the Antecedents... But mainly, I think the idea should be that, once you're an antecedent, you're pretty much a ghost and not coming back. Otherwise, that's one less way to kill an Orobori...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872544#post872544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth mentioning that we were suggesting that after a certain power level, dragons could breed (spawn new hearts)/enter other realms and the like but this was very much end game Imperial Mysteries stuff that never was included.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, see, I was wondering about True Form Orobori being able to breed and lay eggs. Maybe it's like with Werewolves, where the female HAS to stay in True Form for an extended period for it to work...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is also worth mentioning that I was planning on including hearts that end up being discovered/ejected after a certain time in the more exotic realms. Hedge, Underworld, Astral, Abyss, etc. Such creatures would be... influence to say by said realm. </div> </div> </div>I was actually hoping to expand upon that angle with stuff like Crossover Ablutions, which are gained from Reimagining while in contact with other supernaturals. An example is my character Jean's Vampire Fangs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:17:00-07:00","id":872638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872613#post872613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I haven't written in any flavor or anything yet. I should note though that rituals are rituals because someone made them that way, and don't happen with direct interaction with naturally occurring phenomena.<br /> <br /> But only Orobori have antecedents, and I wanted this to be a non-Orobori-Exclusive thing, because non-exclusive powers are what alot of the new stuff is pushing for, and stuff for non-Orobori makes the book have more to offer outside of Orobori, as well as new antagonist concepts. What about an Occultist who knows these powers, and is hunting for a catalyst to do open portals with?<br /> <br /> I had other plans for the Antecedents... But mainly, I think the idea should be that, once you're an antecedent, you're pretty much a ghost and not coming back. Otherwise, that's one less way to kill an Orobori...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sorry for butting in like that. I tend to get an idea in my head very strongly and then blurt it out like it's the best thing since sliced bread. Sorry again if I seemed pushy about it all. <br /> <br /> Just an idea though, for keeping the 'ancestors' thing for mortal users of sorcery, what if it could be done without ancestors or antecedents supporting it but it's more difficult. That way, it could lead into a kind of 'family magic' thing, where each successive generation uses the power of those who went before to strengthen their own magics. Oroboroi have it easy, but these sorcerer families have libraries of lore collected over lifetimes of work and they can be quite powerful. I thought that that might be a way to make mortal sorcerers into an actual power in the world of the oroboroi, more than just 'a sorcerer's messing around with things he doesn't understand' while still allowing that kind of plotline. <br /> <br /> Again, I'm sorry if I'm pushing my ideas too aggressively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:30:57-07:00","id":872641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872638#post872638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry if I'm pushing my ideas too aggressively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh.... No.... It's fine. You're making good points and you're not being pushy, but I'm just saying why I don't like them... I don't plan to have complete control over things here....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just an idea though, for keeping the 'ancestors' thing for mortal users of sorcery, what if it could be done without ancestors or antecedents supporting it but it's more difficult. That way, it could lead into a kind of 'family magic' thing, where each successive generation uses the power of those who went before to strengthen their own magics. Oroboroi have it easy, but these sorcerer families have libraries of lore collected over lifetimes of work and they can be quite powerful. I thought that that might be a way to make mortal sorcerers into an actual power in the world of the oroboroi, more than just 'a sorcerer's messing around with things he doesn't understand' while still allowing that kind of plotline. </div> </div> </div>This could be a good setup of Pilot Lights, Finders, and Inheritors, and would also tie in Occultists...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:43:29-07:00","id":872648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872641#post872641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This could be a good setup of Pilot Lights, Finders, and Inheritors, and would also tie in Occultists...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought, plus there's the ever-clich\u00e9d 'estranged family member inherits Grimoire' plotline that you could run. The occult libraries or lore might be of interest to an oroboros of a more sorcerous persuasion, which could be spun out into some legal fiddling and double-dealing in order to get your hands on it. If you're willing to go that far, you could even arrange for the deaths of a sorcerer family, after setting yourself up to inherit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T18:52:12-07:00","id":872795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872479#post872479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, um, thanks. I have experience...</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies, I did not mean to imply you had no experience; I was just impressed because you're clearly much better at this than I was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872479#post872479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, you don't have to worry about me becoming beholden to your ideas: I have pretty high hubris, and will not hesitate to toss out whatever you throw in for something that seems better. I just wanted some antecedents around for guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good to hear; I was far too meek when I was lead developer and I'd hate to poison your efforts. It's good to know I won't be able to derail you.<br /> There's still the problem of my not being compatible with Chronicles of Darkness, which means no new mechanics from me. Still, I'll try to help where I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872479#post872479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, well, I can work with whatever you give me on the images...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my favorite illustration of the bunch.<br /> Anyway...<br /> This too is good to hear. I can draw generic monsters and pass them to you, and you can use them to break up particularly large segments of text. I think I'll stick to divinity 3 and above, though; they're the most fun to draw and a more skilled artist than I would be a better fit for human drawings (I'm hit-and-miss in that regard and they're much more time consuming to produce).<br /> <br /> By your take on that particular image, am I to believe you wish the book to be full color? Would you prefer black-and-white drawings which you can colorize on your own, or do you want submissions to be inked in advance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T09:22:42-07:00","id":873129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development?p=872795#post872795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies, I did not mean to imply you had no experience; I was just impressed because you're clearly much better at this than I was.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I never said you implied that. Why is everyone apologizing to me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is good to hear; I was far too meek when I was lead developer and I'd hate to poison your efforts. It's good to know I won't be able to derail you.<br /> There's still the problem of my not being compatible with Chronicles of Darkness, which means no new mechanics from me. Still, I'll try to help where I can. </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I'd just like to keep that solid connection to the old project, as well as have other people's input and work here, so this isn't just &quot;Raccoon writes some things based on his thoughts on an entirely different project.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, my favorite illustration of the bunch.<br /> Anyway...<br /> This too is good to hear. I can draw generic monsters and pass them to you, and you can use them to break up particularly large segments of text. I think I'll stick to divinity 3 and above, though; they're the most fun to draw and a more skilled artist than I would be a better fit for human drawings (I'm hit-and-miss in that regard and they're much more time consuming to produce). </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I might even be fine with having 2 clashing art styles for Dragons (True Form Orobori) and everything else. I'm looking at going through and updating those drawings you made before. I can draw pretty good concept art, but I'm not fast when it comes to more dynamic poses...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By your take on that particular image, am I to believe you wish the book to be full color? Would you prefer black-and-white drawings which you can colorize on your own, or do you want submissions to be inked in advance? </div> </div> </div>I.... I think I'd like images like the one you've used in your avatar...<br /> <br /> But, if not, I can do a better job than that if you just give me sketches and poses. For now, all we can really incorporate is images for various greater concepts in the book. (no characters until we have new narrative) You'll see what I'm talking about relatively soon.<br /> <br /> When we start playtesting, and I run my forum campaign, I'm thinking a quick route to an effective narrative is to lift the writing straight from that, so I'll also want concept sketches of those characters. That should happen some time in May.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 04-24-2016, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:48:23-07:00","id":873181,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">NEW THREAD!</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-embers-reboot</a></b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T04:18:06-08:00","id":1472953,"title":"","content":"[Recites the ancient languages and performs Thread Necromancy]<br /> <br /> Hi everyone! So, a while back I had someone ask me to make an interactive version of character sheet for what I believe is a play testing version of Dragon The Embers (of which the play testing version of the pdf is listed on my site). Not really realizing it was a play testing version I decided to rebuild the sheet from scratch. I have that finished, and you can download it here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/DragonTheEmbers_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/DragonTheEmbers_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/DragonTheEmbers_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/DragonTheEmbers_2-Page_Interactive.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I ran across this thread and realized that not only is there is another version, there is actually a reboot. I am super behind on this I guess...lol.<br /> <br /> Soooo... should I make an update to the sheet for the version listed on page 1 of this thread, or should